#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Act 1: Where the Onion Service sets up its introduction points"
msgstr "Akt 1: Onion-tjänsten konfigurerar sina introduktionspunkter"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Act 2: Where the Onion Service publishes its descriptors"
msgstr "Akt 2: Onion-tjänsten publicerar sina deskriptorer"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Act 3:  Where a client wants to visit the Onion Service"
msgstr "Akt 3: En klient vill besöka onion-tjänsten"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Act 4: Where the client introduces itself to the Onion Service"
msgstr "Akt 4: Klienten presenterar sig för onion-tjänsten"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Act 5:  Where the client verify onion address signature"
msgstr "Akt 5: Klienten verifierar onion-adressens signatur"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Act 6: Where the client establishes a rendezvous point"
msgstr "Akt 6: Klienten upprättar en mötespunkt"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Act 7: Where the Onion Service rendezvous with the client"
msgstr "Akt 7: Onion-tjänsten möter klienten"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Act 8: Where the rendezvous point verifies the client's secret"
msgstr "Akt 8: Mötespunkten verifierar klientens hemlighet"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Act 9: Where the Onion Service rendezvous with the client"
msgstr "Akt 9: Onion-tjänsten möter klienten"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"All the previous steps were just set up for the Onion Service so that it's "
"reachable by clients."
msgstr ""
"Alla tidigare steg var endast förberedelser för att göra onion-tjänsten "
"nåbar för klienter."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "An Onion Service's IP address is protected."
msgstr "En onion-tjänsts IP-adress är skyddad."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"And inside the descriptor, there are the introduction points that allow the "
"client to introduce themselves to SecureDrop's Onion Service."
msgstr ""
"I deskriptorn finns introduktionspunkterna som gör det möjligt för klienten "
"att presentera sig för SecureDrops onion-tjänst."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"As the first step in the protocol, the Onion Service will contact a bunch of "
"Tor relays and ask them to act as its _introduction points_ by establishing "
"long-term circuits to them."
msgstr ""
"Som första steg i protokollet kontaktar onion-tjänsten ett antal Tor-reläer "
"och ber dem fungera som dess _introduktionspunkter_ genom att upprätta "
"långvariga kretsar till dem."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Before the introduction takes place, the client (in this case, you) picks a "
"Tor relay and establishes a circuit to it."
msgstr ""
"Innan introduktionen sker väljer klienten – i det här fallet du – ett Tor-"
"relä och upprättar en krets till det."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "End-to-end authentication"
msgstr "Totalsträcksautentisering"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "End-to-end encryption"
msgstr "Totalsträckskryptering"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Finally, using the rendezvous point, a Tor circuit is formed between you and "
"your newspaper's SecureDrop Onion Service."
msgstr ""
"Slutligen bildas en Tor-krets mellan dig och din tidnings SecureDrop-onion-"
"tjänst via mötespunkten."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"For this reason, the Onion Service assembles an _Onion Service descriptor_, "
"containing a list of its introduction points (and \"authentication keys\"), "
"and signs this descriptor with the Onion Service's _identity private key_."
msgstr ""
"Därför sammanställer onion-tjänsten en _deskriptor för onion-tjänsten_ som "
"innehåller en lista över dess introduktionspunkter och "
"”autentiseringsnycklar”. Deskriptorn signeras med onion-tjänstens _privata "
"identitetsnyckel_."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Further resources"
msgstr "Ytterligare resurser"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Here are some more resources if you want to learn more:"
msgstr "Här är några fler resurser om du vill lära dig mer:"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Here is a detailed breakdown of how this happens:"
msgstr "Här följer en detaljerad genomgång av hur det går till:"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"In general, the complete connection between client and Onion Service "
"consists of 6 relays: 3 of them were picked by the client, with the third "
"being the rendezvous point, and the other 3 were picked by the Onion Service."
msgstr ""
"Den fullständiga anslutningen mellan klienten och onion-tjänsten består i "
"allmänhet av sex reläer: tre väljs av klienten, där det tredje är "
"mötespunkten, och de övriga tre väljs av onion-tjänsten."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"In particular, an Onion Service's address looks like this: "
"`vww6ybal4bd7szmgncyruucpgfkqahzddi37ktceo3ah7ngmcopnpyyd.onion`"
msgstr ""
"En onion-tjänsts adress kan exempelvis se ut så här: "
"`vww6ybal4bd7szmgncyruucpgfkqahzddi37ktceo3ah7ngmcopnpyyd.onion`"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"In this case, the client has the onion address of SecureDrop and want to "
"visit it, so they connect to the service with Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"I det här fallet har klienten SecureDrops onion-adress och vill besöka "
"tjänsten, så klienten ansluter med Tor Browser."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Is your network filtered and you can't open ports on your firewall?"
msgstr "Är nätverket filtrerat så att du inte kan öppna portar i brandväggen?"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"It uses an anonymized Tor circuit to do this upload so that it does not "
"reveal its location."
msgstr ""
"Uppladdningen görs via en anonymiserad Tor-krets så att platsen inte "
"avslöjas."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Let's imagine that your local newspaper decides to set up an Onion Service "
"(using [SecureDrop](https://securedrop.org/)) to receive anonymous tips."
msgstr ""
"Föreställ dig att din lokaltidning bestämmer sig för att konfigurera en "
"onion-tjänst med [SecureDrop](https://securedrop.org/) för att ta emot "
"anonyma tips."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Location hiding"
msgstr "Dold plats"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "NAT punching"
msgstr "Genomträngning av NAT"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "No impersonation is possible, which is generally not the case."
msgstr ""
"Ingen kan utge sig för att vara tjänsten, vilket vanligtvis annars är "
"möjligt."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Now let's fast-forward to the point where an actual client wants to visit "
"the service."
msgstr ""
"Nu snabbspolar vi till den tidpunkt då en verklig klient vill besöka "
"tjänsten."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Now that the introduction points are set up, we need to create a way for "
"clients to be able to find them."
msgstr ""
"När introduktionspunkterna är konfigurerade behöver vi skapa ett sätt för "
"klienter att hitta dem."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Now the next thing that needs to happen is that the client goes to the "
"_distributed hash table_ from **Step 2** and ask for the signed descriptor "
"of SecureDrop's Onion Service."
msgstr ""
"Därefter går klienten till den _distribuerade hashtabellen_ från **steg 2** "
"och begär den signerade deskriptorn för SecureDrops onion-tjänst."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Now the question becomes **what kind of protocol is needed to achieve all "
"these properties?**"
msgstr ""
"Frågan blir nu **vilket slags protokoll som krävs för att uppnå alla dessa "
"egenskaper**."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Onion service traffic is encrypted from the client to the onion host."
msgstr ""
"Trafiken till onion-tjänsten är krypterad från klienten till onion-värden."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Onion services are an overlay network on top of TCP/IP, so in some sense IP "
"addresses are not even meaningful to Onion Services: they are not even used "
"in the protocol."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster är ett överlagringsnätverk ovanpå TCP/IP. På sätt och vis "
"saknar IP-adresser därför betydelse för onion-tjänster: de används inte ens "
"i protokollet."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Onion services are services that can only be accessed over Tor."
msgstr "Onion-tjänster är tjänster som endast kan nås via Tor."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Onion services don't need open ports because they punch through NAT. They "
"only establish outgoing connections."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster behöver inga öppna portar eftersom de tar sig igenom NAT. De "
"upprättar endast utgående anslutningar."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Onion services offer various privacy and security benefits to their users."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster ger sina användare flera fördelar för integritet och säkerhet."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Presentations about Onion Services: [Understanding Tor Onion Services and "
"Their Use Cases - HOPE XI 2016](https://www.youtube.com/watch?"
"v=VmsFxBEN3fc), [DEF CON 25 - Roger Dingledine - Next Generation Tor Onion "
"Services](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Di7qAVidy1Y)."
msgstr ""
"Presentationer om onion-tjänster: [Understanding Tor Onion Services and "
"Their Use Cases – HOPE XI 2016](https://www.youtube.com/watch?"
"v=VmsFxBEN3fc), [DEF CON 25 – Roger Dingledine – Next Generation Tor Onion "
"Services](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Di7qAVidy1Y)."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Running an Onion Service gives your users all the security of HTTPS with the "
"added privacy benefits of Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"Genom att driva en onion-tjänst ger du användarna hela HTTPS-säkerheten samt "
"de ytterligare integritetsfördelarna med Tor Browser."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Say you want to anonymously send some tax fraud data to your local newspaper "
"through its SecureDrop."
msgstr ""
"Anta att du anonymt vill skicka uppgifter om skattebedrägeri till din "
"lokaltidning via dess SecureDrop."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "That's one of the reasons we can achieve the security properties above."
msgstr ""
"Det är en av anledningarna till att vi kan uppnå säkerhetsegenskaperna ovan."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "The Onion Service Protocol: Overview"
msgstr "Protokollet för onion-tjänster: översikt"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The Onion Service connects to the rendezvous point (through an anonymized "
"circuit) and sends the \"one-time secret\" to it."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänsten ansluter till mötespunkten via en anonymiserad krets och "
"skickar engångshemligheten till den."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The Onion Service protocol uses the Tor network so that the client can "
"introduce itself to the service, and then set up a rendezvous point with the "
"service over the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Protokollet för onion-tjänster använder Tor-nätverket så att klienten kan "
"presentera sig för tjänsten och sedan upprätta en mötespunkt med tjänsten "
"över Tor-nätverket."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The Onion Service upload that signed descriptor to a _distributed hash "
"table_, which is part of the Tor network, so that clients can also get it."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänsten laddar upp den signerade deskriptorn till en _distribuerad "
"hashtabell_ som ingår i Tor-nätverket, så att klienterna kan hämta den."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The Onion Service will hide and protect itself behind the Tor network by "
"only allowing access through three introduction points that it connects to "
"through a three-hop Tor circuit."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänsten döljer och skyddar sig bakom Tor-nätverket genom att endast "
"tillåta åtkomst via tre introduktionspunkter som den ansluter till genom Tor-"
"kretsar med tre hopp."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The [Tor design paper](https://spec.torproject.org/tor-design) describing "
"the original design."
msgstr ""
"[Tors designartikel](https://spec.torproject.org/tor-design) beskriver den "
"ursprungliga utformningen."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The [Tor v3 Onion Services](https://spec.torproject.org/rend-spec-v3) "
"protocol specification."
msgstr ""
"Protokollspecifikationen för [Tors v3-onion-tjänster](https://"
"spec.torproject.org/rend-spec-v3)."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The _identity private key_ used here is the private part of the **public key "
"that is encoded in the Onion Service address**."
msgstr ""
"Den _privata identitetsnyckeln_ som används här är den privata delen av "
"**den offentliga nyckel som är kodad i onion-tjänstens adress**."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The client asks the relay to become their rendezvous point and give it an "
"\"one-time secret\" that will be used as part of the rendezvous procedure."
msgstr ""
"Klienten ber reläet att bli dess mötespunkt och ger det en engångshemlighet "
"som används i mötesförfarandet."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The introduction point passes your details (secret string and rendezvous "
"address) on to the Onion Service, which runs multiple verification processes "
"to decide whether you're trustworthy or not."
msgstr ""
"Introduktionspunkten vidarebefordrar dina uppgifter – den hemliga strängen "
"och mötesadressen – till onion-tjänsten, som genomför flera kontroller för "
"att avgöra om du är betrodd."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The rendezvous point makes one final verification to match the secret "
"strings from you and service (the latter also comes from you but has been "
"relayed through the service)."
msgstr ""
"Mötespunkten gör en sista kontroll för att jämföra den hemliga strängen från "
"dig med strängen från tjänsten. Den senare kommer också från dig men har "
"vidarebefordrats genom tjänsten."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"The rendezvous point simply relays (end-to-end encrypted) messages from "
"client to service and vice versa."
msgstr ""
"Mötespunkten vidarebefordrar endast totalsträckskrypterade meddelanden från "
"klienten till tjänsten och i motsatt riktning."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"These circuits are anonymized circuits, so the server does not reveal the "
"service location to the introduction points."
msgstr ""
"Kretsarna är anonymiserade, så servern avslöjar inte tjänstens plats för "
"introduktionspunkterna."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"This could happen if you are in a university campus, an office, an airport, "
"or pretty much anywhere."
msgstr ""
"Det kan exempelvis vara fallet på ett universitetsområde, ett kontor, en "
"flygplats eller nästan var som helst."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "This is like getting strong SSL/HTTPS for free."
msgstr "Det motsvarar att få stark SSL/HTTPS utan kostnad."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"This looks weird and random because it's the _identity public key_ of the "
"Onion Service."
msgstr ""
"Adressen ser underlig och slumpmässig ut eftersom den är onion-tjänstens "
"_offentliga identitetsnyckel_."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "This provides _location hiding_ to this connection."
msgstr "Detta ger anslutningen egenskapen _dold plats_."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"This provides the _end-to-end authentication_ security property, since we "
"are now sure that this descriptor could only be produced by that Onion "
"Service and no one else."
msgstr ""
"Detta ger säkerhetsegenskapen _totalsträcksautentisering_, eftersom vi nu "
"vet att deskriptorn endast kan ha skapats av just den onion-tjänsten."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "This was just a high-level overview of the Tor Onion Services protocol."
msgstr ""
"Detta var endast en översiktlig beskrivning av Tors protokoll för onion-"
"tjänster."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Usually, people connect to an IP address and are done, but how can you "
"connect to something that does not have an IP address?"
msgstr ""
"Vanligtvis ansluter människor till en IP-adress och saken är klar, men hur "
"ansluter man till något som inte har en IP-adress?"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"Usually, reaching a website does not mean that a man-in-the-middle did not "
"reroute to some other location (e.g. DNS attacks)."
msgstr ""
"När du når en vanlig webbplats betyder det inte nödvändigtvis att en man-i-"
"mitten inte har dirigerat om dig till en annan plats, till exempel genom ett "
"DNS-angrepp."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"When a user visits a particular onion, they know that the content they are "
"seeing can only come from that particular onion."
msgstr ""
"När en användare besöker en viss onion-adress vet användaren att innehållet "
"endast kan komma från just den onion-tjänsten."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"When the client receives the signed descriptor, they verify the signature of "
"the descriptor using the public key that is encoded in the onion address."
msgstr ""
"När klienten tar emot den signerade deskriptorn verifierar den signaturen "
"med den offentliga nyckel som är kodad i onion-adressen."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Why Onion Services?"
msgstr "Varför onion-tjänster?"

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid ""
"You find the onion address for the newspaper's SecureDrop from a public "
"website or friend."
msgstr ""
"Du hittar onion-adressen till tidningens SecureDrop på en offentlig "
"webbplats eller får den av en vän."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "Learn how Onion Services work."
msgstr "Lär dig hur onion-tjänster fungerar."

#: content/onion-services/overview/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/overview/
msgid "How do Onion Services work?"
msgstr "Hur fungerar onion-tjänster?"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "(Optional) Step 5: Running multiple Onion Services"
msgstr "(Valfritt) Steg 5: Kör flera onion-tjänster"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"**Tip:** A good practice to avoid leaking an Onion Service to a local "
"network is to run Onion Services over Unix sockets instead of a TCP socket."
msgstr ""
"**Tips:** En bra metod för att undvika att en onion-tjänst läcker till ett "
"lokalt nätverk är att köra onion-tjänster över Unix-socketar i stället för "
"en TCP-socket."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"All the following `HiddenServicePort` lines refer to this `HiddenServiceDir` "
"line, until you add another `HiddenServiceDir` line:"
msgstr ""
"Alla följande `HiddenServicePort`-rader hör till den här `HiddenServiceDir`-"
"raden tills du lägger till ännu en `HiddenServiceDir`-rad:"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Apache is available in the main repository of multiple Linux and *BSD "
"distributions."
msgstr "Apache finns i huvudförrådet för flera Linux- och *BSD-distributioner."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"As a first step, you should set up a web server locally, like Nginx, Apache, "
"or your favorite web server."
msgstr ""
"Som första steg bör du konfigurera en lokal webbserver, till exempel Nginx, "
"Apache eller den webbserver du föredrar."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"As an example, we will cover how to set up an onionsite with Nginx and "
"Apache on Debian."
msgstr ""
"Som exempel visar vi hur en onion-webbplats konfigureras med Nginx och "
"Apache på Debian."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"As part of this guide, we will assume you have a functional Tor in your "
"machine."
msgstr ""
"I den här guiden förutsätter vi att du har en fungerande Tor-installation på "
"datorn."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"By default, the web server will be running on `localhost:80` at the end of "
"the installation."
msgstr ""
"Som standard körs webbservern på `localhost:80` när installationen är klar."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Depending on your operating system and setup, your Tor configuration file "
"can be at a different location or look different."
msgstr ""
"Beroende på operativsystem och konfiguration kan Tors konfigurationsfil "
"finnas på en annan plats eller se annorlunda ut."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Finally, if you plan to keep your service available for a long time, you "
"might want to make a backup copy of the `private_key` file somewhere."
msgstr ""
"Om du planerar att hålla tjänsten tillgänglig under lång tid bör du "
"slutligen säkerhetskopiera filen `private_key` på en annan plats."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"For example, in Nginx and using Tor with Unix sockets, the configuration "
"would look like this:"
msgstr ""
"Med Nginx och Tor över Unix-socketar skulle konfigurationen exempelvis se ut "
"så här:"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"For the technical details of how the Onion Service protocol works, see our "
"Onion Service protocol page."
msgstr ""
"Tekniska detaljer om hur protokollet för onion-tjänster fungerar finns på "
"vår sida om protokollet."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"If Tor starts up again, great. Otherwise, something is wrong. First look at "
"your logfiles for hints."
msgstr ""
"Om Tor startar igen är allt bra. Annars är något fel. Börja med att leta "
"efter ledtrådar i loggfilerna."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"If it doesn't work, look in your logs for some hints, and keep playing with "
"it until it works."
msgstr ""
"Om det inte fungerar, leta efter ledtrådar i loggarna och fortsätt justera "
"konfigurationen tills den fungerar."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"If you get stuck or want to do more, find a friend who can help you or join "
"our [tor-onions](https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-"
"onions) mailing list to speak with other operators."
msgstr ""
"Om du kör fast eller vill göra mer kan du be en vän om hjälp eller gå med i "
"vår e-postlista [tor-onions](https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/"
"listinfo/tor-onions) för att prata med andra operatörer."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"If you have a static website, but never installed Nginx or Apache, another "
"project to try is [OnionShare](https://onionshare.org), where running an "
"onionsite will be easier: guided with a graphic interface and with minimal "
"configuration."
msgstr ""
"Om du har en statisk webbplats men aldrig har installerat Nginx eller Apache "
"kan du prova [OnionShare](https://onionshare.org). Där är det enklare att "
"köra en onion-webbplats med ett grafiskt gränssnitt och minimal "
"konfiguration."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"If you want to forward multiple virtual ports for a single Onion Service, "
"just add more `HiddenServicePort` lines."
msgstr ""
"Lägg till fler `HiddenServicePort`-rader om du vill vidarebefordra flera "
"virtuella portar för en enda onion-tjänst."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"If you want to run multiple Onion Services from the same Tor client, just "
"add another `HiddenServiceDir` line."
msgstr ""
"Lägg till ännu en `HiddenServiceDir`-rad om du vill köra flera onion-"
"tjänster från samma Tor-klient."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"If you're running multiple onionsites on the same web server, remember to "
"edit your web server virtual host file and add the onion address for each "
"website."
msgstr ""
"Om du kör flera onion-webbplatser på samma webbserver måste du redigera "
"webbserverns Virtual Host-fil och lägga till onion-adressen för varje "
"webbplats."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"If your keys leak, other people can impersonate your Onion Service, deeming "
"it compromised, useless, and dangerous to visit."
msgstr ""
"Om nycklarna läcker kan andra utge sig för att vara din onion-tjänst. Då är "
"tjänsten komprometterad, oanvändbar och farlig att besöka."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"It is important to note that an Onion Service configured like this will be "
"readable by anybody who knows or discovers the address."
msgstr ""
"Observera att en onion-tjänst som konfigureras på detta sätt kan läsas av "
"alla som känner till eller hittar adressen."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"It will print some warnings or error messages. That should give you an idea "
"of what went wrong."
msgstr ""
"Då skrivs varningar eller felmeddelanden ut som bör ge en uppfattning om vad "
"som gick fel."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Make sure this is the case."
msgstr "Kontrollera att så är fallet."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Nginx is available in the main repository of multiple Linux and *BSD "
"distributions."
msgstr "Nginx finns i huvudförrådet för flera Linux- och *BSD-distributioner."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Now save your `torrc` and restart Tor."
msgstr "Spara nu `torrc` och starta om Tor."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Now that you have an onionsite working, you may want to deploy [Onion-"
"Location](../advanced/onion-location/), or use tools like Docker, [Heroku]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/hiro/onions-on-heroku), [Terraform](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/hiro/terraform-onions), [Ansible](https://"
"galaxy.ansible.com/systemli/onion) or [stem](https://stem.torproject.org/"
"tutorials/over_the_river.html) to automate the management of your Onion "
"Services."
msgstr ""
"När onion-webbplatsen fungerar kanske du vill driftsätta [Onion-Location](../"
"advanced/onion-location/) eller använda verktyg som Docker, [Heroku](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/hiro/onions-on-heroku), [Terraform](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/hiro/terraform-onions), [Ansible](https://"
"galaxy.ansible.com/systemli/onion) eller [stem](https://stem.torproject.org/"
"tutorials/over_the_river.html) för att automatisera hanteringen av onion-"
"tjänsterna."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Now to get your Onion Service address, go to your `HiddenServiceDir` "
"directory, and find a file named `hostname`."
msgstr ""
"Gå till katalogen `HiddenServiceDir` och leta efter filen `hostname` för att "
"få onion-tjänstens adress."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Now you can connect to your Onion Service using Tor Browser, and you should "
"get the HTML page you set up back in **Step 1**."
msgstr ""
"Nu kan du ansluta till onion-tjänsten med Tor Browser. HTML-sidan som du "
"konfigurerade i **steg 1** bör visas."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Once your web server is set up, make sure it works: open your browser and go "
"to http://localhost/."
msgstr ""
"När webbservern är konfigurerad kontrollerar du att den fungerar genom att "
"öppna webbläsaren och gå till http://localhost/."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Onion services version 2 is deprecated and is no longer supported since the "
"0.4.6.1-alpha Tor release, in 2021."
msgstr ""
"Version 2 av onion-tjänster är föråldrad och har inte fått stöd sedan Tor-"
"version 0.4.6.1-alpha år 2021."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Please read the blog post [Onion Service version deprecation timeline]"
"(https://blog.torproject.org/v2-deprecation-timeline) for more information."
msgstr ""
"Läs blogginlägget [Tidsplan för utfasning av versioner av onion-tjänster]"
"(https://blog.torproject.org/v2-deprecation-timeline) för mer information."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Read more about [Client authorization](../advanced/client-auth/) "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"Läs mer i dokumentationen om [klientauktorisering](../advanced/client-auth/)."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Setting up a web server can be complex."
msgstr "Det kan vara komplicerat att konfigurera en webbserver."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Some onionsite operators may not want to disclose their Onion Service "
"location."
msgstr ""
"Vissa operatörer av onion-webbplatser vill kanske inte avslöja onion-"
"tjänstens plats."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Step 0: Get a working Tor"
msgstr "Steg 0: Skaffa en fungerande Tor-installation"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Step 1: Get a web server working"
msgstr "Steg 1: Konfigurera en fungerande webbserver"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Step 2: Configure your Tor Onion Service"
msgstr "Steg 2: Konfigurera din Tor-onion-tjänst"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Step 3: Restart Tor and check that it worked"
msgstr "Steg 3: Starta om Tor och kontrollera att det fungerade"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Step 4: Test that your Onion Service works"
msgstr "Steg 4: Testa att onion-tjänsten fungerar"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Step 6: Security advice and more tips"
msgstr "Steg 6: Säkerhetsråd och fler tips"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"That is not an easy task, and these resources will help on how to make this "
"possible:"
msgstr ""
"Det är ingen enkel uppgift. Följande resurser hjälper dig att göra det "
"möjligt:"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"The `HiddenServiceDir` line specifies the directory which should contain "
"information and cryptographic keys for your Onion Service."
msgstr ""
"Raden `HiddenServiceDir` anger katalogen som ska innehålla information och "
"kryptografiska nycklar för onion-tjänsten."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"The `HiddenServicePort` line specifies a _virtual port_ (that is, the port "
"that people visiting your Onion Service will be using), and in the above "
"case it says that any traffic incoming to port 80 of your Onion Service "
"should be redirected to `127.0.0.1:80` (which is where the web server from "
"step 1 is listening)."
msgstr ""
"Raden `HiddenServicePort` anger en _virtuell port_ – porten som besökare på "
"onion-tjänsten använder. I exemplet ovan innebär raden att all trafik som "
"kommer till port 80 på onion-tjänsten omdirigeras till `127.0.0.1:80`, där "
"webbservern från steg 1 lyssnar."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"The `hostname` file in your Onion Service configuration directory contains "
"the hostname for your new onion v3 service."
msgstr ""
"Filen `hostname` i onion-tjänstens konfigurationskatalog innehåller "
"värdnamnet för din nya v3-onion-tjänst."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"The default version of Onion Services is version 3 and its address is 56 "
"characters long, without the `http://` and `.onion` parts."
msgstr ""
"Standardversionen av onion-tjänster är version 3. Adressen är 56 tecken "
"lång, utan delarna `http://` och `.onion`."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"The next step is opening the config file of Tor (torrc) and doing the "
"appropriate configurations to setup an Onion Service."
msgstr ""
"Nästa steg är att öppna Tors konfigurationsfil (torrc) och göra de "
"inställningar som krävs för att konfigurera en onion-tjänst."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"The other files are your Onion Service keys, so it is imperative that these "
"are kept private."
msgstr ""
"De andra filerna är onion-tjänstens nycklar och måste ovillkorligen hållas "
"privata."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Then try putting a file in the main HTML directory, and make sure it shows "
"up when you access the site."
msgstr ""
"Prova sedan att lägga en fil i huvudkatalogen för HTML och kontrollera att "
"den visas när du öppnar webbplatsen."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Therefore, you need to configure your web server so it doesn't give away any "
"information about you, your computer, or your location."
msgstr ""
"Du måste därför konfigurera webbservern så att den inte avslöjar information "
"om dig, din dator eller din plats."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "This guide shows you how to set up an Onion Service for your website."
msgstr ""
"Den här guiden visar hur du konfigurerar en onion-tjänst för din webbplats."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "To install `apache2` package:"
msgstr "Installera paketet `apache2`:"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "To install `nginx` package:"
msgstr "Installera paketet `nginx`:"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "To set up Tor, please follow the [Tor installation guide](./install/)."
msgstr ""
"Följ [installationsguiden för Tor](./install/) för att konfigurera Tor."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Tor should be up and running correctly for this guide to work."
msgstr "Tor måste vara igång och fungera korrekt för att guiden ska fungera."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"Typically, there are typos in the `torrc` or wrong directory permissions "
"(See the [logging FAQ](https://www.torproject.org/docs/faq#Logs) entry if "
"you don't know how to enable or find your log file.)"
msgstr ""
"Vanliga orsaker är skrivfel i `torrc` eller felaktiga katalogbehörigheter. "
"Se posten om [loggning i vanliga frågor](https://www.torproject.org/docs/"
"faq#Logs) om du inte vet hur loggfilen aktiveras eller hittas."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"We recommend you install a new separate web server for your Onion Service, "
"since even if you already have one installed, you may be using it (or want "
"to use it later) for a regular website."
msgstr ""
"Vi rekommenderar att du installerar en ny, separat webbserver för onion-"
"tjänsten. Även om du redan har en installerad kanske du använder den, eller "
"senare vill använda den, för en vanlig webbplats."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"When Tor starts, it will automatically create the `HiddenServiceDir` that "
"you specified (if necessary)."
msgstr ""
"När Tor startar skapar programmet automatiskt den angivna katalogen "
"`HiddenServiceDir` om det behövs."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"You can make Onion Services require authentication, and only users with a "
"private key will access the service."
msgstr ""
"Du kan kräva autentisering för onion-tjänster så att endast användare med en "
"privat nyckel får åtkomst."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "You should also know where Tor's configuration files are."
msgstr "Du bör också veta var Tors konfigurationsfiler finns."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "You will need to add the following two lines to your `torrc` file:"
msgstr "Lägg till följande två rader i filen `torrc`:"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"You will want to change the `HiddenServiceDir` line, so that it points to an "
"actual directory that is readable/writeable by the user that will be running "
"Tor."
msgstr ""
"Ändra raden `HiddenServiceDir` så att den pekar på en verklig katalog som "
"användaren som kör Tor kan läsa och skriva till."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"[Onion services best practices](https://riseup.net/en/security/network-"
"security/tor/onionservices-best-practices) by Riseup Collective."
msgstr ""
"[Bästa praxis för onion-tjänster](https://riseup.net/en/security/network-"
"security/tor/onionservices-best-practices) av Riseup Collective."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid ""
"[OnionScan](https://onionscan.org/) is a tool to check if your onionsite is "
"leaking information that could compromise your anonymity like your server IP "
"address."
msgstr ""
"[OnionScan](https://onionscan.org/) är ett verktyg som kontrollerar om onion-"
"webbplatsen läcker information som kan äventyra din anonymitet, till exempel "
"serverns IP-adress."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "[Operational Security](../advanced/opsec/)."
msgstr "[Operativ säkerhet](../advanced/opsec/)."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.cta
#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.cta
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "Get Started"
msgstr "Kom igång"

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Learn how to set up an onionsite of your very own."
msgstr "Lär dig konfigurera en egen onion-webbplats."

#: content/onion-services/setup/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/
msgid "Set up Your Onion Service"
msgstr "Konfigurera din onion-tjänst"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "**Admin access:** To install Tor you need root privileges."
msgstr ""
"**Administratörsåtkomst:** Du behöver root-behörighet för att installera Tor."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "**Do not use the packages in Ubuntu's universe**."
msgstr "**Använd inte paketen i Ubuntus universe-arkiv**."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "1. Configure Tor Package repository"
msgstr "1. Konfigurera Tors paketförråd"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "1. Configure Tor package repository"
msgstr "1. Konfigurera Tors paketförråd"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "1. Download latest release and dependencies"
msgstr "1. Hämta den senaste versionen och beroendena"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "1. Install a package manager"
msgstr "1. Installera en pakethanterare"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "1. Package Installation"
msgstr "1. Installera paketet"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/exit/centos-rhel/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/exit/debian-ubuntu/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/exit/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/exit/opensuse/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/exit/centos-rhel/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/exit/debian-ubuntu/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/exit/freebsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/exit/opensuse/
msgid "1. Package installation"
msgstr "1. Installera paketet"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/bridge/alpine/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/bridge/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/bridge/opensuse/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/bridge/alpine/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/bridge/openbsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/bridge/opensuse/
msgid "2. Install Tor"
msgstr "2. Installera Tor"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/
msgid "2. Package installation"
msgstr "2. Installera paketet"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"Add the following to /etc/yum.repos.d/tor.repo and then install the tor "
"package."
msgstr ""
"Lägg till följande i /etc/yum.repos.d/tor.repo och installera sedan paketet "
"tor."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"Below all commands that need to be run as root user like apt and dpkg are "
"prepended with '#', while commands to be run as user with '$' resembling the "
"standard prompt in a terminal."
msgstr ""
"Nedan föregås alla kommandon som måste köras som root-användare, till "
"exempel apt och dpkg, av ”#”. Kommandon som ska köras som vanlig användare "
"föregås av ”$”, i likhet med den vanliga terminalprompten."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/bridge/debian-ubuntu/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/bridge/debian-ubuntu/
msgid "Debian / Ubuntu"
msgstr "Debian/Ubuntu"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"Enable the Torproject package repository by following the [instructions]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/little-t-tor/getting-started/installing/)."
msgstr ""
"Aktivera The Tor Projects paketförråd genom att följa [instruktionerna]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/little-t-tor/getting-started/installing/)."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "If you are using Homebrew in a Terminal window, run:"
msgstr "Om du använder Homebrew i ett terminalfönster kör du:"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "If you are using Macports in a Terminal window, run:"
msgstr "Om du använder MacPorts i ett terminalfönster kör du:"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"If you're building from source, first install [libevent](http://"
"www.monkey.org/~provos/libevent/), and make sure you have openssl and zlib "
"(including the -devel packages if applicable)."
msgstr ""
"Om du bygger från källkod ska du först installera [libevent](http://"
"www.monkey.org/~provos/libevent/) och kontrollera att openssl och zlib finns "
"installerade, inklusive eventuella -devel-paket."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"In the past they have not reliably been updated. That means you could be "
"missing stability and security fixes."
msgstr ""
"Tidigare har de inte alltid uppdaterats tillförlitligt. Det kan innebära att "
"du går miste om stabilitets- och säkerhetskorrigeringar."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "Installing Tor from source"
msgstr "Installera Tor från källkod"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"Now you can run tor as src/app/tor (0.4.3.x and later), or you can run `make "
"install` (as root if necessary) to install it into /usr/local/, and then you "
"can start it just by running tor."
msgstr ""
"Nu kan du köra tor som src/app/tor (0.4.3.x och senare), eller köra `make "
"install` – som root om det behövs – för att installera det i /usr/local/. "
"Därefter kan du starta det genom att köra tor."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/bridge/openbsd/contents.lr:page.title
#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.title
#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/bridge/openbsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid "OpenBSD"
msgstr "OpenBSD"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"The latest release of Tor can be found on the [download](https://"
"www.torproject.org/download/tor/) page."
msgstr ""
"Den senaste Tor-utgåvan finns på [hämtningssidan](https://www.torproject.org/"
"download/tor/)."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "There are two package manager on OS X: Homebrew and Macports."
msgstr "Det finns två pakethanterare för OS X: Homebrew och MacPorts."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"To install Homebrew follow the instructions on [brew.sh](https://brew.sh/)."
msgstr ""
"Installera Homebrew genom att följa anvisningarna på [brew.sh](https://"
"brew.sh/)."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"To install Macports follow the instructions on [macports.org/install.php]"
"(https://www.macports.org/install.php)."
msgstr ""
"Installera MacPorts genom att följa anvisningarna på [macports.org/"
"install.php](https://www.macports.org/install.php)."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid ""
"To open a root terminal you have several options: sudo su, or sudo -i, or su "
"-l. Note that sudo asks for your user password, while su expects the root "
"password of your system."
msgstr ""
"Du kan öppna en root-terminal på flera sätt: sudo su, sudo -i eller su -l. "
"Observera att sudo begär ditt användarlösenord medan su förväntar sig "
"systemets root-lösenord."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "You can use the package manager of your choice."
msgstr "Du kan använda valfri pakethanterare."

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "macOS"
msgstr "macOS"

#: content/onion-services/setup/install/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/setup/install/
msgid "How to install Tor"
msgstr "Så installerar du Tor"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"\"DW is a global advocate for freedom of opinion and freedom of speech. […] "
"It is therefore a logical step for us to also use Tor to reach people in "
"censored markets who previously had limited or no access to free media.\" "
"[Deutsche Welle](https://www.dw.com/en/dw-websites-accessible-via-tor-"
"protocol/a-51338328)"
msgstr ""
"”DW är en global förespråkare för åsikts- och yttrandefrihet. […] Det är "
"därför ett naturligt steg för oss att även använda Tor för att nå människor "
"på censurerade marknader som tidigare hade begränsad eller ingen tillgång "
"till fria medier.” [Deutsche Welle](https://www.dw.com/en/dw-websites-"
"accessible-via-tor-protocol/a-51338328)"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"\"The browser can obscure who is using it and what data is being accessed, "
"which can help people avoid government surveillance and censorship. "
"Countries including China, Iran and Vietnam are among those who have tried "
"to block access to the BBC News website or programmes.\" [BBC](https://"
"www.bbc.com/news/technology-50150981)"
msgstr ""
"”Webbläsaren kan dölja vem som använder den och vilka uppgifter som hämtas, "
"vilket kan hjälpa människor att undvika statlig övervakning och censur. "
"Kina, Iran och Vietnam hör till de länder som har försökt blockera åtkomsten "
"till BBC News webbplats eller program.” [BBC](https://www.bbc.com/news/"
"technology-50150981)"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"> I developed OnionShare to make this file sharing process over the Tor "
"network more accessible to everyone."
msgstr ""
"> Jag utvecklade OnionShare för att göra den här processen för fildelning "
"över Tor-nätverket tillgängligare för alla."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"> I first saw the need for this tool when I learned about how David Miranda, "
"the partner of my colleague Glenn Greenwald, got detained for nine hours at "
"a London airport while he was trying to fly home to Brazil."
msgstr ""
"> Jag insåg först behovet av verktyget när jag fick veta att David Miranda, "
"partner till min kollega Glenn Greenwald, hade frihetsberövats i nio timmar "
"på en flygplats i London när han försökte flyga hem till Brasilien."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"> I knew that he could have securely sent the documents over the internet "
"using a Tor Onion Service, one of the most underappreciated technologies on "
"the internet, and avoided the risk of physically traveling with them."
msgstr ""
"> Jag visste att han kunde ha skickat dokumenten säkert över internet med en "
"Tor-onion-tjänst – en av internets mest underskattade tekniker – och "
"undvikit risken med att resa fysiskt med dem."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"> Working on a journalism assignment for the Guardian, Miranda was carrying "
"a USB stick with sensitive documents."
msgstr ""
"> Miranda arbetade med ett journalistiskt uppdrag för The Guardian och bar "
"ett USB-minne med känsliga dokument."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"> You know what you're saying during a phone call, or what you're writing in "
"an email. But you have hardly any control over the metadata you produce, "
"because it is generated automatically. [...] In sum, metadata can tell your "
"surveillant virtually everything they'd ever want or need to know about you, "
"except what's actually going on inside your head."
msgstr ""
"> Du vet vad du säger under ett telefonsamtal eller skriver i ett e-"
"postmeddelande. Men du har nästan ingen kontroll över de metadata du "
"producerar, eftersom de skapas automatiskt. [...] Sammanfattningsvis kan "
"metadata berätta nästan allt som en övervakare någonsin kan vilja eller "
"behöva veta om dig, förutom vad som faktiskt pågår i ditt huvud."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"> — [OnionShare 2 release announcement](https://blog.torproject.org/new-"
"release-onionshare-2)"
msgstr ""
"> — [Versionsmeddelande för OnionShare 2](https://blog.torproject.org/new-"
"release-onionshare-2)"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "A client that wants to access the Onion Service does the same."
msgstr "En klient som vill komma åt onion-tjänsten gör samma sak."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"A great example of this use case is the chat program [Ricochet Refresh]"
"(https://ricochetrefresh.net/)."
msgstr ""
"Ett utmärkt exempel på användningsområdet är chattprogrammet [Ricochet "
"Refresh](https://ricochetrefresh.net/)."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"A potential adopter has probably already heard about the Tor Project, the "
"network and even Tor relays, and that's great!"
msgstr ""
"En potentiell användare har sannolikt redan hört talas om The Tor Project, "
"nätverket och kanske även Tor-reläer, vilket är utmärkt."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"All the recipients of this communication need to have Tor Browser installed "
"on their computer to open the onion address."
msgstr ""
"Alla mottagare av kommunikationen måste ha Tor Browser installerat på datorn "
"för att kunna öppna onion-adressen."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "An Onion Service on the Tor network behaves like any other Tor clients."
msgstr ""
"En onion-tjänst i Tor-nätverket fungerar som vilken annan Tor-klient som "
"helst."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"And because of that, there isn't a central server that can be compromised by "
"an attacker."
msgstr "Därför finns ingen central server som en angripare kan kompromettera."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"As Edward Snowden points out in his book, **\"Permanent Record\"** (2019),"
msgstr "Som Edward Snowden påpekar i sin bok **”Permanent Record”** (2019),"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"As a result of this design, Onion Services and its users are immune to "
"attacks related to [bad exit relays](https://blog.torproject.org/bad-exit-"
"relays-may-june-2020)."
msgstr ""
"Tack vare utformningen är onion-tjänster och deras användare immuna mot "
"angrepp som rör [skadliga utgångsreläer](https://blog.torproject.org/bad-"
"exit-relays-may-june-2020)."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"As explained in [Overview](../overview/), there's no central authority that "
"approves or rejects Onion Services."
msgstr ""
"Som förklaras i [översikten](../overview/) finns ingen central myndighet som "
"godkänner eller avvisar onion-tjänster."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"As they're a small fraction of the network, in general, exit relays are "
"overloaded and represent a bottleneck for Tor users' browsing experience."
msgstr ""
"Utgångsreläerna utgör endast en liten del av nätverket. De är därför ofta "
"överbelastade och blir en flaskhals för Tor-användarnas surfupplevelse."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Beyond myths and misperceptions, advocating for Onion Services and privacy "
"enhancing technologies sometimes is challenging."
msgstr ""
"Utöver myter och missuppfattningar kan det ibland vara svårt att förespråka "
"onion-tjänster och integritetsfrämjande teknik."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Beyond websites and onion sites, it's possible to do many things with Onion "
"Services, for example, email."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster kan användas till mycket mer än webbplatser och onion-"
"webbplatser, till exempel e-post."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Censorship technologies are being deployed by different actors, like "
"governments and Internet providers, worldwide to block access to free press "
"and privacy tools."
msgstr ""
"Regeringar, internetleverantörer och andra aktörer världen över använder "
"censurteknik för att blockera åtkomsten till fri press och "
"integritetsverktyg."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Decentralization"
msgstr "Decentralisering"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"E-mail providers like [Riseup](https://riseup.net/en/security/network-"
"security/tor#riseups-tor-onion-services), [Systemli](https://"
"www.systemli.org/service/onion.html) and [many others](https://github.com/"
"ehloonion/onionmx/blob/master/sources/map.yml) protect their users privacy "
"using onionmx."
msgstr ""
"E-postleverantörer som [Riseup](https://riseup.net/en/security/network-"
"security/tor#riseups-tor-onion-services), [Systemli](https://"
"www.systemli.org/service/onion.html) och [många andra](https://github.com/"
"ehloonion/onionmx/blob/master/sources/map.yml) skyddar användarnas "
"integritet med onionmx."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Educate users about privacy by design"
msgstr "Utbilda användarna om inbyggt integritetsskydd"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Even though privacy aware users can adopt tools to protect their "
"communications like OpenPGP, there is plenty of metadata on encrypted "
"emails: for example who is communicating with whom, when, how frequently, "
"where, when it was sent and received, what type of computer it was "
"generated, etc."
msgstr ""
"Även om integritetsmedvetna användare kan använda verktyg som OpenPGP för "
"att skydda kommunikationen finns det gott om metadata i krypterad e-post: "
"exempelvis vilka som kommunicerar med varandra, när, hur ofta och var, när "
"meddelandet skickades och togs emot och vilken typ av dator det skapades på."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"For a broader understanding, read [Onion Services overview](../overview/) "
"and watch these talks: [DEF CON 25 - Next Generation Tor Onion Services]"
"(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Di7qAVidy1Y) and [GPN23 - Onion Services: "
"Design, Protocol and Implementation](https://www.youtube.com/watch?"
"v=Iho4QCkovB0)."
msgstr ""
"Läs [översikten över onion-tjänster](../overview/) och se följande föredrag: "
"[DEF CON 25 – Next Generation Tor Onion Services](https://www.youtube.com/"
"watch?v=Di7qAVidy1Y) och [GPN23 – Onion Services: Design, Protocol and "
"Implementation](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Iho4QCkovB0)."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Freedom of Press and Censorship Circumvention"
msgstr "Pressfrihet och kringgående av censur"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Get inspired by our campaign [#MoreOnionsPorFavor](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/more-onions-porfavor) and teach others about the "
"importance of anonymity."
msgstr ""
"Inspireras av kampanjen [#MoreOnionsPorFavor](https://blog.torproject.org/"
"more-onions-porfavor) och lär andra om anonymitetens betydelse."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "How Onion Services Work"
msgstr "Så fungerar onion-tjänster"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "In Ricochet Refresh, each user is an Onion Service."
msgstr "I Ricochet Refresh är varje användare en onion-tjänst."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"In contrast to running a [Tor relay](../../relay), running a Tor Onion "
"Service does not result in your IP address being publicly listed anywhere, "
"nor does your service relay other Tor traffic."
msgstr ""
"Till skillnad från när du driver ett [Tor-relä](../../relay) listas din IP-"
"adress inte offentligt någonstans när du driver en Tor-onion-tjänst, och "
"tjänsten vidarebefordrar inte heller annan Tor-trafik."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"It is a web application running as an Onion Service that whistleblowers and "
"journalists can anonymously exchange information and files."
msgstr ""
"Det är ett webbprogram som körs som en onion-tjänst och där visselblåsare "
"och journalister kan utbyta information och filer anonymt."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"It makes it possible to host files on your own computer and share (send and "
"receive) using Onion Services."
msgstr ""
"Det gör det möjligt att vara värd för filer på din egen dator och dela dem – "
"skicka och ta emot – via onion-tjänster."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Level up your service privacy"
msgstr "Höj tjänstens integritetsskydd"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Making your service available over Onion Services is an opportunity to "
"educate the general public about Tor and how a more secure way to access the "
"internet looks like: easy as browsing a web page."
msgstr ""
"När du gör tjänsten tillgänglig via onion-tjänster får du en möjlighet att "
"lära allmänheten om Tor och visa hur ett säkrare sätt att använda internet "
"kan vara lika enkelt som att öppna en webbsida."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Many journalists and media organizations use tools based on Onion Services "
"to protect their sources."
msgstr ""
"Många journalister och medieorganisationer använder verktyg som bygger på "
"onion-tjänster för att skydda sina källor."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Metadata obfuscation or elimination"
msgstr "Förvrängning eller eliminering av metadata"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Network sustainability"
msgstr "Ett hållbart nätverk"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Now that you know all the benefits of Onion Services, you may want to set up "
"an [onion site](../setup/) and read about the [protocol overview](../"
"overview/)."
msgstr ""
"När du nu känner till alla fördelar med onion-tjänster kanske du vill "
"konfigurera en [onion-webbplats](../setup/) och läsa [protokollöversikten]"
"(../overview/)."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "One onion a day keeps the surveillance away"
msgstr "En onion om dagen håller övervakningen borta"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Onion services are an excellent example of privacy by design technology, "
"where one is secure and anonymous by default."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster är ett utmärkt exempel på teknik med inbyggt "
"integritetsskydd, där användaren är säker och anonym som standard."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Onion services aren't like a Tor relay in the network."
msgstr "Onion-tjänster fungerar inte som Tor-reläer i nätverket."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Onion services don't use the same circuit path as regular Tor connections."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster använder inte samma kretsväg som vanliga Tor-anslutningar."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"OnionShare was developed after a human rights violation during the Snowden "
"revelations in 2013,"
msgstr ""
"OnionShare utvecklades efter en människorättskränkning i samband med "
"Snowdens avslöjanden 2013,"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Operators don't use the regular DNS infrastructure and do not need to "
"purchase or register a domain name."
msgstr ""
"Operatörerna använder inte den vanliga DNS-infrastrukturen och behöver inte "
"köpa eller registrera ett domännamn."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Originally developed by Aaron Swartz, [SecureDrop](https://securedrop.org/) "
"is an open source whistleblower submission system maintained by [Freedom of "
"the Press Foundation](https://freedom.press) and deployed by many news "
"organizations around the world."
msgstr ""
"[SecureDrop](https://securedrop.org/) utvecklades ursprungligen av Aaron "
"Swartz och är ett system med öppen källkod där visselblåsare kan lämna "
"material. Det underhålls av [Freedom of the Press Foundation](https://"
"freedom.press) och används av många nyhetsorganisationer världen över."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Other providers like [Proton](https://proton.me/news/protonmail-tor-"
"censorship) allow users to read and send their e-mail securely and "
"anonymously over their webclient that serves an onion site."
msgstr ""
"Andra leverantörer, till exempel [Proton](https://proton.me/news/protonmail-"
"tor-censorship), låter användare läsa och skicka e-post säkert och anonymt "
"via en webbklient som tillhandahåller en onion-webbplats."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Protect sources, whistleblowers, and journalists"
msgstr "Skydda källor, visselblåsare och journalister"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Read the news organizations announcement about their onion site:"
msgstr "Läs nyhetsorganisationernas meddelanden om sina onion-webbplatser:"

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Regular Tor connections already provide censorship circumvention, but only "
"Onion Services can anonymize both parts of communication - users and "
"provider -, creating a metadata free communication between the user of the "
"service and the service itself."
msgstr ""
"Vanliga Tor-anslutningar kringgår redan censur, men endast onion-tjänster "
"kan anonymisera båda parterna i kommunikationen – användaren och "
"leverantören – och skapa en kommunikation utan metadata mellan tjänstens "
"användare och själva tjänsten."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Ricochet uses Onion Services to build secure communication with these "
"features: metadata resistant, anonymous, and decentralized."
msgstr ""
"Ricochet använder onion-tjänster för att skapa säker kommunikation som är "
"motståndskraftig mot metadataanalys, anonym och decentraliserad."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Started in 2011 by a group of Italians, the project is now developed by the "
"[Hermes Center for Transparency and Digital Human Rights](https://"
"www.hermescenter.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Projektet startades 2011 av en grupp italienare och utvecklas nu av [Hermes "
"Center for Transparency and Digital Human Rights](https://"
"www.hermescenter.org/)."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "That's the case of Deutsche Welle, BBC, The Markup and other newsrooms."
msgstr ""
"Det gäller bland andra Deutsche Welle, BBC, The Markup och andra redaktioner."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"The Onion Service to become available on the network connects to rendezvous "
"nodes."
msgstr ""
"För att bli tillgänglig i nätverket ansluter onion-tjänsten till mötesnoder."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"The Onion Services use the Tor network to eliminate information about where "
"they are situated."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster använder Tor-nätverket för att undanröja information om var "
"de finns."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "The address of an Onion Service is automatically generated."
msgstr "Adressen till en onion-tjänst skapas automatiskt."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"The traffic generated by Onion Services doesn't leave the Tor network, and "
"therefore, these onion circuits free up exit relay bandwidth for others."
msgstr ""
"Trafiken från onion-tjänster lämnar inte Tor-nätverket. Onion-kretsarna "
"frigör därför bandbredd på utgångsreläerna åt andra."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"There are different use cases, and approaching potential adopters with a "
"specific use case instead of another, can engage them and lead to new onions "
"services being setup."
msgstr ""
"Det finns olika användningsområden. Om du närmar dig potentiella användare "
"med ett särskilt användningsområde kan det väcka deras intresse och leda "
"till att nya onion-tjänster konfigureras."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"These talking points will help to explain how Onion Services offer multiple "
"privacy and security benefits in different contexts."
msgstr ""
"Dessa samtalspunkter hjälper dig att förklara hur onion-tjänster ger flera "
"fördelar för integritet och säkerhet i olika sammanhang."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"They share and accept documents from anonymous sources using tools like "
"SecureDrop, GlobaLeaks or OnionShare."
msgstr ""
"De delar och tar emot dokument från anonyma källor med verktyg som "
"SecureDrop, GlobaLeaks och OnionShare."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"This is important because exit relays are a limited resource, making up 20% "
"of the [7000 relays](https://metrics.torproject.org/networksize.html)."
msgstr ""
"Det är viktigt eftersom utgångsreläer är en begränsad resurs och endast "
"utgör 20 procent av de [7 000 reläerna](https://metrics.torproject.org/"
"networksize.html)."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"This means that connections from the client to the server never leave the "
"Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Det innebär att anslutningarna från klienten till servern aldrig lämnar Tor-"
"nätverket."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Thus, a journalist won't know who the author is and can't put the source at "
"risk."
msgstr ""
"Journalisten får därför inte veta vem upphovspersonen är och kan inte "
"utsätta källan för fara."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"To protect freedom of speech and freedom of opinion in censored spaces, "
"major media organizations have made their websites available over Onion "
"Services in the last few years."
msgstr ""
"För att skydda yttrande- och åsiktsfriheten i censurerade miljöer har stora "
"medieorganisationer under de senaste åren gjort sina webbplatser "
"tillgängliga via onion-tjänster."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"Using them eliminates all metadata that may be associated with the service "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Genom att använda dem undanröjs alla metadata som annars kan kopplas till "
"tjänsten."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"When a service is available over Onion Services, it adds diversity to the "
"Tor network since it uses a different set of circuits on the network, "
"avoiding exit relays completely."
msgstr ""
"När en tjänst finns tillgänglig via onion-tjänster ökar den mångfalden i Tor-"
"nätverket, eftersom den använder en annan uppsättning kretsar och helt "
"undviker utgångsreläer."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"When you use the Tor network to browse the web you are not sending any "
"information by default of who you are or where you are connecting from."
msgstr ""
"När du surfar på webben via Tor-nätverket skickar du som standard ingen "
"information om vem du är eller varifrån du ansluter."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"With SecureDrop, sources can only submit documents in a secure and anonymous "
"way, using Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"Med SecureDrop kan källor skicka dokument säkert och anonymt via Tor Browser."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"[GlobaLeaks](https://globaleaks.org) is an open source whistleblowing "
"framework focused on portability and accessibility."
msgstr ""
"[GlobaLeaks](https://globaleaks.org) är ett ramverk med öppen källkod för "
"visselblåsning, med fokus på portabilitet och tillgänglighet."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"[OnionShare](https://onionshare.org) is another tool based on Onion Services "
"used to provide strong anonymity to transmit sensitive files between "
"journalists safely."
msgstr ""
"[OnionShare](https://onionshare.org) är ett annat verktyg som bygger på "
"onion-tjänster och ger stark anonymitet vid säker överföring av känsliga "
"filer mellan journalister."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"[Onionmx](https://github.com/ehloonion/onionmx) is a software that allows "
"the delivery of emails entirely over Onion Services, obfuscating the "
"metadata of who is talking with whom."
msgstr ""
"[Onionmx](https://github.com/ehloonion/onionmx) är programvara som gör det "
"möjligt att leverera e-post helt via onion-tjänster och därmed dölja "
"metadata om vilka som kommunicerar med varandra."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid ""
"[Tor relays](../../relay/types-of-relays/) are part of a [public "
"infrastructure](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html#toprelays), where Tor "
"users encrypted traffic is routed around to reach out the open internet."
msgstr ""
"[Tor-reläer](../../relay/types-of-relays/) ingår i en [offentlig "
"infrastruktur](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html#toprelays) där Tor-"
"användarnas krypterade trafik dirigeras för att nå det öppna internet."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Become an onion advocate and explain the importance of Onion Services."
msgstr "Bli förespråkare för onion-tjänster och förklara varför de är viktiga."

#: content/onion-services/talk/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/onion-services/talk/
msgid "Talk about onions"
msgstr "Prata om onion-tjänster"

#: content/outreach/contents.lr:page.body content/outreach/contents.lr:page.cta
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/
msgid "Tell the world about Tor"
msgstr "Berätta för världen om Tor"

#: content/outreach/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/
msgid ""
"We love it when people bring information about Tor to their community "
"events, conferences, and meetups."
msgstr ""
"Vi uppskattar när människor tar med information om Tor till lokala "
"evenemang, konferenser och träffar."

#: content/outreach/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/
msgid ""
"We've curated some beautiful materials for sharing in-person and on social "
"media we welcome you to use."
msgstr ""
"Vi har sammanställt vackert material som du gärna får använda både vid "
"fysiska möten och i sociala medier."

#: content/outreach/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/
msgid "Bring Tor materials to your next community event."
msgstr "Ta med Tor-material till nästa lokala evenemang."

#: content/outreach/contents.lr:page.title
#: content/outreach/kit/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/outreach/stories/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/outreach/talk/contents.lr:page.section
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/kit/
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/talk/
msgid "Outreach"
msgstr "Sträckande hand"

#: content/outreach/kit/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/kit/
msgid ""
"All material on this session may be freely distributed at will under the "
"[Creative Commons 4.0 Attribution International License](https://"
"creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), unless otherwise noted."
msgstr ""
"Allt material i den här sessionen får spridas fritt enligt [Creative Commons "
"Erkännande 4.0 Internationell](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/"
"4.0/), om inget annat anges."

#: content/outreach/kit/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/kit/
msgid "Street Team Kit"
msgstr "Materialpaket för gatuteam"

#: content/outreach/kit/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/outreach/kit/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/kit/
msgid ""
"This kit includes printable flyers, stickers, and other materials to get "
"people excited about using Tor."
msgstr ""
"Paketet innehåller utskrivbara flygblad, klistermärken och annat material "
"som kan väcka intresse för Tor."

#: content/outreach/kit/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/kit/
msgid "Street team kit"
msgstr "Materialpaket för gatuteam"

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"A public library, a social center, a hackerspace or a room in a university "
"are some spaces that you can usually host your event."
msgstr ""
"Ett offentligt bibliotek, ett socialt centrum, en hackerspace eller ett rum "
"på ett universitet är exempel på platser där du ofta kan ordna evenemanget."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"After confirming a local and date, create a poster and an online invitation "
"to spread the event."
msgstr ""
"När plats och datum har bekräftats skapar du en affisch och en inbjudan på "
"nätet för att sprida information om evenemanget."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"After the meetup, clean up the space, remove the posters and send your notes "
"to the [Tor Relays](https://lists.torproject.org/mailman3/postorius/lists/"
"tor-relays.lists.torproject.org/) mailing list or post on the [Tor Forum]"
"(https://forum.torproject.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Efter träffen städar du lokalen, tar ned affischerna och skickar "
"anteckningarna till e-postlistan [Tor Relays](https://lists.torproject.org/"
"mailman3/postorius/lists/tor-relays.lists.torproject.org/) eller publicerar "
"dem på [Tor Forum](https://forum.torproject.org/)."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"Before the meetup, organize the space. Buy some chips and snacks, hang some "
"[posters](../kit/) nearby the local, so people can find easily."
msgstr ""
"Förbered lokalen före träffen. Köp chips och tilltugg och sätt upp några "
"[affischer](../kit/) i närheten så att deltagarna lätt hittar dit."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"Choose a date and time that is convenient for your group and the local space."
msgstr "Välj ett datum och en tid som passar gruppen och lokalen."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"Connect with a local space that will allow you to meet for an hour or two."
msgstr "Hitta en lokal plats där ni får träffas i en eller två timmar."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"During the activity take notes about questions, how many knew about Tor "
"before, how many are relay operators, etc."
msgstr ""
"Anteckna under aktiviteten vilka frågor som ställs, hur många som kände till "
"Tor sedan tidigare, hur många som driver reläer och så vidare."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"Find a meetup facilitator and draft an agenda, for example, question & "
"answer about Tor, how to setup relays."
msgstr ""
"Hitta en mötesledare och skriv en dagordning, till exempel frågor och svar "
"om Tor och hur reläer konfigureras."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid "If you have some printed materials and/or Tor swag, put it on a table."
msgstr "Lägg eventuellt tryckt material och Tor-profilprodukter på ett bord."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid "Load your presentation and wait a few minutes to people arrive."
msgstr ""
"Läs in presentationen och vänta några minuter på att deltagarna ska anlända."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"On weekends or during week days, after working hours (7 pm) might be better."
msgstr ""
"Helger eller vardagskvällar efter arbetstid, exempelvis klockan 19, kan "
"fungera bäst."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid ""
"Organized by the community, meetups are a great way to find and strengthen "
"the privacy supporters community in your local area."
msgstr ""
"Träffar som organiseras av gemenskapen är ett utmärkt sätt att hitta och "
"stärka gemenskapen av integritetsförespråkare i ditt område."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid "Read and follow our [best practices](../../training/best-practices/)."
msgstr "Läs och följ vår [bästa praxis](../../training/best-practices/)."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Step 1"
msgstr "Steg 1"

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Step 2"
msgstr "Steg 2"

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Step 3"
msgstr "Steg 3"

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid "Step 4"
msgstr "Steg 4"

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid "Step 5"
msgstr "Steg 5"

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid "Step 6"
msgstr "Steg 6"

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid "Learn how to organize a Tor meetup with your friends."
msgstr "Lär dig ordna en Tor-träff med dina vänner."

#: content/outreach/meetup/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/meetup/
msgid "Organize a Tor meetup"
msgstr "Ordna en Tor-träff"

#: content/outreach/stories/aiden/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/aiden/
msgid ""
"The internet would be only limited to watching the propaganda they serve me "
"everyday even on streets..."
msgstr ""
"Internet skulle begränsas till den propaganda som de visar mig varje dag, "
"till och med på gatorna …"

#: content/outreach/stories/aiden/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/aiden/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/aiden/
msgid ""
"Tor helped me learn new things. I'm in a country where you can get locked up "
"for having different opinions than my government."
msgstr ""
"Tor hjälpte mig att lära mig nya saker. Jag bor i ett land där man kan "
"fängslas för att ha andra åsikter än regeringen."

