#: content/outreach/stories/aiden/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/aiden/
msgid "Aiden"
msgstr "Aiden"

#: content/outreach/stories/akio/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/akio/
msgid "I use Tor to participate in grassroots anti-nuclear weapons activism."
msgstr "Jag använder Tor för att delta i gräsrotsaktivism mot kärnvapen."

#: content/outreach/stories/akio/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/akio/
msgid "This is quite dangerous so Tor is absolutely essential."
msgstr "Det är ganska farligt, så Tor är helt nödvändigt."

#: content/outreach/stories/akio/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/akio/
msgid ""
"I use Tor to participate in grassroots anti-nuclear weapons activism. This "
"is quite dangerous so Tor is absolutely essential."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor för att delta i gräsrotsaktivism mot kärnvapen. Det är "
"ganska farligt, så Tor är helt nödvändigt."

#: content/outreach/stories/akio/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/akio/
msgid "Akio"
msgstr "Akio"

#: content/outreach/stories/alexis/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alexis/
msgid ""
"During the past 4-5 years, I have used the Tor Browser to connect to "
"\"thousands\" of sites."
msgstr ""
"Under de senaste fyra–fem åren har jag använt Tor Browser för att ansluta "
"till ”tusentals” webbplatser."

#: content/outreach/stories/alexis/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alexis/
msgid "I cannot express in just a few words how much I love Tor."
msgstr ""
"Det går inte att med några få ord uttrycka hur mycket jag uppskattar Tor."

#: content/outreach/stories/alexis/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alexis/
msgid "I face minimum risk, except for corporate business tracking."
msgstr "Jag utsätts för mycket liten risk, bortsett från företagens spårning."

#: content/outreach/stories/alexis/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alexis/
msgid ""
"I use Tor Browser as my everyday browser, nearly 100% of the time. I am in "
"the USA."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor Browser som min vanliga webbläsare nästan hela tiden. Jag "
"bor i USA."

#: content/outreach/stories/alexis/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alexis/
msgid ""
"Tor has helped me to preserve my anonymity and protect my privacy, which are "
"of great importance to me online."
msgstr ""
"Tor har hjälpt mig att bevara min anonymitet och skydda min integritet, "
"vilket är mycket viktigt för mig på nätet."

#: content/outreach/stories/alexis/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alexis/
msgid ""
"Without Tor, I would feel like I had a hole in me, an empty feeling, "
"uncomfortable, not good."
msgstr ""
"Utan Tor skulle det kännas som om något saknades inom mig – en tom, "
"obehaglig och dålig känsla."

#: content/outreach/stories/alexis/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alexis/
msgid ""
"I use Tor Browser as my everyday browser, nearly 100% of the time. I am in "
"USA. I face minimum risk, except for corporate business tracking. During the "
"past 4-5 years, I have used the Tor Browser to connect to \"thousands\" of "
"sites."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor Browser som min vanliga webbläsare nästan hela tiden. Jag "
"bor i USA. Jag utsätts för mycket liten risk, bortsett från företagens "
"spårning. Under de senaste fyra–fem åren har jag använt Tor Browser för att "
"ansluta till ”tusentals” webbplatser."

#: content/outreach/stories/alexis/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alexis/
msgid "Alexis"
msgstr "Alexis"

#: content/outreach/stories/alva/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/alva/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alva/
msgid "I am a trans-lesbian and I would rather decide who to tell this to."
msgstr ""
"Jag är transperson och lesbisk och vill själv bestämma vem jag berättar det "
"för."

#: content/outreach/stories/alva/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alva/
msgid ""
"I am able to be more confident talking about this with people I meet online."
msgstr "Jag kan prata tryggare om det med människor som jag träffar på nätet."

#: content/outreach/stories/alva/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alva/
msgid "Keeping my social and sexual lives separate."
msgstr "Jag håller mitt sociala liv och sexliv åtskilda."

#: content/outreach/stories/alva/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alva/
msgid "Mitigating risk of unnecessary exposure and judgement."
msgstr "Det minskar risken för onödig exponering och att bli dömd."

#: content/outreach/stories/alva/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alva/
msgid "This has helped with my confidence offline too."
msgstr "Det har också stärkt mitt självförtroende utanför nätet."

#: content/outreach/stories/alva/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/alva/
msgid "Alva"
msgstr "Alva"

#: content/outreach/stories/amani/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/amani/
msgid ""
"I don't believe online security, privacy or anonymity are only for "
"criminals, but are an inherent right in a democratic republic."
msgstr ""
"Jag anser inte att säkerhet, integritet eller anonymitet på nätet endast är "
"till för brottslingar, utan att de är grundläggande rättigheter i en "
"demokratisk republik."

#: content/outreach/stories/amani/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/amani/
msgid ""
"I have never done anything remotely illegal online, I fervently believe that "
"my personal data, my browsing habits etc. are my business, and I refuse to "
"have someone looking over my shoulder if I can prevent it at all."
msgstr ""
"Jag har aldrig gjort något ens avlägset olagligt på nätet. Jag anser starkt "
"att mina personuppgifter och surfvanor är min ensak och vägrar låta någon "
"titta över axeln på mig om jag över huvud taget kan förhindra det."

#: content/outreach/stories/amani/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/amani/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/amani/
msgid ""
"I think online security and privacy are CRITICAL to maintain a free society."
msgstr ""
"Jag anser att säkerhet och integritet på nätet är AVGÖRANDE för att bevara "
"ett fritt samhälle."

#: content/outreach/stories/amani/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/amani/
msgid ""
"Security and privacy are not just a right, but an obligation for all freedom-"
"loving people."
msgstr ""
"Säkerhet och integritet är inte bara rättigheter utan också skyldigheter för "
"alla som älskar frihet."

#: content/outreach/stories/amani/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/amani/
msgid "Amani"
msgstr "Amani"

#: content/outreach/stories/barbara/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/barbara/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/barbara/
msgid ""
"I desperately needed a means to secure my online privacy because I am a "
"cyberstalking victim whose online identity has been both stolen and "
"compromised."
msgstr ""
"Jag behövde desperat ett sätt att skydda min integritet på nätet eftersom "
"jag utsatts för nätstalkning och min identitet på nätet både har stulits och "
"komprometterats."

#: content/outreach/stories/barbara/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/barbara/
msgid "I started using Tor to protect my privacy and protect me from abuse."
msgstr ""
"Jag började använda Tor för att skydda min integritet och skydda mig mot "
"övergrepp."

#: content/outreach/stories/barbara/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/barbara/
msgid "Barbara"
msgstr "Barbara"

#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/biljana/
msgid ""
"An internet without Tor is an internet I wouldn't want to use for many "
"things."
msgstr ""
"Ett internet utan Tor är ett internet som jag inte skulle vilja använda till "
"särskilt mycket."

#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/biljana/
msgid ""
"Currently governments of nearly all states have passed or are planning on "
"new police laws."
msgstr ""
"Regeringarna i nästan alla stater har nyligen antagit eller planerar nya "
"polislager."

#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/biljana/
msgid "I am a left-wing political activist..."
msgstr "Jag är vänsterpolitisk aktivist …"

#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/biljana/
msgid ""
"I use Tor in my daily political work to stay a bit under the radar of secret "
"agencies and police."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor i mitt dagliga politiska arbete för att hålla mig något "
"under underrättelsetjänsternas och polisens radar."

#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/biljana/
msgid ""
"It helps me stay anonymous on the internet and do research without being "
"followed."
msgstr ""
"Det hjälper mig att förbli anonym på internet och bedriva forskning utan att "
"följas."

#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/biljana/
msgid ""
"Not only that I don't want to share all my personal data with random strange "
"companies, I also don't want to face repression for legitimate human rights "
"political work."
msgstr ""
"Jag vill inte bara undvika att dela alla mina personuppgifter med "
"slumpmässiga okända företag, utan också slippa förtryck på grund av legitimt "
"politiskt människorättsarbete."

#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/biljana/
msgid ""
"These laws are against basic human rights and open possibilities of mass-"
"surveillance."
msgstr ""
"Lagarna strider mot grundläggande mänskliga rättigheter och öppnar för "
"massövervakning."

#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/biljana/
msgid ""
"Thus, technologies like Tor are essential not only for the people trying to "
"stop these law aggravations but for all of us."
msgstr ""
"Teknik som Tor är därför nödvändig, inte bara för dem som försöker stoppa "
"dessa lagförsämringar utan för oss alla."

#: content/outreach/stories/biljana/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/biljana/
msgid "Biljana"
msgstr "Biljana"

#: content/outreach/stories/branka/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/branka/
msgid ""
"I have patients who work on legislation that can mean billions of dollars to "
"major telecom, social media, and search concerns."
msgstr ""
"Jag har patienter som arbetar med lagstiftning som kan vara värd miljarder "
"dollar för stora telekomföretag, sociala medier och sökföretag."

#: content/outreach/stories/branka/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/branka/
msgid ""
"I use Tor to do much of my research when I think there is a risk of "
"correlating it to patient visits."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor för mycket av min forskning när jag anser att det finns "
"risk för att sökningarna kopplas till patientbesök."

#: content/outreach/stories/branka/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/branka/
msgid "I'm a doctor in a very political town."
msgstr "Jag är läkare i en mycket politisk stad."

#: content/outreach/stories/branka/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/branka/
msgid ""
"When I have to do research on diseases and treatment or look into aspects of "
"my patients' histories, I am well aware that my search histories might be "
"correlated to patient visits and leak information about their health, "
"families, and personal lives."
msgstr ""
"När jag behöver undersöka sjukdomar och behandlingar eller granska delar av "
"mina patienters bakgrund är jag väl medveten om att min sökhistorik kan "
"kopplas till patientbesök och läcka information om deras hälsa, familjer och "
"privatliv."

#: content/outreach/stories/branka/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/branka/
msgid ""
"I'm a doctor in a very political town. I have patients who work on "
"legislation that can mean billions of dollars to major telecom, social "
"media, and search concerns."
msgstr ""
"Jag är läkare i en mycket politisk stad. Jag har patienter som arbetar med "
"lagstiftning som kan vara värd miljarder dollar för stora telekomföretag, "
"sociala medier och sökföretag."

#: content/outreach/stories/branka/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/branka/
msgid "Branka"
msgstr "Branka"

#: content/outreach/stories/braylen/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/braylen/
msgid ""
"I don't want that anyone knows about these diseases who I don't want to tell "
"about this."
msgstr ""
"Jag vill inte att någon som jag inte själv har berättat det för ska känna "
"till sjukdomarna."

#: content/outreach/stories/braylen/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/braylen/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/braylen/
msgid ""
"I use the Tor Browser to research about mental diseases, e.g. depression, "
"that occur in our family."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor Browser för att söka information om psykiska sjukdomar, "
"till exempel depression, som förekommer i vår familj."

#: content/outreach/stories/braylen/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/braylen/
msgid ""
"That's why I use Tor for researching about anything related to these "
"diseases."
msgstr "Därför använder jag Tor för all forskning som rör dessa sjukdomar."

#: content/outreach/stories/braylen/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/braylen/
msgid "Braylen"
msgstr "Braylen"

#: content/outreach/stories/carmen/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/carmen/
msgid ""
"Being able to protect my patients' personal information was of paramount "
"importance."
msgstr ""
"Det var av största vikt att kunna skydda mina patienters personuppgifter."

#: content/outreach/stories/carmen/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/carmen/
msgid ""
"I was a family physician and clinical psychiatrist for 25 years, often "
"working with members of marginalized and persecuted groups."
msgstr ""
"Jag arbetade som allmänläkare och klinisk psykiater i 25 år, ofta med "
"personer från marginaliserade och förföljda grupper."

#: content/outreach/stories/carmen/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/carmen/
msgid ""
"I was a family physician and clinical psychiatrist for 25 years, often "
"working with members of marginalized and persecuted groups. Being able to "
"protect my patients' personal information was of paramount importance."
msgstr ""
"Jag arbetade som allmänläkare och klinisk psykiater i 25 år, ofta med "
"personer från marginaliserade och förföljda grupper. Det var av största vikt "
"att kunna skydda mina patienters personuppgifter."

#: content/outreach/stories/carmen/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/carmen/
msgid "Carmen"
msgstr "Carmen"

#: content/outreach/stories/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/
msgid ""
"This is a collection of anonymous user stories from people who rely on Tor "
"to protect their privacy and anonymity."
msgstr ""
"Det här är en samling anonyma användarberättelser från människor som "
"förlitar sig på Tor för att skydda sin integritet och anonymitet."

#: content/outreach/stories/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/
msgid ""
"We encourage you to share their experiences with your network, friends and "
"family, or as part of your work to promote the use of privacy-preserving "
"technologies like ours and help us defend strong online protections."
msgstr ""
"Vi uppmuntrar dig att dela deras erfarenheter med ditt nätverk, dina vänner "
"och din familj eller som en del av ditt arbete med att främja "
"integritetsskyddande teknik som vår och hjälpa oss att försvara ett starkt "
"skydd på nätet."

#: content/outreach/stories/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/
msgid ""
"There are many reasons why people rely on Tor's privacy protections. Learn "
"more about the real-life experiences of our diverse user base and help us "
"spread the word."
msgstr ""
"Det finns många skäl till att människor förlitar sig på Tors "
"integritetsskydd. Läs om verkliga erfarenheter från vår mångsidiga "
"användargrupp och hjälp oss att sprida budskapet."

#: content/outreach/stories/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/
msgid "User stories"
msgstr "Användarberättelser"

#: content/outreach/stories/dakota/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/dakota/
msgid ""
"I use Tor and other encrypted services and believe that all digital services "
"and applications should be encrypted."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor och andra krypterade tjänster och anser att alla digitala "
"tjänster och program bör vara krypterade."

#: content/outreach/stories/dakota/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/dakota/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/dakota/
msgid ""
"In a world in which the Patriot Act has removed basic protections guaranteed "
"by the Fourth Amendment, US citizens have lost way too much in privacy "
"rights to risk any transaction on an insecure platform."
msgstr ""
"I en värld där Patriot Act har undanröjt grundläggande skydd som garanteras "
"av USA:s fjärde författningstillägg har amerikanska medborgare förlorat "
"alldeles för mycket av sin rätt till integritet för att våga genomföra någon "
"transaktion på en osäker plattform."

#: content/outreach/stories/dakota/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/dakota/
msgid ""
"The lack of an enforceable privacy standard in the U. S. make caution "
"necessary when dealing with any digital communication."
msgstr ""
"Avsaknaden av en rättsligt verkställbar integritetsstandard i USA gör det "
"nödvändigt att vara försiktig vid all digital kommunikation."

#: content/outreach/stories/dakota/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/dakota/
msgid "Dakota"
msgstr "Dakota"

#: content/outreach/stories/diego/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/diego/
msgid "I'm from Brazil, and I've been using it for over 3 years."
msgstr "Jag kommer från Brasilien och har använt Tor i över tre år."

#: content/outreach/stories/diego/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/diego/
msgid ""
"Tor Browser has helped me a lot in protecting me from fingerprinting on the "
"web."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser har hjälpt mig mycket att skydda mig mot fingeravtrycksspårning "
"på webben."

#: content/outreach/stories/diego/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/diego/
msgid ""
"I'm from Brazil, and I've been using it for over 3 years. Tor has helped me "
"a lot in protecting me from fingerprinting on the web."
msgstr ""
"Jag kommer från Brasilien och har använt Tor i över tre år. Tor har hjälpt "
"mig mycket att skydda mig mot fingeravtrycksspårning på webben."

#: content/outreach/stories/diego/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/diego/
msgid "Diego"
msgstr "Diego"

#: content/outreach/stories/ethan/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ethan/
msgid "(Although they don't have the same attitude to privacy as I do)."
msgstr "(Även om de inte har samma inställning till integritet som jag.)"

#: content/outreach/stories/ethan/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ethan/
msgid ""
"As teenagers, they, or their friends, are bumping into issues regarding sex, "
"drugs, social media, and bullying."
msgstr ""
"Som tonåringar stöter de eller deras vänner på frågor som rör sex, droger, "
"sociala medier och mobbning."

#: content/outreach/stories/ethan/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ethan/
msgid ""
"I also encourage my children to use Tor for their research for the same "
"reasons."
msgstr ""
"Jag uppmuntrar också mina barn att använda Tor för sin informationssökning "
"av samma skäl."

#: content/outreach/stories/ethan/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ethan/
msgid "I am a father of two teenagers."
msgstr "Jag är far till två tonåringar."

#: content/outreach/stories/ethan/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ethan/
msgid ""
"I use Tor to do the research to basically avoid telling Google (and others) "
"that my children have these issues."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor för informationssökningen, i huvudsak för att undvika att "
"berätta för Google och andra att mina barn har sådana problem."

#: content/outreach/stories/ethan/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ethan/
msgid ""
"It would be unethical of any parent NOT to do so and expose their children’s "
"issues to these corporations."
msgstr ""
"Det vore oetiskt av en förälder att INTE göra det och därmed avslöja barnens "
"problem för dessa företag."

#: content/outreach/stories/ethan/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ethan/
msgid ""
"They are pretty open about many of these issues and so I try to be up to "
"date with research, information, and details if anything arises."
msgstr ""
"De är ganska öppna om många av frågorna, så jag försöker hålla mig "
"uppdaterad med forskning, information och detaljer om något uppstår."

#: content/outreach/stories/ethan/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ethan/
msgid ""
"I am a father of two teenagers. As teenagers, they, or their friends, are "
"bumping into issues regarding sex, drugs, social media, and bullying."
msgstr ""
"Jag är far till två tonåringar. Som tonåringar stöter de eller deras vänner "
"på frågor som rör sex, droger, sociala medier och mobbning."

#: content/outreach/stories/ethan/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ethan/
msgid "Ethan"
msgstr "Ethan"

#: content/outreach/stories/fumie/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/fumie/
msgid ""
"I used Tor to obtain documents from Wikileaks, which helped expose local "
"surveillance by military units of janitorial union organizing meetings, "
"groups pressing for the rights of migrant workers etc."
msgstr ""
"Jag använde Tor för att hämta dokument från WikiLeaks. De bidrog till att "
"avslöja hur lokala militära enheter övervakade möten om organisering av "
"lokalvårdarnas fackförbund, grupper som arbetade för migrantarbetares "
"rättigheter och liknande."

#: content/outreach/stories/fumie/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/fumie/
msgid "I used Tor to obtain documents from Wikileaks."
msgstr "Jag använde Tor för att hämta dokument från WikiLeaks."

#: content/outreach/stories/fumie/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/fumie/
msgid "Fumie"
msgstr "Fumie"

#: content/outreach/stories/gabriella/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/gabriella/
msgid ""
"I've been using Tor for more than a year, and the Internet certainly "
"wouldn't be as free without Tor."
msgstr ""
"Jag har använt Tor i över ett år, och internet skulle definitivt inte vara "
"lika fritt utan Tor."

#: content/outreach/stories/gabriella/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/gabriella/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/gabriella/
msgid ""
"Tor makes sure I have a generic internet profile, free from any "
"specifications."
msgstr ""
"Tor ser till att jag har en allmän internetprofil utan särskiljande "
"egenskaper."

#: content/outreach/stories/gabriella/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/gabriella/
msgid "Gabriella"
msgstr "Gabriella"

#: content/outreach/stories/galla/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/galla/
msgid "I am a simple user."
msgstr "Jag är en vanlig användare."

#: content/outreach/stories/galla/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/galla/
msgid "I love Tor's system and everything that it stands for."
msgstr "Jag uppskattar Tors system och allt som det står för."

#: content/outreach/stories/galla/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/galla/
msgid ""
"I love privacy-related tools and I am very interested in encryption, "
"decryption and security."
msgstr ""
"Jag tycker mycket om integritetsverktyg och är väldigt intresserad av "
"kryptering, dekryptering och säkerhet."

#: content/outreach/stories/galla/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/galla/
msgid "I use Tor for my privacy as well as to access region-restricted sites."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor för min integritet och för att komma åt webbplatser som är "
"regionbegränsade."

#: content/outreach/stories/galla/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/galla/
msgid ""
"I am a simple user. I love privacy-related tools and I am very interested in "
"encryption, decryption and security."
msgstr ""
"Jag är en vanlig användare. Jag tycker mycket om integritetsverktyg och är "
"väldigt intresserad av kryptering, dekryptering och säkerhet."

#: content/outreach/stories/galla/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/galla/
msgid "Galla"
msgstr "Galla"

#: content/outreach/stories/hasim/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/hasim/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/hasim/
msgid "I decided to take back my privacy and I have been using Tor ever since."
msgstr ""
"Jag bestämde mig för att återta min integritet och har använt Tor sedan dess."

#: content/outreach/stories/hasim/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/hasim/
msgid ""
"I no longer fear the internet and I have the Tor team to thank for that."
msgstr ""
"Jag är inte längre rädd för internet, och det har jag Tor-teamet att tacka "
"för."

#: content/outreach/stories/hasim/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/hasim/
msgid "It has given me peace of mind... It has been empowering."
msgstr "Det har gett mig sinnesro … Det har gjort mig starkare."

#: content/outreach/stories/hasim/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/hasim/
msgid "Hasim"
msgstr "Hasim"

#: content/outreach/stories/isabella/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/isabella/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/isabella/
msgid ""
"The politics [here] is kind of crazy so I kind of fear about any of my data "
"stored by the government."
msgstr ""
"Politiken här är ganska galen, så jag är rädd för att regeringen lagrar mina "
"uppgifter."

#: content/outreach/stories/isabella/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/isabella/
msgid "They can be really easily misused for life-threatening purposes."
msgstr "De kan mycket lätt missbrukas på sätt som hotar människors liv."

#: content/outreach/stories/isabella/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/isabella/
msgid "Isabella"
msgstr "Isabella"

#: content/outreach/stories/israa/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/israa/
msgid ""
"Although my physical well being is not threatened by the mass surveillance I "
"mentally feel much more at ease knowing that my browsing history is "
"protected by using Tor."
msgstr ""
"Även om massövervakningen inte hotar mitt fysiska välbefinnande känner jag "
"mig mentalt mycket lugnare när jag vet att min webbhistorik skyddas genom "
"Tor."

#: content/outreach/stories/israa/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/israa/
msgid ""
"I do not face any direct threats or risks regarding my use of the internet, "
"and solely use Tor to avoid mass surveillance of my browsing history."
msgstr ""
"Jag utsätts inte för några direkta hot eller risker när jag använder "
"internet. Jag använder Tor enbart för att undvika massövervakning av min "
"webbhistorik."

#: content/outreach/stories/israa/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/israa/
msgid "I'm in the UK."
msgstr "Jag bor i Storbritannien."

#: content/outreach/stories/israa/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/israa/
msgid ""
"Otherwise my ISP would have a full 24/7 record of my browsing which by law "
"has to be kept by them for a full 12 months."
msgstr ""
"Annars skulle min internetleverantör ha fullständig information om mitt "
"surfande dygnet runt, och enligt lag måste den sparas i tolv månader."

#: content/outreach/stories/israa/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/israa/
msgid ""
"I'm in the UK. I do not face any direct threats or risks regarding my use of "
"the internet, and solely use Tor to avoid mass surveillance of my browsing "
"history."
msgstr ""
"Jag bor i Storbritannien. Jag utsätts inte för några direkta hot eller "
"risker när jag använder internet. Jag använder Tor enbart för att undvika "
"massövervakning av min webbhistorik."

#: content/outreach/stories/israa/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/israa/
msgid "Israa"
msgstr "Israa"

#: content/outreach/stories/jackson/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/jackson/
msgid "But I use Tor to protect others."
msgstr "Men jag använder Tor för att skydda andra."

#: content/outreach/stories/jackson/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/jackson/
msgid ""
"It is such an important issue for journalists and activists so I want to "
"support strengthening privacy and encryption laws to serve all users."
msgstr ""
"Det är en så viktig fråga för journalister och aktivister att jag vill "
"stödja starkare lagar om integritet och kryptering som skyddar alla "
"användare."

#: content/outreach/stories/jackson/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/jackson/
msgid "Really, I personally don’t need to worry much about my privacy."
msgstr ""
"Personligen behöver jag egentligen inte oroa mig särskilt mycket för min "
"integritet."

#: content/outreach/stories/jackson/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/jackson/
msgid ""
"Really, I personally don’t need to worry much about my privacy. But I use "
"Tor to protect others."
msgstr ""
"Personligen behöver jag egentligen inte oroa mig särskilt mycket för min "
"integritet. Men jag använder Tor för att skydda andra."

#: content/outreach/stories/jackson/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/jackson/
msgid "Jackson"
msgstr "Jackson"

#: content/outreach/stories/kai/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/kai/
msgid ""
"Encryption is the only way to ensure they can securly voice their opinion."
msgstr ""
"Kryptering är det enda sättet att se till att de tryggt kan uttrycka sina "
"åsikter."

#: content/outreach/stories/kai/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/kai/
msgid ""
"Even in some parts of Europe sharing your own opinion or beliefs on "
"politics, religion, abortion, sexual orientation etc. is dangerous and can "
"easily lead to severe consequences."
msgstr ""
"Även i vissa delar av Europa kan det vara farligt att uttrycka egna åsikter "
"eller övertygelser om politik, religion, abort, sexuell läggning och "
"liknande, och det kan lätt få allvarliga följder."

#: content/outreach/stories/kai/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/kai/
msgid ""
"I live in Europe and am not by any means an important, critical or "
"endangered person, but I have friends in other parts of the world to whom "
"anonymity and privacy through encryption is crucial."
msgstr ""
"Jag bor i Europa och är inte på något sätt en viktig, kritisk eller hotad "
"person, men jag har vänner i andra delar av världen för vilka anonymitet och "
"integritet genom kryptering är avgörande."

#: content/outreach/stories/kai/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/kai/
msgid ""
"I live in Europe and am not by any means an important, critical or "
"endangered person, but I have friends in other parts of the world to whom "
"anonymity and privacy through encryption is crucial. Encryption is the only "
"way to ensure they can securly voice their opinion."
msgstr ""
"Jag bor i Europa och är inte på något sätt en viktig, kritisk eller hotad "
"person, men jag har vänner i andra delar av världen för vilka anonymitet och "
"integritet genom kryptering är avgörande. Kryptering är det enda sättet att "
"se till att de tryggt kan uttrycka sina åsikter."

#: content/outreach/stories/kai/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/kai/
msgid "Kai"
msgstr "Kai"

#: content/outreach/stories/luca/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/luca/
msgid ""
"I strongly believe encryption is essential for a healthy democracy, for the "
"privacy of every human being on this planet and to combat/reduce government "
"abuse of power and mass surveillance."
msgstr ""
"Jag anser starkt att kryptering är avgörande för en sund demokrati, för "
"varje människas integritet och för att motverka eller minska statligt "
"maktmissbruk och massövervakning."

#: content/outreach/stories/luca/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/luca/
msgid ""
"I strongly believe encryption is essential for a healthy democracy, for the "
"privacy of every human being on this planet  and to combat/reduce government "
"abuse of power and mass surveillance."
msgstr ""
"Jag anser starkt att kryptering är avgörande för en sund demokrati, för "
"varje människas integritet och för att motverka eller minska statligt "
"maktmissbruk och massövervakning."

#: content/outreach/stories/luca/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/luca/
msgid "Luca"
msgstr "Luca"

#: content/outreach/stories/milena/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/milena/
msgid "It enables me to access content I couldn't from my country's IP range."
msgstr ""
"Det gör att jag kan komma åt innehåll som inte är tillgängligt från mitt "
"lands IP-intervall."

#: content/outreach/stories/milena/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/milena/
msgid ""
"Onion services are the most reliable tool to keep access to devices behind "
"one-way firewalls."
msgstr ""
"Onion-tjänster är det mest tillförlitliga verktyget för att behålla åtkomst "
"till enheter bakom enkelriktade brandväggar."

#: content/outreach/stories/milena/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/milena/
msgid ""
"Protects me from different identities being correlated via IP address or "
"browser features."
msgstr ""
"Det skyddar mig från att olika identiteter kopplas samman genom IP-adressen "
"eller webbläsarens egenskaper."

#: content/outreach/stories/milena/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/milena/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/milena/
msgid ""
"Tor helps me stay outside of filter bubbles and protects me from being "
"tracked."
msgstr ""
"Tor hjälper mig att hålla mig utanför filterbubblor och skyddar mig mot "
"spårning."

#: content/outreach/stories/milena/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/milena/
msgid "Milena"
msgstr "Milena"

#: content/outreach/stories/morgan/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/morgan/
msgid ""
"I am in the United States. Tor has helped me get around my very strict "
"school ISP when researching sensitive topics such as lgbt resources, as I "
"have not come out as trans yet. My school seemed to block every VPN I "
"attempted to use, so I tried tor, and it worked flawlessly. My life would be "
"a mess without it."
msgstr ""
"Jag bor i USA. Tor har hjälpt mig att kringgå skolans mycket strikta "
"internetleverantör när jag söker information om känsliga ämnen, till exempel "
"hbtq-resurser, eftersom jag ännu inte har berättat att jag är transperson. "
"Skolan verkade blockera alla VPN-tjänster som jag försökte använda, så jag "
"provade Tor och det fungerade utan problem. Utan Tor skulle mitt liv vara "
"kaotiskt."

#: content/outreach/stories/morgan/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/morgan/
msgid ""
"I am in the United States. Tor has helped me get around my very strict "
"school ISP when researching sensitive topics such as lgbt resources."
msgstr ""
"Jag bor i USA. Tor har hjälpt mig att kringgå skolans mycket strikta "
"internetleverantör när jag söker information om känsliga ämnen, till exempel "
"hbtq-resurser."

#: content/outreach/stories/morgan/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/morgan/
msgid "Morgan"
msgstr "Morgan"

#: content/outreach/stories/nia/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/nia/
msgid ""
"All transactions must use encryption: e-mails, messages, hard drives, "
"individual files, require encryption."
msgstr ""
"Alla transaktioner måste använda kryptering: e-post, meddelanden, hårddiskar "
"och enskilda filer behöver krypteras."

#: content/outreach/stories/nia/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/nia/
msgid ""
"Encryption is important because it protects the work of those who hold to "
"account the ones in power."
msgstr ""
"Kryptering är viktig eftersom den skyddar arbetet hos dem som ställer "
"makthavare till svars."

#: content/outreach/stories/nia/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/nia/
msgid "Journalism isn't free and fair."
msgstr "Journalistiken är inte fri och rättvis."

#: content/outreach/stories/nia/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/nia/
msgid ""
"You are free to say what you feel at the of risk job loss and prison for "
"expressing anything contrary to the wishes of whoever is in power of your "
"jurisdiction - you have that right to say it and suffer."
msgstr ""
"Du är fri att säga vad du tycker med risk för att förlora arbetet eller "
"fängslas om du uttrycker något som strider mot önskemålen hos den som har "
"makten i din jurisdiktion – du har rätt att säga det och lida följderna."

#: content/outreach/stories/nia/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/nia/
msgid ""
"Journalism isn't free and fair. You are free to say what you feel at the "
"risk of job loss and prison for expressing anything contrary to the wishes "
"of whoever is in power of your jurisdiction - you have that right to say it "
"and suffer."
msgstr ""
"Journalistiken är inte fri och rättvis. Du är fri att säga vad du tycker med "
"risk för att förlora arbetet eller fängslas om du uttrycker något som "
"strider mot önskemålen hos den som har makten i din jurisdiktion – du har "
"rätt att säga det och lida följderna."

#: content/outreach/stories/nia/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/nia/
msgid "Nia"
msgstr "Nia"

#: content/outreach/stories/noor/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/noor/
msgid "I live in Iran and the police state is vigorously spying on people."
msgstr "Jag bor i Iran, och polisstaten övervakar människor intensivt."

#: content/outreach/stories/noor/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/noor/
msgid ""
"Without Tor we would be shut off from the world, no one hearing our voice."
msgstr ""
"Utan Tor skulle vi vara avskurna från världen och ingen skulle höra våra "
"röster."

#: content/outreach/stories/noor/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/noor/
msgid ""
"I live in Iran and the police state is vigorously spying on people. Without "
"Tor we would be shut off from the world, no one hearing our voice."
msgstr ""
"Jag bor i Iran, och polisstaten övervakar människor intensivt. Utan Tor "
"skulle vi vara avskurna från världen och ingen skulle höra våra röster."

#: content/outreach/stories/noor/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/noor/
msgid "Noor"
msgstr "Noor"

#: content/outreach/stories/oliver/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/oliver/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/oliver/
msgid ""
"I think our data is being manipulated, used against to shape our "
"worldview...my aim is to avoid 'misinformation' and stop online bullying."
msgstr ""
"Jag tror att våra uppgifter manipuleras och används mot oss för att forma "
"vår världsbild … Mitt mål är att undvika ”desinformation” och stoppa "
"nätmobbning."

#: content/outreach/stories/oliver/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/oliver/
msgid "Oliver"
msgstr "Oliver"

#: content/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/
msgid "I live in the UK."
msgstr "Jag bor i Storbritannien."

#: content/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/
msgid ""
"I use Tor on a daily basis, and also use a paid-for VPN service when not "
"using Tor."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor dagligen och använder även en betald VPN-tjänst när jag "
"inte använder Tor."

#: content/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/
msgid ""
"I was incredibly disturbed by the Edward Snowden revelations about NSA mass "
"surveillance."
msgstr ""
"Jag blev oerhört upprörd av Edward Snowdens avslöjanden om NSA:s "
"massövervakning."

#: content/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/
msgid ""
"The UK Government's own legislation of DRIPA and the Investigatory Powers "
"Act made it even more necessary in my opinion to protect my browsing history "
"from the government's intrusive snooping."
msgstr ""
"Den brittiska regeringens lagstiftning, DRIPA och Investigatory Powers Act, "
"gjorde det enligt min mening ännu viktigare att skydda min webbhistorik från "
"regeringens påträngande övervakning."

#: content/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/
msgid "This led me to start using the Tor browser."
msgstr "Det fick mig att börja använda Tor Browser."

#: content/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/
msgid ""
"I live in the UK. I was incredibly disturbed by the Edward Snowden "
"revelations about NSA mass surveillance. This led me to start using the Tor "
"browser."
msgstr ""
"Jag bor i Storbritannien. Jag blev oerhört upprörd av Edward Snowdens "
"avslöjanden om NSA:s massövervakning. Det fick mig att börja använda Tor "
"Browser."

#: content/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/pittiulaaq/
msgid "Pittiulaaq"
msgstr "Pittiulaaq"

#: content/outreach/stories/plinio/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/plinio/
msgid ""
"Even there are sites that use services and resources that are also blocked "
"for my country."
msgstr ""
"Det finns även webbplatser som använder tjänster och resurser som också är "
"blockerade i mitt land."

#: content/outreach/stories/plinio/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/plinio/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/plinio/
msgid "I am a software developer and programming teacher and I live in Cuba."
msgstr "Jag är programvaruutvecklare och programmeringslärare och bor på Kuba."

#: content/outreach/stories/plinio/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/plinio/
msgid ""
"There are many sites with information that I need to be able to do my work "
"that are blocked due to absurd laws."
msgstr ""
"Många webbplatser med information som jag behöver för mitt arbete är "
"blockerade på grund av absurda lagar."

#: content/outreach/stories/plinio/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/plinio/
msgid "Plinio"
msgstr "Plinio"

#: content/outreach/stories/ren/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ren/
msgid ""
"Big corporations and companies have no morals and don't hesitate to share "
"personal information for profit."
msgstr ""
"Stora koncerner och företag saknar moral och tvekar inte att dela "
"personuppgifter för ekonomisk vinning."

#: content/outreach/stories/ren/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ren/
msgid ""
"Even basic entertainment apps collect everything they can from our devices "
"and sell that data to others."
msgstr ""
"Till och med enkla underhållningsappar samlar in allt de kan från våra "
"enheter och säljer uppgifterna vidare."

#: content/outreach/stories/ren/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ren/
msgid ""
"Our data was shared without our permission from sources like our healthcare "
"provider and employer."
msgstr ""
"Uppgifter om oss har delats utan vårt tillstånd av bland andra vårdgivare "
"och arbetsgivare."

#: content/outreach/stories/ren/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ren/
msgid ""
"Since all our devices know everything about us, having encrypted connections "
"is one of the few ways that we can at least prevent the data that is already "
"being stolen from being stolen again during its transfer."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom våra enheter känner till allt om oss är krypterade anslutningar ett "
"av få sätt att åtminstone förhindra att uppgifter som redan stjäls blir "
"stulna igen under överföringen."

#: content/outreach/stories/ren/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ren/
msgid ""
"Big corporations and companies have no morals and don't hesitate to share "
"personal information for profit. Our data was shared without our permission "
"from sources like our healthcare provider and employer."
msgstr ""
"Stora koncerner och företag saknar moral och tvekar inte att dela "
"personuppgifter för ekonomisk vinning. Uppgifter om oss har delats utan vårt "
"tillstånd av bland andra vårdgivare och arbetsgivare."

#: content/outreach/stories/ren/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/ren/
msgid "Ren"
msgstr "Ren"

#: content/outreach/stories/riley/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/riley/
msgid "Although attitudes are changing, it might bar me from getting a job."
msgstr ""
"Även om attityderna håller på att förändras kan det hindra mig från att få "
"ett arbete."

#: content/outreach/stories/riley/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/riley/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/riley/
msgid ""
"The knowledge that I'm queer might lead a mob to my location (with "
"potentially-deadly consequences) and ostracism from my family (on whom I'm "
"currently economically dependent)."
msgstr ""
"Kunskapen om att jag är queer kan leda en folkmassa till min plats, med "
"potentiellt dödliga följder, och göra att min familj stöter bort mig. Jag är "
"för närvarande ekonomiskt beroende av dem."

#: content/outreach/stories/riley/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/riley/
msgid ""
"To protect my online activities, I need strong computer security, but I "
"can't make it  *too* obvious, and Tor is easy plug-and-play that does not "
"draw suspicion."
msgstr ""
"För att skydda mina aktiviteter på nätet behöver jag stark datasäkerhet, men "
"det får inte vara *alltför* uppenbart. Tor är enkelt att börja använda och "
"väcker inga misstankar."

#: content/outreach/stories/riley/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/riley/
msgid "Riley"
msgstr "Riley"

#: content/outreach/stories/rotislav/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/rotislav/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/rotislav/
msgid "I use Tor for social media posting on sites that restrict free speech."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor för att publicera i sociala medier på webbplatser som "
"begränsar yttrandefriheten."

#: content/outreach/stories/rotislav/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/rotislav/
msgid "Rotislav"
msgstr "Rotislav"

#: content/outreach/stories/sachin/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sachin/
msgid "Encryption is privacy, as simple as that."
msgstr "Kryptering är integritet, så enkelt är det."

#: content/outreach/stories/sachin/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sachin/
msgid ""
"Privacy should be the default, giving away information should be the "
"exception."
msgstr "Integritet bör vara standard och att lämna ut information undantaget."

#: content/outreach/stories/sachin/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sachin/
msgid ""
"The only real question we should ask ourselves is \"do I have a good reason "
"to share this personal information?\""
msgstr ""
"Den enda verkliga frågan vi bör ställa oss är: ”Har jag ett gott skäl att "
"dela den här personliga informationen?”"

#: content/outreach/stories/sachin/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sachin/
msgid "This way of thinking is extremely unhealthy."
msgstr "Det tankesättet är mycket osunt."

#: content/outreach/stories/sachin/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sachin/
msgid ""
"We should never wonder \"do I have something to hide, do I have a reason to "
"not give this information?\""
msgstr ""
"Vi bör aldrig undra: ”Har jag något att dölja, har jag ett skäl att inte "
"lämna ut informationen?”"

#: content/outreach/stories/sachin/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sachin/
msgid ""
"Encryption is privacy, as simple as that. Privacy should be the default, "
"giving away information should be the exception."
msgstr ""
"Kryptering är integritet, så enkelt är det. Integritet bör vara standard och "
"att lämna ut information undantaget."

#: content/outreach/stories/sachin/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sachin/
msgid "Sachin"
msgstr "Sachin"

#: content/outreach/stories/sofia/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sofia/
msgid "I educated myself free from state propaganda."
msgstr "Jag utbildade mig utan statlig propaganda."

#: content/outreach/stories/sofia/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sofia/
msgid ""
"It got me out of the social bubble and I was able to get insides, ideas and "
"views from many different social groups."
msgstr ""
"Det tog mig ut ur den sociala bubblan och gav mig insikter, idéer och "
"perspektiv från många olika samhällsgrupper."

#: content/outreach/stories/sofia/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sofia/
msgid "Tor helped me very much."
msgstr "Tor hjälpte mig väldigt mycket."

#: content/outreach/stories/sofia/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sofia/
msgid "Tor helped me very much. I educated myself free from state propaganda."
msgstr ""
"Tor hjälpte mig väldigt mycket. Jag utbildade mig utan statlig propaganda."

#: content/outreach/stories/sofia/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sofia/
msgid "Sofia"
msgstr "Sofia"

#: content/outreach/stories/stanislava/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/stanislava/
msgid ""
"Being a dissident is hard enough, privacy is already heavily curtailed, so "
"anonymized communication is a godsend."
msgstr ""
"Det är svårt nog att vara dissident, och integriteten är redan kraftigt "
"beskuren. Anonymiserad kommunikation är därför en välsignelse."

#: content/outreach/stories/stanislava/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/stanislava/
msgid ""
"I later tried to obfuscate my identity, but I found that my government has "
"surprisingly broad powers to track down dissidents."
msgstr ""
"Senare försökte jag dölja min identitet, men upptäckte att regeringen har "
"förvånansvärt långtgående befogenheter att spåra dissidenter."

#: content/outreach/stories/stanislava/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/stanislava/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/stanislava/
msgid "I'm a political activist, part of a semi-criminalized minority."
msgstr ""
"Jag är politisk aktivist och tillhör en delvis kriminaliserad minoritet."

#: content/outreach/stories/stanislava/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/stanislava/
msgid ""
"In my younger years I entered the public debate openly, and as a result got "
"harassed by government agencies."
msgstr ""
"När jag var yngre deltog jag öppet i den offentliga debatten och blev därför "
"trakasserad av myndigheter."

#: content/outreach/stories/stanislava/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/stanislava/
msgid ""
"Only by using anonymizing means, among which Tor is key, can I get my "
"message out without having police come to \"check my papers\" in the middle "
"of the night."
msgstr ""
"Endast genom anonymiseringsmetoder, där Tor är avgörande, kan jag sprida "
"mitt budskap utan att polisen kommer mitt i natten för att ”kontrollera mina "
"papper”."

#: content/outreach/stories/stanislava/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/stanislava/
msgid ""
"Tor allows me freedom to publish my message to the world without being "
"personally persecuted for it."
msgstr ""
"Tor ger mig friheten att publicera mitt budskap för världen utan att "
"personligen förföljas för det."

#: content/outreach/stories/stanislava/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/stanislava/
msgid "Stanislava"
msgstr "Stanislava"

#: content/outreach/stories/suad/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/suad/
msgid ""
"During political unrest while the government tightens their grip on other "
"censorship circumvention alternatives, Tor with obfuscation plugins remain "
"the only solution."
msgstr ""
"Under politiska oroligheter, när regeringen skärper greppet om andra sätt "
"att kringgå censur, är Tor med kamouflerande tillägg den enda återstående "
"lösningen."

#: content/outreach/stories/suad/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/suad/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/suad/
msgid "I live in Iran and I have been using Tor for censorship circumvention."
msgstr "Jag bor i Iran och har använt Tor för att kringgå censur."

#: content/outreach/stories/suad/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/suad/
msgid ""
"It made it possible to access information on Youtube, Twitter, Blogger and "
"countless other sites."
msgstr ""
"Det gjorde det möjligt att komma åt information på YouTube, Twitter, Blogger "
"och otaliga andra webbplatser."

#: content/outreach/stories/suad/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/suad/
msgid "Tor changed my personal life in many ways."
msgstr "Tor förändrade mitt privatliv på många sätt."

#: content/outreach/stories/suad/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/suad/
msgid "Suad"
msgstr "Suad"

#: content/outreach/stories/sunil/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/sunil/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sunil/
msgid ""
"I'm using Tor for accessing the internet freely. I need it because in my "
"country internet is censored."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor för att få fri tillgång till internet. Jag behöver det "
"eftersom internet censureras i mitt land."

#: content/outreach/stories/sunil/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sunil/
msgid ""
"If the Tor network was not available some day, I'm sure I will be stopped "
"behind the www-door."
msgstr ""
"Om Tor-nätverket inte fanns tillgängligt en dag är jag säker på att jag "
"skulle bli stående utanför webben."

#: content/outreach/stories/sunil/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sunil/
msgid ""
"Tor does not have any alternatives and VPN services are not working properly "
"in my country or are not free and I don't have any payment methods for "
"paying the cost of them."
msgstr ""
"Tor har inga verkliga alternativ. VPN-tjänster fungerar inte ordentligt i "
"mitt land eller är inte kostnadsfria, och jag saknar betalningsmetoder för "
"att betala dem."

#: content/outreach/stories/sunil/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sunil/
msgid ""
"Tor is free and multi platform. Im using it on [my] Android phone, on my "
"Macbook and Windows desktop everywhere."
msgstr ""
"Tor är kostnadsfritt och fungerar på flera plattformar. Jag använder det "
"överallt: på min Android-telefon, min MacBook och min Windows-dator."

#: content/outreach/stories/sunil/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/sunil/
msgid "Sunil"
msgstr "Sunil"

#: content/outreach/stories/tadija/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/tadija/
msgid ""
"I am proud of you guys defending our freedom and try to support you as much "
"as I can."
msgstr ""
"Jag är stolt över att ni försvarar vår frihet och försöker stödja er så "
"mycket jag kan."

#: content/outreach/stories/tadija/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/tadija/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/tadija/
msgid "Tor Browser is the last defense line of the free internet."
msgstr "Tor Browser är det fria internets sista försvarslinje."

#: content/outreach/stories/tadija/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/tadija/
msgid "Tadija"
msgstr "Tadija"

#: content/outreach/stories/taimo/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/taimo/
msgid ""
"The biggest threat from this I see is not actively from the government "
"themselves, who are simply misguided, but any access from third party black "
"hat hackers who could get access to the database and themselves use it "
"maliciously."
msgstr ""
"Det största hotet jag ser är inte i första hand regeringen själv, som helt "
"enkelt är vilseledd, utan att illasinnade hackare från tredje part kan få "
"tillgång till databasen och använda den i skadliga syften."

#: content/outreach/stories/taimo/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/taimo/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/taimo/
msgid ""
"The risks I face from not using Tor are not immediate, and mostly focus "
"around the government consolidating information on it's population and the "
"potential for this to go wrong."
msgstr ""
"Riskerna med att inte använda Tor är inte omedelbara. De handlar främst om "
"att regeringen samlar information om befolkningen och möjligheten att detta "
"går fel."

#: content/outreach/stories/taimo/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/taimo/
msgid "Taimo"
msgstr "Taimo"

#: content/outreach/stories/taylor/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/taylor/
msgid "I have been using Tor for 2 years."
msgstr "Jag har använt Tor i två år."

#: content/outreach/stories/taylor/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/taylor/
msgid ""
"I was concerned about [my] privacy after hearing about Yahoo mail and Gmail "
"handing over private email to government officials."
msgstr ""
"Jag blev orolig för min integritet efter att ha hört att Yahoo Mail och "
"Gmail överlämnade privat e-post till myndigheter."

#: content/outreach/stories/taylor/contents.lr:story.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/taylor/
msgid "It helped my peace of mind knowing that I have some privacy left."
msgstr ""
"Det gav mig sinnesro att veta att jag fortfarande har ett visst mått av "
"integritet."

#: content/outreach/stories/taylor/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/taylor/
msgid ""
"I was concerned about [my] privacy after hearing about yahoo mail and gmail "
"handing over private email to government officials."
msgstr ""
"Jag blev orolig för min integritet efter att ha hört att Yahoo Mail och "
"Gmail överlämnade privat e-post till myndigheter."

#: content/outreach/stories/taylor/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/taylor/
msgid "Taylor"
msgstr "Taylor"

#: content/outreach/stories/tyler/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/tyler/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/tyler/
msgid ""
"Encryption is like putting a letter in an envelope before posting it: It’s "
"common sense."
msgstr ""
"Kryptering är som att lägga ett brev i ett kuvert innan man postar det: det "
"är sunt förnuft."

#: content/outreach/stories/tyler/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/tyler/
msgid "Tyler"
msgstr "Tyler"

#: content/outreach/stories/velia/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/velia/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/velia/
msgid ""
"I use Tor and other encrypted communications methods to communicate with "
"journalists and human rights advocates."
msgstr ""
"Jag använder Tor och andra krypterade kommunikationsmetoder för att "
"kommunicera med journalister och människorättsförsvarare."

#: content/outreach/stories/velia/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/velia/
msgid "Velia"
msgstr "Velia"

#: content/outreach/stories/wei/contents.lr:story.body
#: content/outreach/stories/wei/contents.lr:story.summary
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/wei/
msgid ""
"Encryption is essential for secure internet use. If communication services "
"are not encrypted when discussing politics, it will be difficult to have a "
"free discussion because people will be worried that government agencies may "
"be eavesdropping."
msgstr ""
"Kryptering är avgörande för säker användning av internet. Om "
"kommunikationstjänster inte är krypterade när politik diskuteras blir en fri "
"diskussion svår, eftersom människor oroar sig för att myndigheter kan "
"avlyssna dem."

#: content/outreach/stories/wei/contents.lr:story.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/stories/wei/
msgid "Wei"
msgstr "Wei"

#: content/outreach/talk/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/talk/
msgid ""
"Here you'll find materials on basic Tor explainers and concepts, ideas for "
"preparing a Tor talk, suggested social media posts, and more."
msgstr ""
"Här hittar du material som förklarar grunderna och centrala begrepp i Tor, "
"idéer för att förbereda ett föredrag om Tor, förslag på inlägg i sociala "
"medier och mycket mer."

#: content/outreach/talk/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/outreach/talk/
msgid "Talk about Tor"
msgstr "Prata om Tor"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"1. The relay's IP address or fingerprint. The fingerprint is a forty-"
"character hex string such as `203933ED4E55EF8A3C3518427D1A1ED6A4CC285E`."
msgstr ""
"1. Reläets IP-adress eller fingeravtryck. Fingeravtrycket är en hexadecimal "
"sträng med 40 tecken, till exempel "
"`203933ED4E55EF8A3C3518427D1A1ED6A4CC285E`."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "2. What kind of behavior did you see?"
msgstr "2. Vilket beteende såg du?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "3. Any additional information we'll need to reproduce the issue."
msgstr ""
"3. All ytterligare information som vi behöver för att återskapa problemet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"A bad relay is one that either doesn't work properly or tampers with our "
"users' connections."
msgstr ""
"Ett dåligt relä är ett relä som inte fungerar korrekt eller manipulerar "
"användarnas anslutningar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "Additionally, we can drop relays from the consensus entirely."
msgstr "Vi kan dessutom ta bort reläer helt från konsensus."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"After a relay is reported and we've verified the behavior we'll attempt to "
"contact the relay operator."
msgstr ""
"När ett relä har rapporterats och vi har verifierat beteendet försöker vi "
"kontakta reläoperatören."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Also, if your relay is stolen or goes missing, please report it as well, so "
"we can blocklist it in case whoever took it puts it back online."
msgstr ""
"Rapportera även om reläet blir stulet eller försvinner, så att vi kan "
"blockera det om personen som tog det sätter det på nätet igen."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Also, there is more information about specific relays available on our "
"metrics website via the [relay-search portal](https://metrics.torproject.org/"
"rs.html)."
msgstr ""
"Mer information om enskilda reläer finns även på vår mätwebbplats via "
"[portalen för reläsökning](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"BadExit - Never use the relay as an exit relay (for relays that e.g. show "
"broken DNS resolver configurations)"
msgstr ""
"BadExit – använd aldrig reläet som utgångsrelä, exempelvis för reläer med "
"trasig DNS-resolverkonfiguration"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "Do you actively look for bad relays?"
msgstr "Letar ni aktivt efter dåliga reläer?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "How do I report a bad relay?"
msgstr "Hur rapporterar jag ett dåligt relä?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"However, if you need help with anything Tor-related, please use the [Tor "
"Forum](https://forum.torproject.net/c/support/) instead."
msgstr ""
"Behöver du hjälp med något Tor-relaterat ska du i stället använda [Tor Forum]"
"(https://forum.torproject.net/c/support/)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"If you are using Tor Browser you can check which exit relay you got at any "
"time by visiting [the circuit icon on the URL bar](https://"
"support.torproject.org/tor-browser/features/managing-identities/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder Tor Browser kan du när som helst se vilket utgångsrelä du har "
"fått genom att öppna [kretsikonen i URL-fältet](https://"
"support.torproject.org/tor-browser/features/managing-identities/)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"If you encounter a bad relay then please let us know and write to `bad-"
"relays AT lists DOT torproject DOT org`."
msgstr ""
"Meddela oss om du stöter på ett dåligt relä genom att skriva till `bad-"
"relays AT lists DOT torproject DOT org`."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"If your relay has been flagged as a BadExit or got the MiddleOnly flag then "
"please let us know (see above for contact info) so we can work together to "
"fix the underlying issue."
msgstr ""
"Meddela oss om reläet har markerats med BadExit eller fått flaggan "
"MiddleOnly – se kontaktuppgifterna ovan – så att vi tillsammans kan åtgärda "
"det bakomliggande problemet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Many bad relays are caught thanks to our wider community, so many thanks for "
"all your help and vigilance."
msgstr ""
"Många dåliga reläer upptäcks tack vare vår bredare gemenskap. Stort tack för "
"all hjälp och vaksamhet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"MiddleOnly - Only use the relay in a middle position without any relevant "
"flag, like the HSDir flag"
msgstr ""
"MiddleOnly – använd reläet endast i en mellanposition och utan någon "
"relevant flagga, till exempel HSDir"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "My relay was given the BadExit or MiddleOnly flag. What's up?"
msgstr "Mitt relä fick flaggan BadExit eller MiddleOnly. Vad har hänt?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Often we can sort things out but if not (or the relay lacks contact "
"information) we'll flag it to prevent it from continuing to be used."
msgstr ""
"Ofta kan vi reda ut situationen. Om det inte går, eller om reläet saknar "
"kontaktuppgifter, flaggar vi det så att det inte fortsätter användas."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "Please include the following in your report:"
msgstr "Ta med följande i rapporten:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Please let us know by sending an email to `bad-relays AT lists DOT "
"torproject DOT org`."
msgstr ""
"Meddela oss genom att skicka e-post till `bad-relays AT lists DOT torproject "
"DOT org`."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Ran into a misconfigured, malicious, or suspicious relay while using Tor?"
msgstr ""
"Har du stött på ett felkonfigurerat, skadligt eller misstänkt relä när du "
"använde Tor?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"The description of bad relays as well as the criteria for rejecting them can "
"be found in the [Network Health wiki](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"network-health/team/-/wikis/Criteria-for-rejecting-bad-relays)."
msgstr ""
"En beskrivning av dåliga reläer och kriterierna för att avvisa dem finns på "
"[Network Health-wikin](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/"
"team/-/wikis/Criteria-for-rejecting-bad-relays)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "This can be either through maliciousness or misconfiguration."
msgstr "Det kan bero på illvilligt beteende eller felkonfiguration."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "We have two types of flags we can apply:"
msgstr "Vi kan använda två typer av flaggor:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "What happens to bad relays?"
msgstr "Vad händer med dåliga reläer?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "What is a bad relay?"
msgstr "Vad är ett dåligt relä?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Which of those options we deploy depends on the severity of the issue, and "
"if the relay can still be safely used in certain situations."
msgstr ""
"Vilket alternativ vi använder beror på hur allvarligt problemet är och om "
"reläet fortfarande kan användas säkert i vissa situationer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Yes. For our automated issue detection see e.g. [exitmap](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/exitmap)."
msgstr ""
"Ja. Ett exempel på vår automatiska problemidentifiering är [exitmap](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/exitmap)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.section
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "Community Resources"
msgstr "Gemenskapens resurser"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Learn how to report relays that either don't work properly or tamper with "
"our users' connections"
msgstr ""
"Lär dig rapportera reläer som inte fungerar korrekt eller manipulerar "
"användarnas anslutningar"

#: content/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.title
#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/bad-relays/
msgid "Bad relays"
msgstr "Dåliga reläer"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"A bad relay is one that either do not work properly or tamper with our "
"users' connections. This can be either through maliciousness or "
"misconfiguration."
msgstr ""
"Ett dåligt relä är ett relä som inte fungerar korrekt eller manipulerar "
"användarnas anslutningar. Det kan bero på illvilligt beteende eller "
"felkonfiguration."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "Also see the [Tor Exit Guidelines](tor-exit-guidelines)."
msgstr "Se även [riktlinjerna för Tor-utgångsreläer](tor-exit-guidelines)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"And, most importantly, make sure to email tshirt@torproject.org and [claim "
"your swag](swag). It's our way of saying thanks for defending privacy and "
"free speech online."
msgstr ""
"Viktigast av allt: skicka e-post till tshirt@torproject.org och [begär dina "
"profilprodukter](swag). Det är vårt sätt att tacka dig för att du försvarar "
"integritet och yttrandefrihet på nätet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "At your company or organization"
msgstr "På ditt företag eller i din organisation"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "At your university"
msgstr "På ditt universitet"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Becoming a Torservers partner is a good way to become more involved in the "
"Tor relay community, and can help you connect with dedicated relay operators "
"around the world for solidarity and support."
msgstr ""
"Att bli partner till Torservers är ett bra sätt att engagera sig mer i Tor-"
"relägemenskapen och få kontakt med hängivna reläoperatörer världen över för "
"solidaritet och stöd."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "Congratulations, you're officially a Tor relay operator! What now?"
msgstr "Grattis, du är nu officiellt Tor-reläoperatör! Vad händer härnäst?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Depending on your location and connections within the technical community of "
"the area, the last one may be the hardest step."
msgstr ""
"Beroende på var du befinner dig och dina kontakter i områdets "
"teknikgemenskap kan det sista steget vara det svåraste."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Exit relay operators should understand the potential risks associated with "
"running an exit relay."
msgstr ""
"Operatörer av utgångsreläer bör förstå de möjliga riskerna med att driva ett "
"sådant relä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Exits are the ones that present some legal concerns, but operators under "
"most circumstances will be able to handle legal matters by having an abuse "
"response letter, running the exit from a location that isn't their home, and "
"reading through some of the legal resources that Tor-supportive lawyers have "
"put together."
msgstr ""
"Utgångsreläer medför vissa juridiska frågor. Under de flesta omständigheter "
"kan operatörer hantera dem genom att ha ett färdigt svar på "
"missbruksanmälningar, köra reläet från en annan plats än hemmet och läsa de "
"juridiska resurser som Tor-vänliga jurister har sammanställt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"For the majority of operators in most countries, bridges and guard/middle "
"relays are very low risk."
msgstr ""
"För de flesta operatörer i de flesta länder innebär broar och vakt-/"
"mellanreläer mycket liten risk."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Get in touch with your local digital rights organization to see if they have "
"recommendations about legal assistance, and if you're not sure what "
"organizations are working in your region, [write to EFF](https://www.eff.org/"
"about/contact) and see if they can help connect you."
msgstr ""
"Kontakta din lokala organisation för digitala rättigheter och fråga om "
"rekommendationer för juridisk hjälp. Om du inte vet vilka organisationer som "
"arbetar i din region kan du [skriva till EFF](https://www.eff.org/about/"
"contact) och fråga om de kan förmedla en kontakt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"If you do not know anyone in your social network interested in running "
"relays, one place to meet people is [your local hackerspace](https://"
"wiki.hackerspaces.org/Hackerspaces)."
msgstr ""
"Om ingen i ditt sociala nätverk är intresserad av att driva reläer kan du "
"träffa människor på [din lokala hackerspace](https://wiki.hackerspaces.org/"
"Hackerspaces)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"If you work at a Tor-friendly company or organization, that's another ideal "
"place to run a relay."
msgstr ""
"Om du arbetar på ett Tor-vänligt företag eller i en Tor-vänlig organisation "
"är det också en idealisk plats att driva ett relä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"In general it's a good idea to consult with a lawyer before deciding to "
"operate an exit relay, especially if you live in a place where exit relay "
"operators have been harassed, or if you're the only exit relay operator in "
"your region."
msgstr ""
"Det är i allmänhet klokt att rådgöra med en jurist innan du bestämmer dig "
"för att driva ett utgångsrelä, särskilt om du bor på en plats där operatörer "
"har trakasserats eller om du är den enda utgångsreläoperatören i regionen."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"In many countries operating as a corporation instead of as an individual can "
"also get you certain legal protections."
msgstr ""
"I många länder kan du också få ett visst rättsligt skydd genom att driva "
"verksamheten som ett företag i stället för som privatperson."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"It is extremely important to maintain good relationships with these ISPs."
msgstr ""
"Det är oerhört viktigt att upprätthålla goda relationer med "
"internetleverantörerna."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"It is important to respond to abuse complaints in a timely manner (usually "
"within 24 hours). If the hoster gets annoyed by the amount of abuse you can "
"reduce the amount of ports allowed in your exit policy."
msgstr ""
"Det är viktigt att svara snabbt på klagomål om missbruk, vanligen inom 24 "
"timmar. Om värdleverantören störs av mängden klagomål kan du minska antalet "
"portar som tillåts i utgångspolicyn."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "Legal resources"
msgstr "Juridiska resurser"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Many bad relays are caught thanks to our wider community, so many thanks for "
"all your help and vigilance! Learn how you can report [bad relays](bad-"
"relays)."
msgstr ""
"Många dåliga reläer upptäcks tack vare vår bredare gemenskap. Stort tack för "
"all hjälp och vaksamhet! Lär dig rapportera [dåliga reläer](bad-relays)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Many computer science departments, university libraries, and individual "
"students and faculty run relays from university networks."
msgstr ""
"Många datavetenskapliga institutioner, universitetsbibliotek samt enskilda "
"studenter och lärare driver reläer från universitetsnätverk."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Once you have a trusted group of people, depending on your region, it is "
"often advised to create some type of non-profit corporation."
msgstr ""
"När du har en betrodd grupp människor rekommenderas det ofta, beroende på "
"region, att bilda någon typ av ideell organisation."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Operators can put together their own abuse complaint template responses from "
"one of many templates that Tor has created: [Tor Abuse Templates](tor-abuse-"
"templates)."
msgstr ""
"Operatörer kan skapa egna svarsmallar för klagomål om missbruk utifrån någon "
"av de många mallar som Tor har tagit fram: [Tors mallar för missbrukssvar]"
"(tor-abuse-templates)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "Other docs we like:"
msgstr "Annan dokumentation som vi uppskattar:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "Other resources"
msgstr "Andra resurser"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Please document your experience with new hosters on the following page: "
"[GoodBadISPs](good-bad-isps)"
msgstr ""
"Dokumentera gärna dina erfarenheter av nya värdleverantörer på följande "
"sida: [GoodBadISPs](good-bad-isps)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "Responding to abuse complaints"
msgstr "Svara på klagomål om missbruk"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "Running a relay with other people"
msgstr "Driva ett relä tillsammans med andra"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Running relays is more fun with other people! You can work with your "
"university department, your employer or institution, or an organization like "
"[Torservers.net](https://torservers.net) to run a relay."
msgstr ""
"Det är roligare att driva reläer tillsammans med andra! Du kan samarbeta med "
"din universitetsinstitution, arbetsgivare eller organisation, eller med en "
"organisation som [Torservers.net](https://torservers.net), för att driva ett "
"relä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Small local ISPs often have extra bandwidth, and may be interested in "
"supporting your group with some bandwidth or rackspace."
msgstr ""
"Små lokala internetleverantörer har ofta extra bandbredd och kan vara "
"intresserade av att stödja gruppen med bandbredd eller plats i ett "
"serverrack."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Some companies running relays include [Brass Horn Communications](https://"
"brasshorncommunications.uk/), [Quintex Alliance Consulting](https://"
"www.quintex.com/), [Private Internet Access](https://"
"www.privateinternetaccess.com/), [Boing Boing](https://boingboing.net/) and "
"OmuraVPN."
msgstr ""
"Företag som driver reläer är bland andra [Brass Horn Communications](https://"
"brasshorncommunications.uk/), [Quintex Alliance Consulting](https://"
"www.quintex.com/), [Private Internet Access](https://"
"www.privateinternetaccess.com/), [Boing Boing](https://boingboing.net/) och "
"OmuraVPN."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Some organizations running Tor relays include Digital Courage, [Access Now]"
"(https://www.accessnow.org/), [Derechos Digitales](https://"
"tor.derechosdigitales.org), [Enjambre Digital](https://tor.enjambre.net/) "
"and Lebanon Libraries in New Hampshire."
msgstr ""
"Organisationer som driver Tor-reläer är bland andra Digital Courage, [Access "
"Now](https://www.accessnow.org/), [Derechos Digitales](https://"
"tor.derechosdigitales.org), [Enjambre Digital](https://tor.enjambre.net/) "
"och Lebanon Libraries i New Hampshire."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"The [EFF Tor Legal FAQ](/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq) "
"answers many common questions about relay operation and the law. We also "
"like [Noisebridge's wiki](https://www.noisebridge.net/wiki/Noisebridge_Tor/"
"FBI) for additional legal resources."
msgstr ""
"[EFF:s juridiska vanliga frågor om Tor](/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-"
"legal-faq) besvarar många vanliga frågor om relädrift och juridik. Vi "
"rekommenderar även [Noisebridges wiki](https://www.noisebridge.net/wiki/"
"Noisebridge_Tor/FBI) med ytterligare juridiska resurser."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "The next steps are figuring out hardware, traffic, and server hosting."
msgstr "Nästa steg är att ordna maskinvara, trafik och servervärd."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"There is also more info about running a relay at the [Tor FAQ](https://"
"support.torproject.org/relay-operators/)."
msgstr ""
"Mer information om att driva reläer finns i [Tors vanliga frågor](https://"
"support.torproject.org/relay-operators/)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"There should be mutual trust between the people in the group, and members "
"should commit to running relays for the long term."
msgstr ""
"Människorna i gruppen bör lita på varandra och förbinda sig att driva reläer "
"långsiktigt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"These universities include the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT "
"CSAIL), Boston University, the University of Waterloo, the University of "
"Washington, Northeastern University, Karlstad University, Universitaet "
"Stuttgart, and Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nuremberg."
msgstr ""
"Universiteten omfattar Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT CSAIL), "
"Boston University, University of Waterloo, University of Washington, "
"Northeastern University, Karlstad University, Universität Stuttgart och "
"Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"This is useful for having a bank account, shared ownership, grant "
"applications, etc."
msgstr ""
"Det är användbart för att ha ett bankkonto, delat ägande, ansöka om bidrag "
"och liknande."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"To learn more about how to get support for a relay on your university's "
"network, check out EFF's resources: Tor on campus [Part 1 - It's Been Done "
"Before and Should Happen Again](https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2014/08/tor-"
"campus-part-i-its-been-done-and-should-happen-again) and [Part 2 - "
"Icebreakers and Risk Mitigation Strategies](https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/"
"2014/08/tor-campus-part-ii-icebreakers-and-risk-mitigation-strategies)."
msgstr ""
"Läs EFF:s resurser om du vill veta mer om hur du får stöd för ett relä på "
"universitetets nätverk: Tor on Campus [del 1 – It’s Been Done Before and "
"Should Happen Again](https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2014/08/tor-campus-part-i-"
"its-been-done-and-should-happen-again) och [del 2 – Icebreakers and Risk "
"Mitigation Strategies](https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2014/08/tor-campus-part-"
"ii-icebreakers-and-risk-mitigation-strategies)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"To start a Torservers partner, the most important thing is to have a group "
"of people (3-5 suggested to start) interested in helping with the various "
"activities required for running relays."
msgstr ""
"Det viktigaste för att starta en Torservers-partner är en grupp människor – "
"till en början rekommenderas tre till fem – som vill hjälpa till med de "
"olika aktiviteter som krävs för att driva reläer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"Torservers is an independent, global network of organizations that help the "
"Tor network by running high bandwidth Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"Torservers är ett oberoende globalt nätverk av organisationer som hjälper "
"Tor-nätverket genom att driva Tor-reläer med hög bandbredd."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid "Torservers.net"
msgstr "Torservers.net"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"You can check out traffic and other statistics for your relay at our [Relay "
"Search](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html) (your relay will appear on "
"\"Relay Search\" about 3 hours after you started it)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan se trafik och annan statistik för reläet i vår [reläsökning](https://"
"metrics.torproject.org/rs.html). Reläet visas där ungefär tre timmar efter "
"att du har startat det."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"a letter Boing Boing used to respond to a US federal subpoena about their "
"exit relay: [What happened when we got subpoenaed over our Tor exit node]"
"(https://boingboing.net/2015/08/04/what-happened-when-the-fbi-sub.html)"
msgstr ""
"ett brev som Boing Boing använde för att svara på en federal amerikansk "
"stämning om deras utgångsrelä: [What happened when we got subpoenaed over "
"our Tor exit node](https://boingboing.net/2015/08/04/what-happened-when-the-"
"fbi-sub.html)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"abuse response templates from Coldhak, an organization in Canada that runs "
"multiple relays: [DMCA Template](https://github.com/coldhakca/abuse-"
"templates/blob/master/dmca.template), [Generic Abuse Template](https://"
"github.com/coldhakca/abuse-templates/blob/master/generic.template)."
msgstr ""
"svarsmallar för missbruksanmälningar från Coldhak, en kanadensisk "
"organisation som driver flera reläer: [DMCA-mall](https://github.com/"
"coldhakca/abuse-templates/blob/master/dmca.template), [allmän missbruksmall]"
"(https://github.com/coldhakca/abuse-templates/blob/master/generic.template)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
msgid ""
"How to get involved with the Tor relay operator community, advice on "
"responding to abuse complaints, and how to start an organization dedicated "
"to relay operation."
msgstr ""
"Så engagerar du dig i gemenskapen av Tor-reläoperatörer, råd om svar på "
"klagomål om missbruk och hur du startar en organisation som är inriktad på "
"relädrift."

#: content/relay/community-resources/contents.lr:page.title
#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.section
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "Community and legal resources"
msgstr "Gemenskapsresurser och juridiska resurser"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**Although we are not aware of an individual being sued, prosecuted, or "
"convicted for running a Tor relay**, law enforcement in the United States "
"and other countries has occasionally mistakenly investigated individuals "
"running a Tor relay."
msgstr ""
"**Även om vi inte känner till någon privatperson som har stämts, åtalats "
"eller dömts för att driva ett Tor-relä** har brottsbekämpande myndigheter i "
"USA och andra länder ibland felaktigt utrett personer som driver Tor-reläer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**Educate them about Tor**. In most instances, properly configured Tor "
"relays will have no useful data for inquiring parties, and you should feel "
"free to educate them on this point."
msgstr ""
"**Informera dem om Tor.** Korrekt konfigurerade Tor-reläer har i de flesta "
"fall inga användbara uppgifter för den som gör förfrågan, och du kan gärna "
"förklara det."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**Maybe**. While EFF cannot promise legal representation for all Tor relay "
"operators, it [will assist relay operators](https://www.eff.org/pages/legal-"
"assistance) in assessing the situation and will try to locate qualified "
"legal counsel when necessary."
msgstr ""
"**Kanske.** EFF kan inte lova juridiskt ombud åt alla Tor-reläoperatörer, "
"men organisationen [hjälper reläoperatörer](https://www.eff.org/pages/legal-"
"assistance) att bedöma situationen och försöker vid behov hitta kvalificerat "
"juridiskt ombud."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "**No**, this is risky and not recommended."
msgstr "**Nej**, det är riskabelt och rekommenderas inte."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**No**. All new technologies create legal uncertainties, and Tor is no "
"exception."
msgstr ""
"**Nej.** All ny teknik skapar juridisk osäkerhet, och Tor är inget undantag."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**No**. Although the developers attempt to verify that Tor relays listed in "
"the directory maintained by the core developers are stable and have adequate "
"bandwidth, neither they nor EFF can guarantee the personal trustworthiness "
"or reliability of the individuals who run those relays."
msgstr ""
"**Nej.** Utvecklarna försöker kontrollera att Tor-reläerna i katalogen som "
"underhålls av kärnutvecklarna är stabila och har tillräcklig bandbredd, men "
"varken utvecklarna eller EFF kan garantera reläoperatörernas personliga "
"tillförlitlighet eller hederlighet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**No**. Tor has been developed to be a tool for free expression, privacy, "
"and human rights. It is not a tool designed or intended to be used to break "
"the law, either by Tor users or Tor relay operators."
msgstr ""
"**Nej.** Tor har utvecklats som ett verktyg för yttrandefrihet, integritet "
"och mänskliga rättigheter. Det är varken utformat eller avsett för lagbrott, "
"vare sig av Tor-användare eller Tor-reläoperatörer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**No**. Tor's developers are available to answer technical questions, but "
"they are not lawyers and cannot give legal advice. Nor do they have any "
"ability to prevent illegal activity that may occur through Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"**Nej.** Tors utvecklare kan svara på tekniska frågor, men de är inte "
"jurister och kan inte ge juridisk rådgivning. De kan inte heller förhindra "
"olaglig verksamhet som kan förekomma genom Tor-reläer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**No**. You may be technically capable of modifying the Tor source code or "
"installing additional software to monitor or log plaintext that exits your "
"relay."
msgstr ""
"**Nej.** Det kan vara tekniskt möjligt att ändra Tors källkod eller "
"installera ytterligare programvara för att övervaka eller logga okrypterad "
"trafik som lämnar reläet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**Yes**. Be as transparent as possible about the fact that you're running an "
"exit relay."
msgstr "**Ja.** Var så öppen som möjligt med att du driver ett utgångsrelä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**Yes**. Make sure you have a Tor-friendly ISP that knows you're running an "
"exit relay and supports you in that goal."
msgstr ""
"**Ja.** Kontrollera att du har en Tor-vänlig internetleverantör som känner "
"till att du driver ett utgångsrelä och stöder dig i det."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"**Yes.** A federal law, 47 U.S.C. § 230 (often called Section 230), provides "
"legal immunity for online intermediaries that host or republish speech."
msgstr ""
"**Ja.** Den federala amerikanska lagen 47 U.S.C. § 230, ofta kallad Section "
"230, ger rättslig immunitet åt mellanhänder på nätet som är värd för eller "
"återpublicerar yttranden."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Also, if you received this document from anywhere besides the EFF web site "
"or https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-"
"faq, it may be out of date. Follow the link to get the latest version."
msgstr ""
"Om du har fått dokumentet från någon annan plats än EFF:s webbplats eller "
"https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq "
"kan det dessutom vara inaktuellt. Följ länken för den senaste versionen."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"An exit relay may forward traffic that is considered unlawful, and that "
"traffic may be attributed to the operator of a relay."
msgstr ""
"Ett utgångsrelä kan vidarebefordra trafik som anses olaglig, och trafiken "
"kan tillskrivas reläoperatören."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"And Russian authorities wrongfully arrested math instructor and Tor relay "
"operator [Dmitry Bogatov](https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2017/04/access-now-"
"and-eff-condemn-arrest-tor-node-operator-dmitry-bogatov-russia), though they "
"later cleared him of [charges](https://web.archive.org/web/20190617062802/"
"https://tass.com/society/986636)."
msgstr ""
"Ryska myndigheter grep dessutom felaktigt matematikläraren och Tor-"
"reläoperatören [Dmitry Bogatov](https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2017/04/access-"
"now-and-eff-condemn-arrest-tor-node-operator-dmitry-bogatov-russia), även om "
"han senare friades från [anklagelserna](https://web.archive.org/web/"
"20190617062802/https://tass.com/society/986636)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Another federal law, 17 U.S.C. § 512(a), part of the Digital Millennium "
"Copyright Act, provides a legal safe harbor against copyright infringement "
"claims based on material that is simply transmitted without modification, as "
"a Tor relay does."
msgstr ""
"En annan federal amerikansk lag, 17 U.S.C. § 512(a), som ingår i Digital "
"Millennium Copyright Act, ger ett rättsligt säkerhetsundantag från anspråk "
"på upphovsrättsintrång för material som endast överförs oförändrat, vilket "
"ett Tor-relä gör."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "Can EFF promise that I won't get in trouble for running a Tor relay?"
msgstr "Kan EFF lova att jag inte får problem för att jag driver ett Tor-relä?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Different factual situations and different legal jurisdictions will result "
"in different answers to a number of questions."
msgstr ""
"Olika faktiska omständigheter och rättsordningar ger olika svar på flera av "
"frågorna."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Do Tor's core developers make any promises about the trustworthiness or "
"reliability of Tor relays that are listed in their directory?"
msgstr ""
"Ger Tors kärnutvecklare några garantier för att Tor-reläerna i deras katalog "
"är hederliga eller tillförlitliga?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Do not examine anyone's communications without first talking to a lawyer."
msgstr "Granska inte någons kommunikation utan att först tala med en jurist."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Does U.S. law provide any protections for the Tor network against civil "
"lawsuits?"
msgstr ""
"Ger amerikansk lag Tor-nätverket något skydd mot civilrättsliga stämningar?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"EFF believes that Tor relays should be protected from copyright liability "
"for the acts of their users because a Tor relay operator can raise an "
"immunity defense under Section 512 of DMCA as well as defenses under "
"copyright's secondary liability doctrines."
msgstr ""
"EFF anser att Tor-reläer bör skyddas från upphovsrättsligt ansvar för "
"användarnas handlingar, eftersom en Tor-reläoperatör kan åberopa immunitet "
"enligt avsnitt 512 i DMCA och invändningar enligt upphovsrättens regler om "
"sekundärt ansvar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"EFF has written a [short template](tor-dmca-response) to help you write a "
"response to your ISP, university, etc., to let them know about the details "
"of the Digital Millennium Copyright Act's safe harbor, and how Tor fits in."
msgstr ""
"EFF har skrivit en [kort mall](tor-dmca-response) som hjälper dig att svara "
"internetleverantören, universitetet eller liknande och förklara detaljerna i "
"Digital Millennium Copyright Acts säkerhetsundantag och hur Tor passar in."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "Exit Relays"
msgstr "Utgångsreläer"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Exit relays raise special concerns because the traffic that exits from them "
"can be traced back to the relay's IP address."
msgstr ""
"Utgångsreläer medför särskilda frågor eftersom trafiken som lämnar dem kan "
"spåras tillbaka till reläets IP-adress."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"For example, in 2016 Seattle police [mistakenly raided](https://"
"web.archive.org/web/20191210114929/https://www.thestranger.com/slog/"
"2016/04/08/23914735/judge-who-authorized-police-search-of-seattle-privacy-"
"activists-wasnt-told-they-operate-tor-network/) the home of a privacy "
"activist operating a Tor exit relay."
msgstr ""
"År 2016 gjorde polisen i Seattle exempelvis en [felaktig husrannsakan]"
"(https://web.archive.org/web/20191210114929/https://www.thestranger.com/slog/"
"2016/04/08/23914735/judge-who-authorized-police-search-of-seattle-privacy-"
"activists-wasnt-told-they-operate-tor-network/) hemma hos en "
"integritetsaktivist som drev ett Tor-utgångsrelä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"For information on what to do if law enforcement seeks access to your "
"digital devices, check out EFF's [Know Your Rights](https://www.eff.org/wp/"
"know-your-rights) guide."
msgstr ""
"Information om vad du bör göra om en brottsbekämpande myndighet vill få "
"tillgång till dina digitala enheter finns i EFF:s guide [Know Your Rights]"
"(https://www.eff.org/wp/know-your-rights)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"For more information about responding to abuse complaints and other "
"inquiries, check out the [Tor Abuse FAQ](https://support.torproject.org/"
"abuse) and the collection of [abuse response templates](../tor-abuse-"
"templates/) on the Tor Project's website."
msgstr ""
"Mer information om hur du svarar på klagomål om missbruk och andra "
"förfrågningar finns i [Tors vanliga frågor om missbruk](https://"
"support.torproject.org/abuse) och samlingen med [svarsmallar för missbruk]"
"(../tor-abuse-templates/) på The Tor Projects webbplats."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"For that reason, it's best not to run your exit relay in your home or using "
"your home Internet connection."
msgstr ""
"Därför är det bäst att inte driva utgångsreläet hemma eller via hemmets "
"internetanslutning."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Furthermore, your communications with Tor's developers are not protected by "
"any legal privilege, so law enforcement or civil litigants could subpoena "
"and obtain any information you give to them."
msgstr ""
"Din kommunikation med Tors utvecklare omfattas dessutom inte av någon "
"juridisk sekretess, så brottsbekämpande myndigheter eller civilrättsliga "
"parter kan begära ut och få den information som du lämnar till dem."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "General Information"
msgstr "Allmän information"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Given those risks, you should instead consider running your exit relay in a "
"commercial facility that is supportive of Tor. Have a separate IP address "
"for your exit relay, and don't route your own traffic through it."
msgstr ""
"Med tanke på riskerna bör du i stället överväga att driva utgångsreläet i en "
"kommersiell anläggning som stöder Tor. Använd en separat IP-adress för "
"reläet och dirigera inte din egen trafik genom det."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Got a DMCA notice? Check out our [sample response letter](tor-dmca-response)!"
msgstr ""
"Har du fått ett DMCA-meddelande? Läs vårt [exempelsvar](tor-dmca-response)!"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "Has anyone ever been sued or prosecuted for running Tor?"
msgstr "Har någon någonsin stämts eller åtalats för att driva Tor?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "How should I deal with a police visit/raid/interrogation?"
msgstr ""
"Hur bör jag agera vid ett polisbesök, en husrannsakan eller ett förhör?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"However, EFF believes so strongly that those running Tor relays shouldn't be "
"liable for traffic that passes through the relay that we're running our own "
"middle relay."
msgstr ""
"EFF är dock så övertygat om att Tor-reläoperatörer inte bör vara ansvariga "
"för trafik som passerar genom reläet att organisationen driver ett eget "
"mellanrelä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"However, Tor relay operators in the United States can possibly create civil "
"and even criminal liability for themselves under state or federal wiretap "
"laws if they monitor, log, or disclose Tor users' communications, while non-"
"U.S. operators may be subject to similar laws."
msgstr ""
"Tor-reläoperatörer i USA kan dock eventuellt ådra sig civilrättsligt och "
"till och med straffrättsligt ansvar enligt delstatliga eller federala "
"avlyssningslagar om de övervakar, loggar eller lämnar ut Tor-användarnas "
"kommunikation. Operatörer utanför USA kan omfattas av liknande lagar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"However, if you do decide to waive your right to the assistance of counsel "
"and answer questions without an attorney present, be sure to tell the truth."
msgstr ""
"Om du ändå avstår från rätten till juridiskt ombud och svarar på frågor utan "
"att en advokat är närvarande måste du tala sanning."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"However, no court has yet addressed these issues in the context of Tor "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"Ingen domstol har dock ännu behandlat frågorna specifikt i samband med Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If I receive a subpoena or other information request from law enforcement or "
"anyone else related to my Tor relay, what should I do?"
msgstr ""
"Vad bör jag göra om jag får en stämning eller annan begäran om information "
"från en brottsbekämpande myndighet eller någon annan med anledning av mitt "
"Tor-relä?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If law enforcement becomes interested in traffic from your exit relay, it's "
"possible that officers will mistakenly attribute that traffic as originating "
"from your home."
msgstr ""
"Om en brottsbekämpande myndighet intresserar sig för trafik från "
"utgångsreläet kan tjänstemännen felaktigt tro att trafiken kommer från ditt "
"hem."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If possible, get an [ARIN](https://www.arin.net/) registration for your exit "
"relay that displays contact information for you, not your ISP."
msgstr ""
"Skaffa om möjligt en registrering hos [ARIN](https://www.arin.net/) för "
"utgångsreläet som visar dina kontaktuppgifter i stället för "
"internetleverantörens."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If you are a Tor relay operator willing to stand up and help set a clear "
"legal precedent establishing that merely running a relay does not create "
"copyright liability for either operators or their bandwidth providers, EFF "
"is interested in hearing from you."
msgstr ""
"EFF vill gärna höra från Tor-reläoperatörer som är beredda att stå upp och "
"bidra till ett tydligt prejudikat om att enbart relädrift inte skapar "
"upphovsrättsligt ansvar för operatören eller dess bandbreddsleverantör."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If you are detained and questioned by police, you have a right to request to "
"speak with an attorney before and during any questioning."
msgstr ""
"Om polisen frihetsberövar och förhör dig har du rätt att begära att få tala "
"med en advokat före och under förhöret."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If you are not willing to deal with that risk, a bridge or middle relay may "
"be a better fit for you."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte är beredd att hantera risken kan en bro eller ett mellanrelä "
"passa dig bättre."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If you are uncomfortable with this uncertainty, you may consider using a "
"reduced exit policy (such as the default policy suggested by the Tor "
"Project) to try to minimize traffic types that are often targeted in "
"copyright complaints."
msgstr ""
"Om du känner dig obekväm med osäkerheten kan du överväga en begränsad "
"utgångspolicy, till exempel standardpolicyn som The Tor Project föreslår, "
"för att försöka minimera trafiktyper som ofta leder till "
"upphovsrättsklagomål."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If you do decide to run an exit relay from your home despite these risks, "
"please review Tor’s recommendations, including telling your ISP and "
"obtaining a separate IP address for the exit relay."
msgstr ""
"Om du trots riskerna bestämmer dig för att driva ett utgångsrelä hemifrån "
"bör du läsa Tors rekommendationer, bland annat att informera "
"internetleverantören och skaffa en separat IP-adress för reläet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If you like, you should consider submitting a copy of your notice to the "
"Lumen Database. The email address for submissions is team@lumendatabase.org."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också överväga att skicka en kopia av meddelandet till Lumen "
"Database. Adressen för bidrag är team@lumendatabase.org."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"If your exit traffic draws the attention of the government or disgruntled "
"private party, you want them to figure out quickly and easily that you are "
"part of the Tor network and not responsible for the content."
msgstr ""
"Om utgångstrafiken drar till sig regeringens eller en missnöjd privat parts "
"uppmärksamhet vill du att de snabbt och enkelt ska kunna fastställa att du "
"ingår i Tor-nätverket och inte ansvarar för innehållet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"In the United States, the data may be protected by the Electronic "
"Communications Privacy Act, and relay operators outside of the United States "
"may be subject to similar data protection laws."
msgstr ""
"I USA kan uppgifterna skyddas av Electronic Communications Privacy Act. "
"Reläoperatörer utanför USA kan omfattas av liknande dataskyddslagar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Indeed, police have mistakenly attributed traffic from an exit relay as "
"coming from the relay’s operator."
msgstr ""
"Polisen har faktiskt felaktigt tillskrivit trafik från utgångsreläer till "
"reläoperatören."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Inquiries to EFF for the purpose of securing legal representation or "
"referrals should be directed to our intake coordinator by sending an email "
"to info at eff.org."
msgstr ""
"Förfrågningar till EFF i syfte att få juridiskt ombud eller en hänvisning "
"ska skickas till organisationens samordnare på adressen info at eff.org."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Inquiries to EFF for the purpose of securing legal representation should be "
"directed to our intake coordinator (info at eff.org)."
msgstr ""
"Förfrågningar till EFF i syfte att få juridiskt ombud ska skickas till "
"organisationens samordnare på adressen info at eff.org."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "Is it a good idea to let others know that I'm running an exit relay?"
msgstr "Är det bra att berätta för andra att jag driver ett utgångsrelä?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"It is best to say \"I want my attorney and I choose to remain silent\" and "
"then refuse questioning until you have a chance to talk to a lawyer."
msgstr ""
"Det är bäst att säga ”Jag vill tala med min advokat och väljer att förbli "
"tyst” och sedan vägra svara på frågor tills du har fått tala med en jurist."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "Lumen encourages submissions from people outside the United States too."
msgstr "Lumen uppmuntrar även personer utanför USA att skicka in material."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Lying to law enforcement may lead to more trouble than for whatever it was "
"they wanted to talk to you about in the first place."
msgstr ""
"Att ljuga för brottsbekämpande myndigheter kan ge större problem än det de "
"ursprungligen ville tala med dig om."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "My ISP, university, etc. just sent me a DMCA notice. What should I do?"
msgstr ""
"Min internetleverantör, mitt universitet eller liknande har skickat ett DMCA-"
"meddelande till mig. Vad bör jag göra?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"NOTE: This FAQ is for informational purposes only and does not constitute "
"legal advice."
msgstr ""
"OBSERVERA: Dessa vanliga frågor är endast avsedda som information och utgör "
"inte juridisk rådgivning."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Note that although EFF cannot practice law outside of the United States, it "
"will still try to assist non-U.S. relay operators in finding local "
"representation."
msgstr ""
"Även om EFF inte kan utöva juridik utanför USA försöker organisationen "
"hjälpa reläoperatörer i andra länder att hitta lokalt ombud."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Note that template only refers to U.S. jurisdictions, and is intended only "
"to address copyright complaints that are based on a relay of allegedly "
"infringing material through the Tor node."
msgstr ""
"Observera att mallen endast gäller amerikanska jurisdiktioner och endast är "
"avsedd för upphovsrättsklagomål som bygger på att material som påstås göra "
"intrång har vidarebefordrats genom Tor-noden."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Of course, you should avoid keeping any sensitive or personal information on "
"the computer hosting your exit relay, and you never should use that machine "
"for any illegal purpose."
msgstr ""
"Du bör naturligtvis undvika att förvara känslig eller personlig information "
"på datorn som är värd för utgångsreläet, och du bör aldrig använda den för "
"olagliga ändamål."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Our aim is to provide a general description of the legal issues surrounding "
"Tor in the United States."
msgstr ""
"Vårt mål är att ge en allmän beskrivning av de juridiska frågorna kring Tor "
"i USA."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Set up a notice like [this](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-running-"
"exit-node) to explain that you're running an exit relay that's part of the "
"Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Skapa ett meddelande som [det här](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-"
"running-exit-node) för att förklara att du driver ett utgångsrelä som ingår "
"i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Set up a reverse DNS name for the IP address that makes clear that the "
"computer is an exit relay."
msgstr ""
"Konfigurera ett omvänt DNS-namn för IP-adressen som tydligt visar att datorn "
"är ett utgångsrelä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Should I contact the Tor developers when I have legal questions about Tor or "
"to inform them if I suspect Tor is being used for illegal purposes?"
msgstr ""
"Bör jag kontakta Tors utvecklare när jag har juridiska frågor om Tor eller "
"vill informera dem om att jag misstänker att Tor används för olagliga "
"ändamål?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "Should I run an exit relay from my home?"
msgstr "Bör jag driva ett utgångsrelä hemifrån?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Should I snoop on the plaintext traffic that exits through my Tor relay?"
msgstr "Bör jag avlyssna den okrypterade trafik som lämnar mitt Tor-relä?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "Should I tell my ISP that I'm running an exit relay?"
msgstr ""
"Bör jag berätta för internetleverantören att jag driver ett utgångsrelä?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "Should I use Tor or encourage the use of Tor for illegal purposes?"
msgstr ""
"Bör jag använda Tor eller uppmuntra användning av Tor för olagliga ändamål?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Such inquiries will be kept confidential subject to the limits of the "
"attorney/client privilege."
msgstr ""
"Sådana förfrågningar behandlas konfidentiellt inom gränserna för sekretessen "
"mellan advokat och klient."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "That may attract the attention of private litigants or law enforcement."
msgstr ""
"Det kan dra till sig uppmärksamhet från privata kärande eller "
"brottsbekämpande myndigheter."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project [suggests](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-running-"
"exit-node) the following ways to let others know that you're running an exit "
"relay:"
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project [föreslår](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-running-"
"exit-node) följande sätt att informera andra om att du driver ett "
"utgångsrelä:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project's blog has some excellent [recommendations](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-running-exit-node) for running an exit with as "
"little risk as possible. We suggest that you review their advice before "
"setting up an exit relay."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Projects blogg har utmärkta [rekommendationer](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/blog/tips-running-exit-node) för att driva ett "
"utgångsrelä med så liten risk som möjligt. Läs gärna råden innan du "
"konfigurerar ett relä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"The Tor community maintains a list of ISPs that are particularly Tor-savvy, "
"as well as ones that aren't."
msgstr ""
"Tor-gemenskapen underhåller en lista över internetleverantörer som är "
"särskilt kunniga om Tor och över sådana som inte är det."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Therefore, please do not act on this information alone; if you have any "
"specific legal problems, issues, or questions, seek a complete review of "
"your situation with a lawyer licensed to practice in your jurisdiction."
msgstr ""
"Handla därför inte enbart utifrån den här informationen. Om du har ett "
"specifikt juridiskt problem eller en fråga bör du låta en jurist med "
"behörighet i din jurisdiktion göra en fullständig bedömning av situationen."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"These relays do not directly forward traffic to the Internet and so can't be "
"easily mistaken for the origin of allegedly unlawful content."
msgstr ""
"Reläerna vidarebefordrar inte trafik direkt till internet och kan därför "
"inte lika lätt misstas för ursprunget till innehåll som påstås vara olagligt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"This could mean the difference between having your computer seized by law "
"enforcement and being left alone."
msgstr ""
"Det kan vara skillnaden mellan att brottsbekämpande myndigheter beslagtar "
"datorn och att du lämnas i fred."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"This could result in law enforcement raiding your home, seizing your "
"computer, and suspecting you of criminal activity."
msgstr ""
"Det kan leda till att brottsbekämpande myndigheter gör husrannsakan hemma "
"hos dig, beslagtar datorn och misstänker dig för brott."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"This has resulted in police suspecting Tor relay operators of crimes and "
"sometimes [seizing computer](https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2011/08/why-ip-"
"addresses-alone-dont-identify-criminals) equipment, including Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"Det har lett till att polisen har misstänkt Tor-reläoperatörer för brott och "
"ibland [beslagtagit datorutrustning](https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2011/08/"
"why-ip-addresses-alone-dont-identify-criminals), däribland Tor-reläer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"This way, you'll receive any abuse complaints and can respond to them "
"directly. Otherwise, try to ensure that your ISP forwards abuse complaints "
"that it receives to you."
msgstr ""
"På så sätt får du alla klagomål om missbruk och kan svara direkt. Försök "
"annars se till att internetleverantören vidarebefordrar klagomål som den tar "
"emot till dig."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"This will help ensure that your Internet access isn't cut off due to abuse "
"complaints."
msgstr ""
"Det bidrar till att internetanslutningen inte stängs av på grund av klagomål "
"om missbruk."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"This will help us recognize trends and issues that the lawyers might want to "
"focus on."
msgstr ""
"Det hjälper oss att identifiera trender och frågor som juristerna kan behöva "
"fokusera på."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Though there are important exceptions for certain criminal and intellectual "
"property-based claims, Section 230’s immunity protects online services, such "
"as the Tor network, against a range of laws that might otherwise be used to "
"hold them legally responsible for what others say and do."
msgstr ""
"Även om det finns viktiga undantag för vissa straffrättsliga anspråk och "
"anspråk som rör immateriella rättigheter skyddar immuniteten i Section 230 "
"nättjänster som Tor-nätverket mot flera lagar som annars skulle kunna "
"användas för att hålla dem juridiskt ansvariga för vad andra säger och gör."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"To the extent you do maintain logs, however, you should not disclose them to "
"any third party without first consulting a lawyer."
msgstr ""
"Om du ändå sparar loggar bör du inte lämna ut dem till någon tredje part "
"utan att först rådgöra med en jurist."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"Tor's core developers further reserve the right to refuse a Tor relay "
"operator's request to be listed in their directory or to remove any relay "
"from their directory for any reason."
msgstr ""
"Tors kärnutvecklare förbehåller sig dessutom rätten att avvisa en "
"reläoperatörs begäran om att tas med i katalogen eller att av någon "
"anledning ta bort ett relä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"We believe that running a Tor relay, including an exit relay that allows "
"people to anonymously send and receive traffic, is legal under U.S. law. Law "
"enforcement, however, [often misunderstands](https://www.eff.org/wp/"
"unreliable-informants-ip-addresses-digital-tips-and-police-raids) how Tor "
"works and has occasionally attributed illegal traffic on the network as "
"originating from a Tor exit relay."
msgstr ""
"Vi anser att det är lagligt enligt amerikansk lag att driva ett Tor-relä, "
"inklusive ett exit-relä som gör det möjligt för människor att anonymt skicka "
"och ta emot trafik. Polisen [missförstår](https://www.eff.org/wp/unreliable-"
"informants-ip-addresses-digital-tips-and-police-raids) dock ofta hur Tor "
"fungerar och har ibland tillskrivit olaglig trafik på nätverket som "
"härrörande från ett Tor exit-relä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"We cannot guarantee that you will never face any legal liability as a result "
"of running a Tor relay."
msgstr ""
"Vi kan inte garantera att du aldrig får något juridiskt ansvar till följd av "
"att du driver ett Tor-relä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"While we believe that running an exit relay is legal, it is practically "
"impossible to stop the use of an exit relay for illegal activity."
msgstr ""
"Även om vi anser att det är lagligt att driva ett utgångsrelä är det "
"praktiskt taget omöjligt att hindra att reläet används för olaglig "
"verksamhet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "Will EFF represent me if I get in trouble for running a Tor relay?"
msgstr "Företräder EFF mig om jag får problem för att jag driver ett Tor-relä?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"You can contact info@eff.org if you face a specific legal issue. We will try "
"to assist you, but given EFF's small size, we cannot guarantee that we can "
"help everyone."
msgstr ""
"Kontakta info@eff.org om du får ett specifikt juridiskt problem. Vi försöker "
"hjälpa dig, men eftersom EFF är en liten organisation kan vi inte garantera "
"att alla får hjälp."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"You may receive legal inquiries where you are prohibited by law from telling "
"anyone about the request. We believe that, at least in the United States, "
"such gag orders do not prevent you from talking to a lawyer, including "
"calling a lawyer to find representation."
msgstr ""
"Du kan få juridiska förfrågningar som du enligt lag inte får berätta om. Vi "
"anser att sådana yppandeförbud, åtminstone i USA, inte hindrar dig från att "
"tala med en jurist, exempelvis genom att ringa en advokat för att hitta ett "
"ombud."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid ""
"FAQ written by the Electronic Frontier Foundation (EFF). Last updated March "
"27, 2020."
msgstr ""
"Vanliga frågor skrivna av Electronic Frontier Foundation (EFF). Senast "
"uppdaterade den 27 mars 2020."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/
msgid "The Legal FAQ for Tor Relay Operators"
msgstr "Juridiska vanliga frågor för Tor-reläoperatörer"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"(The Tor Project has an [abuse collection of templates](../../tor-abuse-"
"templates/) to help you respond to other types of abuse complaints, too.)"
msgstr ""
"(The Tor Project har även en [samling svarsmallar för missbruk](../../tor-"
"abuse-templates/) som hjälper dig att svara på andra typer av klagomål.)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Also, if you received this document from anywhere other than the EFF web "
"site or [tor-dmca-response](../tor-dmca-response), it may be out of date."
msgstr ""
"Om du har fått dokumentet från någon annan plats än EFF:s webbplats eller "
"[tor-dmca-response](../tor-dmca-response) kan det dessutom vara inaktuellt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"As you know, the DMCA creates four \"safe harbors\" for service providers to "
"protect them from copyright liability for the acts of their users, when the "
"ISPs fulfill certain requirements. (17 U.S.C. 512)"
msgstr ""
"Som du känner till skapar DMCA fyra säkerhetsundantag för "
"tjänsteleverantörer som skyddar dem från upphovsrättsligt ansvar för "
"användarnas handlingar, under förutsättning att leverantörerna uppfyller "
"vissa krav. (17 U.S.C. 512)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Before sending any response to your ISP, you may want to seek the advice of "
"an attorney licensed to practice in your jurisdiction."
msgstr ""
"Innan du skickar ett svar till internetleverantören kan du vilja rådfråga en "
"jurist som har rätt att verka i din jurisdiktion."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "Dear [ISP]:"
msgstr "Kära [ISP]:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "Follow the link to get the latest version."
msgstr "Följ länken för att få den senaste versionen."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"For these reasons, I am not an infringer of copyright in any materials that "
"are transmitted through the Tor node that I run, either directly or under a "
"theory of contributory or vicarious liability."
msgstr ""
"Av dessa skäl gör jag inte intrång i upphovsrätten till material som "
"överförs genom Tor-noden jag driver, vare sig direkt eller enligt en teori "
"om medverkande eller ställföreträdande ansvar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Fortunately, copyright law should provide protections from many of them both "
"to you and to your upstream provider."
msgstr ""
"Lyckligtvis bör upphovsrätten ge både dig och din överordnade leverantör "
"skydd mot många sådana anspråk."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"I do not select the material transmitted through the Tor node that I run, "
"and I have no practical means of either identifying the source of such "
"material or preventing its transmission."
msgstr ""
"Jag väljer inte materialet som överförs genom Tor-noden jag driver och har "
"ingen praktisk möjlighet att identifiera materialets källa eller förhindra "
"överföringen."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"I do nothing to encourage or promote the use of the Tor network for "
"copyright infringement."
msgstr ""
"Jag gör inget för att uppmuntra eller främja användning av Tor-nätverket för "
"upphovsrättsintrång."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"I hope, as an organization committed to protecting the privacy of its "
"customers, you'll agree that this is a valuable technology."
msgstr ""
"Jag hoppas att ni som organisation med åtagandet att skydda kundernas "
"integritet håller med om att detta är värdefull teknik."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "If not, please contact me with any further questions."
msgstr "Kontakta mig annars gärna om ni har fler frågor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"If you have and implement such a policy, and you otherwise qualify for the "
"safe harbor, you should be free from fear of copyright damages."
msgstr ""
"Om ni har och tillämpar en sådan policy och i övrigt uppfyller kraven för "
"säkerhetsundantaget bör ni inte behöva befara skadestånd för "
"upphovsrättsintrång."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"If you're not comfortable including so much legal explanation, feel free to "
"invite the ISP to contact EFF for a fuller discussion."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte känner dig bekväm med att ta med så mycket juridisk förklaring "
"kan du gärna be internetleverantören kontakta EFF för en utförligare "
"diskussion."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"If your Internet host forwards a copyright complaint to you, you can use "
"this template to write a response, though you will need to customize it to "
"your situation."
msgstr ""
"Om internetvärden vidarebefordrar ett upphovsrättsklagomål till dig kan du "
"använda mallen som utgångspunkt för ett svar, men du måste anpassa den efter "
"din situation."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "In addition, it's up to you to comply with your ISP's terms of service."
msgstr ""
"Du ansvarar dessutom för att följa internetleverantörens användarvillkor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Instead, the \"conduit\" safe harbor of section 512(a) of the DMCA has "
"different and less burdensome eligibility requirements, as the D.C. Circuit "
"Court of Appeals held in RIAA v. Verizon (see https://scholar.google.com/"
"scholar_case?case=15815830240179540527) and the Eighth Circuit Court of "
"Appeals confirmed in RIAA v. Charter (see https://scholar.google.com/"
"scholar_case?case=11547531128234336420)."
msgstr ""
"Säkerhetsundantaget för ”ren vidarebefordran” i avsnitt 512(a) i DMCA har i "
"stället andra och mindre betungande behörighetskrav, vilket "
"appellationsdomstolen för District of Columbia fastställde i RIAA v. Verizon "
"(se https://scholar.google.com/scholar_case?case=15815830240179540527) och "
"appellationsdomstolen för åttonde kretsen bekräftade i RIAA v. Charter (se "
"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_case?case=11547531128234336420)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"It does not host any content. Rather, it is part of a network of nodes on "
"the Internet that simply pass packets among themselves before sending them "
"to their destinations, just as any Internet intermediary does."
msgstr ""
"Noden är inte värd för något innehåll. Den ingår i stället i ett nätverk av "
"noder på internet som endast skickar paket mellan varandra innan de "
"överlämnas till sina mål, precis som andra mellanhänder på internet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Note to Tor relay operators: In this litigious era, anyone providing routing "
"services may face copyright complaints for transmitted content."
msgstr ""
"Till Tor-reläoperatörer: i en tid av många rättsprocesser kan alla som "
"tillhandahåller dirigeringstjänster få upphovsrättsklagomål om överfört "
"innehåll."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "Please also ensure all the statements are true for you."
msgstr "Kontrollera även att alla påståenden stämmer för dig."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Thank you for forwarding me the notice you received from [copyright "
"claimant] regarding [content]. I would like to assure you that I am not "
"hosting the claimed infringing materials, and furthermore, the Digital "
"Millennium Copyright Act's (\"DMCA\") safe harbors likely protect you from "
"liability arising from this complaint. The notice is likely based upon "
"misunderstandings about the law and about some of the software I run."
msgstr ""
"Tack för att ni vidarebefordrade meddelandet från [upphovsrättsinnehavaren] "
"om [innehållet]. Jag vill försäkra er om att jag inte är värd för det "
"material som påstås göra intrång. Digital Millennium Copyright Acts (”DMCA”) "
"säkerhetsundantag skyddar er dessutom sannolikt från ansvar med anledning av "
"klagomålet. Meddelandet bygger troligen på missförstånd av lagen och av viss "
"programvara som jag kör."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Thank you for working with me on this matter. As a loyal subscriber, I "
"appreciate your notifying me of this issue and hope that the protections of "
"DMCA 512 put any concerns you may have to rest."
msgstr ""
"Tack för samarbetet i frågan. Som trogen abonnent uppskattar jag att ni "
"informerade mig och hoppas att skyddet i DMCA 512 undanröjer era eventuella "
"farhågor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"The DMCA's requirements vary depending on the ISP's role. You may be "
"familiar with the \"notice and takedown\" provisions of section 512(c) of "
"the DMCA; however, those do not apply when an ISP merely acts as a conduit."
msgstr ""
"Kraven i DMCA varierar beroende på internetleverantörens roll. Ni känner "
"kanske till bestämmelserna om ”meddelande och borttagning” i avsnitt 512(c) "
"i DMCA. De gäller dock inte när en internetleverantör endast fungerar som "
"vidarebefordrare."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"The copyright notice you received was likely triggered by a program I run "
"called Tor. Tor is network software that helps users to enhance their "
"privacy, security, and safety online."
msgstr ""
"Upphovsrättsmeddelandet som ni fick utlöstes sannolikt av ett program som "
"jag kör och som heter Tor. Tor är nätverksprogramvara som hjälper användare "
"att förbättra sin integritet, säkerhet och trygghet på nätet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"The difference is that Tor tunnels the connections such that no hop can "
"learn both the source and destination of the packets, giving users "
"protection from nefarious snooping on network traffic."
msgstr ""
"Skillnaden är att Tor tunnlar anslutningarna så att inget hopp kan få veta "
"både källan och målet för paketen. Det skyddar användarna mot illvillig "
"avlyssning av nätverkstrafik."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"The result is that, unlike most other Internet traffic, the final IP address "
"that the recipient receives is not the IP address of the sender."
msgstr ""
"Till följd av detta är den slutliga IP-adressen som mottagaren ser, till "
"skillnad från för den mesta andra internettrafiken, inte avsändarens IP-"
"adress."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Therefore, you should continue to be protected under the DMCA 512(a) safe "
"harbor without taking any further action."
msgstr ""
"Ni bör därför även fortsättningsvis skyddas av säkerhetsundantaget i DMCA "
"512(a) utan att vidta några ytterligare åtgärder."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"This template is intended as a starting point, but you should tailor it to "
"your own circumstances."
msgstr ""
"Mallen är avsedd som en utgångspunkt, men du bör anpassa den efter dina "
"omständigheter."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"This template letter is for informational purposes only and does not "
"constitute legal advice."
msgstr ""
"Brevexemplet är endast avsett som information och utgör inte juridisk "
"rådgivning."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Tor protects users against hazards such as harassment, spam, and identity "
"theft. Initial development of Tor, including deployment of a public-use Tor "
"network, was a project of the U.S. Naval Research Laboratory, with funding "
"from ONR and DARPA. (For more on Tor, see https://www.torproject.org/.)"
msgstr ""
"Tor skyddar användare mot risker som trakasserier, skräppost och "
"identitetsstöld. Den inledande utvecklingen av Tor, inklusive "
"driftsättningen av ett offentligt Tor-nätverk, var ett projekt vid U.S. "
"Naval Research Laboratory med finansiering från ONR och DARPA. (Mer "
"information om Tor finns på https://www.torproject.org/.)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Under DMCA 512(a), service providers like you are typically protected from "
"damages for copyright infringement claims if you also maintain \"a policy "
"that provides for termination in appropriate circumstances of subscribers "
"and account holders of the service provider's system or network who are "
"repeat infringers.\""
msgstr ""
"Enligt DMCA 512(a) skyddas tjänsteleverantörer som ni vanligen från "
"skadestånd vid anspråk på upphovsrättsintrång om ni även upprätthåller ”en "
"policy som under lämpliga omständigheter föreskriver avslutande av "
"abonnenter och kontoinnehavare i tjänsteleverantörens system eller nätverk "
"som upprepade gånger gör intrång”."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "Very truly yours,"
msgstr "Med vänlig hälsning,"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Whether and how you should respond when you or your ISP has received a "
"copyright notice will turn on the particular facts of your situation."
msgstr ""
"Om och hur du bör svara när du eller internetleverantören har fått ett "
"upphovsrättsmeddelande beror på de särskilda omständigheterna."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"While the Tor node that I run may appear to be the source of material that "
"is alleged to be copyright-infringing, I do not host that material."
msgstr ""
"Även om Tor-noden jag driver kan se ut att vara källan till material som "
"påstås göra intrång i upphovsrätten är jag inte värd för materialet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid ""
"Written by the Electronic Frontier Foundation ([EFF](https://www.eff.org/)). "
"Last updated March 27, 2020."
msgstr ""
"Skrivet av Electronic Frontier Foundation ([EFF](https://www.eff.org/)). "
"Senast uppdaterat den 27 mars 2020."

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "Your customer, [User]"
msgstr "Er kund, [Användare]"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "Got a DMCA notice? Check out our sample response letter!"
msgstr "Har du fått ett DMCA-meddelande? Läs vårt exempelsvar!"

#: content/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/
msgid "Response template for Tor relay operator to ISP"
msgstr "Svarsmall från Tor-reläoperatör till internetleverantör"

#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
msgid ""
"**Always check the <abbr title=\"Terms of Service\">TOS</abbr> and <abbr "
"title=\"Acceptable Use Policy\">AUP</abbr> before running a relay. They are "
"prone to change and some of this information may be out of date.**"
msgstr ""
"**Kontrollera alltid <abbr title=\"Användarvillkor\">användarvillkoren</"
"abbr> och <abbr title=\"Policy för godtagbar användning\">policyn för "
"godtagbar användning</abbr> innan du driver ett relä. De ändras ofta och en "
"del av informationen kan vara inaktuell.**"

#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "**Try to avoid** the following hosters:"
msgstr "**Försök undvika** följande värdleverantörer:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
msgid ""
"Be sure to provide useful information like how much bandwidth you pushed, "
"whether you thought the deal was cheap or expensive, how hard you had to "
"work to make them understand what's going on, how long your server has been "
"running, and whether you'd recommend them to others. Also include dates."
msgstr ""
"Lämna användbar information, exempelvis hur mycket bandbredd du överförde, "
"om du tyckte att avtalet var billigt eller dyrt, hur svårt det var att få "
"leverantören att förstå situationen, hur länge servern har varit igång och "
"om du skulle rekommendera leverantören till andra. Ta även med datum."

#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
msgid ""
"For network diversity and stronger anonymity, you should avoid providers and "
"countries that already attract a lot of Tor capacity. [Metrics](https://"
"metrics.torproject.org/) is a great tool that allows you to group "
"probabilities by country and AS (autonomous systems), so you can more easily "
"identify networks you want to avoid."
msgstr ""
"För nätverksmångfald och starkare anonymitet bör du undvika leverantörer och "
"länder som redan står för en stor del av Tors kapacitet. [Metrics](https://"
"metrics.torproject.org/) är ett utmärkt verktyg där du kan gruppera "
"sannolikheter efter land och AS (autonoma system) och därmed lättare "
"identifiera nätverk som du vill undvika."

#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
msgid ""
"Since non-exits do not attract complaints, it should be fine to run them "
"without contacting the hoster first. Make sure you understand their policies "
"regarding bandwidth, especially on \"unlimited\" (fair use) contracts. For "
"exit relays, you should read the fine [Tor Exit Guidelines](../tor-exit-"
"guidelines) first."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom reläer som inte är utgångar inte drar till sig klagomål bör det gå "
"bra att köra dem utan att kontakta värdleverantören först. Kontrollera att "
"du förstår leverantörens bandbreddspolicy, särskilt för ”obegränsade” avtal "
"med skälig användning. För utgångsreläer bör du först läsa de utförliga "
"[riktlinjerna för Tor-utgångsreläer](../tor-exit-guidelines)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
msgid "These hosts already have many Tor nodes being hosted there."
msgstr "Dessa värdar har redan många Tor-noder."

#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
msgid ""
"This page aims to list community experiences with Tor and various Internet "
"Service Providers (ISPs) around the world. Some ISPs are Tor-friendly, some "
"are not. Some are competent and clueful about Tor or about security in "
"general. Let us know!"
msgstr ""
"Sidan sammanställer gemenskapens erfarenheter av Tor och olika "
"internetleverantörer världen över. Vissa leverantörer är Tor-vänliga, andra "
"inte. Vissa är kompetenta och kunniga om Tor eller säkerhet i allmänhet. "
"Berätta gärna för oss!"

#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
msgid "Some ISPs are Tor-friendly, some are not"
msgstr "Vissa internetleverantörer är Tor-vänliga, andra inte"

#: content/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/good-bad-isps/
msgid "Good Bad ISPs"
msgstr "Bra och dåliga internetleverantörer"

#: content/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/
msgid "Below, you can find a list of organizations that run relays."
msgstr "Nedan finns en lista över organisationer som driver reläer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/
msgid ""
"Please let us know if you would like your organization to be listed on this "
"page."
msgstr "Meddela oss om du vill att din organisation ska tas med på sidan."

#: content/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/
msgid ""
"Some organizations are dedicated to this purpose only and they are called "
"Relay Associations."
msgstr ""
"Vissa organisationer är helt inriktade på detta och kallas reläföreningar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/
msgid "There are several organizations around the world that run Tor relays."
msgstr "Flera organisationer världen över driver Tor-reläer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/
msgid ""
"Relay associations are independent organizations that runs relays in the Tor "
"network."
msgstr ""
"Reläföreningar är oberoende organisationer som driver reläer i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/relay-associations/
msgid "Relay Associations"
msgstr "Reläföreningar"

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid ""
"(We want to make sure our shirts help outreach happen all around the world, "
"so please understand if we can't send you 5 shirts for your 5 excellent "
"relays.)"
msgstr ""
"(Vi vill att våra tröjor ska bidra till utåtriktat arbete över hela världen, "
"så ha förståelse för att vi kanske inte kan skicka fem tröjor för dina fem "
"utmärkta reläer.)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid ""
"As a thank you, you can earn a Tor t-shirt by contributing in one of these "
"ways:"
msgstr ""
"Som tack kan du förtjäna en Tor-tröja genom att bidra på något av följande "
"sätt:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid ""
"Do research on Tor and anonymity, solve some of our bugs, or establish "
"yourself as a Tor advocate."
msgstr ""
"Forska om Tor och anonymitet, lös några av våra programfel eller etablera "
"dig som Tor-förespråkare."

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid "Help out in other ways. Maintain a translation. Run Tor trainings."
msgstr ""
"Hjälp till på andra sätt. Underhåll en översättning. Håll utbildningar om "
"Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid ""
"If you're operating a fast relay or you've done something else cool, email "
"us at tshirt at torproject.org with the details."
msgstr ""
"Om du driver ett snabbt relä eller har gjort något annat bra kan du skicka "
"informationen till tshirt at torproject.org."

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid "Operate a Tor bridge (webtunnel or obfs4) for at least 3 months."
msgstr "Driv en Tor-bro (WebTunnel eller obfs4) i minst tre månader."

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid "Operate a Tor relay (exit or non-exit) for at least 6 months."
msgstr "Driv ett Tor-relä, med eller utan utgång, i minst sex månader."

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project values the dedication of volunteers who help keep the "
"network strong and open for everyone."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project värdesätter engagemanget hos volontärerna som hjälper till "
"att hålla nätverket starkt och öppet för alla."

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid ""
"There are [a variety of colors, shapes, and sizes](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/community/team/-/wikis/tshirts) available in the "
"great roots design that Leiah Jansen made for us, as well as some older "
"designs."
msgstr ""
"Det finns [flera färger, former och storlekar](https://gitlab.torproject.org/"
"tpo/community/team/-/wikis/tshirts) med den fina rotdesign som Leiah Jansen "
"skapade åt oss, samt några äldre designer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid "Write a good support program and get a lot of people to use it."
msgstr "Skriv ett bra supportprogram och få många att använda det."

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid ""
"If you're operating a fast relay or you've done something else cool, you're "
"eligible to receive our swag."
msgstr ""
"Om du driver ett snabbt relä eller har gjort något annat bra kan du få våra "
"profilprodukter."

#: content/relay/community-resources/swag/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/swag/
msgid "Swag"
msgstr "Profilprodukter"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "<ip>\" https://check.torproject.org/cgi-bin/TorBulkExitList.py"
msgstr "<ip>\" https://check.torproject.org/cgi-bin/TorBulkExitList.py"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "<web server here>."
msgstr "<webbserver här>."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Abuse Scenarios"
msgstr "Missbruksscenarier"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Additionally, if your news reader supports killfiles, you may be interested "
"in using the Tor Bulk Exit list script to download a list of IPs to include "
"in your killfile for posts that match \"NNTP-Posting-Host:"
msgstr ""
"Om din nyhetsläsare stöder killfiler kan du även använda skriptet Tor Bulk "
"Exit List för att hämta en lista med IP-adresser som ska tas med i din "
"killfil för inlägg som matchar ”NNTP-Posting-Host:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Additionally, the Tor project provides an automated DNSRBL for you to query "
"to flag orders coming from Tor nodes as requiring special review: https://"
"www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en"
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project tillhandahåller dessutom en automatisk DNSRBL som du kan "
"fråga för att markera beställningar från Tor-noder som sådana som kräver "
"särskild granskning: https://www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Additionally, the Tor project provides an automated DNSRBL for you to query "
"to flag visitors coming from Tor nodes as requiring special treatment: "
"https://www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project tillhandahåller dessutom en automatisk DNSRBL som du kan "
"fråga för att markera besökare från Tor-noder som sådana som kräver särskild "
"behandling: https://www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"After all has been discussed, offer a follow up conversation within a week. "
"Make sure your agreed upon changes are implemented. Neither the ISP nor "
"Complainant may want to do this, but the fact that you offered is in your "
"credit. This may help them feel \"comfortable\" with you."
msgstr ""
"När allt har diskuterats erbjuder du ett uppföljningssamtal inom en vecka. "
"Kontrollera att de överenskomna ändringarna genomförs. Varken "
"internetleverantören eller den klagande behöver vilja göra det, men "
"erbjudandet talar till din fördel och kan få dem att känna sig tryggare med "
"dig."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"All templates should include the Common Boilerplate below, and append some "
"additional paragraphs depending on the specific Scenario."
msgstr ""
"Alla mallar ska innehålla den gemensamma standardtexten nedan och "
"kompletteras med ytterligare stycken beroende på det aktuella scenariot."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Arrange to talk with or directly email the complainant."
msgstr "Ordna ett samtal med eller skicka e-post direkt till den klagande."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"As can be seen from the overview page, the Tor network is designed to make "
"tracing of users impossible."
msgstr ""
"Som framgår av översiktssidan är Tor-nätverket utformat för att göra det "
"omöjligt att spåra användare."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Before You Start"
msgstr "Innan du börjar"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Below are a collection of letters you can use to respond to your ISP about "
"their complaint in regards to your Tor exit server."
msgstr ""
"Nedan finns en samling brev som du kan använda för att svara "
"internetleverantören på klagomål om din Tor-utgångsserver."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Brute Force Web Attacks"
msgstr "Webbangrepp med råstyrka"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Brute force login attempts can be reduced/slowed by Captchas, which is the "
"approach taken by Gmail for this same problem."
msgstr ""
"Inloggningsförsök med råstyrka kan minskas eller bromsas med CAPTCHA-test, "
"vilket är samma metod som Gmail använder för problemet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Client connections are routed through multiple relays, and are multiplexed "
"together on the connections between relays."
msgstr ""
"Klientanslutningar dirigeras genom flera reläer och multiplexeras "
"tillsammans på anslutningarna mellan reläerna."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Comment/Forum Spam"
msgstr "Skräppost i kommentarer och forum"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Common Boilerplate (Tor Intro)"
msgstr "Gemensam standardtext (introduktion till Tor)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Contacting this address will give you better luck at actually having this "
"abuser's Google Groups account canceled than will chasing down Tor nodes, "
"proxies, and open wireless access points."
msgstr ""
"Det är större chans att missbrukarens Google Groups-konto faktiskt stängs om "
"du kontaktar adressen än om du försöker spåra Tor-noder, proxyservrar och "
"öppna trådlösa åtkomstpunkter."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Did you contact their abuse department?"
msgstr "Kontaktade du deras missbruksavdelning?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Discuss options. Options that have been offered to relay operators:"
msgstr ""
"Diskutera alternativen. Följande alternativ har erbjudits reläoperatörer:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "DoS Attacks and Scraping Robots"
msgstr "DoS-angrepp och insamlingsrobotar"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "During the conversation make sure you explain a few points:"
msgstr "Se till att förklara några punkter under samtalet:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "E-Commerce Fraud"
msgstr "Bedrägerier inom e-handel"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Feel free to improve them if you feel they fall short of this goal."
msgstr "Förbättra dem gärna om du anser att de inte uppfyller målet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"For serious incidents, traditional police work techniques of running stings "
"and investigating to determine means, motive, and opportunity are still very "
"effective."
msgstr ""
"Vid allvarliga incidenter är traditionellt polisarbete med kontrollerade "
"insatser och utredningar av medel, motiv och tillfälle fortfarande mycket "
"effektivt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Format and Philosophy of Templates"
msgstr "Mallarnas format och filosofi"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Google Groups Spam"
msgstr "Skräppost i Google Groups"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Hacked Gmail, Web Forum, or Misc Account Access"
msgstr "Kapade Gmail-konton, webbforum eller andra konton"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Hacking (PHP Webshells, XSS, SQL Injection)"
msgstr "Hackning (PHP-webbskal, XSS, SQL-injektion)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"However, be aware that this may be just one jerk amongst many legitimate Tor "
"users who use your forums."
msgstr ""
"Tänk dock på att det kan röra sig om en enda besvärlig person bland många "
"legitima Tor-användare på forumet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"However, it is possible that your rate limiting alarms simply experienced a "
"false positive due to the amount of traffic that flows through the router."
msgstr ""
"Det är dock möjligt att larmen för hastighetsbegränsning endast gav ett "
"falskt positivt resultat på grund av trafikmängden som går genom routern."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"However, rather than banning legitimate Tor users from using your service in "
"general, we recommend ensuring that such services are updated and maintained "
"to free of vulnerabilities that can lead to situations such as this (PHP "
"webshell/XSS compromise/SQL Injection compromise)."
msgstr ""
"I stället för att generellt förbjuda legitima Tor-användare från tjänsten "
"rekommenderar vi att tjänsterna uppdateras och underhålls så att de inte har "
"sårbarheter som kan leda till sådana situationer, exempelvis kompromettering "
"genom PHP-webbskal, XSS eller SQL-injektion."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"However, we still recommend using the general approach, as the attack will "
"likely simply reappear from an open proxy or other IP once Tor is blocked."
msgstr ""
"Vi rekommenderar ändå den allmänna metoden, eftersom angreppet sannolikt "
"bara återkommer från en öppen proxy eller annan IP-adress när Tor har "
"blockerats."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"If a serious abuse complaint not covered by this template set arrives, the "
"best answer is to follow a pattern with the complaining party."
msgstr ""
"Om ett allvarligt klagomål om missbruk som inte omfattas av mallarna kommer "
"in är det bästa svaret att följa ett återkommande mönster med den klagande "
"parten."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"If it is in fact a serious problem specific to Tor, the Tor project provides "
"an automated DNSRBL for you to query to block login attempts coming from Tor "
"nodes: https://www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en"
msgstr ""
"Om det verkligen är ett allvarligt problem som är specifikt för Tor "
"tillhandahåller The Tor Project en automatisk DNSRBL som du kan fråga för "
"att blockera inloggningsförsök från Tor-noder: https://www.torproject.org/"
"projects/tordnsel.html.en"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"If the attack is real and ongoing, however, the Tor project provides an "
"automated DNSRBL for you to query to block login attempts coming from Tor "
"nodes: https://www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en"
msgstr ""
"Om angreppet är verkligt och pågår tillhandahåller The Tor Project en "
"automatisk DNSRBL som du kan fråga för att blockera inloggningsförsök från "
"Tor-noder: https://www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"If this fails, DoS attempts can also be solved with iptables-based rate "
"limiting solutions, load balancers such as nginx, and also IPS devices, but "
"be aware that Internet traffic is not always uniform in quantity by IP, due "
"to large corporate and even national outproxies, NATs, and services like Tor."
msgstr ""
"Om detta misslyckas kan DoS-försök också lösas med iptables-baserade "
"lösningar för hastighetsbegränsning, lastbalanserare som nginx och även IPS-"
"enheter, men var medveten om att internettrafiken inte alltid är enhetlig i "
"kvantitet per IP, på grund av stora företags och till och med nationella "
"outproxies, NATs och tjänster som Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"If you are concerned about SSH scans, you might consider running your SSHD "
"on a port other than the default of 22."
msgstr ""
"Om SSH-skanningar oroar dig kan du överväga att köra SSHD på en annan port "
"än standardporten 22."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In addition, our nodes do not allow SMTP traffic to be sent using our IPs."
msgstr ""
"Våra noder tillåter dessutom inte att SMTP-trafik skickas från våra IP-"
"adresser."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In fact, Google provides a free Captcha service, complete with code for easy "
"inclusion in a number of systems to help other sites deal"
msgstr ""
"Google tillhandahåller faktiskt en kostnadsfri CAPTCHA-tjänst med kod som "
"enkelt kan integreras i flera system för att hjälpa andra webbplatser att "
"hantera"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In fact, Google provides a free Captcha service, complete with code for easy "
"inclusion in a number of systems to help other sites deal with this issue: "
"https://code.google.com/apis/recaptcha/intro.html"
msgstr ""
"Google tillhandahåller faktiskt en kostnadsfri CAPTCHA-tjänst med kod som "
"enkelt kan integreras i flera system för att hjälpa andra webbplatser att "
"hantera problemet: https://code.google.com/apis/recaptcha/intro.html"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In fact, all [objective evidence](http://boingboing.net/2011/08/12/south-"
"korea-to-abandon-real-name-internet-policy.html) seems to indicate that it "
"has only created new markets for organized crime to preside over."
msgstr ""
"Alla [objektiva belägg](http://boingboing.net/2011/08/12/south-korea-to-"
"abandon-real-name-internet-policy.html) tyder faktiskt på att det endast har "
"skapat nya marknader som den organiserade brottsligheten kan kontrollera."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In fact, in my experience, the fraud processing teams contracted by many "
"ISPs simply mark all requests from Tor nodes as fraud using that very list."
msgstr ""
"Min erfarenhet är faktiskt att bedrägerigrupper som anlitas av många "
"internetleverantörer helt enkelt märker alla begäranden från Tor-noder som "
"bedrägerier med just den listan."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In general however, we believe that problems like this are best solved by "
"improving the service to defend against the attack from the Internet at "
"large."
msgstr ""
"Vi anser dock generellt att sådana problem bäst löses genom att förbättra "
"tjänsten så att den kan försvara sig mot angreppet från internet i stort."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In general, we believe that problems like this are best solved by improving "
"the service to defend against the attack from the Internet at large rather "
"than specifically tailoring behavior for Tor."
msgstr ""
"Vi anser generellt att sådana problem bäst löses genom att förbättra "
"tjänsten så att den försvarar sig mot angreppet från internet i stort, i "
"stället för att anpassa beteendet särskilt för Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In general, we believe that problems like this are best solved by improving "
"your service to defend against the attack from the Internet at large."
msgstr ""
"Vi anser generellt att sådana problem bäst löses genom att förbättra "
"tjänsten så att den kan försvara sig mot angreppet från internet i stort."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In many cases, your ISP will be involved as a conduit for the 3rd party "
"complainant. Your ISP wants to know:"
msgstr ""
"I många fall fungerar internetleverantören som mellanhand för den klagande "
"tredje parten. Internetleverantören vill veta:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"In serious cases, such as harassment email or death threats, it is often "
"helpful to draw an analogy to situations in the physical world where an "
"action is perpetrated by an anonymous individual (such as delivering the "
"notice via postal mail)."
msgstr ""
"I allvarliga fall, till exempel trakasserier via e-post eller dödshot, är "
"det ofta bra att dra en parallell till situationer i den fysiska världen där "
"en anonym person begår handlingen, exempelvis genom att skicka meddelandet "
"per post."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Inspecting the headers reveals that the abuse complaint address for Google "
"Groups is groups-abuse@google.com."
msgstr ""
"En granskning av huvudena visar att adressen för att anmäla missbruk i "
"Google Groups är groups-abuse@google.com."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"It also provides a Bulk Exit List service for retrieving the entire list: "
"https://check.torproject.org/cgi-bin/TorBulkExitList.py"
msgstr ""
"Tjänsten erbjuder även Tor Bulk Exit List för att hämta hela listan: https://"
"check.torproject.org/cgi-bin/TorBulkExitList.py"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"It appears that your specific abuse complaint was generated by an "
"authenticated Google Groups user."
msgstr ""
"Det verkar som om klagomålet om missbruk skapades av en autentiserad Google "
"Groups-användare."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "It has also been reviewed by someone who works in Abuse at a major ISP."
msgstr ""
"Texten har även granskats av någon som arbetar med missbruksärenden hos en "
"stor internetleverantör."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"It is also possible to download a list of all Tor exit IPs that will connect "
"to your SSH port: https://check.torproject.org/cgi-bin/TorBulkExitList.py?"
"ip=YOUR_IP&port=22"
msgstr ""
"Det går även att hämta en lista över alla Tor-utgångs-IP-adresser som kan "
"ansluta till din SSH-port: https://check.torproject.org/cgi-bin/"
"TorBulkExitList.py?ip=YOUR_IP&port=22"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"It is also possible to download a list of all Tor exit IPs that will connect "
"to your server port:"
msgstr ""
"Det går även att hämta en lista över alla Tor-utgångs-IP-adresser som kan "
"ansluta till serverporten:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"It was written by someone with experience working with various ISPs who had "
"issues with a Tor exit node on their network."
msgstr ""
"Texten skrevs av någon med erfarenhet av att arbeta med olika "
"internetleverantörer som hade problem med ett Tor-utgångsrelä i sitt nätverk."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Many worms, scanners, and botnets scan the entire Internet looking for SSH "
"logins."
msgstr ""
"Många maskar, skannrar och botnät skannar hela internet efter SSH-"
"inloggningar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Other Template Sets"
msgstr "Andra uppsättningar mallar"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Our recommendation is to treat this event as though there was a login from "
"an open wireless access point in your city. Reset your password, and if you "
"don't have antivirus already, download the free AVG: http://free.avg.com/us-"
"en/download, Spybot SD: https://www.safer-networking.org/, and/or AdAware: "
"http://www.lavasoft.com/?domain=lavasoftusa.com."
msgstr ""
"Vi rekommenderar att du behandlar händelsen som en inloggning från en öppen "
"trådlös åtkomstpunkt i din stad. Återställ lösenordet. Om du inte redan har "
"antivirus kan du hämta kostnadsfria AVG: http://free.avg.com/us-en/download, "
"Spybot SD: https://www.safer-networking.org/ och/eller AdAware: http://"
"www.lavasoft.com/?domain=lavasoftusa.com."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "PHP Relay or Exploited Webmail Account Spam"
msgstr "Skräppost via PHP-relä eller komprometterat webbaserat e-postkonto"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Please see [Tips for Running an Exit Node with Minimal Harassment](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/tips-running-exit-node) and [Tor Exit Guidelines](../tor-"
"exit-guidelines/) for more info, before reading this document."
msgstr ""
"Läs [Tips for Running an Exit Node with Minimal Harassment](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/tips-running-exit-node) och [riktlinjerna för Tor-"
"utgångsreläer](../tor-exit-guidelines/) innan du läser dokumentet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Read the [Tor Overview](https://2019.www.torproject.org/about/"
"overview.html.en). Be prepared to summarize and answer basic questions. "
"Assume the person with whom you're going to converse knows nothing about "
"Tor. Assume this same person isn't going to trust anything you say."
msgstr ""
"Läs [översikten över Tor](https://2019.www.torproject.org/about/"
"overview.html.en). Var beredd att sammanfatta och svara på grundläggande "
"frågor. Utgå från att personen du ska tala med inte vet något om Tor och "
"inte kommer att lita på det du säger."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Remind them that traditional policework can still be used to determine who "
"had the means, motive, and opportunity to commit the crime."
msgstr ""
"Påminn om att traditionellt polisarbete fortfarande kan användas för att "
"fastställa vem som hade medel, motiv och tillfälle att begå brottet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "SSH Bruteforce Attempts"
msgstr "SSH-försök med råstyrka"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Scraping and robot activity can be reduced/slowed by Captchas, which is the "
"approach taken by Gmail for this same problem."
msgstr ""
"Insamling och robotaktivitet kan minskas eller bromsas med CAPTCHA-test, "
"vilket är samma metod som Gmail använder för problemet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "See https://www.torproject.org/about/torusers.html.en for more info."
msgstr ""
"Mer information finns på https://www.torproject.org/about/torusers.html.en."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Slow DoS attacks [aimed to consume the Apache MaxClients limit](http://"
"www.guerilla-ciso.com/archives/2049) can be alleviated by reducing the "
"httpd.conf TimeOut and KeepAliveTimeout config values to 15-30 and raising "
"the ServerLimit and MaxClients values to something like 3000."
msgstr ""
"Långsamma DoS-angrepp [som försöker förbruka Apaches MaxClients-gräns]"
"(http://www.guerilla-ciso.com/archives/2049) kan lindras genom att minska "
"konfigurationsvärdena TimeOut och KeepAliveTimeout i httpd.conf till 15–30 "
"och höja ServerLimit och MaxClients till exempelvis 3000."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"So it is even possible this is a legitimate order, but was flagged as fraud "
"solely based on IP, especially if you contract out fraud detection to a "
"third party."
msgstr ""
"Det kan alltså vara en legitim beställning som har markerats som bedrägeri "
"enbart på grund av IP-adressen, särskilt om bedrägeriidentifieringen har "
"lagts ut på en tredje part."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "The IP address in question is a Tor exit node."
msgstr "IP-adressen i fråga tillhör ett Tor-utgångsrelä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The ISP is not at fault and not liable for your actions. This is normally "
"the case, but the poor abuse person dealing with the issues just wants to "
"hear it isn't the ISPs problem. They will move on after they are comfortable."
msgstr ""
"Internetleverantören har inte gjort något fel och ansvarar inte för dina "
"handlingar. Så är det vanligen, men den person som hanterar missbruksärendet "
"vill bara höra att problemet inte är internetleverantörens. När personen "
"känner sig trygg med det går den vidare."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The ISP/Complainant demands you disable Tor. You may want a new ISP as a "
"result."
msgstr ""
"Internetleverantören eller den klagande kräver att du inaktiverar Tor. Det "
"kan vara ett skäl att byta internetleverantör."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The ISP/Complainant may suggest you convert to a non-exit node. In this "
"case, you may want to counter with a reduced exit policy, such as the one "
"suggested in [item #6 of the above blog post](https://blog.torproject.org/"
"tips-running-exit-node)."
msgstr ""
"Internetleverantören eller den klagande kan föreslå att du omvandlar reläet "
"till ett relä utan utgång. Du kan då föreslå en begränsad utgångspolicy, "
"till exempel den i [punkt 6 i blogginlägget ovan](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/tips-running-exit-node)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The ISP/Complainant may very well demand to see logfiles. Fortunately, by "
"default, nothing sensitive is disclosed. You may want a new ISP if they "
"demand access to log files ad hoc."
msgstr ""
"Internetleverantören eller den klagande kan kräva att få se loggfiler. "
"Lyckligtvis lämnas som standard inget känsligt ut. Om leverantören "
"godtyckligt kräver åtkomst till loggarna kan du vilja byta leverantör."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The ISP/Complainant states they will firewall off the traffic on the default "
"ports. You may want a new ISP as a result."
msgstr ""
"Internetleverantören eller den klagande uppger att trafiken på "
"standardportarna kommer att blockeras med brandvägg. Det kan vara ett skäl "
"att byta internetleverantör."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The Tor Project provides an automated DNSRBL for you to query to flag posts "
"coming from Tor nodes as requiring special review."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project tillhandahåller en automatisk DNSRBL som du kan fråga för "
"att markera inlägg från Tor-noder som sådana som kräver särskild granskning."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The Tor network is run by some 5000 volunteers who use the free software "
"provided by the Tor Project to run Tor routers."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverket drivs av omkring 5 000 volontärer som använder den fria "
"programvaran från The Tor Project för att köra Tor-routrar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The Tor project does provide an automated DNSRBL for you to query to flag "
"requests from Tor nodes as requiring special treatment: https://"
"www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en"
msgstr ""
"The Tor Project tillhandahåller en automatisk DNSRBL som du kan fråga för "
"att markera begäranden från Tor-noder som sådana som kräver särskild "
"behandling: https://www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The attacker would probably just chain an open proxy after Tor, or just use "
"open wireless and/or a proxy without Tor."
msgstr ""
"Angriparen skulle sannolikt bara lägga en öppen proxy efter Tor eller "
"använda ett öppet trådlöst nätverk och/eller en proxy utan Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The best way to handle abuse complaints is to set up your exit node so that "
"they are less likely to be sent in the first place."
msgstr ""
"Det bästa sättet att hantera klagomål om missbruk är att konfigurera "
"utgångsreläet så att de från början blir mindre sannolika."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The common boilerplate should be abridged or be omitted if the abuse "
"complainant is already familiar with Tor."
msgstr ""
"Den gemensamma standardtexten bör förkortas eller utelämnas om den klagande "
"redan känner till Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The difference between the proactive approach and the reactive approach to "
"abuse is the difference between decentralized fault-tolerant Internet "
"freedom, and fragile, corruptible totalitarian control."
msgstr ""
"Skillnaden mellan ett proaktivt och ett reaktivt sätt att hantera missbruk "
"är skillnaden mellan decentraliserad, feltålig internetfrihet och bräcklig, "
"korrumperbar totalitär kontroll."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The fact that a few logins happened to come from Tor is likely a small blip "
"on your overall login attempt rate."
msgstr ""
"Att några inloggningar råkade komma från Tor är sannolikt bara en mycket "
"liten del av den totala frekvensen av inloggningsförsök."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The following scenario-specific paragraphs should be appended to the Common "
"Boilerplate paragraphs above."
msgstr ""
"Följande scenariespecifika stycken ska läggas till efter den gemensamma "
"standardtexten ovan."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The general format of these templates is to inform the complainant about "
"Tor, to help them to find a solution to their particular issue that works in "
"general for the Internet at large (open wifi, open proxies, botnets, etc), "
"and barring all else, how to block Tor."
msgstr ""
"Mallarnas allmänna format är att informera den klagande om Tor, hjälpa till "
"att hitta en lösning på det specifika problemet som fungerar för internet i "
"stort – öppet Wi-Fi, öppna proxyservrar, botnät och så vidare – och, om "
"inget annat fungerar, beskriva hur Tor blockeras."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The philosophy of the Tor Project is that abuse should be handled "
"proactively by the site administrators, rather than wasting effort and "
"resources on seeking vengeance and chasing ghosts."
msgstr ""
"The Tor Projects filosofi är att webbplatsadministratörer bör hantera "
"missbruk proaktivt i stället för att slösa arbete och resurser på hämnd och "
"spökjakt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"The same list is available through the Tor Bulk Exit List: https://"
"check.torproject.org/cgi-bin/TorBulkExitList.py"
msgstr ""
"Samma lista finns via Tor Bulk Exit List: https://check.torproject.org/cgi-"
"bin/TorBulkExitList.py"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "The system does not record logs of client connections or previous hops."
msgstr "Systemet loggar inte klientanslutningar eller tidigare hopp."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "There is little we can do to trace this matter further."
msgstr "Vi kan inte göra särskilt mycket för att spåra frågan vidare."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "This also does not mean that there is nothing that can be done."
msgstr "Det betyder inte heller att inget kan göras."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "This does not mean that nothing can be done, however."
msgstr "Det betyder dock inte att inget kan göras."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"This is because the Tor network is a censorship resistance, privacy, and "
"anonymity system used by whistle blowers, journalists, Chinese dissidents "
"skirting the Great Firewall, abuse victims, stalker targets, the US "
"military, and law enforcement, just to name a few."
msgstr ""
"Det beror på att Tor-nätverket är ett system för censurmotstånd, integritet "
"och anonymitet som används av bland andra visselblåsare, journalister, "
"kinesiska dissidenter som kringgår den stora brandväggen, offer för "
"övergrepp, personer som utsätts för stalkning, den amerikanska militären och "
"brottsbekämpande myndigheter."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "This is not legal advice."
msgstr "Detta är inte juridisk rådgivning."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"This is the core idea that these abuse complaint templates attempt to instil "
"in the recipient."
msgstr ""
"Detta är den grundläggande tanke som svarsmallarna försöker förmedla till "
"mottagaren."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "This was not written or reviewed by a lawyer."
msgstr "Texten har inte skrivits eller granskats av en jurist."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Threats of Violence (Advice for Real-Time Discussion)"
msgstr "Våldshot (råd för samtal i realtid)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"To further preach to the choir, the identity-based Internet \"driver's "
"licenses\" of South Korea and China have done nothing to curtail cybercrime "
"and Internet abuse."
msgstr ""
"För att ytterligare predika för de redan övertygade: Sydkoreas och Kinas "
"identitetsbaserade ”körkort” för internet har inte gjort något för att "
"begränsa nätbrott eller missbruk av internet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"To help protect yourself while using open wireless, use [HTTPS](https://"
"support.torproject.org/glossary/#https) and encourage the site maintainers "
"to support HTTPS logins."
msgstr ""
"Skydda dig när du använder öppna trådlösa nätverk genom att använda [HTTPS]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/glossary/#https) och uppmuntra "
"webbplatsunderhållarna att stödja HTTPS-inloggningar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Torservers [response template emails](https://www.torservers.net/wiki/abuse/"
"templates)."
msgstr ""
"Torservers [svarsmallar för e-post](https://www.torservers.net/wiki/abuse/"
"templates)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, some people misuse the network. However, compared to the rate "
"of legitimate use (the IP range in question processes nearly a gigabit of "
"traffic per second), [abuse complaints are rare](https://"
"support.torproject.org/abuse/)."
msgstr ""
"Tyvärr missbrukar vissa människor nätverket. Jämfört med den legitima "
"användningen – det aktuella IP-intervallet hanterar nästan en gigabit trafik "
"per sekund – är [klagomål om missbruk sällsynta](https://"
"support.torproject.org/abuse/)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Update the config to disallow traffic to a certain IP range from your exit "
"node. You may want to suggest the complainant use the [Tor DNS RBL](https://"
"2019.www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en) instead."
msgstr ""
"Ändra konfigurationen så att utgångsreläet inte tillåter trafik till ett "
"visst IP-intervall. Du kan föreslå att den klagande i stället använder [Tor "
"DNS RBL](https://2019.www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Upon investigation, it appears that the source of the spam is due to an "
"abusive or compromised webmail gateway running at:"
msgstr ""
"Undersökningen visar att skräpposten verkar komma från en webbaserad e-"
"postgateway som missbrukas eller har komprometterats och körs på:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"Use these to scan to check for keyloggers or spyware that someone with "
"access to your computer may have installed."
msgstr ""
"Använd programmen för att skanna efter tangentloggare eller spionprogram som "
"någon med tillgång till datorn kan ha installerat."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"We provide service to almost a gigabit of traffic per second, 98% of which "
"is web traffic."
msgstr ""
"Vi tillhandahåller nästan en gigabit trafik per sekund, varav 98 procent är "
"webbtrafik."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"We're sorry your account has been brute forced. We can try to prevent our "
"node from connecting to this site, but since the Tor network has 800 or so "
"exits, doing so wouldn't really stop the action long term."
msgstr ""
"Vi beklagar att ditt konto har utsatts för råstyrka. Vi kan försöka hindra "
"vår nod från att ansluta till webbplatsen, men eftersom Tor-nätverket har "
"omkring 800 utgångar skulle det inte stoppa beteendet på lång sikt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "We're sorry your site is experiencing this heavy load from Tor."
msgstr ""
"Vi beklagar att webbplatsen utsätts för den stora belastningen från Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"With respect to your account, given that the attacker used Tor and not a "
"large botnet (or your machine's IP itself), it is likely that your password "
"was either harvested off of your machine from a keylogger, or it was "
"captured via a kiosk, or from open wireless."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom angriparen använde Tor i stället för ett stort botnät eller din "
"egen dators IP-adress är det sannolikt att lösenordet hämtades från datorn "
"av en tangentloggare, fångades på en offentlig dator eller avlyssnades via "
"ett öppet trådlöst nätverk."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"You are a competent server administrator and can address the issue. "
"Minimally, you can at least discuss and respond to the issue intelligently."
msgstr ""
"Du är en kompetent serveradministratör och kan hantera problemet. Du kan "
"åtminstone diskutera och bemöta det på ett kunnigt sätt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"You are a responsible server operator and concerned about the complainant's "
"problem."
msgstr ""
"Du är en ansvarsfull serveroperatör och bryr dig om den klagandes problem."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"You are not insane.  You may be insane, but we don't want the complainant to "
"guess this is true."
msgstr ""
"Du är inte galen. Du kanske är galen, men vi vill inte att den klagande ska "
"ana att det stämmer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "You are not the perpetrator of the issue."
msgstr "Du är inte den som har orsakat problemet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"You can also use this DNSRBL to only allow Tor IPs to read but not post "
"comments: https://www.torproject.org/projects/tordnsel.html.en"
msgstr ""
"Du kan även använda DNSRBL-tjänsten för att endast låta Tor-IP-adresser läsa "
"men inte publicera kommentarer: https://www.torproject.org/projects/"
"tordnsel.html.en"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "You can use this list to create iptables rules to block the network."
msgstr ""
"Du kan använda listan för att skapa iptables-regler som blockerar nätverket."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"You can use this list to help you take a closer look at Tor orders, or to "
"hold them temporarily for additional verification, without losing legitimate "
"customers."
msgstr ""
"Du kan använda listan för att granska beställningar från Tor närmare eller "
"hålla dem tillfälligt för ytterligare verifiering utan att förlora legitima "
"kunder."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"You might also consider a rate limiting solution: https://kvz.io/blog/"
"2007/07/28/block-brute-force-attacks-with-iptables/"
msgstr ""
"Du kan även överväga en lösning för hastighetsbegränsning: https://kvz.io/"
"blog/2007/07/28/block-brute-force-attacks-with-iptables/"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"You might have luck getting rid of this jerk by temporarily limiting account "
"creation to require Gmail accounts before posting, or by requiring account "
"creation be done over non-Tor before posting."
msgstr ""
"Du kanske kan bli av med den besvärliga personen genom att tillfälligt kräva "
"Gmail-konton för att skapa konton och publicera, eller kräva att kontot "
"skapas utan Tor innan publicering tillåts."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Your server is not a spam relay."
msgstr "Servern är inte ett skräppostrelä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Your server is not a trojan/zombie."
msgstr "Servern är inte en trojan eller zombie."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Your server is not compromised."
msgstr "Servern är inte komprometterad."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid ""
"[DMCA Response template for Tor node maintainer to ISP](../eff-tor-legal-"
"faq/) as written by the [EFF](http://www.eff.org)."
msgstr ""
"[DMCA-svarsmall från en Tor-nodoperatör till internetleverantören](../eff-"
"tor-legal-faq/), skriven av [EFF](http://www.eff.org)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "with this issue: https://code.google.com/apis/recaptcha/intro.html"
msgstr "med problemet: https://code.google.com/apis/recaptcha/intro.html"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "How to handle abuse complaints"
msgstr "Hantera klagomål om missbruk"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/
msgid "Tor Abuse Templates"
msgstr "Tors svarsmallar för missbruk"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"\"Cybercrime\" people actually love it when you offer to [teach them about "
"Tor and the Internet](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/talking-german-police-"
"stuttgart) -- they're typically overwhelmed by their jobs and don't have "
"enough background to know where to start."
msgstr ""
"Personer som arbetar med ”nätbrott” uppskattar faktiskt när du erbjuder dig "
"att [lära dem om Tor och internet](https://blog.torproject.org/blog/talking-"
"german-police-stuttgart). De är ofta överhopade av arbete och saknar "
"tillräcklig bakgrund för att veta var de ska börja."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "1. Ask if the ISP is okay with a Tor exit"
msgstr "1. Fråga om internetleverantören godkänner ett Tor-utgångsrelä"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"2. If they come back positively, ask them if they are OK with an IP range "
"reassignment."
msgstr ""
"2. Om svaret är positivt frågar du om de godkänner att ett IP-intervall "
"omfördelas."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"A disclaimer helps give people the right idea about what is behind the "
"traffic coming from these IPs."
msgstr ""
"En ansvarsfriskrivning hjälper människor att förstå vad trafiken från IP-"
"adresserna beror på."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"A good ISP is one that offers cheap bandwidth and is not being used by other "
"members of the Tor community."
msgstr ""
"En bra internetleverantör erbjuder billig bandbredd och används inte redan "
"av andra i Tor-gemenskapen."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"A simple notice can be published without a separate webserver using Tor's "
"\"DirPortFrontPage \" directive."
msgstr ""
"Ett enkelt meddelande kan publiceras utan en separat webbserver med Tors "
"direktiv ”DirPortFrontPage”."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"ARIN uses [SWIP](https://www.arin.net/resources/request/reassignments.html), "
"and RIPE uses something similar."
msgstr ""
"ARIN använder [SWIP](https://www.arin.net/resources/request/"
"reassignments.html), och RIPE använder något liknande."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Also read [How do I make my University / ISP / etc happy with my exit node?]"
"(../tor-relay-universities/)"
msgstr ""
"Läs även [Hur gör jag universitetet, internetleverantören eller liknande "
"nöjda med mitt utgångsrelä?](../tor-relay-universities/)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Also, if they do get a report about your relay, they'll think of you as a "
"helpful expert rather than a potential criminal."
msgstr ""
"Om de senare får en rapport om reläet ser de dig dessutom som en hjälpsam "
"expert i stället för en möjlig brottsling."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Another benefit of an association-like structure is that it might still work "
"even when you leave, if you manage to find successors."
msgstr ""
"En annan fördel med en föreningsliknande struktur är att verksamheten kan "
"fortsätta när du lämnar den, om du lyckas hitta efterträdare."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Answer to abuse complaints in a professional manner within a reasonable time "
"span."
msgstr "Besvara klagomål om missbruk professionellt och inom rimlig tid."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Answering complaints"
msgstr "Besvara klagomål"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"At least law enforcement in Germany regularly uses the fax and phone numbers "
"present in IP records."
msgstr ""
"Åtminstone tyska brottsbekämpande myndigheter använder regelbundet fax- och "
"telefonnumren i IP-registren."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"At least most western countries should have regulations that exclude "
"communication service providers from liability."
msgstr ""
"Åtminstone de flesta västländer bör ha regler som undantar "
"kommunikationstjänsteleverantörer från ansvar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Before you continue, you may ask the Tor community if your choice is a good "
"one."
msgstr "Innan du fortsätter kan du fråga Tor-gemenskapen om ditt val är bra."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Consider preemptively teaching your local law enforcement about Tor."
msgstr ""
"Överväg att i förväg informera de lokala brottsbekämpande myndigheterna om "
"Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Consider using the Reduced Exit Policy."
msgstr "Överväg att använda den begränsade utgångspolicyn."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Contacting them gives you a chance to teach them why Tor is useful to the "
"world (and why it's [not particularly helpful to criminals](https://"
"2019.www.torproject.org/docs/faq-abuse#WhatAboutCriminals))."
msgstr ""
"Genom att kontakta dem får du möjlighet att förklara varför Tor är nyttigt "
"för världen och varför det [inte är särskilt användbart för brottslingar]"
"(https://2019.www.torproject.org/docs/faq-abuse#WhatAboutCriminals)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Depending on the chosen form, setting up a legal body might help with "
"liability, and in general, it helps to appear bigger than you are (and less "
"likely to get raided)."
msgstr ""
"Beroende på vilken form du väljer kan en juridisk person hjälpa i "
"ansvarsfrågor. Generellt hjälper den dig även att framstå som större än du "
"är och mindre sannolik att utsättas för en razzia."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Disk encryption might be useful to protect your node keys, but on the other "
"hand, unencrypted machines are easier to \"audit\" if required. We feel it's "
"best to be able to easily show that you do Tor exiting, and nothing else (on "
"that IP or server)."
msgstr ""
"Diskkryptering kan vara användbart för att skydda nodens nycklar. Å andra "
"sidan är okrypterade datorer enklare att granska om det krävs. Vi anser att "
"det bästa är att enkelt kunna visa att du endast driver en Tor-utgång och "
"inget annat på IP-adressen eller servern."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Find Tor-friendly ISPs."
msgstr "Hitta Tor-vänliga internetleverantörer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Find some professors (or deans!) who like the idea of supporting and/or "
"researching anonymity on the Internet."
msgstr ""
"Hitta några professorer eller dekaner som uppskattar idén att stödja och/"
"eller forska om anonymitet på internet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Germany: [DDG § 7](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/ddg/__7.html) and "
"[Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-"
"content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A32022R2065#d1e2043-1-1)"
msgstr ""
"Tyskland: [DDG § 7](https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/ddg/__7.html) och "
"[artikel 4 i förordning (EU) 2022/2065](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-"
"content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A32022R2065#d1e2043-1-1)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Handling abuse complaints"
msgstr "Hantera klagomål om missbruk"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Hosting"
msgstr "Värdtjänst"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Ideally, use addresses that are not trusted by the IP-based authentication "
"many library-related services use -- if the university's entire IP address "
"space is \"trusted\" to access these library resources, the university is "
"forced to maintain an iron grip on all its addresses."
msgstr ""
"Använd helst adresser som inte är betrodda av den IP-baserade autentisering "
"som många biblioteksrelaterade tjänster använder. Om universitetets hela IP-"
"adressutrymme är ”betrott” för åtkomst till biblioteksresurserna tvingas "
"universitetet hålla ett järngrepp om alla adresser."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If not, you can still explain that you are a non-profit superb large "
"organization filled with security professionals, and that all will be good, "
"and why IP reassignment helps reduce their workload."
msgstr ""
"Om inte kan du fortfarande förklara att ni är en stor och utmärkt ideell "
"organisation fylld av säkerhetsexperter, att allt kommer att gå bra och "
"varför omfördelning av IP-adresser minskar deras arbetsbörda."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If possible, use an extra IP range whose abuse contact doesn't go through "
"the main university abuse team."
msgstr ""
"Använd om möjligt ett extra IP-intervall vars missbrukskontakt inte går via "
"universitetets huvudsakliga missbruksteam."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you can get your own IP block, great. Even if not, many providers will "
"still reassign subblocks to you if you ask."
msgstr ""
"Om du kan få ett eget IP-block är det utmärkt. Annars omfördelar många "
"leverantörer ändå delblock till dig om du ber om det."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you do, and if SMTP is allowed in your exit policy, consider configuring "
"[SPF](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sender_Policy_Framework) on your domain: "
"this will protect you from users using your exit node to forge e-mails which "
"look like they come from you."
msgstr ""
"Om du gör det och SMTP tillåts i utgångspolicyn bör du överväga att "
"konfigurera [SPF](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sender_Policy_Framework) för "
"domänen. Det skyddar dig mot användare som använder utgångsreläet för att "
"förfalska e-post som ser ut att komma från dig."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you feel it might be helpful, we can write you a signed letter confirming "
"this information: Contact us at frontdesk@torproject.org if you need one."
msgstr ""
"Om det skulle hjälpa kan vi skriva ett undertecknat brev som bekräftar "
"informationen. Kontakta frontdesk@torproject.org om du behöver ett."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you have questions about the process, please write an email to [tor-"
"relays mailing list](https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/"
"tor-relays) and we will try to explain the process to you."
msgstr ""
"Om du har frågor om processen kan du skriva till [e-postlistan tor-relays]"
"(https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-relays), så "
"försöker vi förklara den."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you have your own experience of abuse handling, just share it on our "
"public mailing list or write us an email to frontdesk@torproject.org."
msgstr ""
"Om du har egna erfarenheter av att hantera missbruk kan du dela dem på vår "
"offentliga e-postlista eller skriva till frontdesk@torproject.org."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you receive a threatening letter from a lawyer about abusive use or a "
"DMCA complaint, also don't freak out."
msgstr ""
"Få inte panik om du får ett hotfullt brev från en jurist om missbruk eller "
"ett DMCA-klagomål."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you receive an abuse complaint, don't freak out! Here is some advice for "
"you:"
msgstr "Få inte panik om du får ett klagomål om missbruk! Här är några råd:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "If you're not part of an organization, think about starting one!"
msgstr "Överväg att starta en organisation om du inte redan ingår i en."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you're part of an organization that will be running the exit relay (ISP, "
"university, etc), consider teaching your legal people about Tor."
msgstr ""
"Om du ingår i en organisation som ska driva utgångsreläet – "
"internetleverantör, universitet eller liknande – bör du överväga att "
"informera organisationens jurister om Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"If your country is missing here and you know a lawyer who can provide a "
"legal opinion, please get in contact with the Tor Project."
msgstr ""
"Om ditt land saknas i listan och du känner en jurist som kan ge ett "
"juridiskt utlåtande kan du kontakta The Tor Project."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"In addition to the [templates at Torservers.net](https://www.torservers.net/"
"wiki/abuse/templates), you can find many more templates for various "
"scenarios on the [Tor Abuse Templates](../tor-abuse-templates/)."
msgstr ""
"Utöver [mallarna på Torservers.net](https://www.torservers.net/wiki/abuse/"
"templates) finns många fler mallar för olika scenarier bland [Tors "
"svarsmallar för missbruk](../tor-abuse-templates/)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "In any case, add the ISP to the [GoodBadISPs](../good-bad-isps/) page."
msgstr ""
"Lägg i vilket fall till internetleverantören på sidan [GoodBadISPs](../good-"
"bad-isps/)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"In your reply, state clearly that you are not liable for forwarded content "
"passing through your machine, and include the relevant legal references for "
"your country."
msgstr ""
"Ange tydligt i svaret att du inte är ansvarig för vidarebefordrat innehåll "
"som passerar datorn och ta med relevanta laghänvisningar för ditt land."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"It is exceptionally rare to encounter a scenario where none of these "
"templates apply."
msgstr ""
"Det är ytterst sällsynt att inget av dessa mallscenarier är tillämpligt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"It's way better for them to hear about Tor from you, in a relaxed "
"environment, than to hear about it from a stranger over the phone. Make them "
"aware of [EFF's Legal FAQ for Tor Operators](../eff-tor-legal-faq). EFF has "
"also offered to talk to other lawyers to explain the legal aspects of Tor."
msgstr ""
"Det är mycket bättre att de får höra om Tor från dig i en avspänd miljö än "
"från en främling i telefon. Berätta om [EFF:s juridiska vanliga frågor för "
"Tor-operatörer](../eff-tor-legal-faq). EFF har även erbjudit sig att tala "
"med andra jurister och förklara de juridiska aspekterna av Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Legal"
msgstr "Juridik"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Make sure you know the relevant legal paragraphs for common-carrier-like "
"communication services in your country (and the country of your hosting "
"provider!)."
msgstr ""
"Se till att du känner till de relevanta rättsbestämmelserna för "
"kommunikationstjänster som liknar allmänna transportörer i ditt land och i "
"värdleverantörens land."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Make the WHOIS info point as close to you as possible."
msgstr "Låt WHOIS-informationen peka så nära dig som möjligt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "NOTE:"
msgstr "OBSERVERA ATT:"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Once you have identified your ISP, you can follow the two-step advice of "
"TorServers.net."
msgstr ""
"När du har valt internetleverantör kan du följa TorServers.nets råd i två "
"steg."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"One of the biggest reasons exit relays disappear is because the people "
"answering the abuse address get nervous and ask you to stop."
msgstr ""
"En av de främsta orsakerna till att utgångsreläer försvinner är att "
"personerna som svarar på missbruksadressen blir nervösa och ber dig sluta."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Our aim is to provide a general description of the legal issues surrounding "
"Tor exit relaying."
msgstr ""
"Vårt mål är att ge en allmän beskrivning av de juridiska frågorna kring "
"drift av Tor-utgångsreläer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Please add your country's regulations to this list."
msgstr "Lägg gärna till bestämmelserna för ditt land i listan."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Please read all the technical details before getting started. If you have "
"any questions or need help, please contact us at [tor-relays](https://"
"lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-relays)."
msgstr ""
"Läs alla tekniska detaljer innan du börjar. Kontakta oss via [tor-relays]"
"(https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-relays) om du har "
"frågor eller behöver hjälp."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Register a phone number and a fax number as abuse contact."
msgstr ""
"Registrera ett telefonnummer och ett faxnummer som kontaktuppgifter för "
"missbruk."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Roughly 80% are automated reports, and the rest is usually satisfied with "
"[our default reply](https://www.torservers.net/wiki/abuse/templates)."
msgstr ""
"Ungefär 80 procent är automatiska rapporter, och för resten räcker vanligen "
"[vårt standardsvar](https://www.torservers.net/wiki/abuse/templates)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Set reverse DNS to something that signals its use, e.g. 'anonymous-relay', "
"'proxy', 'tor-proxy'. So when other people see the address in their web "
"logs, they will more quickly understand what's going on."
msgstr ""
"Ange ett omvänt DNS-namn som visar användningen, till exempel ”anonymous-"
"relay”, ”proxy” eller ”tor-proxy”. Då förstår andra snabbare vad som händer "
"när de ser adressen i sina webbloggar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Set up an informative website on the exit IP(s) on port 80."
msgstr ""
"Skapa en informativ webbplats på utgångens IP-adress eller IP-adresser på "
"port 80."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Technical"
msgstr "Tekniskt"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"The [Reduced Exit Policy](https://trac.torproject.org/projects/tor/wiki/doc/"
"ReducedExitPolicy) is an alternative to the default exit policy. It allows "
"many Internet services while still blocking the majority of TCP ports."
msgstr ""
"Den [begränsade utgångspolicyn](https://trac.torproject.org/projects/tor/"
"wiki/doc/ReducedExitPolicy) är ett alternativ till standardpolicyn för "
"utgångar. Den tillåter många internettjänster men blockerar fortfarande de "
"flesta TCP-portar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"The people from Torservers.net in Germany found a lawyer who would agree to "
"\"host\" them inside his office."
msgstr ""
"Personerna bakom Torservers.net i Tyskland hittade en jurist som gick med på "
"att ge dem en juridisk hemvist på sitt kontor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"The setup process was easy and cheap. Similar setups probably exist for your "
"country."
msgstr ""
"Konfigurationen var enkel och billig. Liknande lösningar finns förmodligen i "
"ditt land."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"The two-step process usually helps in elevating your request to higher "
"levels of support staff without scaring them off too early, even if you "
"don't end up with your own IP range. Here is a template you can use: "
"[Inquiry](https://www.torservers.net/wiki/hoster/inquiry)"
msgstr ""
"Tvåstegsprocessen hjälper vanligen till att föra begäran till högre nivåer "
"av supportpersonal utan att skrämma dem för tidigt, även om du inte får ett "
"eget IP-intervall. Här är en mall som du kan använda: [Förfrågan](https://"
"www.torservers.net/wiki/hoster/inquiry)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"These guidelines are meant to give you a quick introduction into the "
"business of running your own exit relay."
msgstr ""
"Riktlinjerna är avsedda att ge en snabb introduktion till att driva ett eget "
"utgångsrelä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"They are now a non-profit association (\"eingetragener Verein, "
"gemeinnutzig\") registered inside a lawyer's office."
msgstr ""
"De är nu en ideell förening (”eingetragener Verein, gemeinnützig”) som är "
"registrerad på en juristbyrå."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Things you can do preemptively"
msgstr "Sådant du kan göra i förebyggande syfte"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"This FAQ is for informational purposes only and does not constitute legal "
"advice."
msgstr ""
"Dessa vanliga frågor är endast avsedda som information och utgör inte "
"juridisk rådgivning."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"This drastically reduces the odds that a Bittorrent user will select your "
"node and thus reduces or even eliminates the number of [DMCA complaints](../"
"eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/) you will receive."
msgstr ""
"Det minskar drastiskt sannolikheten att en BitTorrent-användare väljer noden "
"och minskar eller eliminerar därmed antalet [DMCA-klagomål](../eff-tor-legal-"
"faq/tor-dmca-response/) som du får."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"To find an ISP, go through forums and sites where ISPs post their latest "
"deals, and contact them about Tor hosting."
msgstr ""
"Hitta en internetleverantör genom att söka på forum och webbplatser där "
"leverantörer publicerar sina senaste erbjudanden och kontakta dem om Tor-"
"värdtjänster."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Tor at Universities: Find allies."
msgstr "Tor på universitet: hitta allierade."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"TorServers.net is a fairly large Tor exit operator, and we receive only a "
"very small number of complaints, especially compared to the amount of "
"traffic we push."
msgstr ""
"TorServers.net är en ganska stor operatör av Tor-utgångar, men vi får endast "
"mycket få klagomål, särskilt i förhållande till trafikmängden vi överför."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"Torservers.net uses a free German fax-to-email service, call-manager.de, and "
"a VoIP number from Sipgate.de."
msgstr ""
"Torservers.net använder den kostnadsfria tyska fax-till-e-posttjänsten call-"
"manager.de och ett VoIP-nummer från Sipgate.de."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Try to use dedicated IPs, and when possible, dedicated hardware."
msgstr ""
"Försök använda dedikerade IP-adresser och om möjligt dedikerad maskinvara."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"USA: [DMCA 512](https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/512); see [EFF's "
"Legal FAQ for Tor Operators](../eff-tor-legal-faq) (a very good and relevant "
"read for other countries as well)"
msgstr ""
"USA: [DMCA 512](https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/512); se [EFF:s "
"juridiska vanliga frågor för Tor-operatörer](../eff-tor-legal-faq), som även "
"är mycket relevant läsning för andra länder"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"We are not aware of any case that made it near a court, and we will do "
"everything in our power to support you if it does."
msgstr ""
"Vi känner inte till något fall som ens har varit nära att nå domstol, och vi "
"gör allt vi kan för att stödja dig om det skulle hända."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"We have not needed the input of a lawyer in many years of operation "
"following the advice on this page."
msgstr ""
"Under många års verksamhet enligt råden på sidan har vi inte behövt anlita "
"en jurist."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"We very much need diversity, and it does not help if we pool too many exits "
"at one friendly ISP."
msgstr ""
"Vi behöver verkligen mångfald, och det hjälper inte om alltför många "
"utgångar samlas hos en enda vänligt inställd internetleverantör."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"You can also add comments to your range, hinting at your usage as an "
"anonymization service ([Example](https://apps.db.ripe.net/db-web-ui/lookup?"
"source=ripe&key=ZWIEBELFREUNDE&type=mntner))."
msgstr ""
"Du kan även lägga till kommentarer till intervallet som antyder att det "
"används som anonymiseringstjänst ([exempel](https://apps.db.ripe.net/db-web-"
"ui/lookup?source=ripe&key=ZWIEBELFREUNDE&type=mntner))."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid ""
"You can look up if an IP address was listed as an exit relay at a given time "
"at [ExoneraTor](https://exonerator.torproject.org/). Point to that website "
"in your reply to the complaint."
msgstr ""
"På [ExoneraTor](https://exonerator.torproject.org/) kan du kontrollera om en "
"IP-adress var registrerad som utgångsrelä vid en viss tidpunkt. Hänvisa till "
"webbplatsen i svaret på klagomålet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "[Tor Relay Guide](../../)"
msgstr "[Guide för Tor-reläer](../../)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Quick introduction into running your Exit relay"
msgstr "Snabb introduktion till att driva ett utgångsrelä"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-exit-guidelines/
msgid "Tor Exit Guidelines"
msgstr "Riktlinjer för Tor-utgångsreläer"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"(Tor can handle a variety of rate limiting approaches, so this isn't the end "
"of the world)."
msgstr ""
"(Tor kan hantera flera metoder för hastighetsbegränsning, så det är inte "
"hela världen.)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"(We focus on the university scenario, but hopefully you can adapt it to your "
"own situation.)"
msgstr ""
"(Vi fokuserar på universitetsscenariot, men förhoppningsvis kan du anpassa "
"det till din egen situation.)"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Ask for advice from everybody you meet who likes the idea, and try to work "
"your way up the chain to get as many good allies as you can in as many areas "
"as you can."
msgstr ""
"Be alla du möter som uppskattar idén om råd och arbeta dig uppåt i "
"organisationen för att få så många bra allierade som möjligt inom så många "
"områden som möjligt."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Avoid having actual meetings or long email discussions, and make it clear "
"that you don't need their official legal opinion yet."
msgstr ""
"Undvik verkliga möten eller långa e-postdiskussioner och tydliggör att du "
"ännu inte behöver deras officiella juridiska utlåtande."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Avoid putting them on the spot or formally asking permission: most network "
"security people will like the idea of Tor in theory, but they won't be in a "
"position to \"authorize\" your Tor relay."
msgstr ""
"Undvik att ställa dem mot väggen eller formellt be om tillstånd. De flesta "
"nätverkssäkerhetsexperter uppskattar idén med Tor i teorin, men har inte "
"befogenhet att ”godkänna” ditt Tor-relä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Be helpful and take the opportunity to explain to them about Tor and why "
"it's useful to the world. (If they contact you directly for logs, you should "
"send them to your university's lawyers -- acting on it yourself is [almost "
"always a poor idea](../eff-tor-legal-faq/))."
msgstr ""
"Var hjälpsam och ta tillfället i akt att förklara Tor och varför det är "
"nyttigt för världen. Om de kontaktar dig direkt och ber om loggar bör du "
"hänvisa dem till universitetets jurister – att själv agera på begäran är "
"[nästan alltid en dålig idé](../eff-tor-legal-faq/)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Become familiar with [the EFF's template letter regarding DMCA notices for "
"Tor](../eff-tor-legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/), which is quite clear about "
"not putting liability on service providers."
msgstr ""
"Bekanta dig med [EFF:s mallbrev om DMCA-meddelanden för Tor](../eff-tor-"
"legal-faq/tor-dmca-response/), som tydligt beskriver att tjänsteleverantörer "
"inte ska åläggas ansvar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Becoming friends with the lawyers early in the process will avoid situations "
"where they need to learn about everything and make a decision in one day."
msgstr ""
"Om du blir vän med juristerna tidigt i processen undviker du situationer där "
"de måste lära sig allt och fatta ett beslut på en enda dag."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"But it might be extremely restrictive (\"no services of any kind\"), in "
"which case you're going to have a tough road ahead of you."
msgstr ""
"Policyn kan dock vara ytterst begränsande, till exempel ”inga tjänster av "
"något slag”, och då har du en svår väg framför dig."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "Fifth, start finding allies."
msgstr "För det femte: börja hitta allierade."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "First, learn about your university's AUP -- acceptable use policy."
msgstr ""
"För det första: lär dig universitetets policy för godtagbar användning."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"First, you should follow the tips in the [Tor relay documentation](../../), "
"such as picking a descriptive hostname or getting your own IP address."
msgstr ""
"Börja med att följa tipsen i [dokumentationen för Tor-reläer](../../), till "
"exempel att välja ett beskrivande värdnamn eller skaffa en egen IP-adress."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "Fourth, learn a bit about authentication on the Internet."
msgstr "För det fjärde: lär dig lite om autentisering på internet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Hang out on IRC ([irc.oftc.net](https://www.oftc.net) - #tor-relays) for a "
"while and learn more."
msgstr ""
"Tillbringa ett tag på IRC ([irc.oftc.net](https://www.oftc.net) – #tor-"
"relays) och lär dig mer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "If possible, attend a talk by one of the Tor developers."
msgstr "Gå om möjligt på ett föredrag av någon av Tor-utvecklarna."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"If that doesn't work, you can scale back the advertised speed of your relay, "
"by using the `MaxAdvertisedBandwidth` to attract less traffic from the Tor "
"network. Lastly, you can scale back your exit policy."
msgstr ""
"Om det inte fungerar kan du minska reläets annonserade hastighet med "
"`MaxAdvertisedBandwidth` så att det drar till sig mindre trafik från Tor-"
"nätverket. Som sista åtgärd kan du begränsa utgångspolicyn."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"If the administration considers an Internet community that helps other "
"people to be a foreign concept, or if they're used to treating new "
"situations as security risks and telling everybody to quit it, a Tor relay "
"may give you a way to focus the discussion and find allies who want to help "
"change policy."
msgstr ""
"Om administrationen ser en internetgemenskap som hjälper andra som något "
"främmande, eller är van att behandla nya situationer som säkerhetsrisker och "
"be alla sluta, kan ett Tor-relä ge dig ett sätt att fokusera diskussionen "
"och hitta allierade som vill bidra till en policyförändring."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"If the authorities contact your university for logs, be pleasant and helpful."
msgstr ""
"Var vänlig och hjälpsam om myndigheter kontaktar universitetet för att få "
"loggar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"If the university's entire IP address space is \"trusted\" to access these "
"library resources, the university is forced to maintain an iron grip on all "
"its addresses."
msgstr ""
"Om universitetets hela IP-adressutrymme är ”betrott” för åtkomst till "
"biblioteksresurserna tvingas universitetet hålla ett järngrepp om alla "
"adresser."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"If there are too many complaints coming in, there are several approaches you "
"can take to reduce them."
msgstr ""
"Om det kommer in för många klagomål finns flera metoder för att minska dem."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"If they have concerns, or raise questions that you don't know how to answer, "
"work with them to figure out the answers and make them happy."
msgstr ""
"Om de är oroliga eller ställer frågor som du inte kan besvara kan du arbeta "
"tillsammans med dem för att hitta svaren och göra dem nöjda."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"If you have a law school nearby, meet the professors that teach the Internet "
"law classes, and chat with them about Tor and its implications."
msgstr ""
"Om det finns en juridisk fakultet i närheten kan du träffa professorerna som "
"undervisar i interneträtt och tala med dem om Tor och dess konsekvenser."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"If your school has a botnet research group or studies Internet attacks (like "
"at Georgia Tech and UCSD), meet them and learn more about all the scary "
"things already out there on the Internet."
msgstr ""
"Om din skola har en forskargrupp för botnät eller studerar internetangrepp, "
"som Georgia Tech och UCSD, kan du träffa gruppen och lära dig mer om allt "
"skrämmande som redan finns på internet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"In any case, the key here is to become familiar with the laws and their "
"implications and uncertainties."
msgstr ""
"Hur som helst är nyckeln att sätta sig in i lagarna och deras konsekvenser "
"och osäkerheter."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"In short, running a Tor exit node may well require you to become an advocate "
"for anonymity and privacy in the world."
msgstr ""
"Kort sagt kan det mycket väl innebära att du måste bli en förespråkare för "
"anonymitet och integritet i världen om du driver ett Tor-utgångsrelä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"In some cases, you should talk to the network security people before you "
"talk to the lawyers; in some cases, there will be yet other groups that will "
"be critical to educate and bring into the discussion. You'll have to make it "
"up as you go."
msgstr ""
"I vissa fall bör du tala med de nätverkssäkerhetsansvariga innan du talar "
"med juristerna. I andra fall kan det finnas ytterligare grupper som det är "
"avgörande att utbilda och ta med i diskussionen. Du får anpassa "
"tillvägagångssättet efter hand."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"In the US, these appear to be mainly the [DMCA](../eff-tor-legal-faq/) and "
"[CDA](../eff-tor-legal-faq/), and the good news is that many lawyers believe "
"that Tor exit node operators are in the same boat as the ISPs themselves."
msgstr ""
"I USA verkar det främst handla om [DMCA](../eff-tor-legal-faq/) och [CDA](../"
"eff-tor-legal-faq/), och den goda nyheten är att många jurister anser att "
"operatörer av Tor-utgångsreläer befinner sig i samma situation som "
"internetleverantörerna själva."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"In this sense, Tor provides a lever to help you change your organization's "
"policies."
msgstr ""
"I den bemärkelsen ger Tor dig ett verktyg för att hjälpa till att förändra "
"organisationens policyer."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Learn about the types of people and organizations who need secure "
"communications on the Internet."
msgstr ""
"Lär dig om vilka slags personer och organisationer som behöver säker "
"kommunikation på internet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "Mailing list"
msgstr "E-postlista"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Make it clear that you're willing to work with them to make sure it isn't "
"too much hassle on their part; for example, they can pass complaints "
"directly on to you if they like."
msgstr ""
"Gör det tydligt att du är villig att samarbeta med dem för att se till att "
"det inte blir alltför besvärligt för dem. De kan till exempel vidarebefordra "
"klagomål direkt till dig om de vill."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Make sure to keep these discussions informal and small -- invite one of the "
"general counsel out to coffee to discuss \"something neat that may come up "
"later on.\" Feel free to bring along one of the allies you found above, if "
"it makes you more comfortable."
msgstr ""
"Se till att hålla diskussionerna informella och i en liten krets – bjud till "
"exempel ut någon av chefsjuristerna på kaffe för att diskutera ”något "
"intressant som kan bli aktuellt senare”. Ta gärna med någon av de allierade "
"du hittade ovan om det känns tryggare."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Many library-related services use source IP address to decide whether a "
"subscriber is allowed to see their content."
msgstr ""
"Många biblioteksrelaterade tjänster använder källans IP-adress för att "
"avgöra om en prenumerant får ta del av innehållet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Most likely it is ambiguously worded, to let them allow or deny things based "
"on the situation."
msgstr ""
"Den är sannolikt tvetydigt formulerad för att de ska kunna tillåta eller "
"neka saker beroende på situationen."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Note that in many cases you don't even need to be researching the exit node "
"itself -- doing research on the Tor network requires that there be a Tor "
"network, after all, and keeping it going is a community effort."
msgstr ""
"Observera att du i många fall inte ens behöver forska om själva "
"utgångsreläet – forskning om Tor-nätverket förutsätter trots allt att det "
"finns ett Tor-nätverk, och det är en gemensam insats att hålla det igång."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Of course, you need to understand that without actual clear precedent (and "
"even then), it's still possible that a given judge will not interpret things "
"the way the lawyers expect."
msgstr ""
"Du måste naturligtvis förstå att det även utan tydlig rättspraxis – och "
"ibland trots sådan – fortfarande är möjligt att en viss domare inte tolkar "
"saken på det sätt juristerna förväntar sig."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"On the other hand, universities like Berkeley simply add a \"no proxies\" "
"line to their network policies, and are stuck in a battle to patrol every "
"address on their network."
msgstr ""
"Universitet som Berkeley lägger däremot helt enkelt till en rad om att "
"proxyservrar inte är tillåtna i sina nätverkspolicyer och fastnar sedan i en "
"ständig kamp för att övervaka varje adress i nätverket."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Practice explaining Tor and its benefits and consequences to friends and "
"neighbors -- the [abuse FAQ](https://2019.www.torproject.org/faq-abuse) may "
"provide some helpful starting points."
msgstr ""
"Öva på att förklara Tor och dess fördelar och konsekvenser för vänner och "
"grannar – [vanliga frågor om missbruk](https://2019.www.torproject.org/faq-"
"abuse) kan ge några användbara utgångspunkter."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Read the [design overview](https://2019.www.torproject.org/overview.html), "
"the [design paper](https://svn-archive.torproject.org/svn/projects/design-"
"paper/tor-design.pdf), and the [FAQ](https://2019.www.torproject.org/docs/"
"faq.html.en)."
msgstr ""
"Läs [designöversikten](https://2019.www.torproject.org/overview.html), "
"[designrapporten](https://svn-archive.torproject.org/svn/projects/design-"
"paper/tor-design.pdf) och [vanliga frågor](https://2019.www.torproject.org/"
"docs/faq.html.en)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Remember that lawyers are paid to say no unless they have a reason to say "
"yes, so when the time finally comes to ask their opinion on running a Tor "
"exit node, make sure the question is not \"are there any liability issues?"
"\", but rather \"we'd like to do this, can you help us avoid the biggest "
"issues?\" Try to predict what they will say, and try to gain allies among "
"the lawyers who like your cause and want to help."
msgstr ""
"Kom ihåg att jurister får betalt för att säga nej om de inte har skäl att "
"säga ja. När det väl är dags att fråga om deras åsikt om att driva ett Tor-"
"utgångsrelä bör frågan därför inte vara ”finns det några ansvarsfrågor?”, "
"utan snarare ”vi skulle vilja göra detta, kan ni hjälpa oss att undvika de "
"största problemen?”. Försök förutse vad de kommer att säga och hitta "
"allierade bland de jurister som sympatiserar med saken och vill hjälpa till."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Remember that lawyers don't like being told how to interpret laws by a non-"
"lawyer, but they are often pleased to hear that other lawyers have done a "
"lot of the research and leg-work (this is where [the EFF's legal FAQ](../eff-"
"tor-legal-faq/) comes in, along with your law school contacts if you found "
"any)."
msgstr ""
"Kom ihåg att jurister inte tycker om att få höra av en icke-jurist hur lagar "
"ska tolkas, men de brukar uppskatta att få veta att andra jurister redan har "
"gjort mycket av forskningen och förarbetet. Det är här [EFF:s juridiska "
"frågor och svar](../eff-tor-legal-faq/) kommer in, tillsammans med dina "
"kontakter på juristutbildningen om du har hittat några."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Second, learn about your local laws with respect to liability of traffic "
"that exits from your Tor relay."
msgstr ""
"För det andra bör du sätta dig in i den lokala lagstiftningen om ansvar för "
"trafik som lämnar nätverket via ditt Tor-relä."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "Seventh, teach your network security people about Tor."
msgstr "För det sjunde bör du lära de nätverkssäkerhetsansvariga om Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "Sixth, teach your university's lawyers about Tor."
msgstr "För det sjätte bör du lära universitetets jurister om Tor."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"So Harvard doesn't need to be as worried about what other services are "
"running on their network, and it also takes care of off-campus students and "
"faculty."
msgstr ""
"Harvard behöver därför inte oroa sig lika mycket för vilka andra tjänster "
"som körs i nätverket, och lösningen fungerar även för studenter och lärare "
"utanför universitetsområdet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"So if you're interested, you might want to get that started early in the "
"process -- see our [Research Portal](https://research.torproject.org/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du är intresserad kan det vara klokt att sätta igång detta tidigt i "
"processen – se vår [forskningsportal](https://research.torproject.org/)."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Some people have found that their university only tolerates their Tor relay "
"if they're involved in a research project around anonymity."
msgstr ""
"Vissa har upptäckt att deras universitet endast tolererar Tor-reläet om de "
"deltar i ett forskningsprojekt om anonymitet."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Subscribe to [Tor Relays Universities](https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/"
"mailman/listinfo/tor-relays-universities) mailing list (and other education "
"institutions too)."
msgstr ""
"Prenumerera på e-postlistan [Tor Relays Universities](https://"
"lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-relays-universities), som "
"även är avsedd för andra utbildningsinstitutioner."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Take them out to coffee to explain Tor and let them know that you are "
"planning to run a Tor server."
msgstr ""
"Bjud dem på kaffe, förklara Tor och berätta att du planerar att driva en Tor-"
"server."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"The CDA is less clear, because it was written before the modern Internet "
"emerged, but EFF and ACLU are optimistic."
msgstr ""
"CDA är mindre tydlig eftersom lagen skrevs innan det moderna internet växte "
"fram, men EFF och ACLU är optimistiska."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"The best strategy depends on your situation, but here are some tips to get "
"you started."
msgstr ""
"Den bästa strategin beror på situationen, men här är några tips som hjälper "
"dig att komma igång."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"The downside is that your Tor relay's existence is more fragile, since the "
"terms of its demise are already negotiated."
msgstr ""
"Nackdelen är att Tor-reläets fortsatta existens blir mer osäker eftersom "
"villkoren för dess nedläggning redan har förhandlats fram."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"These people are already overworked, and anything you can do to keep work "
"off their plate will make everybody happier."
msgstr ""
"De här personerna är redan överbelastade, och allt du kan göra för att "
"minska deras arbetsbörda gör alla nöjdare."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "Third, learn about Tor's design."
msgstr "För det tredje bör du sätta dig in i Tors utformning."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"This approach has the added benefit that you can draw in other faculty and "
"students in the process."
msgstr ""
"Tillvägagångssättet har den ytterligare fördelen att du kan involvera andra "
"lärare och studenter i processen."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"This may seem like a risky move, but it's way better for them to hear about "
"Tor from you, in a relaxed environment, than to hear about it from a "
"stranger over the phone."
msgstr ""
"Det kan verka riskabelt, men det är mycket bättre att de får höra om Tor "
"från dig i en avslappnad miljö än från en främling i telefon."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"To keep your exit node running long-term, you're going to need the support "
"of the people around you."
msgstr ""
"För att kunna hålla utgångsreläet igång på lång sikt behöver du stöd från "
"människorna omkring dig."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Tor's default log level doesn't provide much that's useful, so if they want "
"copies of your logs, that's fine."
msgstr ""
"Tors standardnivå för loggning innehåller inte mycket användbar information, "
"så om de vill ha kopior av loggarna går det bra."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"Universities like Harvard do the smart thing: their students and faculty "
"have actual methods to authenticate -- say, certificates, or usernames and "
"passwords -- to a central Harvard server and access the library resources "
"from there."
msgstr ""
"Universitet som Harvard gör det smarta: studenter och lärare har faktiska "
"autentiseringsmetoder – till exempel certifikat eller användarnamn och "
"lösenord – för att logga in på en central Harvard-server och komma åt "
"biblioteksresurser därifrån."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"We should encourage all these networks to move to an end-to-end "
"authentication model rather than conflating network location with who's on "
"the other end."
msgstr ""
"Vi bör uppmuntra alla sådana nätverk att övergå till en modell med "
"totalsträcksautentisering i stället för att likställa nätverksplatsen med "
"vem som finns i andra änden."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"You aren't going to keep your Tor exit node a secret from them for long "
"anyway, and like with the lawyers, hearing it from you is way better than "
"hearing it from a stranger on the phone."
msgstr ""
"Du kommer ändå inte att kunna hålla Tor-utgångsreläet hemligt för dem "
"särskilt länge, och precis som med juristerna är det mycket bättre att de "
"får höra om det från dig än från en främling i telefon."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"You might let them know that there are ways you can dial down the potential "
"for abuse complaints, for example by rate limiting or partially restricting "
"your exit policy -- but don't be too eager to offer or take these steps, "
"since once you give up ground here it's very hard to get it back."
msgstr ""
"Du kan berätta att det finns sätt att minska risken för "
"missbruksanmälningar, till exempel genom hastighetsbegränsning eller genom "
"att delvis begränsa utgångspolicyn. Var dock inte alltför snabb med att "
"erbjuda eller vidta sådana åtgärder, eftersom det är mycket svårt att återta "
"mark som du väl har gett upp."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid ""
"You'll also want to learn if there are bandwidth limitations at your "
"organization."
msgstr ""
"Du bör också ta reda på om organisationen har några bandbreddsbegränsningar."

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "How do I make my University / ISP / etc happy with my exit node?"
msgstr ""
"Hur får jag mitt universitet, min internetleverantör eller liknande att "
"acceptera mitt utgångsrelä?"

#: content/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/community-resources/tor-relay-universities/
msgid "Tor Relay Universities"
msgstr "Universitet som driver Tor-reläer"

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.body https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid "By running a Tor relay you can help make the Tor network:"
msgstr "Genom att driva ett Tor-relä kan du bidra till att göra Tor-nätverket:"

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.body https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid ""
"Running a relay requires technical skill and commitment, which is why we've "
"created a wealth of resources to help our relay operators."
msgstr ""
"Att driva ett relä kräver teknisk kunskap och engagemang. Därför har vi "
"skapat en mängd resurser för att hjälpa våra reläoperatörer."

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.body https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid "The Tor network relies on volunteers to donate bandwidth."
msgstr "Tor-nätverket är beroende av att volontärer bidrar med bandbredd."

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.body https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid ""
"The current Tor network is quite small compared to the number of people who "
"need to use Tor, which means we need more dedicated volunteers like you to "
"run relays."
msgstr ""
"Det nuvarande Tor-nätverket är ganska litet jämfört med antalet personer som "
"behöver använda Tor. Därför behövs fler engagerade volontärer som du som "
"driver reläer."

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.body https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid "The more people who run relays, the better the Tor network will be."
msgstr "Ju fler som driver reläer, desto bättre blir Tor-nätverket."

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.body https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid "faster (and therefore more usable)"
msgstr "snabbare och därmed mer användbart"

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.body https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid "more robust against attacks"
msgstr "mer motståndskraftigt mot angrepp"

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.body https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid "more stable in case of outages"
msgstr "stabilare vid driftavbrott"

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.body https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid "safer for its users (spying on more relays is harder than on a few)"
msgstr ""
"säkrare för användarna, eftersom det är svårare att övervaka många reläer än "
"ett fåtal"

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.cta https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid "Grow the Tor network"
msgstr "Utöka Tor-nätverket"

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/
msgid ""
"Relays are the backbone of the Tor network. Help make Tor stronger and "
"faster by running a relay today."
msgstr ""
"Reläerna är Tor-nätverkets ryggrad. Hjälp till att göra Tor starkare och "
"snabbare genom att driva ett relä redan i dag."

#: content/relay/contents.lr:page.title
#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/setup/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/setup/exit/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/setup/guard/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.section
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/exit/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid "Relay Operations"
msgstr "Reläverksamhet"

#: content/relay/getting-help/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/getting-help/
msgid ""
"If you run into problems while setting up your relay, please refer to the "
"[FAQs page](https://support.torproject.org/relay-operators) in the Support "
"Portal."
msgstr ""
"Se sidan med [vanliga frågor](https://support.torproject.org/relay-"
"operators) i supportportalen om du stöter på problem när du konfigurerar "
"reläet."

#: content/relay/getting-help/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/getting-help/
msgid ""
"The list is a great resource for asking (and answering) questions, and for "
"getting to know other relay operators. Make sure to check out the archives!"
msgstr ""
"Listan är en utmärkt resurs för att ställa och besvara frågor och lära känna "
"andra reläoperatörer. Glöm inte att läsa arkivet!"

#: content/relay/getting-help/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/getting-help/
msgid ""
"You can also ask your questions on the public [tor-relays mailing list]"
"(https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-relays) and the "
"[Relay Operator](https://forum.torproject.net/c/support/relay-operator/17) "
"sub-category on the Tor Forum."
msgstr ""
"Du kan även ställa frågor på den offentliga e-postlistan [tor-relays]"
"(https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-relays) och i "
"underkategorin [Relay Operator](https://forum.torproject.net/c/support/relay-"
"operator/17) på Tor-forumet."

#: content/relay/getting-help/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/getting-help/
msgid ""
"You can also get help by joining the IRC channel #tor-relays in the network "
"[irc.oftc.net](https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/#irc-help)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också få hjälp genom att ansluta till IRC-kanalen #tor-relays på "
"nätverket [irc.oftc.net](https://support.torproject.org/get-in-touch/#irc-"
"help)."

#: content/relay/getting-help/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/getting-help/
msgid "How to get help if you run into issues"
msgstr "Så får du hjälp om du stöter på problem"

#: content/relay/getting-help/contents.lr:page.title
#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/getting-help/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/
msgid "Getting help"
msgstr "Få hjälp"

#: content/relay/governance/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/
msgid ""
"As a global community-driven project, it is imperative to establish "
"transparent and effective governance mechanisms to ensure the integrity, "
"security, and reliability of the network."
msgstr ""
"Som ett globalt, gemenskapsdrivet projekt är det avgörande att införa "
"transparenta och effektiva styrmekanismer för att säkerställa nätverkets "
"integritet, säkerhet och tillförlitlighet."

#: content/relay/governance/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/
msgid ""
"By transparently documenting these processes, Tor aims to foster a community-"
"driven approach to network security, enabling collaboration among "
"developers, operators, and users."
msgstr ""
"Genom att dokumentera processerna öppet vill Tor främja ett gemenskapsdrivet "
"arbetssätt för nätverkssäkerhet och möjliggöra samarbete mellan utvecklare, "
"operatörer och användare."

#: content/relay/governance/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/
msgid ""
"Effective governance of relays is crucial for upholding the trust of users "
"and ensuring the continued robustness of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Effektiv styrning av reläerna är avgörande för att upprätthålla användarnas "
"förtroende och Tor-nätverkets fortsatta robusthet."

#: content/relay/governance/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/
msgid ""
"The Tor network operates on principles of openness, inclusivity, and "
"decentralization."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverket bygger på principerna öppenhet, inkludering och "
"decentralisering."

#: content/relay/governance/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/
msgid ""
"This section provides insight into the processes, policies, and structures "
"that govern the operation and use of Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"Det här avsnittet beskriver de processer, policyer och strukturer som styr "
"driften och användningen av Tor-reläer."

