msgid "Governance"
msgstr "Styrning"

#: content/relay/governance/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/
msgid "The processes and policies that govern relays on the Tor network."
msgstr "Processerna och policyerna som styr reläerna i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Having [processes to handle bad relays](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"network-health/team/-/wikis/Bad-relay-work) in open networks like the Tor "
"network is crucial to maintaining user privacy and security."
msgstr ""
"Att ha [processer för att hantera dåliga reläer](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/team/-/wikis/Bad-relay-work) i "
"öppna nätverk som Tor-nätverket är avgörande för att upprätthålla "
"användarnas integritet och säkerhet."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/
msgid "Malicious actors may attempt to join the network to attack Tor users."
msgstr ""
"Illasinnade aktörer kan försöka ansluta sig till nätverket för att angripa "
"Tor-användare."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/
msgid ""
"The following resources are available to help users of the Tor network "
"understand how we handle bad relay work."
msgstr ""
"Följande resurser hjälper Tor-nätverkets användare att förstå hur vi "
"hanterar arbetet med dåliga reläer."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/
msgid ""
"They collaborate with Tor [Directory Authorities](../policies-and-proposals/"
"directory-authority) to take action against identified bad relays."
msgstr ""
"De samarbetar med Tors [katalogauktoriteter](../policies-and-proposals/"
"directory-authority) för att vidta åtgärder mot identifierade dåliga reläer."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/
msgid ""
"To counter these threats, the Network Health team within the Tor Project "
"actively detects and prevents such malicious efforts."
msgstr ""
"För att motverka sådana hot arbetar Network Health-teamet inom The Tor "
"Project aktivt med att upptäcka och förhindra illasinnade försök."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/
msgid ""
"While we strive for transparency at the Tor Project, hunting bad relays is "
"one of the few areas where we are in [need to find a balance between secrecy "
"and openness](https://lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-talk/2014-July/"
"034219.html)."
msgstr ""
"Även om vi eftersträvar öppenhet inom The Tor Project är jakten på dåliga "
"reläer ett av få områden där vi [måste hitta en balans mellan sekretess och "
"öppenhet](https://lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-talk/2014-July/"
"034219.html)."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/
msgid "Handling Bad Relays"
msgstr "Hantering av dåliga reläer"

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/
msgid ""
"**You can view the [rejected fingerprints for 2021 - 2024](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/team/-/wikis/Rejected-fingerprints-"
"found-in-attacks).**"
msgstr ""
"**Du kan se [avvisade fingeravtryck för 2021–2024](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/team/-/wikis/Rejected-fingerprints-"
"found-in-attacks).**"

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/
msgid ""
"However, occasional delays may occur, particularly in cases of ongoing "
"attacks or other rare circumstances."
msgstr ""
"Enstaka förseningar kan dock förekomma, särskilt vid pågående angrepp eller "
"andra sällsynta omständigheter."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/
msgid ""
"In April 2021, we started publishing the list of rejected fingerprints. "
"Nevertheless, volunteers are allowed to explore historical data and document "
"rejected fingerprints from the past if desired."
msgstr ""
"I april 2021 började vi publicera listan över avvisade fingeravtryck. "
"Volontärer får dock undersöka historiska data och dokumentera äldre avvisade "
"fingeravtryck om de vill."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/
msgid ""
"The documentation of these fingerprints serves as a valuable resource for "
"understanding and mitigating attacks on the Tor network, fostering a safer "
"and more secure environment for all users."
msgstr ""
"Dokumentationen av fingeravtrycken är en värdefull resurs för att förstå och "
"motverka angrepp mot Tor-nätverket och bidrar till en tryggare och säkrare "
"miljö för alla användare."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/
msgid ""
"These delays are necessary to prevent attackers from gaining insights into "
"our methods of detecting malicious relays."
msgstr ""
"Förseningarna är nödvändiga för att hindra angripare från att få insyn i "
"våra metoder för att upptäcka illasinnade reläer."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/
msgid ""
"We publish all rejected fingerprints associated with attacks on a monthly "
"basis, typically for the preceding month."
msgstr ""
"Vi publicerar varje månad alla avvisade fingeravtryck som är kopplade till "
"angrepp, vanligtvis för föregående månad."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejected-fingerprints/
msgid "Rejected Fingerprints"
msgstr "Avvisade fingeravtryck"

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"Corner cases may arise where the intention behind a relay's behavior is "
"unclear."
msgstr ""
"Det kan uppstå gränsfall där avsikten bakom ett reläs beteende är oklar."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"For more details on how we address these issues, you can reference our "
"[criteria for rejecting bad relays](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"network-health/team/-/wikis/Criteria-for-rejecting-bad-relays) guide."
msgstr ""
"Mer information om hur vi hanterar sådana problem finns i vår vägledning med "
"[kriterier för att avvisa dåliga reläer](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"network-health/team/-/wikis/Criteria-for-rejecting-bad-relays)."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"However, there are instances where relays may be misconfigured or actively "
"harmful to users."
msgstr ""
"Det förekommer dock reläer som är felkonfigurerade eller aktivt skadliga för "
"användarna."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"If direct communication isn't possible, the relay may be labeled as a "
"\"BadExit,\" indicating that it should no longer handle exit traffic while "
"still remaining within the network."
msgstr ""
"Om direkt kontakt inte är möjlig kan reläet märkas som ”BadExit”, vilket "
"innebär att det inte längre ska hantera utgångstrafik men fortfarande får "
"finnas kvar i nätverket."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"In cases of misconfigured exit relays, which can cause usability issues for "
"users, efforts are made to contact the operator to rectify the problem."
msgstr ""
"När ett felkonfigurerat utgångsrelä orsakar användbarhetsproblem försöker vi "
"kontakta operatören så att problemet kan rättas till."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"In such cases, the relays are swiftly removed from the network to protect "
"users."
msgstr ""
"I sådana fall tas reläerna snabbt bort från nätverket för att skydda "
"användarna."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"In such instances, communication with the operator is essential to determine "
"the appropriate course of action."
msgstr ""
"I sådana situationer är det viktigt att kommunicera med operatören för att "
"avgöra lämplig åtgärd."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"Relays are considered malicious if they engage in behaviors such as DNS "
"poisoning, SSL stripping, or sniffing user traffic."
msgstr ""
"Reläer betraktas som illasinnade om de till exempel ägnar sig åt DNS-"
"förgiftning, SSL-strippning eller avlyssning av användartrafik."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"The Network Health team is responsible for identifying and addressing these "
"issues."
msgstr ""
"Network Health-teamet ansvarar för att identifiera och hantera sådana "
"problem."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"The Tor network relies on the contributions of volunteer relay operators to "
"maintain its integrity and security."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverket är beroende av bidrag från frivilliga reläoperatörer för att "
"upprätthålla sin integritet och säkerhet."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"This collaborative effort helps maintain the integrity and security of the "
"Tor network for all users."
msgstr ""
"Det gemensamma arbetet hjälper till att upprätthålla Tor-nätverkets "
"integritet och säkerhet för alla användare."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"Unlike misconfigured relays, malicious relays are not contacted before "
"removal."
msgstr ""
"Till skillnad från felkonfigurerade reläer kontaktas illasinnade reläers "
"operatörer inte innan reläerna tas bort."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid ""
"We encourage users to [report bad relays](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"network-health/team/-/wikis/Criteria-for-rejecting-bad-relays#reporting-bad-"
"relays) to the Bad Relays mailing list, providing detailed information to "
"aid in investigation and resolution."
msgstr ""
"Vi uppmuntrar användare att [rapportera dåliga reläer](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/team/-/wikis/Criteria-for-rejecting-"
"bad-relays#reporting-bad-relays) till e-postlistan Bad Relays och lämna "
"utförlig information som underlättar utredning och åtgärder."

#: content/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/rejecting-bad-relays-criteria/
msgid "Criteria for Rejecting Bad Relays"
msgstr "Kriterier för att avvisa dåliga reläer"

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/
msgid ""
"By following these policies and actively participating in the proposal "
"process, relay operators can contribute to the security, reliability, and "
"integrity of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Genom att följa policyerna och aktivt delta i förslagsprocessen kan "
"reläoperatörer bidra till Tor-nätverkets säkerhet, tillförlitlighet och "
"integritet."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/
msgid ""
"Policies refer to the rules, guidelines, and best practices that govern the "
"operation of Tor relays and relay operators."
msgstr ""
"Policyer avser regler, riktlinjer och bästa praxis som styr driften av Tor-"
"reläer och reläoperatörernas arbete."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/
msgid ""
"These policies cover various aspects of relay operation, including security, "
"performance, privacy, Tor's network health, and community."
msgstr ""
"Policyerna omfattar olika delar av relädriften, bland annat säkerhet, "
"prestanda, integritet, Tor-nätverkets hälsa och gemenskapen."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/
msgid "Policies and Proposals"
msgstr "Policyer och förslag"

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/
msgid ""
"**[Read our directory authority expectations](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/dir-auth/dir_auth_expectations/) and what "
"the Directory Authorities currently commit to [when dealing with bad relays]"
"(https://community.torproject.org/policies/dir-auth/bad-"
"relays_status_quo/).**"
msgstr ""
"**[Läs våra förväntningar på katalogauktoriteter](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/dir-auth/dir_auth_expectations/) och vad "
"katalogauktoriteterna för närvarande åtar sig [vid hantering av dåliga "
"reläer](https://community.torproject.org/policies/dir-auth/bad-"
"relays_status_quo/).**"

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/
msgid "Directory Authorities"
msgstr "Katalogauktoriteter"

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/
msgid ""
"Directory Authorities are important components within the Tor network that "
"serve as trusted entities responsible for managing and maintaining the list "
"of Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"Katalogauktoriteter är viktiga komponenter i Tor-nätverket och fungerar som "
"betrodda enheter som ansvarar för att hantera och underhålla listan över Tor-"
"reläer."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/
msgid ""
"These authorities are operated by trusted organizations or individuals with "
"a strong commitment to the principles of privacy, security, and network "
"neutrality."
msgstr ""
"Auktoriteterna drivs av betrodda organisationer eller personer med ett "
"starkt engagemang för principerna om integritet, säkerhet och nätneutralitet."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-authority/
msgid ""
"They are a set of specialized servers within the Tor network that "
"collectively generate and distribute a signed document (known as the "
"consensus) containing information about all known Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"De är en uppsättning specialiserade servrar i Tor-nätverket som gemensamt "
"skapar och distribuerar ett signerat dokument, kallat konsensus, med "
"information om alla kända Tor-reläer."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"A [past proposal](https://lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-relays/2020-"
"July/018643.html) suggested requiring physical addresses for verification "
"from relay operators."
msgstr ""
"Ett [tidigare förslag](https://lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-relays/"
"2020-July/018643.html) föreslog att reläoperatörer skulle behöva uppge en "
"fysisk adress för verifiering."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"Additionally, we evaluate proposals based on how well they meet our "
"[established criteria](https://community.torproject.org/policies/relays/"
"evaluation-criteria-for-solution-to-combat-malicious-relays/) for supporting "
"the relay operator community and achieving Tor's overall goals."
msgstr ""
"Dessutom bedömer vi förslag utifrån hur väl de uppfyller våra [fastställda "
"kriterier](https://community.torproject.org/policies/relays/evaluation-"
"criteria-for-solution-to-combat-malicious-relays/) för att stödja "
"reläoperatörsgemenskapen och uppnå Tors övergripande mål."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"But, on the other hand, a small increase in the entry requirements for "
"running relays could also make the network more secure by keeping out bad "
"actors."
msgstr ""
"Å andra sidan kan en liten höjning av tröskeln för att driva reläer också "
"göra nätverket säkrare genom att hålla illasinnade aktörer borta."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"By being open about our decision-making and actions, we aim to foster trust "
"with the Tor community so they can rely on us to safeguard their privacy and "
"security."
msgstr ""
"Genom att vara öppna med våra beslut och åtgärder vill vi skapa förtroende i "
"Tor-gemenskapen så att den kan lita på att vi skyddar användarnas integritet "
"och säkerhet."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"By making the policy public, the Tor community can hold us accountable for "
"its enforcement."
msgstr ""
"När policyn är offentlig kan Tor-gemenskapen hålla oss ansvariga för hur den "
"tillämpas."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"Every proposal is carefully reviewed to check that it aligns with all our "
"community values, as outlined in Tor's [Code of Conduct](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/code_of_conduct/) and [Social Contract]"
"(https://community.torproject.org/policies/social_contract/)."
msgstr ""
"Varje förslag granskas noggrant för att säkerställa att det överensstämmer "
"med alla våra gemenskapsvärderingar, såsom de beskrivs i Tors [uppförandekod]"
"(https://community.torproject.org/policies/code_of_conduct/) och [sociala "
"kontrakt](https://community.torproject.org/policies/social_contract/)."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"For example, our [criteria for rejecting bad relays](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/team/-/wikis/Criteria-for-rejecting-"
"bad-relays) policy defines what qualifies as a malicious relay, and details "
"the steps we take to identify and remove them."
msgstr ""
"Vår policy med [kriterier för att avvisa dåliga reläer](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/team/-/wikis/Criteria-for-rejecting-"
"bad-relays) definierar till exempel vad som räknas som ett illasinnat relä "
"och beskriver de åtgärder vi vidtar för att identifiera och ta bort sådana "
"reläer."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"For example, we want to keep the barrier for running relays low and build a "
"transparent network."
msgstr ""
"Vi vill till exempel hålla tröskeln för att driva reläer låg och bygga ett "
"transparent nätverk."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"For instance, while a proposal might be technically sound, our evaluation "
"criteria go deeper to assess its practicality for relay operators and "
"potential impact on the network's overall health (\"will-it-work\")."
msgstr ""
"Även om ett förslag är tekniskt välgrundat går våra bedömningskriterier "
"längre och bedömer dess praktiska genomförbarhet för reläoperatörer och "
"möjliga påverkan på nätverkets övergripande hälsa – ”kommer det att "
"fungera?”."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"If you’re interested in [submitting a proposal](/relay/governance/policies-"
"and-proposals/proposals), please review [our policies](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/) to understand the principles that govern "
"relays and the relay operator community."
msgstr ""
"Om du är intresserad av att [lämna in ett förslag](/relay/governance/"
"policies-and-proposals/proposals) bör du läsa [våra policyer](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/) för att förstå principerna som styr "
"reläerna och reläoperatörsgemenskapen."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"Keeping user information private and the network secure can be tricky when "
"we also want to be open and accountable, but our evaluation criteria check "
"that we’re on the right path."
msgstr ""
"Det kan vara svårt att hålla användaruppgifter privata och nätverket säkert "
"samtidigt som vi vill vara öppna och ansvariga, men bedömningskriterierna "
"hjälper oss att kontrollera att vi är på rätt väg."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"On top of that, we establish clear and publicly accessible rules and "
"policies to govern specific situations and behaviours. These rules and "
"policies outline what a violation is, and the corresponding actions we take."
msgstr ""
"Utöver detta fastställer vi tydliga och offentligt tillgängliga regler och "
"policyer för särskilda situationer och beteenden. De beskriver vad som utgör "
"en överträdelse och vilka åtgärder vi vidtar."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"One key way we’re delivering this transparency is by making all proposed "
"network health enhancements public knowledge, easy to find, and clear to "
"understand."
msgstr ""
"Ett viktigt sätt att skapa denna transparens är att göra alla föreslagna "
"förbättringar av nätverkets hälsa offentligt kända, lätta att hitta och "
"tydliga att förstå."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"Rather, following our evaluation criteria, we explored [alternative "
"verification methods](https://lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-relays/2023-"
"October/021358.html) that could be less intrusive for the operator community."
msgstr ""
"I enlighet med våra bedömningskriterier undersökte vi i stället [alternativa "
"verifieringsmetoder](https://lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-relays/2023-"
"October/021358.html) som kan vara mindre ingripande för operatörsgemenskapen."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"That's why we created the evaluation criteria; to carefully examine these "
"security concerns without overloading relay operators."
msgstr ""
"Det är därför vi skapade bedömningskriterierna: för att noggrant undersöka "
"säkerhetsfrågorna utan att överbelasta reläoperatörerna."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"The [evaluation criteria for proposals](https://community.torproject.org/"
"policies/relays/evaluation-criteria-for-solution-to-combat-malicious-"
"relays/) are built on some important goals: keeping it easy to set up "
"relays, protecting the network from bad actors, respecting human rights, and "
"following Tor's values of transparency and accountability."
msgstr ""
"[Bedömningskriterierna för förslag](https://community.torproject.org/"
"policies/relays/evaluation-criteria-for-solution-to-combat-malicious-"
"relays/) bygger på flera viktiga mål: att göra det enkelt att konfigurera "
"reläer, skydda nätverket mot illasinnade aktörer, respektera mänskliga "
"rättigheter och följa Tors värderingar om transparens och ansvar."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"The criteria for reviewing proposals go beyond looking at technical "
"feasibility, because we prioritize will-it-work over can-it-work."
msgstr ""
"Kriterierna för att granska förslag går längre än teknisk genomförbarhet, "
"eftersom vi prioriterar om något kommer att fungera framför om det kan "
"fungera."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"These criteria help us keep the Tor network inclusive, safe, and principled."
msgstr ""
"Kriterierna hjälper oss att hålla Tor-nätverket inkluderande, säkert och "
"principfast."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"These criteria serve as a rulebook for any improvements to the relays and "
"processes for people who run them."
msgstr ""
"Kriterierna fungerar som ett regelverk för förbättringar av reläerna och "
"processerna för dem som driver reläer."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"This helps us make sure we don't overburden operators or introduce "
"unintended privacy risks."
msgstr ""
"Det hjälper oss att se till att operatörerna inte överbelastas och att vi "
"inte skapar oavsiktliga integritetsrisker."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"This process helps us maintain a strong and reliable network, with a "
"community of operators who are invested in transparency."
msgstr ""
"Processen hjälper oss att upprätthålla ett starkt och tillförlitligt nätverk "
"med en operatörsgemenskap som värdesätter transparens."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"Though before we set any goals or policies, we try to verify that one set of "
"goals does not negatively impact the other."
msgstr ""
"Innan vi fastställer mål eller policyer försöker vi dock kontrollera att en "
"uppsättning mål inte påverkar en annan negativt."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"Users and operators can monitor how the policy is applied and raise concerns "
"if they believe relays are being unfairly targeted."
msgstr ""
"Användare och operatörer kan följa hur policyn tillämpas och uttrycka oro om "
"de anser att reläer behandlas orättvist."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"We recognize the potential conflicts between our goals for relay operators "
"and our broader goals of user privacy and security."
msgstr ""
"Vi är medvetna om möjliga konflikter mellan våra mål för reläoperatörer och "
"våra bredare mål om användarnas integritet och säkerhet."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"We try to extend our commitment to transparency and accountability across "
"all our processes."
msgstr ""
"Vi försöker låta vårt åtagande om transparens och ansvar genomsyra alla "
"processer."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid ""
"While transparency is a core value, we recognize the potential challenges. "
"We keep our methods for finding suspicious activity as open as we can, even "
"though it might give attackers some insights."
msgstr ""
"Även om transparens är ett kärnvärde är vi medvetna om de möjliga "
"utmaningarna. Vi håller våra metoder för att hitta misstänkt aktivitet så "
"öppna som möjligt, trots att det kan ge angripare viss insyn."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposal-evaluation-criteria/
msgid "Evaluation Criteria for Proposals"
msgstr "Bedömningskriterier för förslag"

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid ""
"Historically, the management of the Tor relay operator community was "
"informal, depending on interactions among [relay operators](../../relay-"
"operators/becoming-relay-operator), [Directory Authorities](../directory-"
"authority), and Tor Project staff during meetups."
msgstr ""
"Historiskt har hanteringen av Tor-reläoperatörsgemenskapen varit informell "
"och byggt på samspel mellan [reläoperatörer](../../relay-operators/becoming-"
"relay-operator), [katalogauktoriteter](../directory-authority) och personal "
"från The Tor Project under sammankomster."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid ""
"However, as the community has grown and become more diverse, a structured "
"process is necessary to evaluate and implement proposals systematically."
msgstr ""
"I takt med att gemenskapen har vuxit och blivit mer mångsidig behövs dock en "
"strukturerad process för att systematiskt bedöma och genomföra förslag."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid ""
"Learn more about the [process for new policies and proposals for the Tor "
"relay operator community](https://community.torproject.org/policies/relays/"
"001-community-relay-operator-process/)."
msgstr ""
"Läs mer om [processen för nya policyer och förslag för Tor-"
"reläoperatörsgemenskapen](https://community.torproject.org/policies/relays/"
"001-community-relay-operator-process/)."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid "The following are sample proposal formats you can use to get started."
msgstr ""
"Nedan finns exempel på förslagsformat som du kan använda för att komma igång."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid ""
"The proposals for relay operators are focused on operational, policy, and "
"community-related aspects specific to the relay operator community, "
"contrasting with the technical specifications covered by [Tor specifications]"
"(https://spec.torproject.org/) (aka torspec)."
msgstr ""
"Förslagen för reläoperatörer fokuserar på drifts-, policy- och "
"gemenskapsfrågor som är specifika för reläoperatörsgemenskapen, till "
"skillnad från de tekniska specifikationerna i [Tor-specifikationerna]"
"(https://spec.torproject.org/), även kallade torspec."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid ""
"The proposals undergo a thorough review process involving drafting, "
"community consensus, and final approval by the proposal editors, ensuring "
"they align with the Tor Project's policies and operational goals."
msgstr ""
"Förslagen genomgår en grundlig granskningsprocess med utarbetande, konsensus "
"i gemenskapen och slutligt godkännande av förslagsredaktörerna, så att de "
"överensstämmer med The Tor Projects policyer och driftsmål."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid ""
"Topics include security measures against malicious relays, expectations for "
"relay operators, sustainability, and guidelines for investigating and "
"removing malicious actors."
msgstr ""
"Ämnena omfattar säkerhetsåtgärder mot illasinnade reläer, förväntningar på "
"reläoperatörer, hållbarhet samt riktlinjer för att utreda och avlägsna "
"illasinnade aktörer."

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid ""
"[Expectations for relay operators](https://community.torproject.org/policies/"
"relays/expectations-for-relay-operators/)"
msgstr ""
"[Förväntningar på reläoperatörer](https://community.torproject.org/policies/"
"relays/expectations-for-relay-operators/)"

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid ""
"[[tor-relays] Process for new policies and proposals for the Tor relay "
"operator community](https://community.torproject.org/policies/relays/001-"
"community-relay-operator-process/)"
msgstr ""
"[[tor-relays] Process för nya policyer och förslag för Tor-"
"reläoperatörsgemenskapen](https://community.torproject.org/policies/relays/"
"001-community-relay-operator-process/)"

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid ""
"[[tor-relays] Proposal: Restrict ContactInfo to Mandatory Email Address]"
"(https://lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-relays/2023-October/021358.html)"
msgstr ""
"[[tor-relays] Förslag: Begränsa ContactInfo till en obligatorisk e-"
"postadress](https://lists.torproject.org/pipermail/tor-relays/2023-October/"
"021358.html)"

#: content/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/proposals/
msgid "New policies and proposals for the Tor relay operator community"
msgstr "Nya policyer och förslag för Tor-reläoperatörsgemenskapen"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"**Read our [Expectations for Relay Operators](../relay-operator-"
"expectations) guide for more detail on what it means to be a good relay "
"operator.**"
msgstr ""
"**Läs vår vägledning om [förväntningar på reläoperatörer](../relay-operator-"
"expectations) för mer information om vad det innebär att vara en bra "
"reläoperatör.**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "1. **Understand the basics of Tor**"
msgstr "1. **Förstå grunderna i Tor**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "2. **Assess your resources**"
msgstr "2. **Bedöm dina resurser**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "3. **Choose your relay type**"
msgstr "3. **Välj relätyp**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "4. **Set up your relay**"
msgstr "4. **Konfigurera reläet**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "5. **Configure Bandwidth and Security Settings**"
msgstr "5. **Konfigurera bandbredds- och säkerhetsinställningar**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "6. **Monitor and Maintain Your Relay**"
msgstr "6. **Övervaka och underhåll reläet**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "7. **Join the Community**"
msgstr "7. **Gå med i gemenskapen**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "8. **Spread the Word**"
msgstr "8. **Sprid informationen**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"Additionally, you'll want to configure security settings to protect your "
"relay from potential attacks and abuse."
msgstr ""
"Dessutom bör du konfigurera säkerhetsinställningar som skyddar reläet mot "
"möjliga angrepp och missbruk."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"As a Tor relay operator, you're part of a global community dedicated to "
"promoting online privacy and freedom."
msgstr ""
"Som Tor-reläoperatör ingår du i en global gemenskap som arbetar för "
"integritet och frihet på nätet."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"As a relay operator, you can configure the bandwidth limits for your relay "
"to ensure it doesn't overwhelm your internet connection."
msgstr ""
"Som reläoperatör kan du ställa in bandbreddsgränser för reläet så att det "
"inte överbelastar internetanslutningen."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"As a relay operator, you can either run an exit relay or a non-exit relay "
"because you cannot operate middle relays alone."
msgstr ""
"Som reläoperatör kan du antingen driva ett utgångsrelä eller ett icke-"
"utgångsrelä, eftersom du inte kan driva enbart mellanreläer."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"At the heart of the Tor network are volunteer-operated relays, which help "
"anonymize and route user traffic."
msgstr ""
"Kärnan i Tor-nätverket är reläer som drivs av volontärer och hjälper till "
"att anonymisera och dirigera användartrafik."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"Becoming a Tor relay operator is a rewarding way to contribute to online "
"privacy and freedom."
msgstr ""
"Att bli Tor-reläoperatör är ett givande sätt att bidra till integritet och "
"frihet på nätet."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"Before diving into becoming a relay operator, it's important that you have a "
"basic understanding of how the Tor network functions."
msgstr ""
"Innan du bestämmer dig för att bli reläoperatör är det viktigt att du har en "
"grundläggande förståelse för hur Tor-nätverket fungerar."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"By following these steps, you can become a valuable contributor to the Tor "
"community and play an important role in  safeguarding online privacy and "
"freedom for users around the world."
msgstr ""
"Genom att följa stegen kan du bli en värdefull bidragsgivare till Tor-"
"gemenskapen och spela en viktig roll för att skydda integritet och frihet på "
"nätet för användare världen över."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"Decide which type of relay you want to operate based on your resources and "
"preferences."
msgstr ""
"Bestäm vilken typ av relä du vill driva utifrån dina resurser och önskemål."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"Encourage others to become relay operators or support the Tor project in "
"other ways."
msgstr ""
"Uppmuntra andra att bli reläoperatörer eller stödja The Tor Project på andra "
"sätt."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "Here's a step-by-step guide to help you get started:"
msgstr "Här är en steg-för-steg-vägledning som hjälper dig att komma igång:"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"If you decide to become a relay operator, make sure you meet the "
"requirements, have some technical expertise, and some time to maintain the "
"relay."
msgstr ""
"Om du bestämmer dig för att bli reläoperatör bör du se till att du uppfyller "
"kraven, har viss teknisk sakkunskap och kan avsätta tid för att underhålla "
"reläet."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"Joining the Tor community allows you to connect with other relay operators, "
"share knowledge and experiences, and contribute to the ongoing development "
"of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Genom att gå med i Tor-gemenskapen kan du komma i kontakt med andra "
"reläoperatörer, dela kunskap och erfarenheter och bidra till Tor-nätverkets "
"fortsatta utveckling."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"Lastly, help raise awareness about the importance of the Tor network and the "
"role of relay operators in maintaining its integrity."
msgstr ""
"Hjälp slutligen till att öka medvetenheten om Tor-nätverkets betydelse och "
"reläoperatörernas roll för att bevara dess integritet."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"Once you've chosen the type of relay you want to operate, you'll need to "
"[configure the relay](../../../setup/) on an operating system you’re "
"comfortable with managing."
msgstr ""
"När du har valt relätyp behöver du [konfigurera reläet](../../../setup/) på "
"ett operativsystem som du känner dig bekväm med att administrera."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "Operating a Tor relay is an ongoing commitment."
msgstr "Att driva ett Tor-relä är ett fortlöpande åtagande."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"There are [three types of relays](../../../types-of-relays/) in the Tor "
"network: entry relays, middle relays, and exit relays."
msgstr ""
"Det finns [tre typer av reläer](../../../types-of-relays/) i Tor-nätverket: "
"ingångsreläer, mellanreläer och utgångsreläer."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"To operate a Tor relay, there are [technical requirements and resources]"
"(../../../relays-requirements/) that you’ll need."
msgstr ""
"För att driva ett Tor-relä behöver du uppfylla vissa [tekniska krav och ha "
"tillräckliga resurser](../../../relays-requirements/)."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"You can follow the [instructions](../../../setup/) carefully to ensure your "
"relay is set up securely and correctly."
msgstr ""
"Följ [anvisningarna](../../../setup/) noggrant för att säkerställa att "
"reläet konfigureras säkert och korrekt."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"You can read through our documentation and try routing traffic through the "
"Tor network using the Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"Du kan läsa dokumentationen och prova att dirigera trafik genom Tor-"
"nätverket med Tor Browser."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid ""
"You'll need to monitor your relay regularly to ensure it's running smoothly "
"and efficiently. This includes checking for software updates, monitoring "
"bandwidth usage, and addressing any issues that may arise."
msgstr ""
"Du behöver regelbundet övervaka reläet för att säkerställa att det fungerar "
"stabilt och effektivt. Det innebär bland annat att söka efter "
"programuppdateringar, följa bandbreddsanvändningen och åtgärda problem som "
"uppstår."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/becoming-relay-operator/
msgid "Becoming a Relay Operator"
msgstr "Bli reläoperatör"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/
msgid ""
"In the past, our approach to organizing the Tor relay operator community "
"relied heavily on the informal dynamics between [relay operators](becoming-"
"relay-operator), [Directory Authorities](../policies-and-proposals/directory-"
"authority), and The Tor Project staff."
msgstr ""
"Tidigare byggde vårt sätt att organisera Tor-reläoperatörsgemenskapen i hög "
"grad på det informella samspelet mellan [reläoperatörer](becoming-relay-"
"operator), [katalogauktoriteter](../policies-and-proposals/directory-"
"authority) och personal från The Tor Project."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/
msgid ""
"Now, through discussions and interactions in meetups and similar events, we "
"collaborate with operators to determine best practices for managing Tor "
"relays."
msgstr ""
"Nu samarbetar vi genom diskussioner och möten med operatörerna för att "
"fastställa bästa praxis för hantering av Tor-reläer."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/
msgid ""
"Operating a relay involves running specialized software that routes "
"encrypted traffic through a series of relays, protecting user privacy and "
"security."
msgstr ""
"Att driva ett relä innebär att köra specialiserad programvara som dirigerar "
"krypterad trafik genom en serie reläer och skyddar användarnas integritet "
"och säkerhet."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/
msgid ""
"Relay operators contribute valuable bandwidth and computing resources to the "
"network, enabling Tor users to access the internet anonymously."
msgstr ""
"Reläoperatörer bidrar med värdefull bandbredd och datorkapacitet till "
"nätverket, vilket gör att Tor-användare kan komma åt internet anonymt."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/
msgid ""
"Relay operators form the backbone of the Tor network, facilitating anonymous "
"and secure internet browsing for users worldwide."
msgstr ""
"Reläoperatörerna utgör Tor-nätverkets ryggrad och möjliggör anonym och säker "
"surfning för användare världen över."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/
msgid ""
"This is beneficial to both user safety and the continued effectiveness of "
"[Directory Authorities](../policies-and-proposals/directory-authority) and "
"The Tor Project."
msgstr ""
"Det gynnar både användarnas säkerhet och den fortsatta effektiviteten hos "
"[katalogauktoriteterna](../policies-and-proposals/directory-authority) och "
"The Tor Project."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/
msgid "Relay Operators"
msgstr "Reläoperatörer"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/
msgid ""
"**See the [full expectations for relay operators](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/relays/expectations-for-relay-"
"operators/).**"
msgstr ""
"**Läs de [fullständiga förväntningarna på reläoperatörer](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/relays/expectations-for-relay-"
"operators/).**"

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/
msgid ""
"If questions about adherence to these expectations come up, our [community "
"policies](https://community.torproject.org/policies/) provide a framework "
"for decision-making and enforcement within the Tor community."
msgstr ""
"Om det uppstår frågor om hur förväntningarna följs ger våra "
"[gemenskapspolicyer](https://community.torproject.org/policies/) ett ramverk "
"för beslut och efterlevnad inom Tor-gemenskapen."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/
msgid ""
"Operators must prioritize user anonymity and security, maintain good "
"operational practices, and align their activities with Tor's values and "
"mission."
msgstr ""
"Operatörer måste prioritera användarnas anonymitet och säkerhet, "
"upprätthålla goda driftsrutiner och se till att deras verksamhet "
"överensstämmer med Tors värderingar och uppdrag."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/
msgid ""
"Relay operators play a crucial role in the health, safety, and "
"sustainability of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Reläoperatörer spelar en avgörande roll för Tor-nätverkets hälsa, säkerhet "
"och hållbarhet."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/
msgid "These expectations help maintain user trust, and network functionality."
msgstr ""
"Förväntningarna bidrar till att upprätthålla användarnas förtroende och "
"nätverkets funktion."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/
msgid ""
"This mutual commitment between the Tor Project and relay operators is vital "
"for the Tor network's continuous success."
msgstr ""
"Det ömsesidiga åtagandet mellan The Tor Project och reläoperatörerna är "
"avgörande för Tor-nätverkets fortsatta framgång."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/
msgid ""
"While they generously invest their time, energy, and resources to support "
"the network, it is essential to have clear expectations to ensure the "
"integrity and security of the entire system."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom de frivilligt investerar tid, energi och resurser för att stödja "
"nätverket är det viktigt med tydliga förväntningar för att säkerställa hela "
"systemets integritet och säkerhet."

#: content/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/relay-operators/relay-operator-expectations/
msgid "Expectations for Relay Operators"
msgstr "Förväntningar på reläoperatörer"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"**Ideally a relay runs on an unmetered plan** or includes 2 TB/month or more."
msgstr ""
"**Helst bör reläet köras med ett abonnemang utan datagräns** eller med minst "
"2 TB per månad."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"A <40 Mbit/s non-exit relay should have at least 512 MB of RAM available."
msgstr ""
"Ett icke-utgångsrelä med en hastighet under 40 Mbit/s bör ha minst 512 MB "
"tillgängligt RAM-minne."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"A non-exit relay faster than 40 Mbit/s should have at least 1 GB of RAM."
msgstr ""
"Ett icke-utgångsrelä som är snabbare än 40 Mbit/s bör ha minst 1 GB RAM-"
"minne."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"A non-exit relay should be able to handle at least 7000 concurrent "
"connections."
msgstr ""
"Ett icke-utgångsrelä bör kunna hantera minst 7 000 samtidiga anslutningar."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"A typical Tor relay needs less than 200 MB for Tor related data (in addition "
"to the operating system itself)."
msgstr ""
"Ett typiskt Tor-relä behöver mindre än 200 MB för Tor-relaterade data, "
"utöver själva operativsystemet."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Able to handle at least 7000 concurrent connections."
msgstr "Kan hantera minst 7 000 samtidiga anslutningar."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Additional IPv6 connectivity is great and recommended/encouraged but not a "
"requirement."
msgstr "IPv6-anslutning är mycket bra och rekommenderas, men är inget krav."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"An IPv4 address (can be dynamic or static (preferred) as long as it stays "
"the same for at least 3 hours)."
msgstr ""
"En IPv4-adress som kan vara dynamisk eller, helst, statisk, så länge den "
"förblir densamma i minst tre timmar."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Any modern CPU should be fine."
msgstr "Vilken modern processor som helst bör fungera."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "At least 1 Mbit/s of upstream and downstream bandwidth."
msgstr "Minst 1 Mbit/s bandbredd både uppströms och nedströms."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "At least 1.5 GB of RAM recommended."
msgstr "Minst 1,5 GB RAM-minne rekommenderas."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "At least 200 MB of disk storage."
msgstr "Minst 200 MB lagringsutrymme."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"At least 512 MB of RAM if the relay is slower than 40 Mbps or 1 GB of RAM if "
"faster than 40 Mbps."
msgstr ""
"Minst 512 MB RAM-minne om reläet är långsammare än 40 Mbit/s, eller 1 GB om "
"det är snabbare än 40 Mbit/s."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Bandwidth and Connections"
msgstr "Bandbredd och anslutningar"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Bridge relay:"
msgstr "Brorelä:"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "CPU"
msgstr "CPU"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Disk Storage"
msgstr "Lagringsutrymme"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Do not run an exit relay from your home."
msgstr "Driv inte ett utgångsrelä hemifrån."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Every relay needs a public IPv4 address - either directly on the host "
"(preferred) or via NAT and port forwarding."
msgstr ""
"Varje relä behöver en offentlig IPv4-adress, antingen direkt på värddatorn "
"(rekommenderas) eller via NAT och portvidarebefordran."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Exit relay:"
msgstr "Utgångsrelä:"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Fast exit relays (>=100 Mbit/s) usually have to handle a lot more concurrent "
"connections (>100k)."
msgstr ""
"Snabba utgångsreläer (≥100 Mbit/s) behöver vanligtvis hantera betydligt fler "
"samtidiga anslutningar (>100 000)."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"For security reasons, Tor relays should not downgrade their tor version from "
"a supported to an unsupported version of tor. Some unsupported versions are "
"insecure. Relays that attempt to downgrade to an insecure version will be "
"rejected from the network automatically."
msgstr ""
"Av säkerhetsskäl bör Tor-reläer inte nedgradera sin Tor-version från en "
"version som stöds till en version som inte stöds. Vissa versioner som inte "
"stöds är osäkra. Reläer som försöker nedgradera till en osäker version "
"avvisas automatiskt från nätverket."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Guard/Middle relay:"
msgstr "Vakt-/mellanrelä:"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Have at least 10 Mbit/s (16 Mbit/s recommended) of upstream and downstream "
"bandwidth."
msgstr ""
"Ha minst 10 Mbit/s (16 Mbit/s rekommenderas) bandbredd både uppströms och "
"nedströms."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Ideal uptime is 24/7 but relays should be up for more than 2 hours a day."
msgstr ""
"Helst bör reläet vara igång dygnet runt, men det bör åtminstone köras mer än "
"två timmar per dag."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Ideally the relay runs on a server which runs 24/7."
msgstr "Helst körs reläet på en server som är igång dygnet runt."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"If the file `/proc/cpuinfo` contains the word aes your CPU has support for "
"AES-NI."
msgstr ""
"Om filen `/proc/cpuinfo` innehåller ordet aes har processorn stöd för AES-NI."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"If you do not know your bandwidth you can use http://beta.speedtest.net to "
"measure it."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte känner till din bandbredd kan du mäta den med http://"
"beta.speedtest.net."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/
msgid ""
"If you don't meet the requirements to run a Tor relay or obfs4 bridge, "
"running a Snowflake proxy is a great way to donate your bandwidth to help "
"users circumvent censorship."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte uppfyller kraven för att driva ett Tor-relä eller en obfs4-bro är "
"en Snowflake-proxy ett utmärkt sätt att bidra med bandbredd och hjälpa "
"användare att kringgå censur."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"If you have a metered plan you might want to configure tor to only use a "
"given amount of [bandwidth or monthly traffic](../setup/post-install/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du har ett abonnemang med datagräns kan du konfigurera Tor så att endast "
"en viss mängd [bandbredd eller månatlig trafik](../setup/post-install/) "
"används."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"If you have less than 10 Mbit/s but at least 1 Mbit/s we recommend you run a "
"[bridge with obfs4 support](../setup/bridge/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du har mindre än 10 Mbit/s men minst 1 Mbit/s rekommenderar vi att du "
"driver en [bro med stöd för obfs4](../setup/bridge/)."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"If you run it behind a consumer-level router at home you will have to try "
"and see if your home router can handle it or if it starts failing."
msgstr ""
"Om du kör reläet bakom en vanlig hemrouter behöver du prova om routern "
"klarar belastningen eller börjar sluta fungera."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"If you want to run more than eight relays you will need more IPv4 addresses."
msgstr "Om du vill driva fler än åtta reläer behöver du fler IPv4-adresser."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "In Summary"
msgstr "Sammanfattning"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"In a position to handle legal notices and potential law enforcement inquiry."
msgstr ""
"Kan hantera juridiska meddelanden och eventuella förfrågningar från "
"brottsbekämpande myndigheter."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"It is recommended that a relay have at least 16 Mbit/s (Mbps) upload "
"bandwidth and 16 Mbit/s (Mbps) download bandwidth available for Tor. More is "
"better."
msgstr ""
"Ett relä rekommenderas ha minst 16 Mbit/s (Mbps) tillgänglig "
"uppladdningsbandbredd och 16 Mbit/s (Mbps) nedladdningsbandbredd. Mer är "
"bättre."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"It is recommended to use CPUs with AESNI support (that will improve "
"performance and allow for up to about ~400-450 Mbps in each direction on a "
"single tor instance on modern CPUs)."
msgstr ""
"Processorer med stöd för AES-NI rekommenderas. Det förbättrar prestandan och "
"kan med moderna processorer ge upp till cirka 400–450 Mbit/s i vardera "
"riktningen för en enskild Tor-instans."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"It is required that a Tor relay be allowed to use a minimum of 100 GByte of "
"outbound traffic (and the same amount of incoming traffic) per month."
msgstr ""
"Ett Tor-relä måste få använda minst 100 GB utgående trafik och lika mycket "
"inkommande trafik per månad."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Memory Requirements"
msgstr "Minneskrav"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Monthly Outbound Traffic"
msgstr "Utgående trafik per månad"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "More (>2 TB/month) is better and recommended."
msgstr "Mer än 2 TB per månad är bättre och rekommenderas."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Must be able to donate at least 100 GByte of traffic a month (ideally 2 TB "
"or more)."
msgstr ""
"Måste kunna bidra med minst 100 GB trafik per månad, helst 2 TB eller mer."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Note: That is only about 1 day worth of traffic on a 10 Mbit/s (Mbps) "
"connection."
msgstr ""
"Obs! Det motsvarar bara ungefär ett dygns trafik med en anslutning på 10 "
"Mbit/s (Mbps)."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Note: You can only run [eight Tor relays](https://lists.torproject.org/"
"pipermail/tor-relays/2023-June/021226.html) per public IPv4 address."
msgstr ""
"Obs! Du kan endast köra [åtta Tor-reläer](https://lists.torproject.org/"
"pipermail/tor-relays/2023-June/021226.html) per offentlig IPv4-adress."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "On an exit relay we recommend at least 1.5 GB of RAM per tor instance."
msgstr ""
"För ett utgångsrelä rekommenderar vi minst 1,5 GB RAM-minne per Tor-instans."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Public IPv4 Address"
msgstr "Offentlig IPv4-adress"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Reboots and tor daemon restarts are fine."
msgstr "Omstarter av datorn och Tor-demonen går bra."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Requirements for Tor relays depend on the type of relay and the bandwidth "
"they provide."
msgstr ""
"Kraven för Tor-reläer beror på relätypen och hur mycket bandbredd de "
"tillhandahåller."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Should be able to handle around 100,000 concurrent connections if faster "
"than 100 Mbit/s."
msgstr ""
"Bör kunna hantera omkring 100 000 samtidiga anslutningar om det är snabbare "
"än 100 Mbit/s."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Similar requirements to a Guard/Middle relay plus"
msgstr "Samma krav som för ett vakt-/mellanrelä, samt följande:"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"The IPv4 address is not required to be static but static IP addresses are "
"preferred."
msgstr ""
"IPv4-adressen behöver inte vara statisk, men en statisk IP-adress "
"rekommenderas."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "The minimum requirements for a relay are 10 Mbit/s (Mbps)."
msgstr "Minimikravet för ett relä är 10 Mbit/s (Mbps)."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"There should be no problem at all with this requirement (all commercially "
"available servers come with at least one IPv4 address)."
msgstr ""
"Det här kravet bör inte innebära några problem, eftersom alla kommersiellt "
"tillgängliga servrar har minst en IPv4-adress."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"This can overwhelm consumer-level routers. If you run the Tor relay from a "
"server (virtual or dedicated) in a data center you will be fine."
msgstr ""
"Det kan överbelasta vanliga hemroutrar. Om du kör Tor-reläet på en virtuell "
"eller dedikerad server i ett datacenter fungerar det bra."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Tor Version"
msgstr "Tor-version"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Tor does not need much disk storage."
msgstr "Tor behöver inte mycket lagringsutrymme."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Tor has no hard uptime requirement but if your relay is not running for more "
"than 2 hours a day its usefulness is limited."
msgstr ""
"Tor har inget strikt drifttidskrav, men om reläet körs mindre än två timmar "
"per dag är nyttan begränsad."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Uptime"
msgstr "Upptid"

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Your IPv4 address should remain unchanged for at least 3 hours (if it "
"regularly changes more often than that, it does not make much sense to run a "
"relay or bridge there since it takes time to distribute the new list of "
"relay IPs to clients - which happens only once every hour)."
msgstr ""
"IPv4-adressen bör förbli oförändrad i minst tre timmar. Om den regelbundet "
"ändras oftare än så är det inte särskilt meningsfullt att driva ett relä "
"eller en bro där, eftersom det tar tid att distribuera den nya listan över "
"reläernas IP-adresser till klienterna och detta endast sker en gång i timmen."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid ""
"Requirements for Tor relays depend on the type of relay and the bandwidth "
"they provide. Learn more about specific relay requirements."
msgstr ""
"Kraven för Tor-reläer beror på relätypen och den bandbredd de "
"tillhandahåller. Läs mer om kraven för olika relätyper."

#: content/relay/relays-requirements/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/relays-requirements/
msgid "Relay requirements"
msgstr "Krav för reläer"

#: content/relay/setup/bridge/alpine/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/bridge/debian-ubuntu/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/bridge/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
