#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid "**Debian and Ubuntu:**"
msgstr "**Debian och Ubuntu:**"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/
msgid "1. Install the required packages"
msgstr "1. Installera de nödvändiga paketen"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid "2.  Edit the configuration file"
msgstr "2. Redigera konfigurationsfilen"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid "3. Automatically reboot"
msgstr "3. Starta om automatiskt"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid "4. Test"
msgstr "4. Testa"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid "If you just want to see the debug output but don't change anything use:"
msgstr "Om du bara vill se felsökningsutdata utan att ändra något använder du:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid ""
"If you want to automatically reboot add the following at the the end of the "
"file `/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/50unattended-upgrades`:"
msgstr ""
"Om du vill starta om automatiskt lägger du till följande längst ned i filen "
"`/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/50unattended-upgrades`:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid ""
"Put the lines below into the configuration file `/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/"
"50unattended-upgrades`, everything that was originally inside the generated "
"file can be removed before you add the lines below."
msgstr ""
"Lägg in raderna nedan i konfigurationsfilen `/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/"
"50unattended-upgrades`. Allt som ursprungligen fanns i den genererade filen "
"kan tas bort innan raderna läggs till."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid ""
"This assumes you will configure the Tor Project's package repository for "
"Debian/Ubuntu, which is documented **[here](https://support.torproject.org/"
"little-t-tor/getting-started/installing/)**."
msgstr ""
"Detta förutsätter att du konfigurerar The Tor Projects paketförråd för "
"Debian/Ubuntu enligt anvisningarna **[här](https://support.torproject.org/"
"little-t-tor/getting-started/installing/)**."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid ""
"Update the file `/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/20auto-upgrades` with the following "
"content"
msgstr ""
"Uppdatera filen `/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/20auto-upgrades` med följande innehåll"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid "You can test your unattended-upgrades setup with the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Du kan testa konfigurationen av unattended-upgrades med följande kommando:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/debian-ubuntu/updates/
msgid "Debian and Ubuntu"
msgstr "Debian och Ubuntu"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid "... or install an alpha release:"
msgstr "… eller installera en alfaversion:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid "2.1. Recommended Steps to Setup `pkg`"
msgstr "2.1. Rekommenderade steg för att konfigurera `pkg`"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/fedora/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/fedora/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid "5. Start the service"
msgstr "5. Starta tjänsten"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
msgid "DragonflyBSD has 2 packages repositories:"
msgstr "DragonFly BSD har två paketarkiv:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid ""
"Here we set `tor` to start at boot time and use the setuid feature, in order "
"to bind to lower ports like 443 (the daemon itself will still run as a "
"regular non-privileged user)."
msgstr ""
"Här konfigurerar vi `tor` så att det startas vid systemstart och använder "
"setuid-funktionen för att kunna binda till lägre portar, såsom 443. Själva "
"demonen körs fortfarande som en vanlig användare utan särskilda behörigheter."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
msgid ""
"Here, it will be similar to what we have on a **FreeBSD** system, and we are "
"going to use HTTPS to fetch our packages, and updates - so here we also need "
"an extra package to help us out (`ca_root_nss`)."
msgstr ""
"Det fungerar ungefär som på ett **FreeBSD**-system. Vi använder HTTPS för "
"att hämta paket och uppdateringar, så även här behövs ett extra paket "
"(`ca_root_nss`)."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/fedora/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/fedora/
msgid "Install the `tor` package:"
msgstr "Installera paketet `tor`:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
msgid "Put the configuration file `/usr/local/etc/tor/torrc` in place"
msgstr "Lägg konfigurationsfilen `/usr/local/etc/tor/torrc` på plats"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
msgid ""
"We can simply edit the **URL** used to point out the repositories on `/usr/"
"local/etc/pkg/repos/df-latest` and that's it! Remember to use **pkg+https://"
"** for Avalon."
msgstr ""
"Du behöver bara redigera den **URL** som pekar på arkiven i `/usr/local/etc/"
"pkg/repos/df-latest`. Kom ihåg att använda **pkg+https://** för Avalon."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/dragonflybsd/
msgid "How to deploy a Middle/Guard relay on DragonFlyBSD"
msgstr "Så distribuerar du ett mellan-/vaktrelä på DragonFly BSD"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/fedora/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/fedora/
msgid "How to deploy a Middle/Guard relay on Fedora"
msgstr "Så distribuerar du ett mellan-/vaktrelä på Fedora"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/fedora/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/fedora/updates/
msgid "Now enable and start automatic updates via:"
msgstr "Aktivera och starta nu automatiska uppdateringar med:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/fedora/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/fedora/updates/
msgid "On Fedora 43 and up, you can enable automatic updates via:"
msgstr "I Fedora 43 och senare kan du aktivera automatiska uppdateringar med:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid "5. Enable `net.inet.ip.random_id`"
msgstr "5. Aktivera `net.inet.ip.random_id`"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid "6. Start the service"
msgstr "6. Starta tjänsten"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid "Here we can choose to install the latest stable version, like:"
msgstr ""
"Här kan vi välja att installera den senaste stabila versionen, till exempel:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid "Install `tor` FreeBSD's package."
msgstr "Installera FreeBSD-paketet `tor`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid "Put the configuration file `/usr/local/etc/tor/torrc` in place:"
msgstr "Lägg konfigurationsfilen `/usr/local/etc/tor/torrc` på plats:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid ""
"So we set up a new directory, and then create a configuration file to "
"override what we need."
msgstr ""
"Skapa därför en ny mapp och sedan en konfigurationsfil som åsidosätter de "
"inställningar som behövs."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid ""
"This article assumes we have already a base installation of FreeBSD running, "
"and only the base system (here, we are running 12.2-RELEASE)."
msgstr ""
"Artikeln förutsätter att en grundinstallation av FreeBSD redan körs och att "
"endast grundsystemet är installerat. Här används 12.2-RELEASE."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid ""
"This configuration file will be `/usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/FreeBSD.conf`."
msgstr "Konfigurationsfilen blir `/usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/FreeBSD.conf`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid ""
"We are keeping the original setting used by `pkg` but setting a new one that "
"will override it."
msgstr ""
"Vi behåller den ursprungliga inställningen som används av `pkg`, men lägger "
"till en ny som åsidosätter den."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/
msgid "How to deploy a Middle/Guard relay on FreeBSD"
msgstr "Så distribuerar du ett mellan-/vaktrelä på FreeBSD"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
msgid ""
"**NOTE:** All steps documented on this page are considering that your server "
"is dedicated to provide a Tor (bridge/guard/exit) relay service. Please be "
"aware that _services will be restarted_ during the automatic software update "
"process documented here."
msgstr ""
"**OBS!** Alla steg på den här sidan förutsätter att servern är avsedd för en "
"Tor-relätjänst, såsom bro, vakt eller utgångsrelä. Tänk på att _tjänster "
"kommer att startas om_ under den automatiska programuppdateringsprocess som "
"beskrivs här."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid "1. Create the Update Script"
msgstr "1. Skapa uppdateringsskriptet"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
msgid "2. Schedule a `cron` Job"
msgstr "2. Schemalägg ett `cron`-jobb"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
msgid "3. Restart `cron`"
msgstr "3. Starta om `cron`"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"Finally, restart the `cron` daemon to make configuration changes be used."
msgstr ""
"Starta slutligen om demonen `cron` så att konfigurationsändringarna börjar "
"användas."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
msgid ""
"For this particular schedule we opt to run the script every 0h00 (depending "
"on your timezone), and will trigger the packages updates process itself "
"depending on the value set to the `$RAND` variable - it's configured to "
"produce a **sleep** between 1980 and 5940 seconds (or: 33 and 99 minutes)."
msgstr ""
"I det här schemat körs skriptet varje dag klockan 00.00, beroende på "
"tidszon. Själva paketuppdateringen startar beroende på värdet i variabeln "
"`$RAND`, som är konfigurerad för att ge en **sleep**-fördröjning på mellan 1 "
"980 och 5 940 sekunder, det vill säga 33–99 minuter."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
msgid ""
"If you are running FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE or above, the base system will be "
"updated via `pkg` as well. Otherwise you would still need to rely on "
"`freebsd-update` or building it from source. For more information, please "
"see the official [FreeBSD Wiki](https://wiki.freebsd.org/pkgbase) or the "
"[Handbook](https://docs.freebsd.org/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE eller senare uppdateras även "
"grundsystemet via `pkg`. Annars behöver du fortfarande använda `freebsd-"
"update` eller bygga från källkod. Mer information finns på den officiella "
"[FreeBSD-wikin](https://wiki.freebsd.org/pkgbase) och i [handboken](https://"
"docs.freebsd.org/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/)."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
msgid ""
"If you want to change the scheduled execution of the update script, "
"configure your [crontab settings](https://crontab.guru/) to a value you "
"would like to use."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill ändra den schemalagda körningen av uppdateringsskriptet kan du "
"ange önskat värde i [crontab-inställningarna](https://crontab.guru/)."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
msgid ""
"Let's use `/root/bin/pkg-upgrade.sh` for our setup. This is how is must look "
"like:"
msgstr ""
"Vi använder `/root/bin/pkg-upgrade.sh` i konfigurationen. Filen ska se ut så "
"här:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
msgid ""
"More information about the use of `jot` in there can be found [here](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/community/relays/-/issues/123) - thanks to our "
"anonymous cypherpunks. Adapt that to your needs should it be more suited to "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Mer information om användningen av `jot` finns [här](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/community/relays/-/issues/123). Tack till våra "
"anonyma cypherpunkare. Anpassa det efter dina behov om det passar bättre."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/freebsd/updates/
msgid ""
"This guide should work for DragonFlyBSD, FreeBSD, and HardenedBSD operating "
"system. It covers _ONLY_ packages updates/upgrades, and does not apply any "
"other patch to base system or kernel."
msgstr ""
"Vägledningen bör fungera för DragonFly BSD, FreeBSD och HardenedBSD. Den "
"omfattar _endast_ paketuppdateringar och uppgraderingar och tillämpar inga "
"andra korrigeringar på grundsystemet eller kärnan."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid "Here we set `tor` to start during boot and call it for the first time:"
msgstr ""
"Här konfigurerar vi `tor` så att det startas vid systemstart och kör det för "
"första gången:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/
msgid "Install `tor` NetBSD's package:"
msgstr "Installera NetBSD-paketet `tor`:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/
msgid "Put the configuration file `/usr/pkg/etc/tor/torrc` in place:"
msgstr "Lägg konfigurationsfilen `/usr/pkg/etc/tor/torrc` på plats:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/netbsd/
msgid "How to deploy a Middle/Guard relay on NetBSD"
msgstr "Så distribuerar du ett mellan-/vaktrelä på NetBSD"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/
msgid "3. Configuration file"
msgstr "3. Konfigurationsfil"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid "4. Change `openfiles-max` and `maxfiles`"
msgstr "4. Ändra `openfiles-max` och `maxfiles`"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid ""
"By default, OpenBSD maintains a rather low limit on the maximum number of "
"open files for a process."
msgstr ""
"OpenBSD har som standard en ganska låg gräns för hur många filer en process "
"får ha öppna."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid ""
"For a daemon such as Tor's, that opens a connection to each and every other "
"relay (currently around 7000 relays), these limits should be raised."
msgstr ""
"För en demon som Tor, som öppnar en anslutning till vart och ett av de andra "
"reläerna – för närvarande omkring 7 000 – bör gränserna höjas."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid ""
"If that's not your case, please adjust the `installurl` configuration file "
"like this:"
msgstr ""
"Om detta inte gäller dig ändrar du konfigurationsfilen `installurl` så här:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid ""
"Latest version of tor will be made avaliable as package for the most recent "
"OpenBSD release and OpenBSD -current(development snapshot), therefore, "
"remember to upgrade OpenBSD on time  and configure automatic software "
"updates."
msgstr ""
"Den senaste Tor-versionen görs tillgänglig som paket för den senaste OpenBSD-"
"versionen och OpenBSD-current, utvecklingsögonblicksbilden. Kom därför ihåg "
"att uppgradera OpenBSD i tid och konfigurera automatiska "
"programuppdateringar."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid "Proceed with `pkg_add` to install the package:"
msgstr "Fortsätt med `pkg_add` för att installera paketet:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid ""
"Recent OpenBSD systems, since 6.5, already have the repository configured on "
"`/etc/installurl` so we do not need to bother changing it."
msgstr ""
"Nyare OpenBSD-system, från och med 6.5, har redan paketförrådet konfigurerat "
"i `/etc/installurl`, så vi behöver inte ändra det."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid ""
"To apply our raised open files limits, make sure to start tor with `rcctl`."
msgstr ""
"Starta Tor med `rcctl` för att de höjda gränserna för öppna filer ska "
"tillämpas."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/
msgid "How to deploy a Middle/Guard relay on OpenBSD"
msgstr "Så distribuerar du ett mellan-/vaktrelä på OpenBSD"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"**NOTE:** All steps documented on this page are considering that your server "
"is dedicated to provide a Tor relay."
msgstr ""
"**OBS!** Alla steg på den här sidan förutsätter att servern är avsedd för "
"att tillhandahålla ett Tor-relä."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid "2. Restart `cron`"
msgstr "2. Starta om `cron`"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid "For this example, we are going to use `/etc/weekly.local`:"
msgstr "I det här exemplet använder vi `/etc/weekly.local`:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"For this particular schedule, we opt to run the script every week on "
"Saturdays at 3h30 (depending on your timezone)."
msgstr ""
"I det här schemat kör vi skriptet varje lördag klockan 03.30, beroende på "
"tidszon."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"It allows us to write our own custom scripts to be called by `cron` in three "
"different local files (depending on our needs, or particular choices):"
msgstr ""
"Det gör att vi kan skriva egna skript som anropas av `cron` i tre olika "
"lokala filer, beroende på behov och val:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"It covers only packages updates/upgrades, and does not apply any other patch "
"to the base system or kernel."
msgstr ""
"Det omfattar endast paketuppdateringar och uppgraderingar och tillämpar inga "
"andra korrigeringar på grundsystemet eller kärnan."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"It will trigger the packages updates process itself, depending on the value "
"set to the `$RAND` variable."
msgstr ""
"Själva paketuppdateringen startar beroende på värdet i variabeln `$RAND`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"It's configured to produce a **sleep** between 0 and 900 seconds (15 "
"minutes)."
msgstr ""
"Den är konfigurerad för att ge en **sleep**-fördröjning på mellan 0 och 900 "
"sekunder, alltså 15 minuter."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"OpenBSD offers us an easy way of running tasks **daily**, **weekly** or "
"**monthly**."
msgstr ""
"OpenBSD gör det enkelt att köra uppgifter **dagligen**, **veckovis** eller "
"**månadsvis**."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"Please be aware that services will be restarted during the automatic "
"software update process documented here."
msgstr ""
"Tänk på att tjänster kommer att startas om under den automatiska "
"programuppdateringsprocess som beskrivs här."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/openbsd/updates/
msgid ""
"This guide should work for recent versions of an OpenBSD operating system."
msgstr "Vägledningen bör fungera för nyare versioner av OpenBSD."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/
msgid "4. Restart the service"
msgstr "4. Starta om tjänsten"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/
msgid ""
"Ensure you update the packages database before installing the package, then "
"call `zypper` to install it:"
msgstr ""
"Uppdatera paketdatabasen innan du installerar paketet och använd sedan "
"`zypper` för att installera det:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/
msgid ""
"One of the most important things to keep your relay secure is to install "
"security updates timely and, ideally, automatically, so you cannot forget "
"about them."
msgstr ""
"En av de viktigaste åtgärderna för att hålla reläet säkert är att installera "
"säkerhetsuppdateringar i tid och helst automatiskt, så att de inte glöms "
"bort."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/
msgid "How to deploy a Middle/Guard relay on openSUSE"
msgstr "Så distribuerar du ett mellan-/vaktrelä på openSUSE"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/
msgid "2. Start the configuration tool"
msgstr "2. Starta konfigurationsverktyget"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/
msgid "3. Configure online updates"
msgstr "3. Konfigurera nätuppdateringar"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/
msgid ""
"Confirm that you have checked the three options above, select OK, and exit."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollera att de tre alternativen ovan är markerade, välj OK och avsluta."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/opensuse/updates/
msgid ""
"If you are running openSUSE on a GUI, YaST2 counts with the same module. "
"Otherwise, run the following command to use the CLI tool:"
msgstr ""
"Om du kör openSUSE med ett grafiskt gränssnitt finns samma modul i YaST2. "
"Kör annars följande kommando för att använda kommandoradsverktyget:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/voidlinux/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/voidlinux/
msgid "To install the `tor` package on Void Linux, please run:"
msgstr "Kör följande för att installera paketet `tor` på Void Linux:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/voidlinux/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/voidlinux/
msgid "How to deploy a Middle/Guard relay on Void Linux"
msgstr "Så distribuerar du ett mellan-/vaktrelä på Void Linux"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"*(Optional. A custom path can be used, though you will have to make "
"necessary modifications in the following steps.)"
msgstr ""
"*(Valfritt. Du kan använda en egen sökväg, men behöver då göra motsvarande "
"ändringar i följande steg.)"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"**Note: You should only run a Windows relay if you can run it 24/7. If you "
"are unable to guarantee that, a [Snowflake](https://"
"snowflake.torproject.org/) is a better way to contribute resources.**"
msgstr ""
"**Obs! Du bör endast driva ett Windows-relä om det kan vara igång dygnet "
"runt. Om du inte kan garantera detta är en [Snowflake](https://"
"snowflake.torproject.org/)-proxy ett bättre sätt att bidra med resurser.**"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"**Note:** Be sure **not** to click the 'Run as administrator' button - this "
"is dangerous!"
msgstr ""
"**Obs!** Klicka **inte** på knappen ”Kör som administratör” – det är farligt!"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"**Notice:** Depending on your systems settings, Tor may fail to start and "
"produce an error indicating it is unable to create files. If this occurs, "
"simply open the Windows Defender Security Center and select \"App & browser "
"control\". Add the tor.exe file to the permissions list, then rerun "
"`tor.exe` from the command line. Tor should now start up normally."
msgstr ""
"**Observera:** Beroende på systeminställningarna kan Tor misslyckas med att "
"starta och visa ett fel om att filer inte kan skapas. Öppna då Windows-"
"säkerhet och välj ”App- och webbläsarkontroll”. Lägg till filen tor.exe i "
"behörighetslistan och kör sedan `tor.exe` igen från kommandoraden. Tor bör "
"nu starta normalt."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "1. Creating a user account for Tor"
msgstr "1. Skapa ett användarkonto för Tor"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"1. Head over to [Download Tor Source code]( https://www.torproject.org/"
"download/tor/) and scroll down to select 'Windows Expert Bundle'."
msgstr ""
"1. Gå till [Hämta Tors källkod]( https://www.torproject.org/download/tor/), "
"rulla ned och välj ”Windows Expert Bundle”."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "1. Navigate to the directory where you extracted Tor's files."
msgstr "1. Gå till mappen där du packade upp Tors filer."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"1. Open your command prompt. Navigate to `C:\\Users\\torrelay\\tor\\Tor` "
"with the command `cd C:\\Users\\torrelay\\tor\\Tor`."
msgstr ""
"1. Öppna Kommandotolken. Gå till `C:\\Users\\torrelay\\tor\\Tor` med "
"kommandot `cd C:\\Users\\torrelay\\tor\\Tor`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "1. To begin, open your Control Panel and select 'Accounts'."
msgstr "1. Börja med att öppna Kontrollpanelen och välja ”Konton”."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"1. Unpack the zipped Expert bundle into your newly created Tor directory. "
"Two folders will be placed there; one called `Tor`, and the other `Data`."
msgstr ""
"1. Packa upp Expert Bundle i den nya Tor-mappen. Där skapas två mappar: "
"`Tor` och `Data`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "2. Downloading and configuring the Windows Expert bundle"
msgstr "2. Hämta och konfigurera Windows Expert Bundle"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "2. Head to your `C:\\Users\\torrelay\\` directory."
msgstr "2. Gå till mappen `C:\\Users\\torrelay\\`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "2. On the left-side menu, select 'Family & other people'."
msgstr "2. Välj ”Familj och andra användare” i menyn till vänster."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"2. Simply Shift + right-click on the `tor.exe` file and select 'Run as other "
"user' from the drop-down menu, and enter the password for your Tor account "
"when prompted."
msgstr ""
"2. Håll ned Skift och högerklicka på filen `tor.exe`. Välj ”Kör som en annan "
"användare” i menyn och ange lösenordet för Tor-kontot när du blir ombedd."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"2. Type `RUNAS /user:torrelay tor.exe` and press enter. If you have your "
"`torrc` file somewhere other than the default location (Like the `home` "
"folder), specify the path with the `-f` flag."
msgstr ""
"2. Skriv `RUNAS /user:torrelay tor.exe` och tryck på Retur. Om filen `torrc` "
"finns på en annan plats än standardplatsen, till exempel i mappen `home`, "
"anger du sökvägen med flaggan `-f`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"2. You should now create a folder called `log` in `C:\\Users\\torrelay\\tor`."
msgstr "2. Skapa nu en mapp med namnet `log` i `C:\\Users\\torrelay\\tor`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "2.1 Downloading"
msgstr "2.1 Hämtning"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "2.2 Configuration"
msgstr "2.2 Konfiguration"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"3. Beside the 'Add another user to this PC' subheader, click the large `+` "
"sign."
msgstr ""
"3. Klicka på det stora `+`-tecknet bredvid underrubriken ”Lägg till en annan "
"användare på den här datorn”."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "3. Create a folder called `tor`."
msgstr "3. Skapa en mapp med namnet `tor`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "3. Starting up your relay"
msgstr "3. Starta reläet"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"3. You should now see Tor starting up in your terminal. Wait until its "
"finished bootstrapping."
msgstr "3. Nu bör Tor starta i terminalen. Vänta tills etableringen är klar."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"3. You will now need to create a torrc file to define the ruleset of your "
"relay."
msgstr ""
"3. Nu behöver du skapa en torrc-fil som definierar reläets regeluppsättning."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "3.1 Method 1: User interface"
msgstr "3.1 Metod 1: Användargränssnitt"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "3.2 Method 2: Command line"
msgstr "3.2 Metod 2: Kommandorad"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"4. A panel will now appear asking for the Windows account information. On "
"the bottom, select the small text that states \"I do not have this users "
"sign-in information\"."
msgstr ""
"4. En panel som frågar efter uppgifter för Windows-kontot visas. Välj den "
"lilla texten längst ned: ”Jag har inte den här personens "
"inloggningsinformation”."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"4. After a short period it should publish its OrPort, and you will be "
"successfully relaying traffic for the Tor Network."
msgstr ""
"4. Efter en kort stund bör reläet offentliggöra sin ORPort, och du "
"vidarebefordrar då trafik åt Tor-nätverket."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "4. Final notes"
msgstr "4. Avslutande anmärkningar"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"4. Open up your newly created `torrc` file in your text editor and populate "
"it with the following contents:"
msgstr ""
"4. Öppna den nya filen `torrc` i en textredigerare och fyll den med följande "
"innehåll:"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "5. Make sure everything is filled in correctly, then save and exit."
msgstr "5. Kontrollera att allt är korrekt ifyllt, spara och avsluta."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"5. On the next panel, select the similar text on the bottom stating \"Set up "
"user without using a Microsoft account\"."
msgstr ""
"5. Välj på nästa panel den liknande texten längst ned: ”Lägg till en "
"användare utan ett Microsoft-konto”."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"6. Enter a username for the user. Anything you like is fine, though within "
"this guide the username `torrelay` will  be used. Then enter a strong "
"password and continue."
msgstr ""
"6. Ange ett användarnamn. Du kan välja vilket du vill, men i den här "
"vägledningen används `torrelay`. Ange sedan ett starkt lösenord och fortsätt."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"Below are detailed instructions on how to perform these steps - please "
"ensure you follow them very carefully, and make any of the necessary "
"modifications outlined along the way."
msgstr ""
"Nedan finns detaljerade anvisningar för stegen. Följ dem mycket noggrant och "
"gör de nödvändiga ändringarna som anges under arbetets gång."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "ContactInfo tor-operator@your-emailaddress-domain"
msgstr "ContactInfo tor-operator@your-emailaddress-domain"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"Example: `RUNAS /user:torrelay \"tor.exe -f C:"
"\\Users\\torrelay\\tor\\Tor\\torrc\"`"
msgstr ""
"Exempel: `RUNAS /user:torrelay \"tor.exe -f C:"
"\\Users\\torrelay\\tor\\Tor\\torrc\"`"

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"First you will need to create a new account to allow Tor to run isolated "
"from your personal configuration as well as have manageable system "
"permissions."
msgstr ""
"Först behöver du skapa ett nytt konto så att Tor kan köras isolerat från din "
"personliga konfiguration och med hanterbara systembehörigheter."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"Setting up a Windows system as a relay requires performing a few simple "
"steps to set up a user account, download the `Windows expert bundle`, "
"implement a torrc configuration file and start up Tor from the command line."
msgstr ""
"För att konfigurera ett Windows-system som relä behöver du skapa ett "
"användarkonto, hämta `Windows Expert Bundle`, skapa en torrc-"
"konfigurationsfil och starta Tor från kommandoraden."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"The default directory path for this file is `C:"
"\\Users\\torrelay\\AppData\\Roaming\\tor\\torrc`, though you can specify a "
"custom location at commandline startup with the `-f` flag. (More below)"
msgstr ""
"Standardplatsen för filen är `C:"
"\\Users\\torrelay\\AppData\\Roaming\\tor\\torrc`, men du kan ange en annan "
"plats vid kommandoradsstart med flaggan `-f`. Mer information finns nedan."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"The next step is to download and install Windows Expert bundle as well as "
"set up your torrc file."
msgstr ""
"Nästa steg är att hämta och installera Windows Expert Bundle och konfigurera "
"torrc-filen."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"There are two methods for starting up your relay for the first time "
"depending on your preferences and needs."
msgstr ""
"Det finns två sätt att starta reläet första gången, beroende på dina behov "
"och önskemål."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid ""
"You'll then need to create an empty file and name it `notices.log` in the "
"`log` folder."
msgstr "Skapa sedan en tom fil med namnet `notices.log` i mappen `log`."

#: content/relay/setup/guard/windows/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/guard/windows/
msgid "How to deploy a Middle/Guard relay on Windows"
msgstr "Så distribuerar du ett mellan-/vaktrelä i Windows"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"**If you enable IPv6 without working IPv6 connectivity, your entire relay "
"will remain unused, regardless of whether IPv4 is working.**"
msgstr ""
"**Om du aktiverar IPv6 utan fungerande IPv6-anslutning kommer hela reläet "
"att förbli oanvänt, även om IPv4 fungerar.**"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"**Note: Tor requires IPv4 connectivity, you can not run a Tor relay on IPv6-"
"only.**"
msgstr ""
"**Obs! Tor kräver IPv4-anslutning. Du kan inte driva ett Tor-relä enbart med "
"IPv6.**"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "**Note:** These are community provided resources."
msgstr "**Obs!** Det här är resurser som tillhandahålls av gemenskapen."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "1. Make sure relay ports can be reached"
msgstr "1. Kontrollera att reläportarna är nåbara"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "2. Verify that your relay works"
msgstr "2. Verifiera att reläet fungerar"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "3. Read about Tor relay lifecycle"
msgstr "3. Läs om Tor-reläets livscykel"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "4. Configuration Management"
msgstr "4. Konfigurationshantering"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "5. Important: if you run more than one Tor instance"
msgstr "5. Viktigt om du kör fler än en Tor-instans"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "6. Add firewall rules to protect against DDoS attacks"
msgstr "6. Lägg till brandväggsregler som skyddar mot DDoS-angrepp"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "7. Optional: Limiting bandwidth usage (and traffic)"
msgstr "7. Valfritt: Begränsa bandbredds- och trafikanvändningen"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "8. Check IPv6 availability"
msgstr "8. Kontrollera om IPv6 är tillgängligt"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "9. Maintaining a relay"
msgstr "9. Underhåll ett relä"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"A good way to monitor a relay for its health state is to have a look at its "
"bandwidth graphs."
msgstr ""
"Ett bra sätt att övervaka reläets hälsa är att granska dess "
"bandbreddsdiagram."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"About 3 hours after you start your relay, it should appear on [Relay Search]"
"(https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html) on the Metrics portal."
msgstr ""
"Omkring tre timmar efter att reläet har startats bör det visas i [Relay "
"Search](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html) på Metrics-portalen."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Additionally, be aware that these rules have been shown to work for "
"particular attacks that have happened in the past."
msgstr ""
"Tänk även på att reglerna har visat sig fungera mot vissa angrepp som "
"inträffat tidigare."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"After your initial installation and start of the tor daemon it is a good "
"idea to make a backup of your relay's long term identity keys."
msgstr ""
"Efter den första installationen och starten av Tor-demonen är det klokt att "
"säkerhetskopiera reläets långlivade identitetsnycklar."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Also see the bandwidth entry in the [FAQ](https://support.torproject.org/"
"relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/)."
msgstr ""
"Se även posten om bandbredd i [vanliga frågor](https://"
"support.torproject.org/relays/performance/bandwidth-shaping/)."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Also, make sure you allow all outgoing connections too, so your relay can "
"reach the other Tor relays, clients and destinations."
msgstr ""
"Se även till att tillåta alla utgående anslutningar så att reläet kan nå "
"andra Tor-reläer, klienter och destinationer."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Another option is to use one of the free services that allow you to check "
"your relay's ORPorts for reachability and send you an email should they "
"become unreachable."
msgstr ""
"Ett annat alternativ är att använda någon av de kostnadsfria tjänster som "
"kontrollerar nåbarheten för reläets OR-portar och skickar e-post om de blir "
"onåbara."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"At the end of the output you should see \"OK.\" if that is not the case, do "
"not enable IPv6 in your torrc configuration file before IPv6 is indeed "
"working."
msgstr ""
"I slutet av utdata ska ”OK.” visas. Om det inte gör det ska du inte aktivera "
"IPv6 i torrc-filen förrän IPv6 verkligen fungerar."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Attacks are constantly evolving and will often need new rules, so please "
"stay connected to update these as necessary, either by subscribing to the "
"relevant project or by subscribing to the [tor-relays](https://"
"lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-relays) mailing list."
msgstr ""
"Angrepp utvecklas ständigt och kräver ofta nya regler. Håll dig därför "
"uppdaterad så att reglerna kan ändras vid behov, antingen genom att följa "
"det berörda projektet eller prenumerera på e-postlistan [tor-relays](https://"
"lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-relays)."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Backup Tor Identity Keys"
msgstr "Säkerhetskopiera Tors identitetsnycklar"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Bandwidth"
msgstr "Bandbredd"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Before enabling your tor daemon to use IPv6 in addition to IPv4 you should "
"do some basic IPv6 connectivity tests."
msgstr ""
"Innan du aktiverar Tor-demonen för att använda IPv6 utöver IPv4 bör du göra "
"några grundläggande anslutningstester för IPv6."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Configuring your firewall to stop too many concurrent connections has been "
"shown to significantly help deal with DDoS attacks against relays."
msgstr ""
"Att konfigurera brandväggen så att den begränsar antalet samtidiga "
"anslutningar har visat sig vara till stor hjälp mot DDoS-angrepp på reläer."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Consider implementing one of the following mechanisms:"
msgstr "Överväg att införa någon av följande mekanismer:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Data in categories (IP version, in/out, etc.) is worse than total data."
msgstr ""
"Uppdelade data, exempelvis efter IP-version eller in-/utgående trafik, är "
"sämre än totaldata."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Default locations of the keys folder:"
msgstr "Standardplatser för nyckelmappen:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Established TCP Connections"
msgstr "Upprättade TCP-anslutningar"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Having a fast relay for some time of the month is preferred over a slow "
"relay for the entire month."
msgstr ""
"Ett snabbt relä under en del av månaden är bättre än ett långsamt relä under "
"hela månaden."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"If it worked fine, make your Tor relay reachable via IPv6 by adding an "
"additional ORPort line to your configuration (example for ORPort 9001):"
msgstr ""
"Om testet fungerade gör du Tor-reläet nåbart via IPv6 genom att lägga till "
"ytterligare en ORPort-rad i konfigurationen, till exempel för ORPort 9001:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "If something goes wrong, it is good to get notified automatically."
msgstr "Om något går fel är det bra att få en automatisk avisering."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"If you are an exit relay with IPv6 connectivity, tell your tor daemon to "
"allow exiting via IPv6 so clients can reach IPv6 destinations:"
msgstr ""
"Om du driver ett utgångsrelä med IPv6-anslutning ska du konfigurera Tor-"
"demonen så att utgångstrafik via IPv6 tillåts och klienter kan nå IPv6-"
"destinationer:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"If you are using a firewall, open a hole in your firewall so incoming "
"connections can reach the ports you will use for your relay (ORPort)."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder en brandvägg öppnar du den så att inkommande anslutningar kan "
"nå portarna som reläet använder, alltså ORPort."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"If you have a global IPv6 address you should be able to find it in the "
"output of the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Om du har en global IPv6-adress bör den visas i utdata från följande "
"kommando:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"If you plan to run more than a single relay, or you want to run a high "
"capacity relay (multiple Tor instances per server) or want to use strong "
"security features like [Offline Master Keys](https://trac.torproject.org/"
"projects/tor/wiki/doc/TorRelaySecurity/OfflineKeys) without performing "
"additional steps manually, you may want to use configuration management for "
"better maintainability."
msgstr ""
"Om du planerar att köra mer än ett enda relä, eller om du vill köra ett "
"högkapacitetsrelä (flera Tor-instanser per server) eller vill använda starka "
"säkerhetsfunktioner som [Offline-huvudnycklar](https://trac.torproject.org/"
"projects/tor/wiki/doc/TorRelaySecurity/OfflineKeys) utan att utföra "
"ytterligare steg manuellt, kanske du vill använda konfigurationshantering "
"för bättre underhåll."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"If you run two relays and they have fingerprints AAAAAAAAAA and BBBBBBBB, "
"you would add the following configuration to set MyFamily:"
msgstr ""
"Om du driver två reläer med fingeravtrycken AAAAAAAAAA och BBBBBBBB lägger "
"du till följande konfiguration för MyFamily:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"If you want to publish traffic statistics, you should aggregate your relays' "
"traffic over at least a day or use bigger aggregation windows for bandwidth "
"if feasable and combine graphs/statistics for multiple relays where possible."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill publicera trafikstatistik bör du sammanställa reläernas trafik "
"över minst ett dygn, använda större sammanställningsintervall för bandbredd "
"när det är möjligt och kombinera diagram och statistik för flera reläer där "
"det går."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"If your logfile (syslog) contains the following entry after starting your "
"tor daemon your relay should be up and running as expected:"
msgstr ""
"Om loggfilen (syslog) innehåller följande post efter att Tor-demonen har "
"startats bör reläet vara igång och fungera som förväntat:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Instead of doing so manually, for big operators we recommend to automate the "
"MyFamily setting via a configuration management solution."
msgstr ""
"För stora operatörer rekommenderar vi att MyFamily-inställningen "
"automatiseras med en lösning för konfigurationshantering i stället för att "
"hanteras manuellt."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"It helps relay operators get notified when their relays or bridges are "
"offline, as well as for other incidents."
msgstr ""
"Den meddelar reläoperatörer när deras reläer eller broar är frånkopplade och "
"vid andra incidenter."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"It takes some time for relay traffic to ramp up, this is especially true for "
"guard relays but to a lesser extent also for exit relays. To understand this "
"process, read about the [lifecycle of a new relay](https://"
"blog.torproject.org/lifecycle-new-relay)."
msgstr ""
"Det tar tid innan trafiken till ett relä ökar. Det gäller särskilt "
"vaktreläer men i viss mån även utgångsreläer. Läs om [ett nytt reläs "
"livscykel](https://blog.torproject.org/lifecycle-new-relay) för att förstå "
"processen."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Manually managing MyFamily for big relay groups is error-prone and can put "
"Tor clients at risk."
msgstr ""
"Manuell hantering av MyFamily för stora relägrupper är felbenägen och kan "
"utsätta Tor-klienter för risk."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Memory"
msgstr "Minne"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Note: **Do not make your private monitoring data graphs public since this "
"could help attackers with deanonymizing Tor users.**"
msgstr ""
"Obs! **Gör inte diagram med privata övervakningsdata offentliga, eftersom "
"det kan hjälpa angripare att avanonymisera Tor-användare.**"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Note: You have to explicitly specify your IPv6 address in square brackets, "
"you can not tell tor to bind to any IPv6 (like you do for IPv4)."
msgstr ""
"Obs! Du måste uttryckligen ange IPv6-adressen inom hakparenteser. Du kan "
"inte be Tor att binda till valfri IPv6-adress på samma sätt som med IPv4."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Numbers are worse than graphs."
msgstr "Siffror är sämre än diagram."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Once you have set up your relay, it will likely run without much work from "
"your side."
msgstr ""
"När reläet väl är konfigurerat kommer det sannolikt att köras utan särskilt "
"mycket arbete från din sida."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Only do this if you have a very secure place for your keys as if stolen, "
"these keys could theoretically allow traffic decryption or impersonation."
msgstr ""
"Gör endast detta om du har en mycket säker plats för nycklarna. Om de blir "
"stulna kan de teoretiskt möjliggöra dekryptering av trafik eller "
"identitetsförfalskning."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Real-time data is worse than historical data."
msgstr "Realtidsdata är sämre än historiska data."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Reporting individual relays is worse than reporting totals for groups of "
"relays. In future, tor will securely aggregate bandwidth statistics, so any "
"individual relay bandwidth reporting will be less secure than tor's "
"statistics."
msgstr ""
"Rapportering om enskilda reläer är sämre än totalsummor för grupper av "
"reläer. I framtiden kommer Tor att sammanställa bandbreddsstatistik på ett "
"säkert sätt, och då blir all individuell bandbreddsrapportering för reläer "
"mindre säker än Tors statistik."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Setting up outage notifications"
msgstr "Konfigurera aviseringar om driftavbrott"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Since relays have a ramp-up time it makes sense to back up the identity key "
"to be able to restore your relay's reputation after a disk failure - "
"otherwise you would have to go through the ramp-up phase again."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom det tar tid för reläer att bygga upp trafik är det klokt att "
"säkerhetskopiera identitetsnyckeln. Då kan reläets anseende återställas "
"efter ett diskfel, i stället för att uppbyggnadsfasen behöver genomföras på "
"nytt."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Smaller periods are worse."
msgstr "Kortare perioder är sämre."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Some practical advice:"
msgstr "Några praktiska råd:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Subscribe to the tor-announce mailing list"
msgstr "Prenumerera på e-postlistan tor-announce"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Swap"
msgstr "Växlingsutrymme"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "System Health Monitoring"
msgstr "Övervakning av systemhälsa"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"The MyFamily setting is simply telling Tor clients what Tor relays are "
"controlled by a single entity/operator/organization, so they are not used in "
"multiple positions in a single circuit."
msgstr ""
"Inställningen MyFamily talar helt enkelt om för Tor-klienterna vilka Tor-"
"reläer som styrs av samma enhet, operatör eller organisation, så att de inte "
"används på flera platser i samma krets."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"The following Ansible Role has specifically been built for Tor relay "
"operators and supports multiple operating systems: [Ansible Relayor](http://"
"github.com/nusenu/ansible-relayor)."
msgstr ""
"Följande Ansible-roll har skapats särskilt för Tor-reläoperatörer och stöder "
"flera operativsystem: [Ansible Relayor](http://github.com/nusenu/ansible-"
"relayor)."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"The following command line will ping the IPv6 addresses of Tor directory "
"authorities from your server:"
msgstr ""
"Följande kommandorad pingar IPv6-adresserna till Tors katalogauktoriteter "
"från servern:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"The following torrc configuration options can be used to restrict bandwidth "
"and traffic:"
msgstr ""
"Följande torrc-alternativ kan användas för att begränsa bandbredd och trafik:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "The location of that line in the configuration file does not matter."
msgstr "Det spelar ingen roll var raden placeras i konfigurationsfilen."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"There are many tools for monitoring this kind of data, [munin](http://munin-"
"monitoring.org/) is one of them and is relatively easy to setup."
msgstr ""
"Det finns många verktyg för att övervaka sådana data. [munin](http://munin-"
"monitoring.org/) är ett av dem och är relativt enkelt att konfigurera."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"There are multiple configuration management solutions for Unix-based "
"operating systems (Ansible, Puppet, Salt, ...)."
msgstr ""
"Det finns flera lösningar för konfigurationshantering i Unix-baserade "
"operativsystem, till exempel Ansible, Puppet och Salt."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"They are located in the \"keys\" subfolder of your DataDirectory (simply "
"make a copy of the entire folder and store it in a secure location)."
msgstr ""
"De finns i undermappen ”keys” i DataDirectory. Kopiera hela mappen och "
"förvara kopian på en säker plats."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"This can be handy if you want to ensure that your Tor relay does not exceed "
"a certain amount of bandwidth or total traffic per day/week/month."
msgstr ""
"Det kan vara användbart om du vill säkerställa att Tor-reläet inte "
"överskrider en viss mängd bandbredd eller total trafik per dag, vecka eller "
"månad."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "This checks only for the listener but does not speak the Tor protocol."
msgstr "Detta kontrollerar endast lyssnaren och använder inte Tor-protokollet."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"This is a very low traffic mailing list and you will get information about "
"new stable tor releases and important security update information: [tor-"
"announce](https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-"
"announce)."
msgstr ""
"Det här är en e-postlista med mycket låg trafik där du får information om "
"nya stabila Tor-utgåvor och viktiga säkerhetsuppdateringar: [tor-announce]"
"(https://lists.torproject.org/cgi-bin/mailman/listinfo/tor-announce)."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"This section lists a few tools that you might find handy as a Tor relay "
"operator."
msgstr ""
"Det här avsnittet innehåller några verktyg som kan vara användbara för en "
"Tor-reläoperatör."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"To avoid putting Tor clients at risk, when operating multiple relays you "
"must set a proper [MyFamily](https://2019.www.torproject.org/docs/tor-"
"manual.html.en#MyFamily) value and have a valid [ContactInfo](https://"
"2019.www.torproject.org/docs/tor-manual.html.en#ContactInfo) in your torrc "
"configuration."
msgstr ""
"För att inte utsätta Tor-klienter för risk måste du ange ett korrekt värde "
"för [MyFamily](https://2019.www.torproject.org/docs/tor-"
"manual.html.en#MyFamily) och giltig [ContactInfo](https://"
"2019.www.torproject.org/docs/tor-manual.html.en#ContactInfo) i torrc-"
"konfigurationen om du driver flera reläer."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"To ensure your relay is healthy and not overwhelmed it makes sense to have "
"some basic system monitoring in place to keep an eye on the following "
"metrics:"
msgstr ""
"För att säkerställa att reläet är friskt och inte överbelastat är det klokt "
"att ha grundläggande systemövervakning för följande mätvärden:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
#: templates/onion-services.html:55
msgid "Tools"
msgstr "Verktyg"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"Tor will not limit its bandwidth usage by default, but supports multiple "
"ways to restrict the used bandwidth and the amount of traffic."
msgstr ""
"Tor begränsar inte bandbreddsanvändningen som standard, men stöder flera "
"sätt att begränsa använd bandbredd och trafikmängd."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"We encourage everyone to enable IPv6 on their relays. This is especially "
"valuable on exit and guard relays."
msgstr ""
"Vi uppmuntrar alla att aktivera IPv6 på sina reläer. Det är särskilt "
"värdefullt för utgångs- och vaktreläer."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"We recommend using [Tor Weather](https://weather.torproject.org/), a "
"notification service developed by the Tor Project."
msgstr ""
"Vi rekommenderar [Tor Weather](https://weather.torproject.org/), en "
"aviseringstjänst som utvecklats av The Tor Project."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"You can also use it to generate PNG pictures showing traffic graphs. [vnstat "
"documentation](https://humdi.net/vnstat/) and [demo output](https://"
"humdi.net/vnstat/cgidemo/)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan även använda det för att skapa PNG-bilder med trafikdiagram. Se "
"[dokumentationen för vnstat](https://humdi.net/vnstat/) och [exempelutdata]"
"(https://humdi.net/vnstat/cgidemo/)."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"You can find the specific ORPort TCP port number in the [Setup page](../../"
"setup) (in the OS specific sections)."
msgstr ""
"Det specifika TCP-portnumret för ORPort finns på [konfigurationssidan](../../"
"setup) i de operativsystemsspecifika avsnitten."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "You can search for your relay using your nickname or IP address."
msgstr "Du kan söka efter reläet med dess smeknamn eller IP-adress."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"You can simply add it next to the first ORPort lines in your torrc file."
msgstr ""
"Du kan helt enkelt lägga till raden bredvid de första ORPort-raderna i torrc-"
"filen."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "You should check them carefully before applying them to your system."
msgstr "Granska dem noggrant innan du tillämpar dem på systemet."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"[Nyx](https://nyx.torproject.org/): is a Tor Project tool (formerly arm) "
"that allows you to see real time data of your relay."
msgstr ""
"[Nyx](https://nyx.torproject.org/) är ett verktyg från The Tor Project, "
"tidigare kallat arm, som visar realtidsdata från reläet."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"[UptimeRobot](https://uptimerobot.com/) is one of these services that allow "
"you to monitor TCP listeners on arbitrary ports."
msgstr ""
"[UptimeRobot](https://uptimerobot.com/) är en av tjänsterna som kan övervaka "
"TCP-lyssnare på valfria portar."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"https://github.com/steinex/tor-ddos: If you would like a more simpler "
"approach without scripts and ipset."
msgstr ""
"https://github.com/steinex/tor-ddos: Om du vill ha ett enklare "
"tillvägagångssätt utan skript och ipset."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"https://github.com/toralf/torutils: If you would like a script to deploy."
msgstr ""
"https://github.com/toralf/torutils: Om du vill använda ett skript för "
"distributionen."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"to both relays. To find your relay's fingerprint you can look into the log "
"files when tor starts up or find the file named \"fingerprint\" in your tor "
"DataDirectory."
msgstr ""
"på båda reläerna. Du hittar reläets fingeravtryck i loggfilerna när Tor "
"startas eller i filen ”fingerprint” i Tors DataDirectory."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid ""
"vnstat: vnstat is a command-line tool that shows the amount of data going "
"through your network connection."
msgstr ""
"vnstat: vnstat är ett kommandoradsverktyg som visar hur mycket data som "
"passerar genom nätverksanslutningen."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.section
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Relay operations"
msgstr "Relädrift"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Learn what to do once your relay is installed"
msgstr "Lär dig vad du ska göra när reläet har installerats"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/
msgid "Relay Post-install and good practices"
msgstr "Efter installationen och god praxis för reläer"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "(By default, this is the `keys` subdirectory of your `DataDir`.)"
msgstr "(Som standard är detta undermappen `keys` i `DataDir`.)"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "(Don't use the one from this example—that isn't your family ID.)"
msgstr "(Använd inte den i exemplet – det är inte ditt familje-ID.)"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"(If you don't, an adversary's relay could falsely claim to be a member of "
"your family.)"
msgstr ""
"(Annars kan en angripares relä felaktigt hävda att det tillhör din familj.)"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"(This might not be a permanent savings, unfortunately: when we transition to "
"postquantum cryptography, we might have to make microdescriptors bigger "
"again. But at least this change will free the room to do so.)"
msgstr ""
"(Besparingen kanske tyvärr inte blir bestående. När vi går över till "
"postkvantkryptografi kan mikrodeskriptorerna behöva bli större igen. "
"Ändringen frigör åtminstone utrymme för det.)"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"(Unfortunately, moving to happy families will create _additional_ work while "
"the transition is going on. We think that it will be worth it in the long "
"run.)"
msgstr ""
"(Övergången till Happy Families skapar tyvärr _extra_ arbete medan den "
"pågår, men vi tror att det lönar sig på lång sikt.)"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "1. Generate a new family key as above."
msgstr "1. Skapa en ny familjenyckel enligt ovan."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "1. Generate a single key for your family."
msgstr "1. Skapa en enda nyckel för familjen."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "2. Copy that key to every relay."
msgstr "2. Kopiera nyckeln till varje relä."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"2. Copy the new family key to every one of your relays, without replacing "
"the old family key."
msgstr ""
"2. Kopiera den nya familjenyckeln till vart och ett av reläerna utan att "
"ersätta den gamla familjenyckeln."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"3. Add the new `FamilyID` line to all of your relays' configurations, "
"without removing the old one."
msgstr ""
"3. Lägg till den nya raden `FamilyID` i konfigurationen för alla reläer utan "
"att ta bort den gamla."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "3. Configure your relays to use that key."
msgstr "3. Konfigurera reläerna så att de använder nyckeln."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"4. Wait for a few days, to give the new family information time to propagate."
msgstr ""
"4. Vänta några dagar så att den nya familjeinformationen hinner spridas."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "5. Remove the old `FamilyID` lines from your relays' configurations."
msgstr "5. Ta bort de gamla raderna `FamilyID` från reläernas konfigurationer."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Additional info: Expected savings from this transition"
msgstr "Ytterligare information: Förväntad besparing genom övergången"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Additional info: How to transition family keys"
msgstr "Ytterligare information: Så byter du familjenycklar"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "At this point, your relays will all be members of _two_ families."
msgstr "Nu tillhör alla reläerna _två_ familjer."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Configuring your relay"
msgstr "Konfigurera reläet"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"Copy the `MyKey.secret_family_key` file (or whatever you called it) into the "
"`KeyDir` of every one of your relay."
msgstr ""
"Kopiera filen `MyKey.secret_family_key`, eller det namn du gav den, till "
"`KeyDir` för vart och ett av reläerna."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Did it work?"
msgstr "Fungerade det?"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"First, you will need to wait until all of your relays are running 0.4.9.2-"
"alpha or later."
msgstr ""
"Först behöver du vänta tills alla reläer kör 0.4.9.2-alpha eller senare."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Generating the family key"
msgstr "Skapa familjenyckeln"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Give it a different filename from the old key."
msgstr "Ge den ett annat filnamn än den gamla nyckeln."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"If one of your relays is compromised, or if you accidentally leak a family "
"key, you'll need to change the key."
msgstr ""
"Om ett av reläerna komprometteras eller om familjenyckeln läcker av misstag "
"behöver du byta nyckel."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"If you did this right, you should see a `family-cert` entry in your relay's "
"descriptor, looking something like this:"
msgstr ""
"Om allt gjordes rätt bör reläets deskriptor innehålla posten `family-cert`, "
"ungefär så här:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"If your relay is running, you'll have to tell it to reload its configuration "
"(typically with a `SIGHUP`.)"
msgstr ""
"Om reläet körs behöver du be det läsa in konfigurationen på nytt, vanligtvis "
"med `SIGHUP`."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"In Tor's current design, to set up relays as members of a family, every "
"relay needs to list _every other member of the family_ in its configuration, "
"and publish that list to clients as well."
msgstr ""
"I Tors nuvarande utformning måste varje relä lista _alla andra "
"familjemedlemmar_ i sin konfiguration och även publicera listan till "
"klienterna för att reläerna ska kunna anges som medlemmar i en familj."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"In Tor, when multiple relays have the same operator(s), they should declare "
"that they are members of a \"family\"."
msgstr ""
"När flera reläer har samma operatör eller operatörer bör de i Tor ange att "
"de tillhör en ”familj”."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "In more detail"
msgstr "Mer detaljerat"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"In the Happy Families design, every relay family is identified by a secret "
"family signing key shared by all family members."
msgstr ""
"I utformningen Happy Families identifieras varje reläfamilj med en hemlig "
"signeringsnyckel som delas av alla familjemedlemmar."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "NOTE: You still need to configure MyFamily!"
msgstr "OBS! Du måste fortfarande konfigurera MyFamily!"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"Once enough of the directory authorities are running 0.4.9.2-alpha or later, "
"they'll include a corresponding entry in your relays' microdescriptors, "
"which will look something like:"
msgstr ""
"När tillräckligt många katalogauktoriteter kör 0.4.9.2-alpha eller senare "
"lägger de till en motsvarande post i reläernas mikrodeskriptorer, ungefär så "
"här:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Optionally, remove the old family keys as well."
msgstr "Du kan även ta bort de gamla familjenycklarna."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Save that `FamilyID` line; you're going to need it!"
msgstr "Spara raden `FamilyID` – du kommer att behöva den!"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "So what you'll need to do is:"
msgstr "Du behöver alltså göra följande:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"The Happy Families design is a new feature in Tor 0.4.9.2-alpha that will "
"(eventually) provide a simpler way to configure relay families, and will "
"also save a lot of traffic when clients are fetching network directory "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Happy Families är en ny funktion i Tor 0.4.9.2-alpha som så småningom ger "
"ett enklare sätt att konfigurera reläfamiljer och dessutom sparar mycket "
"trafik när klienter hämtar nätverkets kataloginformation."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "The basic idea"
msgstr "Grundidén"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"The family members use this key to sign certificates proving that they "
"belong to the family."
msgstr ""
"Familjemedlemmarna använder nyckeln för att signera certifikat som bevisar "
"att de tillhör familjen."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "The file name needs to end with `.secret_family_key`."
msgstr "Filnamnet måste sluta med `.secret_family_key`."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Then, add the `FamilyId` line to your `torrc`."
msgstr "Lägg sedan till raden `FamilyId` i `torrc`."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Then, to generate a family key, run:"
msgstr "Kör sedan följande för att skapa en familjenyckel:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "These lists can be unpleasant to maintain, and expensive to download."
msgstr "Listorna kan vara besvärliga att underhålla och kostsamma att hämta."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"This will create a file called `MyKey.secret_family_key`; it will also write "
"something like this result to standard output:"
msgstr ""
"Det skapar filen `MyKey.secret_family_key` och skriver även ett resultat som "
"liknar detta till standardutdata:"

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "To do this, we recommend a step-wise process."
msgstr "Vi rekommenderar en stegvis process för detta."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, you will still need to configure the `MyFamily` option as you "
"did before: until clients all support Happy Families, they will need to look "
"at the legacy family lists."
msgstr ""
"Tyvärr behöver du fortfarande konfigurera alternativet `MyFamily` på samma "
"sätt som tidigare. Fram till dess att alla klienter stöder Happy Families "
"behöver de använda de äldre familjelistorna."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"We plan to remove `MyFamily` and legacy TAP onion keys at the same time."
msgstr ""
"Vi planerar att ta bort `MyFamily` och de äldre TAP-onionnycklarna samtidigt."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "We'll announce once it is no longer necessary to include `MyFamily`."
msgstr "Vi meddelar när `MyFamily` inte längre behöver anges."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"We're going to try to keep this transitional period as short as is "
"reasonable."
msgstr "Vi försöker hålla övergångsperioden så kort som rimligen är möjligt."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"When we do, we estimate that the resulting network's microdescriptors will "
"be something around 10% of their current size."
msgstr ""
"När det sker uppskattar vi att nätverkets mikrodeskriptorer blir omkring 10 "
"% av sin nuvarande storlek."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid ""
"You should read this if you are a relay operator who needs to configure a "
"family on the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Läs detta om du är reläoperatör och behöver konfigurera en familj i Tor-"
"nätverket."

#: content/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/post-install/family-ids/
msgid "Learn how to configure your relays' FamilyID"
msgstr "Lär dig konfigurera reläernas FamilyID"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid "1. Install the Snowflake addon to your browser"
msgstr "1. Installera Snowflake-tillägget i webbläsaren"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid "1. Use Firefox or Chromium/Chrome as your browser"
msgstr "1. Använd Firefox eller Chromium/Chrome som webbläsare"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid "2. Have WebRTC enabled"
msgstr "2. Aktivera WebRTC"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid "2. Monitor your Snowflake's status and usage"
msgstr "2. Övervaka Snowflake-proxyns status och användning"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid ""
"Chrome users can install our addon from the [Google webstore](https://"
"chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/snowflake/"
"mafpmfcccpbjnhfhjnllmmalhifmlcie)."
msgstr ""
"Chrome-användare kan installera vårt tillägg från [Google Web Store](https://"
"chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/snowflake/"
"mafpmfcccpbjnhfhjnllmmalhifmlcie)."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid ""
"If you are running Firefox, you can install our [Firefox addon](https://"
"addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/torproject-snowflake/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder Firefox kan du installera vårt [Firefox-tillägg](https://"
"addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/torproject-snowflake/)."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid ""
"It will also display an error message if the Snowflake could not connect to "
"clients or the Snowflake bridge."
msgstr ""
"Ett felmeddelande visas även om Snowflake-proxyn inte kunde ansluta till "
"klienter eller Snowflake-bron."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid ""
"It's easiest to leave it running while you browse and it should not "
"interfere with your regular browsing experience."
msgstr ""
"Det enklaste är att låta det köras medan du surfar. Det bör inte störa den "
"vanliga surfningen."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid ""
"Once it is installed, you can toggle the `Enabled` switch to turn it off and "
"on."
msgstr ""
"När tillägget är installerat kan du slå på eller av det med reglaget "
"`Enabled`."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/
msgid ""
"Running a Snowflake proxy as a browser add on is a great low-effort way to "
"donate bandwidth if you don't have access to an always-on highly connected "
"server."
msgstr ""
"Att köra en Snowflake-proxy som webbläsartillägg är ett enkelt sätt att "
"bidra med bandbredd om du inte har tillgång till en ständigt ansluten server "
"som alltid är igång."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/browser/contents.lr:page.body
