msgstr "2. Hämta Docker Compose-filen"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "3. Checking your Docker logs"
msgstr "3. Kontrollera Docker-loggarna"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "4. Automatic updates with Watchtower"
msgstr "4. Automatiska uppdateringar med Watchtower"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid ""
"Download the [docker-compose.yml](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-"
"censorship/pluggable-transports/snowflake/-/raw/main/docker-compose.yml?"
"ref_type=heads) configuration file."
msgstr ""
"Hämta konfigurationsfilen [docker-compose.yml](https://gitlab.torproject.org/"
"tpo/anti-censorship/pluggable-transports/snowflake/-/raw/main/docker-"
"compose.yml?ref_type=heads)."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "If you would like to use it, run the following command:"
msgstr "Om du vill använda den kör du följande kommando:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "Now your snowflake proxy will stay updated automatically!"
msgstr "Nu hålls Snowflake-proxyn automatiskt uppdaterad!"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "Open a terminal and run these commands:"
msgstr "Öppna en terminal och kör följande kommandon:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid ""
"Otherwise, you will need to periodically pull the latest container and "
"restart it manually."
msgstr ""
"Annars behöver du regelbundet hämta den senaste containern och starta om den "
"manuellt."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "Run the command to download it:"
msgstr "Kör följande kommando för att hämta den:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid ""
"The [docker-compose.yml](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-censorship/"
"pluggable-transports/snowflake/-/raw/main/docker-compose.yml?ref_type=heads) "
"file contains a `watchtower` container, configured to automatically check "
"for updates to the snowflake docker container every day, download them and "
"run them."
msgstr ""
"Filen [docker-compose.yml](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-censorship/"
"pluggable-transports/snowflake/-/raw/main/docker-compose.yml?ref_type=heads) "
"innehåller en `watchtower`-container som är konfigurerad att dagligen söka "
"efter uppdateringar till Snowflake-Dockercontainern, hämta dem och köra dem."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"The instructions in this step are for Debian-based systems, but you can find "
"[Docker instructions](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/) for other "
"supported platforms."
msgstr ""
"Anvisningarna i det här steget gäller Debian-baserade system, men det finns "
"[Docker-anvisningar](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/) för andra "
"plattformar som stöds."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "Then, deploy the proxy by running:"
msgstr "Distribuera sedan proxyn genom att köra:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "This command starts the Snowflake proxy in detached mode."
msgstr "Kommandot startar Snowflake-proxyn i frånkopplat läge."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid ""
"This guide will help you set up a standalone [Snowflake](https://"
"snowflake.torproject.org) proxy using Docker to help censored users connect "
"to the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Den här vägledningen hjälper dig att konfigurera en fristående [Snowflake]"
"(https://snowflake.torproject.org)-proxy med Docker så att censurerade "
"användare kan ansluta till Tor-nätverket."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid ""
"We have a [Docker image](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-censorship/"
"pluggable-transports/snowflake/container_registry/11) to ease the setup of a "
"Snowflake proxy."
msgstr ""
"Vi tillhandahåller en [Docker-avbildning](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"anti-censorship/pluggable-transports/snowflake/container_registry/11) som "
"förenklar konfigurationen av en Snowflake-proxy."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "You should now see the output:"
msgstr "Nu bör följande utdata visas:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "and your proxy is up and running!"
msgstr "och proxyn är igång!"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "How to run a standalone Snowflake proxy with Docker"
msgstr "Så kör du en fristående Snowflake-proxy med Docker"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/docker/
msgid "Docker setup"
msgstr "Docker-konfiguration"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/
msgid "2. Enable Snowflake's proxy daemon to start on boot"
msgstr "2. Aktivera Snowflake-proxydemonen så att den startas vid systemstart"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/
msgid "3. Start the service"
msgstr "3. Starta tjänsten"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/
msgid ""
"After installation and configuration, start the Snowflake service manually "
"for the first time with:"
msgstr ""
"Efter installation och konfiguration startar du Snowflake-tjänsten manuellt "
"första gången med:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/
msgid ""
"If you have any issues or need further assistance with the Snowflake proxy "
"commands, you can access the help documentation by running:"
msgstr ""
"Om du har problem eller behöver mer hjälp med kommandona för Snowflake-"
"proxyn kan du öppna hjälpdokumentationen genom att köra:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/
msgid "Install the Snowflake proxy package using FreeBSD's package manager:"
msgstr "Installera paketet för Snowflake-proxyn med FreeBSD:s pakethanterare:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/
msgid "It will keep its same defaults, and allow the proxy service to run."
msgstr "Standardinställningarna behålls och proxytjänsten kan köras."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/
msgid ""
"To ensure the Snowflake proxy service automatically starts on system boot, "
"enable it using the `sysrc` command:"
msgstr ""
"Aktivera Snowflake-proxytjänsten med kommandot `sysrc` så att den startas "
"automatiskt vid systemstart:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/freebsd/
msgid "How to run a standalone Snowflake proxy on FreeBSD"
msgstr "Så kör du en fristående Snowflake-proxy på FreeBSD"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "1. Install Go"
msgstr "1. Installera Go"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "2. Install git and clone Snowflake repository"
msgstr "2. Installera Git och klona Snowflake-kodförrådet"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "3. Build Snowflake proxy"
msgstr "3. Bygg Snowflake-proxyn"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "4. Run the Snowflake proxy"
msgstr "4. Kör Snowflake-proxyn"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "5. Make sure the proxy is started after a reboot of the system"
msgstr "5. Se till att proxyn startas efter en systemomstart"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "6. Keep your Snowflake proxy updated"
msgstr "6. Håll Snowflake-proxyn uppdaterad"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"After you cloned the repository, you can build Snowflake proxy binary by "
"running the command:"
msgstr ""
"När kodförrådet har klonats bygger du den körbara filen för Snowflake-proxyn "
"med kommandot:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "After your proxy finished to compile, you can run it with the command:"
msgstr "När proxyn har kompilerats kan du köra den med kommandot:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "Don't use `root`."
msgstr "Använd inte `root`."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "Edit your crontab by running the command:"
msgstr "Redigera crontab genom att köra:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "Enter the following line (example, adapt paths to your situation)"
msgstr ""
"Lägg till följande rad. Det är ett exempel, så anpassa sökvägarna efter din "
"situation."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"First you will need to install and configure the Go compiler to build the "
"standalone proxy from source code."
msgstr ""
"Först behöver du installera och konfigurera Go-kompilatorn för att bygga den "
"fristående proxyn från källkod."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"If you are running Ubuntu or Debian, you can install Go by executing `sudo "
"apt install golang`."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder Ubuntu eller Debian kan du installera Go genom att köra `sudo "
"apt install golang`."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"If you are running Ubuntu or Debian, you can install git by executing `sudo "
"apt install git`."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder Ubuntu eller Debian kan du installera Git genom att köra "
"`sudo apt install git`."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"If you are using Fedora, Red Hat or Amazon Linux with `sudo yum install git` "
"or `sudo dnf install git`."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder Fedora, Red Hat eller Amazon Linux kör du `sudo yum install "
"git` eller `sudo dnf install git`."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"If you are using Fedora, Red Hat or Amazon Linux with `sudo yum install "
"golang` or `sudo dnf install golang`."
msgstr ""
"Om du använder Fedora, Red Hat eller Amazon Linux kör du `sudo yum install "
"golang` eller `sudo dnf install golang`."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"If you want to save the proxy output to a logfile, for example, to see your "
"proxy usage, you can use:"
msgstr ""
"Om du vill spara proxyns utdata i en loggfil, till exempel för att se hur "
"proxyn används, kan du använda:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"It's recommended to create a separate `snowflake` account with restricted "
"rights on the system."
msgstr ""
"Vi rekommenderar att du skapar ett separat konto med namnet `snowflake` och "
"begränsade rättigheter i systemet."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "Note: On some Linux installations this might not work."
msgstr "Obs! Det kanske inte fungerar i vissa Linux-installationer."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"Note: The command `nohup` allows the program to run in the background even "
"after the terminal is closed, and `&` puts the command in the background "
"immediately."
msgstr ""
"Obs! Kommandot `nohup` låter programmet fortsätta köras i bakgrunden efter "
"att terminalen har stängts, och `&` placerar kommandot i bakgrunden direkt."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "Open your terminal and clone the source code:"
msgstr "Öppna terminalen och klona källkoden:"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "Otherwise consult the documentation for your operating system."
msgstr "Se annars dokumentationen för operativsystemet."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"Otherwise download [Go binary](https://golang.org/dl/) from the official "
"website and follow its [installation instructions](https://go.dev/doc/"
"install)."
msgstr ""
"Hämta annars en [binärfil för Go](https://golang.org/dl/) från den "
"officiella webbplatsen och följ [installationsanvisningarna](https://go.dev/"
"doc/install)."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "Please check your Go version by using the command `go version`."
msgstr "Kontrollera Go-versionen med kommandot `go version`."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"Please execute the following steps with the user account under which the "
"proxy should be executed."
msgstr "Utför följande steg med det användarkonto som proxyn ska köras under."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"Please login using a user account with `sudo` rights or directly with `root` "
"(in the later case omit the `sudo` part in the following commands)."
msgstr ""
"Logga in med ett användarkonto som har `sudo`-behörighet eller direkt som "
"`root`. I det senare fallet utelämnar du `sudo` i följande kommandon."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"Please verify if this is working by rebooting the system and checking the "
"log."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollera att det fungerar genom att starta om systemet och granska loggen."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"Running a Snowflake proxy is an easy way to contribute to the Tor Project's "
"anti-censorship efforts."
msgstr ""
"Att köra en Snowflake-proxy är ett enkelt sätt att bidra till The Tor "
"Projects arbete mot censur."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "Second you need the git client to download the Snowflake source code."
msgstr "Därefter behöver du Git-klienten för att hämta Snowflakes källkod."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"This guide will walk you through the installation, operation, and "
"maintenance of [Snowflake](https://snowflake.torproject.org) proxy on Linux-"
"based systems."
msgstr ""
"Den här vägledningen beskriver hur du installerar, driver och underhåller en "
"[Snowflake](https://snowflake.torproject.org)-proxy på Linux-baserade system."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid ""
"To keep your snowflake proxy updated, execute the following commands every "
"few weeks (login with the user account you used during installing the proxy):"
msgstr ""
"Håll Snowflake-proxyn uppdaterad genom att köra följande kommandon med några "
"veckors mellanrum. Logga in med användarkontot som användes när proxyn "
"installerades."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "You will need **Go 1.21** or newer to run the Snowflake proxy."
msgstr "Du behöver **Go 1.21** eller senare för att köra Snowflake-proxyn."

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "How to compile and run a standalone Snowflake proxy from the source"
msgstr "Så kompilerar och kör du en fristående Snowflake-proxy från källkod"

#: content/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/snowflake/standalone/source/
msgid "Compile Snowflake proxy from the source"
msgstr "Kompilera Snowflake-proxyn från källkod"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "**2.1. Install ACME**"
msgstr "**2.1. Installera ACME**"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "**2.2. Issue a certificate**"
msgstr "**2.2. Utfärda ett certifikat**"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "1. A static IPv4 (preferably);"
msgstr "1. En statisk IPv4-adress, helst."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"2. The ability to expose TCP ports to the Internet (make sure that NAT "
"doesn't get in the way);"
msgstr ""
"2. Möjlighet att exponera TCP-portar mot internet. Se till att NAT inte "
"hindrar detta."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"3. A self-hosted website, including a configurable web server (such as NGINX "
"or Apache) and a domain under your control;"
msgstr ""
"3. En egen webbplats med en konfigurerbar webbserver, till exempel NGINX "
"eller Apache, och en domän som du styr över."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "4. A valid TLS certificate;"
msgstr "4. Ett giltigt TLS-certifikat."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "4.1. Generate a random string"
msgstr "4.1. Skapa en slumpmässig sträng"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "4.2. Create or edit an NGINX vhost"
msgstr "4.2. Skapa eller redigera en virtuell NGINX-värd"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "4.3. Test the vhost configuration and reload NGINX"
msgstr ""
"4.3. Testa konfigurationen av den virtuella värden och läs in NGINX på nytt"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"5. At least 1 GB of memory RAM (4 GB recommended) to support the Tor process "
"and WebTunnel transport."
msgstr ""
"5. Minst 1 GB RAM-minne, 4 GB rekommenderas, för att köra Tor-processen och "
"WebTunnel-transporten."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"Congratulations! You've successfully configured your web server to proxy "
"requests to your Tor bridge."
msgstr ""
"Grattis! Du har nu konfigurerat webbservern så att den vidarebefordrar "
"begäranden till Tor-bron."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"Create a new vhost file such as `/etc/nginx/sites-available/webtunnel-vhost` "
"that forwards traffic to the WebTunnel bridge."
msgstr ""
"Skapa en ny fil för en virtuell värd, till exempel `/etc/nginx/sites-"
"available/webtunnel-vhost`, som vidarebefordrar trafik till WebTunnel-bron."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"Deploying a WebTunnel bridge involves configuring both a web server and a "
"Tor bridge with this pluggable transport."
msgstr ""
"För att distribuera en WebTunnel-bro behöver både en webbserver och en Tor-"
"bro med den pluggbara transporten konfigureras."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"For more details on system requirements, we recommend reading the [Tor relay "
"requirements](../../relays-requirements) page."
msgstr ""
"Mer information om systemkraven finns på sidan med [krav för Tor-reläer]"
"(../../relays-requirements)."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"Here is a full [NGINX vhost with WebTunnel example](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/-/snippets/190)."
msgstr ""
"Här finns ett fullständigt [exempel på en virtuell NGINX-värd med WebTunnel]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/-/snippets/190)."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"If you already have a website domain, you can either use the main domain or "
"create a subdomain."
msgstr ""
"Om du redan har en webbplatsdomän kan du använda huvuddomänen eller skapa en "
"underdomän."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"If your website doesn't have a TLS certificate, you can obtain one by using "
"[acme.sh](https://github.com/acmesh-official/acme.sh), which is an ACME "
"protocol client written in Shell language."
msgstr ""
"Om webbplatsen saknar TLS-certifikat kan du skaffa ett med [acme.sh](https://"
"github.com/acmesh-official/acme.sh), en klient för ACME-protokollet som är "
"skriven i skalspråk."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"In this guide, the WebTunnel bridge is hosted on the same server as your "
"website, but it's possible to host it in a different server."
msgstr ""
"I den här vägledningen finns WebTunnel-bron på samma server som webbplatsen, "
"men den kan även finnas på en annan server."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Install NGINX:"
msgstr "Installera NGINX:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "NGINX vhost block example"
msgstr "Exempel på block för en virtuell NGINX-värd"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"Now, you must install and configure your bridge to receive these requests "
"from the web server."
msgstr ""
"Nu behöver du installera och konfigurera bron så att den tar emot "
"begärandena från webbservern."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Or"
msgstr "Eller"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"Or if you want to use an existing vhost, you can just edit and add the "
"```location {}``` block to it."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill använda en befintlig virtuell värd kan du i stället redigera den "
"och lägga till blocket ```location {}```."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Please follow the second part of this guide."
msgstr "Följ den andra delen av vägledningen."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"Please note that if you don't meet the requirements to run a WebTunnel or "
"obfs4 bridge, running a [Snowflake proxy](../../setup/snowflake) is a great "
"way to donate your bandwidth to help users circumvent censorship."
msgstr ""
"Observera att en [Snowflake-proxy](../../setup/snowflake) är ett utmärkt "
"sätt att bidra med bandbredd och hjälpa användare att kringgå censur om du "
"inte uppfyller kraven för att driva en WebTunnel- eller obfs4-bro."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Replace `$PATH` with the random string."
msgstr "Ersätt `$PATH` med den slumpmässiga strängen."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Replace `example.com` with your website domain."
msgstr "Ersätt `example.com` med webbplatsens domän."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Replace `my@example.com` with your email address:"
msgstr "Ersätt `my@example.com` med din e-postadress:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Set Proxy headers ###"
msgstr "Ange proxyhuvuden ###"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Set WebSocket headers ###"
msgstr "Ange WebSocket-huvuden ###"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Step 1. Configure your domain"
msgstr "Steg 1. Konfigurera domänen"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Step 2. Obtain a valid certificate"
msgstr "Steg 2. Skaffa ett giltigt certifikat"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Step 3. Install NGINX"
msgstr "Steg 3. Installera NGINX"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Step 4. Configure NGINX"
msgstr "Steg 4. Konfigurera NGINX"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Step 5. Configure your Tor WebTunnel bridge"
msgstr "Steg 5. Konfigurera Tor WebTunnel-bron"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"The first part of this guide provides detailed instructions for configuring "
"your web server to support WebTunnel."
msgstr ""
"Den första delen av vägledningen innehåller detaljerade anvisningar för att "
"konfigurera webbservern för WebTunnel."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "The requirements for deploying a WebTunnel bridge are:"
msgstr "Kraven för att distribuera en WebTunnel-bro är:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"The second part, you will choose between two methods for running the "
"WebTunnel bridge: either using Docker or by compiling from the source code."
msgstr ""
"I den andra delen väljer du mellan två metoder för att köra WebTunnel-bron: "
"använda Docker eller kompilera från källkod."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"This guide will help you set up a WebTunnel bridge to help censored users "
"connect to the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Den här vägledningen hjälper dig att konfigurera en WebTunnel-bro så att "
"censurerade användare kan ansluta till Tor-nätverket."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"To coexist with other content on a single port, you should install a reverse "
"proxy, such as NGINX."
msgstr ""
"Installera en omvänd proxy, till exempel NGINX, så att flera typer av "
"innehåll kan använda samma port."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "Web server configuration"
msgstr "Webbserverkonfiguration"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"When clients connect to your web server, they will be redirected to your "
"WebTunnel proxy when they use a secret path."
msgstr ""
"När klienter ansluter till webbservern omdirigeras de till WebTunnel-proxyn "
"om de använder en hemlig sökväg."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "You can generate a random string by running this command:"
msgstr "Du kan skapa en slumpmässig sträng genom att köra följande kommando:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"You have two options available: either compile a Go binary from the [source]"
"(source) or use [Docker](docker)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan antingen kompilera en Go-binärfil från [källkoden](source) eller "
"använda [Docker](docker)."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"[WebTunnel](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-censorship/pluggable-"
"transports/webtunnel) is a pluggable transport that attempts to imitate web "
"browsing activities based on [HTTPT](https://censorbib.nymity.ch/"
"#Frolov2020b)."
msgstr ""
"[WebTunnel](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/anti-censorship/pluggable-"
"transports/webtunnel) är en pluggbar transport som försöker efterlikna "
"webbsurfning utifrån [HTTPT](https://censorbib.nymity.ch/#Frolov2020b)."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid "WebTunnel Bridge"
msgstr "WebTunnel-bro"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/
msgid ""
"Run a WebTunnel bridge to help censored users connect to the Tor network"
msgstr ""
"Driv en WebTunnel-bro för att hjälpa censurerade användare att ansluta till "
"Tor-nätverket"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "0. Configure your domain and web server"
msgstr "0. Konfigurera domänen och webbservern"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid "1. Install Docker runtime"
msgstr "1. Installera Docker-körmiljön"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid "2. Run Dockerized WebTunnel bridge"
msgstr "2. Kör en WebTunnel-bro i Docker"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid "3. Download the WebTunnel docker compose file"
msgstr "3. Hämta Docker Compose-filen för WebTunnel"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid "4. Start your WebTunnel bridge"
msgstr "4. Starta WebTunnel-bron"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid "5. Test your WebTunnel bridge"
msgstr "5. Testa WebTunnel-bron"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"Before you proceed with the instructions below, it's necessary to configure "
"your domain and web server first."
msgstr ""
"Innan du fortsätter med anvisningarna nedan måste du först konfigurera "
"domänen och webbservern."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"By default, your docker WebTunnel bridge will be distributed via  [Bridges "
"website](https://bridges.torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Som standard distribueras WebTunnel-bron i Docker via [webbplatsen Bridges]"
"(https://bridges.torproject.org)."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"It's just there because the pluggable transport specification requires an IP "
"address there."
msgstr ""
"Den finns endast där eftersom specifikationen för pluggbara transporter "
"kräver en IP-adress på platsen."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"Note that this Docker compose file includes auto-update by default, and will "
"update the WebTunnel bridge server without any further action."
msgstr ""
"Observera att Docker Compose-filen innehåller automatiska uppdateringar som "
"standard och uppdaterar WebTunnel-broservern utan ytterligare åtgärder."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"Refer to the first part of the [WebTunnel guide](../../webtunnel) to see how "
"to set up your website domain and web server."
msgstr ""
"Se den första delen av [WebTunnel-vägledningen](../../webtunnel) för att "
"konfigurera webbplatsdomänen och webbservern."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid "Remove `watchtower` to disable this behavior."
msgstr "Ta bort `watchtower` för att inaktivera beteendet."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"Replace `URL` with your domain and path (refer to the first part of the "
"WebTunnel guide), and `OPERATOR_EMAIL` with your email address, then run:"
msgstr ""
"Ersätt `URL` med domänen och sökvägen enligt den första delen av WebTunnel-"
"vägledningen och `OPERATOR_EMAIL` med din e-postadress. Kör sedan:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid "The IPv6 address you get is randomly generated and never used."
msgstr "IPv6-adressen du får skapas slumpmässigt och används aldrig."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"These commands will create an environment file (`.env`) for the "
"configuration of WebTunnel bridge."
msgstr ""
"Kommandona skapar en miljöfil (`.env`) för konfigurationen av WebTunnel-bron."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"This guide will help you set up a WebTunnel bridge using Docker to help "
"censored users connect to the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Den här vägledningen hjälper dig att konfigurera en WebTunnel-bro med Docker "
"så att censurerade användare kan ansluta till Tor-nätverket."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"You can copy and paste the bridge line in Tor Browser, and it should work."
msgstr ""
"Du kan kopiera och klistra in broraden i Tor Browser, och då bör den fungera."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid ""
"You can obtain your bridge line address and verify if it is working by "
"running:"
msgstr "Du kan hämta broraden och kontrollera att den fungerar genom att köra:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid "How to run a WebTunnel bridge on Docker"
msgstr "Så kör du en WebTunnel-bro med Docker"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/docker/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/docker/
msgid "WebTunnel Docker setup"
msgstr "Docker-konfiguration för WebTunnel"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "1. Install Golang"
msgstr "1. Installera Golang"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "2. Clone and compile"
msgstr "2. Klona och kompilera"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "4. Edit your torrc"
msgstr "4. Redigera torrc-filen"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "5. Restart Tor"
msgstr "5. Starta om Tor"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "6. Edit and reload AppArmor tor permission"
msgstr "6. Redigera och läs in AppArmor-behörigheten för Tor på nytt"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "8. Final notes"
msgstr "8. Avslutande anmärkningar"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"After having set up the bridge, it takes approximately three hours for the "
"bridge to show up in Relay Search."
msgstr ""
"När bron har konfigurerats tar det ungefär tre timmar innan den visas i "
"Relay Search."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"After modifying the profile and reloading it, test to see if the tor process "
"can now execute `/usr/local/bin/webtunnel` without any AppArmor denials."
msgstr ""
"När profilen har ändrats och lästs in på nytt testar du om Tor-processen nu "
"kan köra `/usr/local/bin/webtunnel` utan att AppArmor nekar åtkomst."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "And compile the WebTunnel server binary:"
msgstr "Kompilera sedan den körbara filen för WebTunnel-servern:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "And run these commands to enable the Tor Debian repository:"
msgstr "Kör sedan följande kommandon för att aktivera Tors Debian-paketförråd:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"Check the system logs (e.g., `dmesg` or `/var/log/syslog`) to ensure the "
"error doesn't reappear."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollera systemloggarna, till exempel `dmesg` eller `/var/log/syslog`, "
"och se till att felet inte återkommer."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "Clone the WebTunnel git repository:"
msgstr "Klona Git-kodförrådet för WebTunnel:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "EOF"
msgstr "EOF"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"Edit your Tor config file, usually located at `/etc/tor/torrc` and replace "
"its contents with:"
msgstr ""
"Redigera Tors konfigurationsfil, som vanligtvis finns i `/etc/tor/torrc`, "
"och ersätt innehållet med följande:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "Enable and Start tor:"
msgstr "Aktivera och starta Tor:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "Finally, copy the binary to another location:"
msgstr "Kopiera slutligen den körbara filen till en annan plats:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "Finally, update your package list and install Tor:"
msgstr "Uppdatera slutligen paketlistan och installera Tor:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"Finally, you can replace the URL contents with your domain and secret path."
msgstr "Ersätt slutligen URL-innehållet med domänen och den hemliga sökvägen."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"If set to any option other than `HTTPS`, the bridge will not be distributed "
"to users."
msgstr ""
"Om något annat alternativ än `HTTPS` anges distribueras bron inte till "
"användare."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"If you are having trouble setting up your bridge, have a look at our [help "
"section](relay/getting-help)."
msgstr ""
"Se vårt [hjälpavsnitt](relay/getting-help) om du har problem med att "
"konfigurera bron."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"If you copy the hashed fingerprint instead of your bridge fingerprint, you "
"won't be able to connect."
msgstr ""
"Om du kopierar det hashade fingeravtrycket i stället för brons fingeravtryck "
"kan du inte ansluta."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"If your bridge is now running, you can test it by copying and pasting your "
"bridge line into Tor Browser."
msgstr ""
"Om bron nu körs kan du testa den genom att kopiera och klistra in broraden i "
"Tor Browser."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "Import the Tor Project keyring:"
msgstr "Importera The Tor Projects nyckelring:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"Just enter your bridge's `<HASHED FINGERPRINT>` in the form and click "
"\"Search\"."
msgstr "Ange brons `<HASHED FINGERPRINT>` i formuläret och klicka på ”Search”."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"Now, just replace the content below to create your WebTunnel bridge line. "
"10.0.0.2:443 is just a random IP address that's never used. It's just there "
"because the pluggable transport specification requires an IP address there."
msgstr ""
"Ersätt nu bara innehållet nedan för att skapa din WebTunnel-brolinje. "
"10.0.0.2:443 är bara en slumpmässig IP-adress som aldrig används. Den finns "
"bara där för att specifikationen för pluggbar transport kräver en IP-adress "
"där."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"On a Debian-like system, install Tor from the [Tor Debian repository]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/little-t-tor/getting-started/installing/)."
msgstr ""
"Installera Tor från [Tors Debian-paketförråd](https://support.torproject.org/"
"little-t-tor/getting-started/installing/) på ett Debian-liknande system."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"Refer to the first part of the [WebTunnel guide](../../webtunnel) to see how "
"to set up your web server."
msgstr ""
"Se den första delen av [WebTunnel-vägledningen](../../webtunnel) för "
"information om hur webbservern konfigureras."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "Reload the AppArmor profile:"
msgstr "Läs in AppArmor-profilen på nytt:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"Remember to copy only the fingerprint and do not include the bridge nickname."
msgstr "Kom ihåg att endast kopiera fingeravtrycket och inte brons smeknamn."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"This default applies unless an operator explicitly configures the "
"`BridgeDistribution` setting in the torrc file to a different option."
msgstr ""
"Standardvärdet gäller om inte en operatör uttryckligen anger ett annat "
"alternativ för inställningen `BridgeDistribution` i torrc-filen."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"This guide will help you set up a WebTunnel bridge compiled from the source "
"to help censored users connect to the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Den här vägledningen hjälper dig att konfigurera en WebTunnel-bro som "
"kompileras från källkod, så att censurerade användare kan ansluta till Tor-"
"nätverket."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"To allow tor to run your WebTunnel binary, edit the AppArmor `system_tor` "
"profile at `/etc/apparmor.d/system_tor` and add an entry allowing tor to "
"execute WebTunnel:"
msgstr ""
"För att låta Tor köra den körbara WebTunnel-filen redigerar du AppArmor-"
"profilen `system_tor` i `/etc/apparmor.d/system_tor` och lägger till en post "
"som tillåter Tor att köra WebTunnel:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"To build the WebTunnel server binary, you need to install [Golang](https://"
"go.dev/dl/)."
msgstr ""
"För att bygga den körbara filen för WebTunnel-servern behöver du installera "
"[Golang](https://go.dev/dl/)."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"To build your WebTunnel bridge line, you need to copy your bridge "
"`FINGERPRINT`, but don't confuse it with your hashed fingerprint, which is "
"the fingerprint that you will find on the Tor Relay Search website."
msgstr ""
"För att skapa broraden för WebTunnel behöver du kopiera brons `FINGERPRINT`. "
"Förväxla det inte med det hashade fingeravtrycket, som är det fingeravtryck "
"du hittar på webbplatsen Tor Relay Search."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"To confirm your bridge is running with no issues, you should see something "
"like this (usually in /var/log/syslog or run `sudo journalctl -e -u "
"tor@default`):"
msgstr ""
"För att bekräfta att bron körs utan problem bör du se något liknande detta, "
"vanligtvis i /var/log/syslog. Du kan även köra `sudo journalctl -e -u "
"tor@default`:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "You can find this in your torrc line under `ServerTransportOptions`."
msgstr "Det finns på raden `ServerTransportOptions` i torrc-filen."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"You can find your bridge fingerprint in the `/var/lib/tor/fingerprint` file."
msgstr "Brons fingeravtryck finns i filen `/var/lib/tor/fingerprint`."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "You can install Go on Debian by running:"
msgstr "Du kan installera Go på Debian genom att köra:"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"You can monitor your WebTunnel bridge's usage on [Relay Search](https://"
"metrics.torproject.org/rs.html#search)."
msgstr ""
"Du kan övervaka användningen av WebTunnel-bron i [Relay Search](https://"
"metrics.torproject.org/rs.html#search)."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"Your WebTunnel bridge will by default be automatically distributed via the "
"[Bridges website](https://bridges.torproject.org), also known as the `HTTPS` "
"distributor."
msgstr ""
"WebTunnel-bron distribueras som standard automatiskt via [webbplatsen "
"Bridges](https://bridges.torproject.org), även kallad `HTTPS`-distributören."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "`Nickname WebTunnetTest` with the nickname of your bridge."
msgstr "Ersätt smeknamnet i `Nickname WebTunnetTest` med brons smeknamn."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid ""
"`url=https://yourdomain/path` with your WebTunnel url including your domain "
"and secret path;"
msgstr ""
"Ersätt `url=https://yourdomain/path` med WebTunnel-URL:en, inklusive domänen "
"och den hemliga sökvägen."

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "How to run a WebTunnel bridge from the source"
msgstr "Så kör du en WebTunnel-bro från källkod"

#: content/relay/setup/webtunnel-bridge/source/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/setup/webtunnel/source/
msgid "Compile and run WebTunnel from the source"
msgstr "Kompilera och kör WebTunnel från källkod"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "A more diverse network is more resilient to attacks and outages."
msgstr ""
"Ett mer mångsidigt nätverk är mer motståndskraftigt mot angrepp och "
"driftavbrott."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "AS/location diversity"
msgstr "Mångfald av autonoma system och platser"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "Choosing a hosting provider"
msgstr "Välj värdleverantör"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "Choosing an Operating System"
msgstr "Välj operativsystem"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Correct time settings are essential for Tor relays. It is recommended that "
"you use the network time protocol (NTP) for time synchronization and ensure "
"your timezone is set correctly."
msgstr ""
"Korrekta tidsinställningar är avgörande för Tor-reläer. Vi rekommenderar att "
"du använder Network Time Protocol (NTP) för tidssynkronisering och "
"kontrollerar att tidszonen är rätt inställd."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Does the hoster allow Tor exit relays? We recommend you explicitly ask them "
"before getting started."
msgstr ""
"Tillåter värdleverantören Tor-utgångsreläer? Vi rekommenderar att du "
"uttryckligen frågar innan du börjar."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Does the hoster allow custom WHOIS records for your IP addresses? This helps "
"reduce the amount of abuse sent to the hoster instead of you."
msgstr ""
"Tillåter värdleverantören anpassade WHOIS-poster för IP-adresserna? Det "
"minskar antalet missbruksanmälningar som skickas till värdleverantören i "
"stället för till dig."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Does the hoster allow you to set a custom DNS reverse entry? (DNS PTR record)"
msgstr ""
"Tillåter värdleverantören att du anger en anpassad post för omvänd DNS, "
"alltså en DNS-PTR-post?"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Does the hoster provide IPv6 connectivity? It is recommended, but not "
"required."
msgstr ""
"Tillhandahåller värdleverantören IPv6-anslutning? Det rekommenderas men är "
"inget krav."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Does the hoster start to throttle bandwidth after a certain amount of "
"traffic?"
msgstr "Börjar värdleverantören strypa bandbredden efter en viss trafikmängd?"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"For more information on hosting providers and their policies on allowing Tor "
"relays, please see this list maintained by the Tor community: [GoodBadISPs]"
"(../community-resources/good-bad-isps/)."
msgstr ""
"Mer information om värdleverantörer och deras policyer för Tor-reläer finns "
"i listan som underhålls av Tor-gemenskapen: [GoodBadISPs](../community-"
"resources/good-bad-isps/)."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Having access to a high speed internet connection (>=100 Mbit/s in both "
"directions) and a physical piece of computer hardware is the best way to run "
"a relay."
msgstr ""
"Det bästa sättet att driva ett relä är att ha tillgång till en snabb "
"internetanslutning, minst 100 Mbit/s i båda riktningarna, och fysisk "
"datorutrustning."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Having full control over the hardware and connection gives you a more "
"controllable and (if done correctly) secure environment."
msgstr ""
"Full kontroll över utrustningen och anslutningen ger en mer kontrollerbar "
"och, om den hanteras rätt, säker miljö."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "How much monthly traffic is included? Is bandwidth \"unmetered\"?"
msgstr "Hur mycket trafik per månad ingår? Är bandbredden utan datagräns?"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "How well connected is the autonomous system of the hoster?"
msgstr "Hur välanslutet är värdleverantörens autonoma system?"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"If you do not own physical hardware, you could run a relay on a rented "
"dedicated server or virtual private server (VPS)."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte äger fysisk utrustning kan du driva ett relä på en hyrd dedikerad "
"server eller virtuell privat server (VPS)."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "If you plan to run exit relays"
msgstr "Om du planerar att driva utgångsreläer"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"It is best to avoid hosts where many Tor relays are already hosted, but it "
"is still better to add one there than to run no relay at all."
msgstr ""
"Det är bäst att undvika värdar där många Tor-reläer redan finns, men det är "
"fortfarande bättre att lägga till ett relä där än att inte driva något alls."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "Many VPS providers will not allow you to run exit relays."
msgstr "Många VPS-leverantörer tillåter inte utgångsreläer."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "Most relays currently run on Debian."
msgstr "De flesta reläer körs för närvarande på Debian."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "OS Level Configuration"
msgstr "Konfiguration på operativsystemsnivå"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"OS configuration is outside the scope of this guide, but the following "
"points are crucial for a Tor relay, so we want to mention them here "
"nonetheless."
msgstr ""
"Operativsystemskonfiguration ligger utanför vägledningens omfattning, men "
"följande punkter är avgörande för ett Tor-relä och nämns därför ändå."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "Questions to consider when choosing a host"
msgstr "Frågor att överväga när du väljer värd"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Sometimes it is not clear which AS you are buying from in case of resellers."
msgstr ""
"När det gäller återförsäljare är det ibland oklart vilket autonomt system du "
"faktiskt köper tjänsten från."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"Sometimes this is referred to as installing the relay on \"bare metal.\""
msgstr ""
"Det kallas ibland att installera reläet på ”bare metal”, alltså direkt på "
"fysisk maskinvara."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"The following table shows the current OS distribution on the Tor network to "
"give you an idea of how much more non-Linux relays we should have:"
msgstr ""
"Följande tabell visar den nuvarande fördelningen av operativsystem i Tor-"
"nätverket och ger en uppfattning om hur många fler reläer som inte bygger på "
"Linux som behövs:"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"This can cost anywhere between $3.00/month and thousands per month, "
"depending on your provider, hardware configuration, and bandwidth usage."
msgstr ""
"Kostnaden kan vara allt från 3 USD till flera tusen USD per månad, beroende "
"på leverantör, maskinvarukonfiguration och bandbreddsanvändning."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "Time Synchronization (NTP)"
msgstr "Tidssynkronisering (NTP)"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"To answer this question you can use the AS rank of the autonomous systems if "
"you want to compare: (a lower value is better) <https://asrank.caida.org/>"
msgstr ""
"Du kan jämföra de autonoma systemen med deras AS-rankning för att besvara "
"frågan. Ett lägre värde är bättre: <https://asrank.caida.org/>"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "To be sure, ask the host about the AS number before ordering a server."
msgstr ""
"Fråga värdleverantören om AS-numret innan du beställer en server för att "
"vara säker."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"To find out which host and countries are already used by many other "
"operators (that should be avoided) you can use Relay Search:"
msgstr ""
"Du kan använda Relay Search för att ta reda på vilka värdar och länder som "
"redan används av många andra operatörer och därför bör undvikas:"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"We recommend using the operating system you are most familiar with, but if "
"you're able, the network would most benefit from BSD and other non-Linux "
"based relays."
msgstr ""
"Vi rekommenderar det operativsystem som du känner bäst till. Om du har "
"möjlighet gynnas nätverket dock mest av BSD-reläer och andra reläer som inte "
"bygger på Linux."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"What virtualization / hypervisor (if any) does the provider use? Anything "
"but OpenVZ should be fine."
msgstr ""
"Vilken virtualisering eller hypervisor använder leverantören, om någon? Allt "
"utom OpenVZ bör fungera."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"When selecting your hosting provider, consider network diversity on an "
"autonomous system (AS) and country level."
msgstr ""
"När du väljer värdleverantör bör du ta hänsyn till nätverksmångfald på nivån "
"för autonoma system (AS) och länder."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"You can host your own physical hardware at home (do NOT run a Tor exit relay "
"from your home) or in a data center."
msgstr ""
"Du kan vara värd för egen fysisk utrustning hemma – driv **inte** ett Tor-"
"utgångsrelä hemifrån – eller i ett datacenter."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "You can usually ask these questions in a Pre-Sales ticket."
msgstr ""
"Du kan vanligtvis ställa frågorna i ett ärende till försäljningsavdelningen "
"innan köpet."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"You must follow the VPS provider's terms of service, or risk having your "
"account disabled."
msgstr ""
"Du måste följa VPS-leverantörens användarvillkor, annars riskerar kontot att "
"inaktiveras."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"[Autonomous System Level Overview](https://metrics.torproject.org/"
"rs.html#aggregate/as)"
msgstr ""
"[Översikt på nivån för autonoma system](https://metrics.torproject.org/"
"rs.html#aggregate/as)"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"[Country Level Overview](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html#aggregate/cc)"
msgstr ""
"[Översikt per land](https://metrics.torproject.org/rs.html#aggregate/cc)"

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid ""
"How to choose a good hosting provider, what's an AS and Operating System "
"diversity."
msgstr ""
"Så väljer du en bra värdleverantör och vad mångfald av autonoma system och "
"operativsystem innebär."

#: content/relay/technical-considerations/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/technical-considerations/
msgid "Technical considerations"
msgstr "Tekniska överväganden"

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid "(also known as non-exit relays)"
msgstr "(även kallade icke-utgångsreläer)"

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"**Important:** If you are running a relay from home with a single static IP "
"address and are concerned about your IP being blocked by certain online "
"services, consider running a bridge or a Tor [snowflake proxy](../setup/"
"snowflake/) instead."
msgstr ""
"**Viktigt:** Om du driver ett relä hemifrån med en enda statisk IP-adress "
"och oroar dig för att IP-adressen blockeras av vissa nättjänster bör du "
"överväga att driva en bro eller en Tor-[Snowflake-proxy](../setup/"
"snowflake/) i stället."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"A bridge isn't likely to receive any abuse complaints, and since bridges are "
"not listed as public relays, they are unlikely to be blocked by popular "
"services."
msgstr ""
"En bro får sannolikt inga missbruksanmälningar, och eftersom broar inte "
"listas som offentliga reläer blockeras de sannolikt inte av populära "
"tjänster."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid "A guard relay is the first relay (hop) in a Tor circuit."
msgstr "Ett vaktrelä är det första reläet, eller hoppet, i en Tor-krets."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"A middle relay is a relay that acts as the second hop in the Tor circuit."
msgstr "Ett mellanrelä fungerar som det andra hoppet i Tor-kretsen."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"A non-exit Tor relay requires minimal maintenance efforts and bandwidth "
"usage can be highly customized in the Tor configuration."
msgstr ""
"Ett Tor-relä utan utgång kräver mycket lite underhåll och "
"bandbreddsanvändningen kan anpassas noggrant i Tor-konfigurationen."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid "A non-exit relay does not allow exiting in its exit policy."
msgstr "Ett icke-utgångsrelä tillåter ingen utgångstrafik i utgångspolicyn."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"All types of relays are important, but they have different technical "
"requirements and potential legal implications."
msgstr ""
"Alla relätyper är viktiga, men de har olika tekniska krav och möjliga "
"juridiska konsekvenser."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"An institution can not only provide greater bandwidth for the exit, but is "
"better positioned to handle abuse complaints or the rare law enforcement "
"inquiry."
msgstr ""
"En institution kan inte bara tillhandahålla högre bandbredd för "
"utgångsreläet, utan är också bättre rustad att hantera missbruksanmälningar "
"och sällsynta förfrågningar från brottsbekämpande myndigheter."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Any abuse complaints about the exit will go directly to you (via your "
"hosting provider, depending on the WHOIS records)."
msgstr ""
"Alla missbruksanmälningar om utgångsreläet skickas direkt till dig, "
"eventuellt via värdleverantören beroende på WHOIS-posterna."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Because of the legal exposure that comes with running an exit relay, you "
"should not run a Tor exit relay from your home."
msgstr ""
"På grund av den juridiska exponeringen som följer med ett utgångsrelä bör du "
"inte driva ett Tor-utgångsrelä hemifrån."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Bridges are a great option if you can only run a Tor node from your home "
"network, have only one static IP, and don't have a large amount of bandwidth "
"to donate -- we recommend giving your bridge at least 1 Mbit/sec of "
"bandwidth."
msgstr ""
"Broar är ett bra alternativ om du endast kan driva en Tor-nod från "
"hemnätverket, bara har en statisk IP-adress och inte kan bidra med särskilt "
"mycket bandbredd. Vi rekommenderar minst 1 Mbit/s bandbredd för bron."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Bridges are relatively easy, low-risk and low bandwidth Tor nodes to "
"operate, but they have a big impact on users."
msgstr ""
"Broar är relativt enkla Tor-noder med låg risk och liten "
"bandbreddsanvändning, men de har stor betydelse för användarna."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Bridges are useful for Tor users under oppressive regimes or for people who "
"want an extra layer of security because they're worried somebody will "
"recognize that they are contacting a public Tor relay IP address."
msgstr ""
"Broar är användbara för Tor-användare under förtryckande regimer och för "
"personer som vill ha ett extra säkerhetslager eftersom de oroar sig för att "
"någon ska upptäcka att de kontaktar en offentlig IP-adress för ett Tor-relä."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid "Example Tor Circuit:"
msgstr "Exempel på Tor-krets:"

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Exit relays have the greatest legal exposure and liability of all the relays."
msgstr ""
"Utgångsreläer medför den största juridiska exponeringen och ansvarrisken av "
"alla relätyper."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"For example, if a user downloads copyrighted material while using your exit "
"relay, you, the operator may receive a [DMCA notice](https://www.dmca.com/"
"Solutions/view.aspx?ID=712f28a5-93f2-467b-ba92-3d58c8345a32&?ref=sol08a2)."
msgstr ""
"Om en användare till exempel hämtar upphovsrättsskyddat material via ditt "
"utgångsrelä kan du som operatör få ett [DMCA-meddelande](https://"
"www.dmca.com/Solutions/view.aspx?ID=712f28a5-93f2-467b-ba92-3d58c8345a32&?"
"ref=sol08a2)."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Generally, most complaints can be handled pretty easily through [template "
"letters](../community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/)."
msgstr ""
"De flesta klagomål kan i allmänhet hanteras ganska enkelt med [brevmallar]"
"(../community-resources/tor-abuse-templates/)."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid "Guard and middle relays"
msgstr "Vakt- och mellanreläer"

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid "Guard and middle relays usually do not receive abuse complaints."
msgstr "Vakt- och mellanreläer får vanligtvis inga missbruksanmälningar."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"However, all relays are listed in the public Tor relay directory, and as a "
"result, they may be blocked by certain services."
msgstr ""
"Alla reläer finns dock i den offentliga Tor-reläkatalogen och kan därför "
"blockeras av vissa tjänster."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"However, one of the ways Tor can be blocked by governments or ISPs is by "
"blocklisting the IP addresses of these public Tor relays."
msgstr ""
"Ett sätt för myndigheter eller internetleverantörer att blockera Tor är att "
"blocklista IP-adresserna till de offentliga Tor-reläerna."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Ideal exit relay operators are affiliated with some institution, like a "
"[relay association](../community-resources/relay-associations/), a "
"university, a library, a hackerspace or a privacy related organization."
msgstr ""
"Idealiska operatörer av utgångsreläer är anslutna till en institution, till "
"exempel en [reläförening](../community-resources/relay-associations/), ett "
"universitet, bibliotek, hackerspace eller en integritetsorganisation."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"If you are considering running an exit relay, please read the [section on "
"legal considerations](../community-resources) for exit relay operators."
msgstr ""
"Läs [avsnittet om juridiska överväganden](../community-resources) för "
"utgångsreläoperatörer om du överväger att driva ett utgångsrelä."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Please see the [relay requirements](../relays-requirements/) page to learn "
"about the technical requirements for each relay type."
msgstr ""
"Läs sidan med [reläkrav](../relays-requirements/) för information om de "
"tekniska kraven för varje relätyp."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Several countries, including China and Iran, have found ways to detect and "
"block connections to Tor bridges."
msgstr ""
"Flera länder, däribland Kina och Iran, har hittat sätt att upptäcka och "
"blockera anslutningar till Tor-broar."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"The design of the Tor network means that the IP addresses of Tor relays "
"(guard, middle, and exit) are public."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverkets utformning innebär att IP-adresserna till Tor-reläer – vakt-, "
"mellan- och utgångsreläer – är offentliga."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"The exit relay is the final relay in a Tor circuit, the one that sends "
"traffic out to its destination."
msgstr ""
"Utgångsreläet är det sista reläet i en Tor-krets och skickar trafiken vidare "
"till destinationen."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"The services Tor clients are connecting to (website, chat service, email "
"provider, etc) will see the IP address of the exit relay instead of the real "
"IP address of the Tor user."
msgstr ""
"Tjänsterna som Tor-klienter ansluter till, såsom webbplatser, chattjänster "
"och e-postleverantörer, ser utgångsreläets IP-adress i stället för Tor-"
"användarens riktiga IP-adress."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"The so called \"exit policy\" of the relay decides if it is a relay allowing "
"clients to exit or not."
msgstr ""
"Reläets så kallade utgångspolicy avgör om klienter får lämna Tor-nätverket "
"via reläet."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"These include services that either misunderstand how Tor works or "
"deliberately want to censor Tor users, for example, online banking and "
"streaming services."
msgstr ""
"Det omfattar tjänster som antingen missförstår hur Tor fungerar eller "
"avsiktligt vill censurera Tor-användare, till exempel nätbanker och "
"strömningstjänster."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"This alternative can help prevent your non-Tor traffic from being mistakenly "
"blocked as though it's coming from a Tor relay."
msgstr ""
"Alternativet kan förhindra att din trafik utanför Tor av misstag blockeras "
"som om den kom från ett Tor-relä."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"To become a guard relay, the relay has to be stable and fast (at least "
"2MByte/s of upstream and downstream bandwidth) otherwise it will remain a "
"middle relay."
msgstr ""
"För att bli vaktrelä måste reläet vara stabilt och snabbt, med minst 2 MB/s "
"bandbredd både uppströms och nedströms. Annars förblir det ett mellanrelä."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Tor User -> Bridge Relay -> Middle Relay -> Exit Relay -> Destination (i.e "
"example.com)"
msgstr ""
"Tor-användare → brorelä → mellanrelä → utgångsrelä → destination (till "
"exempel example.com)"

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Tor User -> Guard Relay -> Middle Relay -> Exit Relay -> Destination (i.e "
"example.com)"
msgstr ""
"Tor-användare → vaktrelä → mellanrelä → utgångsrelä → destination (till "
"exempel example.com)"

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Tor bridges are relays in the network that are not listed in the public Tor "
"directory, which makes it harder for ISPs and governments to block them."
msgstr ""
"Tor-broar är reläer i nätverket som inte listas i den offentliga Tor-"
"katalogen, vilket gör dem svårare för internetleverantörer och myndigheter "
"att blockera."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Understanding the different kinds of relays is the first step to learning "
"which one is right for you."
msgstr ""
"Att förstå de olika relätyperna är det första steget för att avgöra vilken "
"som passar dig."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid "When using a bridge:"
msgstr "När en bro används:"

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"[Pluggable transports](https://tb-manual.torproject.org/circumvention/), a "
"special kind of bridge, address this by adding an additional layer of "
"obfuscation."
msgstr ""
"[Pluggbara transporter](https://tb-manual.torproject.org/circumvention/) är "
"en särskild typ av bro som motverkar detta genom att lägga till ytterligare "
"ett obfuskeringslager."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid ""
"Bridges, guards, middle relays, and exits all serve important functions in "
"the Tor network. Learn about the different relays you can run."
msgstr ""
"Broar, vaktreläer, mellanreläer och utgångsreläer fyller alla viktiga "
"funktioner i Tor-nätverket. Lär dig mer om de olika reläerna du kan driva."

#: content/relay/types-of-relays/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/relay/types-of-relays/
msgid "Types of relays on the Tor network"
msgstr "Relätyper i Tor-nätverket"

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid ""
"**Note**: This threat model documentation is incomplete and a work-in-"
"progress at this point."
msgstr ""
"**Obs!** Dokumentationen av hotmodellen är ofullständig och fortfarande "
"under arbete."

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid ""
"A comprehensive threat model helps to identify potential vulnerabilities, "
"assess the risks, and design appropriate mitigation strategies to protect "
"both users and the network itself."
msgstr ""
"En heltäckande hotmodell hjälper till att identifiera möjliga sårbarheter, "
"bedöma risker och utforma lämpliga motåtgärder som skyddar både användarna "
"och själva nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid ""
"As an open and decentralized system, Tor relies on a global network of "
"volunteer-operated relays, making it both resilient and a target for various "
"forms of attacks."
msgstr ""
"Tor är ett öppet och decentraliserat system som bygger på ett globalt "
"nätverk av reläer drivna av volontärer. Det gör nätverket både "
"motståndskraftigt och till ett mål för olika slags angrepp."

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid ""
"In this section, we provide a detailed overview of the adversaries targeting "
"Tor, their methods of attack, and the systems in place to counter them, "
"helping Tor continue to serve as a secure platform for privacy-conscious "
"users."
msgstr ""
"I det här avsnittet ger vi en detaljerad översikt över motståndarna som "
"angriper Tor, deras angreppsmetoder och systemen som motverkar dem, så att "
"Tor kan fortsätta vara en säker plattform för integritetsmedvetna användare."

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid ""
"It mainly covers elements we worked on during a project on improving network "
"health."
msgstr ""
"Det omfattar främst delar som vi arbetade med i ett projekt för att "
"förbättra nätverkets hälsa."

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid "Large parts, e.g. related to onion services, are still missing."
msgstr ""
"Stora delar saknas fortfarande, till exempel sådant som gäller onion-"
"tjänster."

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid ""
"The Tor network, designed to safeguard privacy and enable anonymous "
"communication, is constantly under threat from adversaries who seek to "
"exploit its vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverket är utformat för att skydda integritet och möjliggöra anonym "
"kommunikation, men hotas ständigt av motståndare som försöker utnyttja dess "
"sårbarheter."

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid ""
"These threats range from malicious relays attempting to disrupt traffic or "
"compromise user anonymity, to sophisticated surveillance tactics aimed at "
"deanonymizing users or undermining the network’s integrity."
msgstr ""
"Hoten sträcker sig från illasinnade reläer som försöker störa trafiken eller "
"äventyra användarnas anonymitet till avancerade övervakningsmetoder som "
"försöker avanonymisera användare eller undergräva nätverkets integritet."

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid ""
"To defend against these threats, it is important to understand the types of "
"attackers the network faces, their capabilities, and their objectives."
msgstr ""
"För att försvara nätverket mot hoten är det viktigt att förstå vilka typer "
"av angripare det möter, deras förmågor och mål."

#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.cta
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid "Learn about threats"
msgstr "Lär dig om hot"

