#: content/threat-model/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/
msgid "How we mitigate threats to Tor"
msgstr "Så motverkar vi hot mot Tor"

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Additionally, our network health team carries out investigations to discover "
"new or unknown attacks that might bypass automated systems."
msgstr ""
"Dessutom genomför Network Health-teamet utredningar för att upptäcka nya "
"eller okända angrepp som kan kringgå automatiserade system."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Beyond technical measures, Tor emphasizes community-building. A trusted and "
"tight-knit community can make it more difficult for attackers to operate."
msgstr ""
"Utöver tekniska åtgärder betonar Tor vikten av gemenskapsbyggande. En "
"betrodd och sammansvetsad gemenskap kan göra det svårare för angripare att "
"verka."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Building trust within the relay operator community is a long-term effort, "
"that is supported by regular meet-ups, open discussions, and transparent "
"processes aimed at improving the network’s health."
msgstr ""
"Att bygga förtroende i reläoperatörsgemenskapen är ett långsiktigt arbete "
"som stöds av regelbundna sammankomster, öppna diskussioner och transparenta "
"processer för att förbättra nätverkets hälsa."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"Community members can help identify malicious relays by reporting suspicious "
"behavior through channels such as emails or other reporting systems."
msgstr ""
"Gemenskapsmedlemmar kan hjälpa till att identifiera illasinnade reläer genom "
"att rapportera misstänkt beteende via e-post eller andra rapporteringssystem."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"For example, implementing features like HTTPS-only mode in Tor Browser "
"strengthens overall security and helps reduce the risks posed by malicious "
"exit relays."
msgstr ""
"Funktioner som endast HTTPS-läge i Tor Browser stärker till exempel den "
"övergripande säkerheten och minskar riskerna från illasinnade utgångsreläer."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid "Mitigating Malicious Relays"
msgstr "Motverka illasinnade reläer"

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"The open nature of the Tor network means that preventing malicious or "
"misconfigured relays from joining is nearly impossible."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverkets öppna karaktär gör det nästan omöjligt att hindra illasinnade "
"eller felkonfigurerade reläer från att ansluta sig."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"This combination of technical, social, and external improvements forms Tor’s "
"strategy for mitigating threats stemming from malicious relays and keeping "
"the network safe."
msgstr ""
"Kombinationen av tekniska, sociala och externa förbättringar utgör Tors "
"strategi för att motverka hot från illasinnade reläer och hålla nätverket "
"säkert."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"This helps identify relays that may be intentionally tampering with traffic "
"or undermining the network’s security."
msgstr ""
"Det hjälper till att identifiera reläer som avsiktligt kan manipulera trafik "
"eller undergräva nätverkets säkerhet."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"To address this, we take a multi-faceted approach to detect and mitigate "
"these threats."
msgstr ""
"Vi använder ett mångsidigt tillvägagångssätt för att upptäcka och motverka "
"hoten."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"We also stay engaged with third-party applications and tools that can aid in "
"the fight against malicious relays."
msgstr ""
"Vi samarbetar även med tredjepartsappar och verktyg som kan hjälpa till i "
"kampen mot illasinnade reläer."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/bad-relays/
msgid ""
"We’ve set up systems to constantly perform automatic network scans to detect "
"any signs of malicious activity."
msgstr ""
"Vi har infört system som kontinuerligt utför automatiska nätverksskanningar "
"för att upptäcka tecken på illasinnad aktivitet."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/
msgid ""
"As a privacy-focused network, Tor is constantly exposed to a wide range of "
"threats that aim to undermine its security and functionality."
msgstr ""
"Som ett integritetsinriktat nätverk utsätts Tor ständigt för ett brett "
"spektrum av hot som försöker undergräva dess säkerhet och funktion."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/
msgid ""
"By combining technical safeguards, community collaboration, and continuous "
"innovation, Tor actively works to detect and address threats before they can "
"cause harm."
msgstr ""
"Genom att kombinera tekniska skydd, samarbete i gemenskapen och kontinuerlig "
"innovation arbetar Tor aktivt för att upptäcka och hantera hot innan de "
"orsakar skada."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/
msgid "Network threat mitigation systems"
msgstr "System för att motverka nätverkshot"

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/
msgid ""
"These systems are crucial in preserving the safety and reliability of the "
"Tor network, allowing it to continue operating as a secure tool for users "
"around the world."
msgstr ""
"Systemen är avgörande för att bevara Tor-nätverkets säkerhet och "
"tillförlitlighet och låta det fortsätta fungera som ett säkert verktyg för "
"användare världen över."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/
msgid ""
"To fight against these threats, Tor employs a variety of threat mitigation "
"systems designed to protect the network from malicious activity, both "
"technical and social in nature."
msgstr ""
"För att bekämpa hoten använder Tor flera system som skyddar nätverket mot "
"både teknisk och social illasinnad aktivitet."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/
msgid "Network Threats Mitigation"
msgstr "Motverka nätverkshot"

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/
msgid ""
"A key part of defending against DoS threats involves collaboration with the "
"[relay operator community](https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/"
"relay-operators/) and [Directory Authorities](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-"
"authority/)."
msgstr ""
"En viktig del av försvaret mot DoS-hot är samarbetet med "
"[reläoperatörsgemenskapen](https://community.torproject.org/relay/governance/"
"relay-operators/) och [katalogauktoriteterna](https://"
"community.torproject.org/relay/governance/policies-and-proposals/directory-"
"authority/)."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/
msgid "Addressing Denial of Service (DoS) Threats"
msgstr "Hantera överbelastningsangrepp (DoS)"

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/
msgid ""
"However, this system can't handle all the types of DoS attacks the network "
"faces, and redesigning it is beyond the scope of C-Tor."
msgstr ""
"Systemet kan dock inte hantera alla typer av DoS-angrepp som nätverket "
"utsätts för, och en ny utformning ligger utanför C-Tors omfattning."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/
msgid ""
"Mitigating all possible **Denial of Service (DoS)** attacks in the Tor "
"network is a complex task."
msgstr ""
"Det är en komplicerad uppgift att motverka alla möjliga "
"**överbelastningsangrepp (DoS)** i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/
msgid ""
"The current C-Tor implementation includes an anti-DoS system that defends "
"against the most critical vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""
"Den nuvarande C-Tor-implementeringen innehåller ett anti-DoS-system som "
"skyddar mot de mest kritiska sårbarheterna."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/
msgid ""
"Their input has been proved essential in testing potential fixes and "
"workarounds, especially in cases where the current anti-DoS system has "
"limitations that prevent direct solutions."
msgstr ""
"Deras synpunkter har visat sig vara avgörande för att testa möjliga "
"korrigeringar och tillfälliga lösningar, särskilt när begränsningar i det "
"nuvarande anti-DoS-systemet förhindrar direkta lösningar."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/
msgid ""
"These groups have played a crucial role in identifying and understanding DoS "
"attacks in the real world."
msgstr ""
"Grupperna har spelat en avgörande roll för att identifiera och förstå "
"verkliga DoS-angrepp."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/
msgid ""
"To fill these gaps, the remaining DoS vulnerabilities are addressed in the "
"new Rust-based implementation, [Arti](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/"
"arti)."
msgstr ""
"De återstående DoS-sårbarheterna hanteras i den nya Rust-baserade "
"implementeringen [Arti](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/arti)."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/dos-threats/
msgid ""
"We hope that by working together, we can reduce both the short- and long-"
"term impacts of these attacks."
msgstr ""
"Vi hoppas att gemensamt arbete kan minska både de kortsiktiga och "
"långsiktiga konsekvenserna av angreppen."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"A **bandwidth inflation attack** happens when a malicious relay in the Tor "
"network falsely reports a higher bandwidth capacity than it actually has."
msgstr ""
"Ett **bandbreddsinflationsangrepp** inträffar när ett illasinnat relä i Tor-"
"nätverket felaktigt rapporterar en högre bandbreddskapacitet än det faktiskt "
"har."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"Another emerging threat comes from passive application-layer traffic "
"patterns."
msgstr ""
"Ett annat framväxande hot kommer från passiva trafikmönster på programlagret."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"By focusing on the most serious issues, Tor continues to enhance the "
"security and reliability of the network."
msgstr ""
"Genom att fokusera på de allvarligaste problemen fortsätter Tor att "
"förbättra nätverkets säkerhet och tillförlitlighet."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"In a bandwidth inflation attack, the attacker manipulates the system by "
"making their relay appear faster or more capable than it really is."
msgstr ""
"Vid ett bandbreddsinflationsangrepp manipulerar angriparen systemet så att "
"reläet verkar snabbare eller mer kapabelt än det verkligen är."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid "Resolving Information Leaks"
msgstr "Åtgärda informationsläckor"

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"These include cryptographic tagging, manipulation of cell headers, and "
"dropped cells. Tor’s new project, the [Arti](https://gitlab.torproject.org/"
"tpo/core/arti) client, resolves these critical vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""
"Det omfattar kryptografisk taggning, manipulering av cellhuvuden och "
"borttappade celler. Tors nya klientprojekt [Arti](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/arti) åtgärdar dessa kritiska sårbarheter."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"This gives the malicious relay a greater chance of being used in the network."
msgstr ""
"Det ökar sannolikheten för att det illasinnade reläet används i nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"This means that an attacker could monitor traffic and, based on the size, "
"timing, or frequency of data packets, make educated guesses about the "
"content or nature of the user's activity without directly interacting with "
"or altering the data."
msgstr ""
"Det innebär att en angripare kan övervaka trafiken och utifrån datapaketens "
"storlek, tidpunkt eller frekvens göra välgrundade gissningar om innehållet "
"eller typen av användaraktivitet utan att direkt interagera med eller ändra "
"data."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"To counter this, Tor detects and removes relays that falsely inflate their "
"bandwidth, protecting users from these harmful relays."
msgstr ""
"Tor motverkar detta genom att upptäcka och ta bort reläer som felaktigt "
"blåser upp sin bandbredd och skyddar därmed användare från de skadliga "
"reläerna."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"To tackle this, we port a traffic analysis framework and simulator to Arti, "
"which will help in identifying and reducing these risks."
msgstr ""
"För att hantera detta porteras ett ramverk och en simulator för trafikanalys "
"till Arti, vilket hjälper till att identifiera och minska riskerna."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"Tor relays are ranked based on their reported and measured bandwidth, and "
"relays with higher bandwidth are more likely to be chosen by users to route "
"their traffic."
msgstr ""
"Tor-reläer rangordnas efter rapporterad och uppmätt bandbredd, och reläer "
"med högre bandbredd väljs oftare för att dirigera användarnas trafik."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"Tor’s protocol has various information leaks, and while not all have been "
"addressed yet, we focus on mitigating the most severe threats."
msgstr ""
"Tors protokoll har flera informationsläckor. Även om alla ännu inte har "
"åtgärdats fokuserar vi på att motverka de allvarligaste hoten."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/information-leaks/
msgid ""
"We also take action against bandwidth inflation attacks by detecting and "
"removing the malicious relays responsible."
msgstr ""
"Vi bekämpar även bandbreddsinflationsangrepp genom att upptäcka och ta bort "
"de ansvariga illasinnade reläerna."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"By having important conversations in the open, any attempts to harm the "
"project are more easily noticed and stopped."
msgstr ""
"När viktiga diskussioner förs öppet blir försök att skada projektet lättare "
"att upptäcka och stoppa."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"First, we keep discussions public and transparent. This openness helps to "
"build trust within the community and between contributors and the Tor "
"Project itself."
msgstr ""
"För det första håller vi diskussionerna offentliga och transparenta. "
"Öppenheten bidrar till att bygga förtroende inom gemenskapen och mellan "
"bidragsgivarna och The Tor Project."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid "Handling malicious relays, for example, is a group effort."
msgstr "Hantering av illasinnade reläer är till exempel en gemensam insats."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"In addition, Tor plans to share database dumps publicly so researchers can "
"help verify the data and its integrity, adding an extra layer of protection "
"against manipulation."
msgstr ""
"Tor planerar dessutom att offentliggöra databasdumpar så att forskare kan "
"hjälpa till att verifiera data och deras integritet, vilket ger ytterligare "
"skydd mot manipulering."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid "Mitigating Attacks on the Tor Project"
msgstr "Motverka angrepp mot The Tor Project"

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"Regular communication and clear policies also help to prevent confusion and "
"keep everyone aligned toward the same goals."
msgstr ""
"Regelbunden kommunikation och tydliga policyer hjälper också till att "
"förhindra förvirring och hålla alla inriktade på samma mål."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"The community and staff work together to identify and remove bad relays, so "
"the network stays secure."
msgstr ""
"Gemenskapen och personalen samarbetar för att identifiera och ta bort dåliga "
"reläer så att nätverket förblir säkert."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"This means that targeting or intimidating one person won’t stop the work "
"from getting done."
msgstr ""
"Det innebär att arbetet inte stoppas genom att en enda person utsätts för "
"angrepp eller hot."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"Though defending against targeted attacks is challenging, our approach—"
"combining transparency, teamwork,"
msgstr ""
"Även om det är svårt att försvara sig mot riktade angrepp hjälper vårt "
"arbetssätt – en kombination av transparens, lagarbete,"

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid "To address these threats, we do a few key things."
msgstr "Vi vidtar några centrala åtgärder för att hantera hoten."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"To protect our infrastructure, Tor takes extra precautions. Databases are "
"only accessible internally, and the information is shared through secure "
"systems designed to prevent disruption."
msgstr ""
"Tor vidtar extra försiktighetsåtgärder för att skydda infrastrukturen. "
"Databaser är endast åtkomliga internt, och information delas genom säkra "
"system som är utformade för att förhindra störningar."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"Tor’s open environment allows anyone to contribute by writing code or "
"engaging in discussions."
msgstr ""
"Tors öppna miljö låter vem som helst bidra genom att skriva kod eller delta "
"i diskussioner."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"Transparency is key, as it makes it harder for adversaries to exploit gaps "
"in communication or processes."
msgstr ""
"Transparens är avgörande eftersom den gör det svårare för motståndare att "
"utnyttja luckor i kommunikationen eller processerna."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"When it comes to defending against attacks on staff or specific systems, we "
"rely on teamwork, among other things."
msgstr ""
"För att försvara oss mot angrepp på personal eller särskilda system förlitar "
"vi oss bland annat på lagarbete."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"While this openness makes participation easy, it also presents opportunities "
"for adversaries to disrupt the project."
msgstr ""
"Även om öppenheten gör det enkelt att delta ger den också motståndare "
"möjligheter att störa projektet."

#: content/threat-model/mitigation/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/mitigation/project/
msgid ""
"and secure infrastructure—helps the project remain strong and resilient in "
"the face of threats."
msgstr ""
"och säker infrastruktur – projektet att förbli starkt och motståndskraftigt "
"mot hot."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "**Client-side attackers:**"
msgstr "**Angripare på klientsidan:**"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "**Local attackers:**"
msgstr "**Lokala angripare:**"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "**Network attackers:**"
msgstr "**Nätverksangripare:**"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "**Project attackers:**"
msgstr "**Projektangripare:**"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "1. Revealing User Identities"
msgstr "1. Avslöja användarnas identiteter"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "2. Exploiting Tor Users"
msgstr "2. Utnyttja Tor-användare"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "3. Disrupting the Network"
msgstr "3. Störa nätverket"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "4. Weakening the Tor Project"
msgstr "4. Försvaga The Tor Project"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"An attacker is any individual, group, or organization that aims to "
"compromise the security, anonymity, or integrity of the Tor network or the "
"Tor Project itself."
msgstr ""
"En angripare är en person, grupp eller organisation som försöker äventyra "
"säkerheten, anonymiteten eller integriteten hos Tor-nätverket eller The Tor "
"Project."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Another goal may be to disrupt the Tor network, making it unreliable or "
"slowing it down."
msgstr ""
"Ett annat mål kan vara att störa Tor-nätverket så att det blir opålitligt "
"eller långsamt."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Attackers may also target the Tor project directly, attempting to undermine "
"its development, credibility, or organizational structure."
msgstr ""
"Angripare kan även rikta sig direkt mot The Tor Project och försöka "
"undergräva dess utveckling, trovärdighet eller organisationsstruktur."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Attackers may seek to exploit Tor users by stealing assets like "
"cryptocurrencies (e.g., Bitcoin) or siphoning off private and confidential "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Angripare kan försöka utnyttja Tor-användare genom att stjäla tillgångar som "
"kryptovalutor, till exempel bitcoin, eller komma över privat och "
"konfidentiell information."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Attackers might flood the network with traffic to that slow down the network "
"or reduce the overall reliability of Tor services, making it less effective "
"and accessible for users."
msgstr ""
"Angripare kan översvämma nätverket med trafik för att göra det långsammare "
"eller minska Tor-tjänsternas övergripande tillförlitlighet, så att de blir "
"mindre effektiva och tillgängliga för användarna."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"By identifying these attackers, we can better develop strategies to protect "
"the network and its users."
msgstr ""
"Genom att identifiera angriparna kan vi utveckla bättre strategier för att "
"skydda nätverket och dess användare."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"By watching and intercepting traffic, these attackers can aim to profit "
"financially or gather sensitive data that can be used for malicious purposes."
msgstr ""
"Genom att övervaka och fånga upp trafik kan angriparna försöka tjäna pengar "
"eller samla in känsliga uppgifter för illasinnade ändamål."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"By weakening the project, attackers aim to diminish the effectiveness of Tor "
"as a tool for privacy and freedom online."
msgstr ""
"Genom att försvaga projektet försöker angripare minska Tors effektivitet som "
"ett verktyg för integritet och frihet på nätet."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "Goals of attackers"
msgstr "Angriparnas mål"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"However, various entities, with different motivations and capabilities, pose "
"threats to this system."
msgstr ""
"Olika aktörer med skilda motiv och förmågor utgör dock hot mot systemet."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"If attackers succeed in deanonymizing users, they can strip away this "
"protection, expose sensitive activities, compromise privacy, and potentially "
"link users to their real-world identities."
msgstr ""
"Om angripare lyckas avanonymisera användare kan de beröva dem skyddet, "
"avslöja känsliga aktiviteter, äventyra integriteten och eventuellt koppla "
"användarna till deras verkliga identiteter."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Local attackers, like ISPs or compromised Wi-Fi networks, can monitor and "
"manipulate a user’s traffic, or disrupt their connection to the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Lokala angripare, till exempel internetleverantörer eller komprometterade Wi-"
"Fi-nätverk, kan övervaka och manipulera en användares trafik eller störa "
"anslutningen till Tor-nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"One of the main goals of attackers may be to uncover the identities of Tor "
"users."
msgstr ""
"Ett av angriparnas främsta mål kan vara att avslöja Tor-användarnas "
"identiteter."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Operating within the Tor Network, they can influence the network by "
"injecting or manipulating traffic through the relays they run, potentially "
"compromising the anonymity of users."
msgstr ""
"Genom att verka inuti Tor-nätverket kan de påverka det genom att mata in "
"eller manipulera trafik via reläer som de driver och därmed eventuellt "
"äventyra användarnas anonymitet."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Our threat model identifies these entities and provides a foundational "
"understanding of the possible threats faced by the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Vår hotmodell identifierar dessa aktörer och ger en grundläggande förståelse "
"för de möjliga hot som Tor-nätverket utsätts för."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Project attackers focus on The Tor Project itself, trying to introduce "
"vulnerabilities or disrupt operations by targeting Tor software, "
"infrastructure, or key personnel."
msgstr ""
"Projektangripare fokuserar på själva The Tor Project och försöker införa "
"sårbarheter eller störa verksamheten genom att angripa Tor-programvara, "
"infrastruktur eller nyckelpersoner."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "Some of these goals include:"
msgstr "Några av målen är:"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"The Tor network is designed to provide anonymity and privacy for its users."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverket är utformat för att ge användarna anonymitet och integritet."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "The attackers we are primarily focused on include:"
msgstr "De angripare som vi främst fokuserar på är:"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"These attackers may have various motivations, ranging from surveillance and "
"data theft to disrupting the network’s functionality."
msgstr ""
"Angriparna kan ha olika motiv, från övervakning och datastöld till att störa "
"nätverkets funktion."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"This could include introducing vulnerabilities into the software, "
"discrediting the project, or creating conflicts within the community."
msgstr ""
"Det kan innebära att införa sårbarheter i programvaran, misskreditera "
"projektet eller skapa konflikter inom gemenskapen."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"This prevents users from securely accessing the internet, and persistent "
"disruptions can undermine trust in Tor and their privacy protection."
msgstr ""
"Det hindrar användarna från att säkert komma åt internet, och ihållande "
"störningar kan undergräva förtroendet för Tor och dess integritetsskydd."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "Tor’s strength lies in providing privacy to its users."
msgstr "Tors styrka ligger i att skydda användarnas integritet."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Understanding what attackers aim to achieve can help users and developers "
"better defend against these threats."
msgstr ""
"Genom att förstå vad angriparna försöker uppnå kan användare och utvecklare "
"bättre försvara sig mot hoten."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid ""
"Using a Tor client, these attackers might aim to degrade the network's "
"performance by jamming it with traffic."
msgstr ""
"Genom att använda en Tor-klient kan angriparna försöka försämra nätverkets "
"prestanda genom att överbelasta det med trafik."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/
msgid "Who is an attacker?"
msgstr "Vem är en angripare?"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"![An image showing a sample of how DDoS is carried out](/static/images/"
"threat-model/client-side.png \"title='DDoS attack on Tor' class='img-"
"fluid'\")"
msgstr ""
"![En bild som visar ett exempel på hur DDoS utförs](/static/images/threat-"
"model/client-side.png \"title='DDoS-angrepp mot Tor' class='img-fluid'\")"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"![An image showing positions of bad relays on the Tor network](/static/"
"images/threat-model/network.png \"title='Bad Relays on the Tor Network' "
"class='img-fluid'\")"
msgstr ""
"![En bild som visar dåliga reläers positioner i Tor-nätverket](/static/"
"images/threat-model/network.png \"title='Dåliga reläer i Tor-nätverket' "
"class='img-fluid'\")"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "1. Traffic Analysis: Watching how data moves"
msgstr "1. Trafikanalys: Övervaka hur data förflyttas"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "2. Malicious Relays: Bad friends in the chain"
msgstr "2. Illasinnade reläer: Dåliga vänner i kedjan"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "3. Deanonymization: Revealing your identity"
msgstr "3. Avanonymisering: Avslöja din identitet"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "4. DDoS Attacks: Overloading the network"
msgstr "4. DDoS-angrepp: Överbelasta nätverket"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "5. Working with ISPs: Spying through your internet provider"
msgstr ""
"5. Samarbete med internetleverantörer: Spionera genom din internetleverantör"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"A Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attack is when an attacker sends so "
"much traffic to a website or network that it gets overwhelmed and stops "
"working."
msgstr ""
"Ett distribuerat överbelastningsangrepp (DDoS) innebär att en angripare "
"skickar så mycket trafik till en webbplats eller ett nätverk att det "
"överbelastas och slutar fungera."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"A [**malicious relay**](../../../relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/) is "
"like a friend in the chain who secretly opens the letter and reads it or "
"even changes it before passing it on."
msgstr ""
"Ett [**illasinnat relä**](../../../relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/) är "
"som en vän i kedjan som i hemlighet öppnar brevet och läser eller till och "
"med ändrar det innan det skickas vidare."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"As Tor offers protection, it also faces numerous threats from attackers who "
"aim to undermine its security."
msgstr ""
"Samtidigt som Tor ger skydd utsätts det för många hot från angripare som "
"försöker undergräva säkerheten."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "Attackers can use different tricks to do this."
msgstr "Angripare kan använda olika knep för att göra detta."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Attackers might do something similar by observing patterns in your online "
"activity by running [bad relays](../../../relay/governance/handling-bad-"
"relays/) and deploying DDoS attacks to get more traffic routed over their "
"own relays."
msgstr ""
"Angripare kan göra något liknande genom att observera mönster i din "
"nätaktivitet, driva [dåliga reläer](../../../relay/governance/handling-bad-"
"relays/) och genomföra DDoS-angrepp för att dirigera mer trafik via sina "
"egna reläer."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "Attackers use a similar method called **traffic analysis**."
msgstr "Angripare använder en liknande metod som kallas **trafikanalys**."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"But what if one of these relays is operated by someone with bad intentions?"
msgstr ""
"Men vad händer om ett av reläerna drivs av någon med illasinnade avsikter?"

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"By comparing these patterns, they can guess which Tor user is connected to "
"which website or service, even if the data itself is encrypted."
msgstr ""
"Genom att jämföra mönstren kan de gissa vilken Tor-användare som är ansluten "
"till en viss webbplats eller tjänst, även om själva informationen är "
"krypterad."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"By understanding how Tor works and the risks involved, you can make informed "
"choices to protect your privacy."
msgstr ""
"Genom att förstå hur Tor fungerar och vilka risker som finns kan du fatta "
"välgrundade beslut för att skydda din integritet."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Deanonymization is when someone figures out who you really are, even though "
"you’re trying to stay anonymous."
msgstr ""
"Avanonymisering innebär att någon tar reda på vem du verkligen är trots att "
"du försöker vara anonym."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Each friend passes the letter to the next, and the final friend delivers it "
"to the recipient."
msgstr ""
"Varje vän skickar brevet vidare till nästa, och den sista vännen levererar "
"det till mottagaren."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Even though the letter is sealed, someone watching can guess who you’re "
"writing to by seeing who you gave the letter to and who received it at the "
"other end."
msgstr ""
"Trots att brevet är förseglat kan någon som övervakar förloppet gissa vem du "
"skriver till genom att se vem du gav brevet till och vem som tog emot det i "
"andra änden."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"For instance, an attacker might keep watch of your internet connection "
"(perhaps through your Internet Service Provider)."
msgstr ""
"En angripare kan till exempel övervaka din internetanslutning, kanske genom "
"din internetleverantör."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"If an attacker doesn’t want people to use Tor, they might send a huge amount "
"of traffic to Tor’s relays, making it hard or impossible for real users to "
"connect."
msgstr ""
"Om en angripare inte vill att människor ska använda Tor kan den skicka "
"enorma mängder trafik till Tor-reläerna och göra det svårt eller omöjligt "
"för riktiga användare att ansluta."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"If an attacker runs an exit relay (the last relay before your data leaves "
"the Tor network), they could try to spy on your data if it’s not properly "
"encrypted."
msgstr ""
"Om en angripare driver ett utgångsrelä, det sista reläet innan data lämnar "
"Tor-nätverket, kan den försöka spionera på informationen om den inte är "
"korrekt krypterad."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"If an attacker sees data going into the Tor network from your computer and "
"sees similar data coming out on the other side, they might guess that the "
"data is connected, even though it’s encrypted."
msgstr ""
"Om en angripare ser data gå in i Tor-nätverket från din dator och liknande "
"data komma ut på andra sidan kan den gissa att informationen hör ihop, trots "
"att den är krypterad."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Imagine someone knocks on your door, and as soon as you open it, they "
"quickly take a picture of you."
msgstr ""
"Föreställ dig att någon knackar på dörren och snabbt tar ett foto av dig så "
"fort du öppnar."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Imagine your mail carrier (ISP) could choose specific sorting facilities "
"they control, not to open your letters, but to monitor where they go and "
"when."
msgstr ""
"Föreställ dig att brevbäraren, alltså internetleverantören, kan välja "
"särskilda sorteringscentraler som den styr över – inte för att öppna breven, "
"utan för att övervaka vart och när de skickas."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "Imagine you’re sending a secret letter through a series of friends."
msgstr ""
"Föreställ dig att du skickar ett hemligt brev genom en kedja av vänner."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"In some cases, attackers might work with ISPs to monitor or control what you "
"do online."
msgstr ""
"I vissa fall kan angripare samarbeta med internetleverantörer för att "
"övervaka eller styra vad du gör på nätet."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"In some countries, ISPs might be forced to monitor or block Tor traffic, "
"making it harder for you to use the network."
msgstr ""
"I vissa länder kan internetleverantörer tvingas övervaka eller blockera Tor-"
"trafik, vilket gör det svårare att använda nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Internet Service Providers (ISPs) are the companies that connect you to the "
"internet."
msgstr "Internetleverantörer är företagen som ansluter dig till internet."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"It’s like flooding a store with so many customers that no one can get "
"through the door."
msgstr ""
"Det är som att fylla en butik med så många kunder att ingen kan komma in "
"genom dörren."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "People who want to break Tor's protections use many different methods."
msgstr "Personer som vill bryta Tors skydd använder många olika metoder."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Similarly, local adversaries can manipulate your Tor traffic to ensure it "
"passes through their controlled Guards or Bridges (the first connection "
"points in the Tor network)."
msgstr ""
"På liknande sätt kan lokala motståndare manipulera Tor-trafiken så att den "
"passerar deras egna vakter eller broar, alltså de första "
"anslutningspunkterna i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Some relays receive data, some pass it along, and others send it out of the "
"network."
msgstr ""
"Vissa reläer tar emot data, andra skickar dem vidare och ytterligare andra "
"skickar dem ut ur nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"The Tor network relies on volunteers to run [relays](../../../relay/) (like "
"the friends in our secret letter example)."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverket är beroende av volontärer som driver [reläer](../../../"
"relay/), ungefär som vännerna i exemplet med det hemliga brevet."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"These attackers can attempt to breach Tor users' privacy through a range of "
"tactics, ranging from complex technical trickery to simple lies."
msgstr ""
"Angriparna kan försöka kränka Tor-användarnas integritet med många olika "
"metoder, från avancerade tekniska knep till enkla lögner."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"They didn’t need to follow you around all day to figure out where you live—"
"they just needed to catch you at the right moment."
msgstr ""
"De behövde inte följa efter dig hela dagen för att ta reda på var du bor – "
"de behövde bara fånga dig vid rätt tillfälle."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"They don’t need to read your messages—they can try to figure out who’s "
"talking to whom just by watching how data moves through the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"De behöver inte läsa meddelandena, utan kan försöka avgöra vem som "
"kommunicerar med vem genom att observera hur data rör sig genom Tor-"
"nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Through this, they can notice that you send a specific amount of data into "
"the Tor network at a certain time, or the data exiting the Tor network with "
"similar timing and size."
msgstr ""
"De kan då se att du skickar en viss mängd data till Tor-nätverket vid en "
"viss tidpunkt och att data med liknande tidpunkt och storlek lämnar "
"nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"To prevent this from happening, always use HTTPS websites, which encrypt "
"your traffic end-to-end, and avoid transmitting sensitive information over "
"unencrypted connections while using Tor."
msgstr ""
"Använd alltid webbplatser med HTTPS, som krypterar trafiken från ände till "
"ände, och skicka inte känslig information över okrypterade anslutningar när "
"du använder Tor."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "To stay safe online, it's essential to be aware of these threats."
msgstr "För att vara säker på nätet är det viktigt att känna till hoten."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Tor offers a powerful tool for online privacy, but it's important to "
"understand that it's not invincible."
msgstr ""
"Tor är ett kraftfullt verktyg för integritet på nätet, men det är viktigt "
"att förstå att det inte är osårbart."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"Whether you're a regular Tor user or just interested in online privacy, "
"understanding these concerns is critical to your online safety."
msgstr ""
"Oavsett om du använder Tor regelbundet eller bara är intresserad av "
"integritet på nätet är det avgörande för säkerheten att förstå dessa problem."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid ""
"While they can't read your traffic, this increases their chances of tracking "
"your activity and potentially identifying you through traffic patterns."
msgstr ""
"Även om de inte kan läsa trafiken ökar det deras möjlighet att spåra din "
"aktivitet och eventuellt identifiera dig genom trafikmönster."

#: content/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/network-attackers/how-attackers-work/
msgid "How Attackers Work"
msgstr "Så arbetar angripare"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"![An image showing positions of client-side threats on the Tor network](/"
"static/images/threat-model/client-side.png \"title='Client Threats' "
"class='img-fluid'\")"
msgstr ""
"![En bild som visar positioner för hot på klientsidan i Tor-nätverket](/"
"static/images/threat-model/client-side.png \"title='Klienthot' class='img-"
"fluid'\")"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"A Denial of Service (DoS) attack is a tactic where an attacker attempts to "
"make a service, in this case, the Tor network, hard to use for its intended "
"users."
msgstr ""
"Ett överbelastningsangrepp (DoS) är en metod där en angripare försöker göra "
"en tjänst, i det här fallet Tor-nätverket, svår att använda för de avsedda "
"användarna."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid "A Tor client is software that lets you use the Tor network."
msgstr "En Tor-klient är programvara som låter dig använda Tor-nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"Client-side attackers are individuals or entities that use a Tor client to "
"carry out attacks on the network."
msgstr ""
"Angripare på klientsidan är personer eller aktörer som använder en Tor-"
"klient för att angripa nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"Client-side attackers can execute DoS attacks to degrade the performance of "
"the Tor network, causing disruptions that impact all users."
msgstr ""
"Angripare på klientsidan kan genomföra DoS-angrepp som försämrar Tor-"
"nätverkets prestanda och orsakar störningar för alla användare."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid "Denial of Service (DoS) attacks"
msgstr "Överbelastningsangrepp (DoS)"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"However, the network faces various threats, even from people who just use a "
"Tor client."
msgstr ""
"Nätverket utsätts dock för olika hot, även från personer som bara använder "
"en Tor-klient."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"Instead, they rely on their access to the internet and a Tor client to "
"execute their attacks."
msgstr ""
"De förlitar sig i stället på internetåtkomst och en Tor-klient för att "
"genomföra angreppen."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"One of the primary threats posed by client-side attackers is the ability to "
"perform a Denial of Service (DoS) attack."
msgstr ""
"Ett av de främsta hoten från angripare på klientsidan är möjligheten att "
"genomföra ett överbelastningsangrepp (DoS)."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"The Tor network is designed to protect users' privacy by routing their "
"internet traffic through a series of relays, making it difficult to trace "
"their online activities."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverket är utformat för att skydda användarnas integritet genom att "
"dirigera internettrafiken genom en serie reläer, vilket gör nätaktiviteten "
"svår att spåra."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"The most common Tor client is the Tor Browser, which is similar to a regular "
"web browser but with built-in privacy protections."
msgstr ""
"Den vanligaste Tor-klienten är Tor Browser, som liknar en vanlig webbläsare "
"men har inbyggt integritetsskydd."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"The result is a significantly slowed network, making it difficult for "
"legitimate users to connect or use Tor effectively."
msgstr ""
"Resultatet är ett betydligt långsammare nätverk som gör det svårt för "
"legitima användare att ansluta eller använda Tor effektivt."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"These client-side attackers, while limited in their capabilities compared to "
"more sophisticated attackers, can still pose significant risks to the "
"network's performance and reliability."
msgstr ""
"Även om angripare på klientsidan har mer begränsade förmågor än mer "
"avancerade angripare kan de ändå utgöra betydande risker för nätverkets "
"prestanda och tillförlitlighet."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"They could flood the network with an overwhelming amount of traffic using "
"external services, or exploiting the Tor protocol itself."
msgstr ""
"De kan översvämma nätverket med en överväldigande trafikmängd genom externa "
"tjänster eller genom att utnyttja själva Tor-protokollet."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"This disruption can also frustrate relay operators, sometimes leading them "
"to shut down their relays, which inadvertently weakens the network—a "
"potential goal of the attacker."
msgstr ""
"Störningen kan också frustrera reläoperatörer och ibland få dem att stänga "
"av sina reläer, vilket oavsiktligt försvagar nätverket och kan vara ett av "
"angriparens mål."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"This traffic might not necessarily come from a single client but could be "
"distributed across many clients in a coordinated attack."
msgstr ""
"Trafiken behöver inte komma från en enda klient, utan kan fördelas över "
"många klienter i ett samordnat angrepp."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid "Understanding Client-side Adversaries"
msgstr "Förstå motståndare på klientsidan"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid ""
"Unlike more advanced attackers, they do not control any relays or "
"infrastructure within the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Till skillnad från mer avancerade angripare styr de inga reläer eller någon "
"infrastruktur i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/client-side/
msgid "Client-side Attackers on the Tor Network"
msgstr "Angripare på klientsidan i Tor-nätverket"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/
msgid ""
"![An image showing positions of bad actors on the Tor network](/static/"
"images/threat-model/threat-position.png \"title='Threats to Tor' class='img-"
"fluid'\")"
msgstr ""
"![En bild som visar illasinnade aktörers positioner i Tor-nätverket](/static/"
"images/threat-model/threat-position.png \"title='Hot mot Tor' class='img-"
"fluid'\")"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/
msgid "Attackers can just use a Tor client or be an ISP/WiFi operator."
msgstr ""
"Angripare kan helt enkelt använda en Tor-klient eller vara "
"internetleverantörer eller Wi-Fi-operatörer."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/
msgid ""
"By understanding these tactics, we can better protect the Tor network and "
"its users from potential attacks."
msgstr ""
"Genom att förstå metoderna kan vi bättre skydda Tor-nätverket och dess "
"användare mot möjliga angrepp."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/
msgid ""
"The Tor network helps maintain online privacy and anonymity, but it is not "
"immune to attacks."
msgstr ""
"Tor-nätverket bidrar till integritet och anonymitet på nätet, men är inte "
"immunt mot angrepp."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/
msgid ""
"They might also be part of the Network, or our community and engage in "
"mailing list discussions, proposal work etc."
msgstr ""
"De kan också vara en del av nätverket eller gemenskapen och delta i "
"diskussioner på e-postlistor, förslagsarbete och liknande."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/
msgid ""
"This section explores the different ways attackers might position themselves "
"on or around the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Det här avsnittet undersöker de olika sätt som angripare kan positionera sig "
"i eller omkring Tor-nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/
msgid ""
"Understanding how attackers can position themselves as local clients or "
"within the Tor network is crucial to safeguarding its users and ensuring the "
"network remains secure."
msgstr ""
"Att förstå hur angripare kan positionera sig som lokala klienter eller inuti "
"Tor-nätverket är avgörande för att skydda användarna och hålla nätverket "
"säkert."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/
msgid ""
"We will examine the strategies they use, the risks they pose, and how these "
"threats can be mitigated."
msgstr ""
"Vi granskar deras strategier, riskerna de medför och hur hoten kan motverkas."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/
msgid "Threat Positioning on the Tor Network"
msgstr "Hotpositioner i Tor-nätverket"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"![An image showing positions of local threats on the Tor network](/static/"
"images/threat-model/local.png \"title='Local Threats' class='img-fluid'\")"
msgstr ""
"![En bild som visar lokala hots positioner i Tor-nätverket](/static/images/"
"threat-model/local.png \"title='Lokala hot' class='img-fluid'\")"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"**Covert Channel Exploits:** If a local adversary additionally operates an "
"exit relay (the final node in the Tor circuit before traffic exits to the "
"internet), they could exploit certain vulnerabilities, such as dropped "
"cells, to leak your information or deanonymize you secretly."
msgstr ""
"**Utnyttjande av dolda kanaler:** Om en lokal motståndare dessutom driver "
"ett utgångsrelä, den sista noden i Tor-kretsen innan trafiken lämnar "
"nätverket, kan den utnyttja vissa sårbarheter, till exempel borttappade "
"celler, för att i hemlighet läcka information eller avanonymisera dig."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"**NetFlow Analysis:** An ISP or hosting provider could perform [NetFlow "
"analysis](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/team/-/issues/"
"42), a technique that monitors traffic flows in a network."
msgstr ""
"**NetFlow-analys:** En internet- eller värdleverantör kan utföra [NetFlow-"
"analys](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/network-health/team/-/issues/42), "
"en metod som övervakar trafikflöden i ett nätverk."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid "1. **Controlling Traffic Routes:**"
msgstr "1. **Styra trafikvägar:**"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid "2. **Exploiting Information Leaks:**"
msgstr "2. **Utnyttja informationsläckor:**"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"A dropped cell refers to a piece of data (called a cell) that is "
"intentionally discarded or ignored by a node in the network, and when a cell "
"is dropped, it means the data doesn't move forward in the network."
msgstr ""
"En borttappad cell är en datadel, kallad cell, som avsiktligt kastas eller "
"ignoreras av en nod i nätverket. När en cell tappas skickas informationen "
"inte vidare i nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"Although, the ISPs or hosting providers that manage the Tor relays you use "
"to connect to the Tor network, as well as any other ISPs and routers along "
"your path to the network, are also considered local adversaries."
msgstr ""
"Internet- eller värdleverantörerna som hanterar Tor-reläerna du använder för "
"att ansluta till Tor-nätverket, liksom andra internetleverantörer och "
"routrar längs vägen till nätverket, betraktas också som lokala motståndare."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"By analyzing these flows, they might identify patterns that confirm whether "
"specific traffic belongs to a particular user, thus aiding in "
"deanonymization attempts."
msgstr ""
"Genom att analysera flödena kan de hitta mönster som bekräftar om viss "
"trafik tillhör en viss användare och därmed underlätta "
"avanonymiseringsförsök."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"By doing this, they increase their chances of monitoring your traffic and "
"potentially deanonymizing you. This manipulation can be subtle and difficult "
"for users to detect, making it a potent threat."
msgstr ""
"På så sätt ökar de möjligheten att övervaka trafiken och eventuellt "
"avanonymisera dig. Manipuleringen kan vara subtil och svår för användaren "
"att upptäcka, vilket gör den till ett allvarligt hot."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid "Examples of Local Adversary Attacks"
msgstr "Exempel på angrepp från lokala motståndare"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"For example, these leaks might reveal patterns in your traffic that could "
"make it easier for an attacker to deanonymize you or link your activities "
"back to you."
msgstr ""
"Läckorna kan till exempel avslöja trafikmönster som gör det lättare för en "
"angripare att avanonymisera dig eller koppla aktiviteterna till dig."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid "How Local Adversaries attack the network"
msgstr "Så angriper lokala motståndare nätverket"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"Local adversaries are in a unique position to take advantage of these leaks "
"because they can closely monitor your connection to the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Lokala motståndare har särskilt goda möjligheter att utnyttja läckorna "
"eftersom de kan övervaka anslutningen till Tor-nätverket på nära håll."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"Local adversaries can manipulate the routing of your Tor traffic to ensure "
"it only passes through Guards or Bridges (the first point of connection in "
"the Tor network) that they control."
msgstr ""
"Lokala motståndare kan manipulera dirigeringen av Tor-trafiken så att den "
"endast passerar vakter eller broar som de styr över, alltså de första "
"anslutningspunkterna i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"Local adversaries may not have the broad capabilities of those who control "
"or monitor different relays in the network, but they are still dangerous "
"because they can focus on the specific connections that pass through their "
"systems."
msgstr ""
"Lokala motståndare har kanske inte samma omfattande förmåga som aktörer som "
"styr eller övervakar olika reläer i nätverket, men är ändå farliga eftersom "
"de kan fokusera på de särskilda anslutningar som passerar genom deras system."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid "Some of the key ways they can attack the Tor users include:"
msgstr "Några av de viktigaste sätten de kan angripa Tor-användare är:"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"Their proximity to your connection path gives them unique opportunities to "
"gather information or manipulate your traffic in ways that more distant "
"adversaries cannot."
msgstr ""
"Närheten till din anslutningsväg ger dem unika möjligheter att samla in "
"information eller manipulera trafiken på sätt som mer avlägsna motståndare "
"inte kan."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"These attackers include entities like your WiFi router administrator, "
"Internet Service Provider (ISP), hosting provider, or Virtual Private "
"Network (VPN) service."
msgstr ""
"Angriparna kan till exempel vara administratören för Wi-Fi-routern, "
"internetleverantören, värdleverantören eller VPN-tjänsten."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid "These local adversaries can execute a variety of attacks, including:"
msgstr "De lokala motståndarna kan utföra flera slags angrepp, bland annat:"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"This method, known as a dropped cells covert channel vector, could allow the "
"attacker to deanonymize you, or gather information about your activities on "
"the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Metoden, som kallas en dold kanal med borttappade celler, kan låta "
"angriparen avanonymisera dig eller samla in information om dina aktiviteter "
"i Tor-nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid ""
"Your Tor usage can leak data that local adversaries might want to exploit."
msgstr ""
"Din användning av Tor kan läcka data som lokala motståndare vill utnyttja."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/local/
msgid "Local Attackers on the Tor Network"
msgstr "Lokala angripare i Tor-nätverket"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid "1. Running Malicious Relays"
msgstr "1. Driva illasinnade reläer"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid "2. Exploiting Information Leaks"
msgstr "2. Utnyttja informationsläckor"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid "3. Denial of Service (DoS) Attacks"
msgstr "3. Överbelastningsangrepp (DoS)"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"A DoS attack can also frustrate volunteers running relays, potentially "
"leading them to shut down their relays, which weakens the network and makes "
"it more vulnerable to further attacks."
msgstr ""
"Ett DoS-angrepp kan även frustrera volontärer som driver reläer och få dem "
"att stänga av reläerna, vilket försvagar nätverket och gör det mer sårbart "
"för ytterligare angrepp."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"A deeper understanding of these threats and continuous vigilance are "
"essential to maintaining the security and usability of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"En djupare förståelse för hoten och ständig vaksamhet är avgörande för att "
"upprätthålla Tor-nätverkets säkerhet och användbarhet."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"A network adversary running relays can take advantage of these leaks to:"
msgstr ""
"En nätverksmotståndare som driver reläer kan utnyttja läckorna för att:"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"An attacker could operate a malicious exit relay—the final node where "
"traffic exits the Tor network and reaches the open internet— intentionally "
"designed to steal sensitive data like cryptocurrencies, hijack online "
"accounts, log user activity, or exploit vulnerabilities in Tor's protocol."
msgstr ""
"En angripare kan driva ett illasinnat utgångsrelä – den sista noden där "
"trafik lämnar Tor-nätverket och når det öppna internet – som avsiktligt "
"utformats för att stjäla känsliga data som kryptovalutor, kapa nätkonton, "
"logga användaraktivitet eller utnyttja sårbarheter i Tor-protokollet."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"As the Tor project relies on volunteers for relays and external funding, "
"frequent attacks could discourage operators and impact funding, both "
"critical for keeping the network operational."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom The Tor Project är beroende av volontärer för reläerna och av "
"extern finansiering kan återkommande angrepp avskräcka operatörer och "
"påverka finansieringen, som båda är avgörande för att hålla nätverket igång."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Assist other deanonymization attempts by providing additional data that "
"makes it easier to confirm which traffic belongs to a specific user."
msgstr ""
"Hjälpa andra avanonymiseringsförsök genom att tillhandahålla ytterligare "
"data som gör det lättare att bekräfta vilken trafik som tillhör en viss "
"användare."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid "Collect data that can be used to deanonymize users."
msgstr "Samla in data som kan användas för att avanonymisera användare."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Deanonymize users directly by correlating traffic patterns between the entry "
"and exit points of the Tor network."
msgstr ""
"Avanonymisera användare direkt genom att korrelera trafikmönster mellan Tor-"
"nätverkets ingångs- och utgångspunkter."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid "Disrupt communication between Tor users and the network."
msgstr "Störa kommunikationen mellan Tor-användare och nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Exploit vulnerabilities in the Tor protocol to generate large amounts of "
"traffic, overwhelming the network."
msgstr ""
"Utnyttja sårbarheter i Tor-protokollet för att skapa stora trafikmängder som "
"överbelastar nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid "How Network Adversaries attack Tor"
msgstr "Så angriper nätverksmotståndare Tor"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"If users perceive the network as unsafe or slow, they may stop using it, "
"reducing the overall anonymity of the network (since more users make it "
"harder to track individual traffic)."
msgstr ""
"Om användare uppfattar nätverket som osäkert eller långsamt kan de sluta "
"använda det, vilket minskar nätverkets övergripande anonymitet eftersom fler "
"användare gör enskild trafik svårare att spåra."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Malicious relays may also be purposefully misconfigured to introduce "
"vulnerabilities into the network."
msgstr ""
"Illasinnade reläer kan också avsiktligt felkonfigureras för att införa "
"sårbarheter i nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Network adversaries can also use DoS attacks to degrade the performance of "
"the Tor network, making it slow or unreliable."
msgstr ""
"Nätverksmotståndare kan också använda DoS-angrepp för att försämra Tor-"
"nätverkets prestanda och göra det långsamt eller opålitligt."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Network adversaries can carry out a variety of attacks, which can generally "
"fall into three broad categories: running malicious relays that risks user "
"safety and security, manipulating Tor’s protocol to leak information, and "
"performing denial of service (DoS) attacks."
msgstr ""
"Nätverksmotståndare kan genomföra många slags angrepp som i stora drag "
"faller i tre kategorier: driva illasinnade reläer som utsätter användarnas "
"säkerhet för risk, manipulera Tor-protokollet för att läcka information och "
"utföra överbelastningsangrepp (DoS)."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Network attackers often run relays that are configured to harm the network "
"or users in some way."
msgstr ""
"Nätverksangripare driver ofta reläer som är konfigurerade för att på något "
"sätt skada nätverket eller användarna."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Network attackers pose a significant threat to the security and reliability "
"of the network."
msgstr ""
"Nätverksangripare utgör ett betydande hot mot nätverkets säkerhet och "
"tillförlitlighet."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid "Spy on traffic passing through them."
msgstr "Spionera på trafik som passerar genom dem."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"The goal of a DoS attack is often to discourage users from using Tor by "
"making it so slow or unusable that they switch to less secure alternatives."
msgstr ""
"Målet med ett DoS-angrepp är ofta att avskräcka användare från Tor genom att "
"göra nätverket så långsamt eller oanvändbart att de övergår till mindre "
"säkra alternativ."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"The presence of malicious or misconfigured relays, along with the potential "
"for DoS attacks, can severely undermine Tor’s security, reliability, and "
"reputation."
msgstr ""
"Illasinnade eller felkonfigurerade reläer och möjliga DoS-angrepp kan "
"allvarligt undergräva Tors säkerhet, tillförlitlighet och anseende."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Their goal may be to deanonymize users, degrade network performance, or "
"damage Tor’s reputation."
msgstr ""
"Deras mål kan vara att avanonymisera användare, försämra nätverkets "
"prestanda eller skada Tors anseende."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"These attackers are those who run or compromise relays within the network, "
"or manipulate traffic to exploit weaknesses in the Tor protocol."
msgstr ""
"Det är angripare som driver eller komprometterar reläer i nätverket eller "
"manipulerar trafik för att utnyttja svagheter i Tor-protokollet."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid "These attacks might:"
msgstr "Angreppen kan:"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"These information leaks are detailed in [*Proposal 344*](https://"
"spec.torproject.org/proposals/344-protocol-info-leaks.html), which "
"highlights the severity of each one."
msgstr ""
"Informationsläckorna beskrivs i detalj i [*förslag 344*](https://"
"spec.torproject.org/proposals/344-protocol-info-leaks.html), som framhäver "
"hur allvarlig varje läcka är."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"These relays might not follow proper protocol, resulting in traffic that "
"leaks information, making it easier to track users."
msgstr ""
"Reläerna kanske inte följer protokollet korrekt, vilket kan leda till trafik "
"som läcker information och gör användarna lättare att spåra."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"This allows the attacker to intercept and manipulate traffic, posing "
"significant risks to users relying on Tor for secure, anonymous browsing."
msgstr ""
"Det gör att angriparen kan fånga upp och manipulera trafik och medför "
"betydande risker för användare som förlitar sig på Tor för säker och anonym "
"surfning."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Tor actively works to detect and remove these relays, but attackers often "
"attempt to bypass detection by concealing the true nature of their relays, "
"such as lying about key relay properties or frustrating Tor’s scanning "
"efforts."
msgstr ""
"Tor arbetar aktivt med att upptäcka och ta bort reläerna, men angripare "
"försöker ofta undgå upptäckt genom att dölja reläernas verkliga natur, till "
"exempel genom att ljuga om viktiga reläegenskaper eller försvåra Tors "
"skanningar."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Tor’s protocol, while designed to protect user anonymity, has known "
"information leaks or \"[side channels](https://spec.torproject.org/proposals/"
"344-protocol-info-leaks.html)\" that attackers can exploit."
msgstr ""
"Tor-protokollet är utformat för att skydda användarnas anonymitet men har "
"kända informationsläckor eller [sidokanaler](https://spec.torproject.org/"
"proposals/344-protocol-info-leaks.html) som angripare kan utnyttja."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"Use external services to flood the network with traffic, causing congestion."
msgstr ""
"Använda externa tjänster för att översvämma nätverket med trafik och orsaka "
"överbelastning."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"While Tor has systems in place to detect and remove these threats, attackers "
"are constantly evolving their tactics to avoid detection and weaken the "
"network."
msgstr ""
"Tor har system som upptäcker och tar bort hoten, men angriparna utvecklar "
"ständigt sina metoder för att undgå upptäckt och försvaga nätverket."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"While not all require running relays to exploit, network adversaries who "
"operate relays are in a better position to see more traffic and perform "
"traffic analysis, making their attacks more effective."
msgstr ""
"Alla läckor kräver inte att en angripare driver reläer, men "
"nätverksmotståndare med egna reläer har bättre möjligheter att se mer trafik "
"och utföra trafikanalys, vilket gör angreppen effektivare."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid ""
"[Malicious relays](../../../relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/) can be "
"designed to:"
msgstr ""
"[Illasinnade reläer](../../../relay/governance/handling-bad-relays/) kan "
"utformas för att:"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/network/
msgid "Network Attackers on the Tor Network"
msgstr "Nätverksangripare i Tor-nätverket"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"![An image showing positions of bad actors in the Tor community](/static/"
"images/threat-model/project.png \"title='Tor Community with bad actors' "
"class='img-fluid'\")"
msgstr ""
"![En bild som visar illasinnade aktörers positioner i Tor-gemenskapen](/"
"static/images/threat-model/project.png \"title='Tor-gemenskapen med "
"illasinnade aktörer' class='img-fluid'\")"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid "1. **Infiltrating communication channels**:"
msgstr "1. **Infiltrera kommunikationskanaler:**"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid "2. **Spreading fear, uncertainty, and doubt**:"
msgstr "2. **Sprida rädsla, osäkerhet och tvivel:**"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid "3. **Interfering with governance**:"
msgstr "3. **Störa styrningen:**"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid "4. **Targeting key staff**:"
msgstr "4. **Rikta sig mot nyckelpersoner:**"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid "5. **Attacking infrastructure related to bad-relay work:**"
msgstr "5. **Angripa infrastruktur som används i arbetet mot dåliga reläer:**"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"By attacking this infrastructure, they might aim to undermine the detection "
"systems and allow their malicious relays to operate undetected, ultimately "
"weakening the network's defenses."
msgstr ""
"Genom att angripa infrastrukturen kan de försöka undergräva "
"detekteringssystemen och låta sina illasinnade reläer verka oupptäckta, "
"vilket i slutändan försvagar nätverkets försvar."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid "How project adversaries can attack Tor"
msgstr "Så kan projektmotståndare angripa Tor"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"In any open-source project like Tor, it's essential to be aware of potential "
"adversaries who exploit the transparency and openness of our workflows and "
"communication channels."
msgstr ""
"I ett projekt med öppen källkod som Tor är det viktigt att vara medveten om "
"möjliga motståndare som utnyttjar transparensen och öppenheten i våra "
"arbetsflöden och kommunikationskanaler."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"Individuals working on attack detection or mitigation may face direct "
"intimidation, bribery attempts, or indirect attacks on the infrastructure "
"they rely on."
msgstr ""
"Personer som arbetar med att upptäcka eller motverka angrepp kan utsättas "
"för direkta hot, mutförsök eller indirekta angrepp på den infrastruktur som "
"de förlitar sig på."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"Project adversaries are individuals or groups who take advantage of our open "
"system to disrupt or manipulate the Tor network and its community."
msgstr ""
"Projektmotståndare är personer eller grupper som utnyttjar vårt öppna system "
"för att störa eller manipulera Tor-nätverket och dess gemenskap."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"The infrastructure supporting the detection and mitigation of malicious "
"relays is a key target for adversaries."
msgstr ""
"Infrastrukturen för att upptäcka och motverka illasinnade reläer är ett "
"viktigt mål för motståndare."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid "Their tactics may include:"
msgstr "Deras metoder kan omfatta:"

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"These adversaries may aim to weaken our network and disrupt our community by "
"infiltrating discussions, shaping decisions, or attacking the infrastructure "
"that supports our project."
msgstr ""
"Motståndarna kan försöka försvaga nätverket och störa gemenskapen genom att "
"infiltrera diskussioner, påverka beslut eller angripa infrastrukturen som "
"stöder projektet."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"These attackers may join mailing lists, forums, or other community spaces to "
"influence discussions, steer proposals, and create division."
msgstr ""
"Angriparna kan gå med i e-postlistor, forum eller andra gemenskapsutrymmen "
"för att påverka diskussioner, styra förslag och skapa splittring."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"They may also attempt to disrupt proposal processes, particularly those "
"related to community governance and the Tor development roadmap, to weaken "
"the project's direction."
msgstr ""
"De kan också försöka störa förslagsprocesser, särskilt sådana som gäller "
"gemenskapsstyrning och Tors utvecklingsplan, för att försvaga projektets "
"riktning."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid ""
"They may attempt to erode trust in Tor by sharing misleading or harmful "
"information on both internal and external platforms."
msgstr ""
"De kan försöka urholka förtroendet för Tor genom att sprida vilseledande "
"eller skadlig information på interna och externa plattformar."

#: content/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/threat-model/threat-positioning/project/
msgid "Threats to The Tor Project"
msgstr "Hot mot The Tor Project"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "**Agenda:**"
msgstr "**Dagordning:**"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "**Location:**"
msgstr "**Plats:**"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "**Material:**"
msgstr "**Material:**"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "**Promotion:**"
msgstr "**Marknadsföring:**"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "**Safety and security:**"
msgstr "**Trygghet och säkerhet:**"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "After the training"
msgstr "Efter utbildningen"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Ask participants whether they feel comfortable with their picture being "
"taken. You may purchase red and green lanyards for participants to wear"
msgstr ""
"Fråga deltagarna om de känner sig bekväma med att fotograferas. Du kan "
"skaffa röda och gröna nyckelband som deltagarna kan bära"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Before the training"
msgstr "Före utbildningen"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Best Practices"
msgstr "Bästa praxis"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Create a link list of all the resources you'll be talking about. This "
"includes downloads and PDFs of handouts."
msgstr ""
"Skapa en länklista över alla resurser som du ska tala om, inklusive "
"hämtningslänkar och PDF-filer med utdelningsmaterial."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Create an agenda for the training."
msgstr "Skapa en dagordning för utbildningen."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Decide how you will facilitate a safer space. We recommend using the [Tor "
"Code of Conduct](../code-of-conduct/)."
msgstr ""
"Bestäm hur du ska skapa ett tryggare utrymme. Vi rekommenderar att du "
"använder [Tors uppförandekod](../code-of-conduct/)."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Design and print localized handouts for some of the more difficult concepts "
"that you'll be teaching."
msgstr ""
"Utforma och skriv ut lokaliserat utdelningsmaterial om några av de svårare "
"begreppen som du ska undervisa om."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Determine how you'll do hands-on assistance at your training."
msgstr "Bestäm hur praktisk hjälp ska ges under utbildningen."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "During the training"
msgstr "Under utbildningen"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Establish an emergency protocol in case something goes wrong:"
msgstr "Fastställ ett nödprotokoll om något skulle gå fel:"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Find a location that is accessible and affordable."
msgstr "Hitta en plats som är tillgänglig och prisvärd."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Good preparation is essential to an effective and safe training, so we've "
"curated some resources to help you make the most of your training event."
msgstr ""
"God förberedelse är avgörande för en effektiv och säker utbildning. Därför "
"har vi sammanställt resurser som hjälper dig att få ut så mycket som möjligt "
"av utbildningstillfället."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Has enough chairs and tables for everyone."
msgstr "Har tillräckligt med stolar och bord för alla."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Have someone you trust on the outside on standby in case something happens."
msgstr "Ha någon du litar på utanför evenemanget i beredskap om något händer."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "How will you assess the needs of your group? What needs can you meet?"
msgstr "Hur ska du bedöma gruppens behov? Vilka behov kan du tillgodose?"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"How will you assess the skill level of your group? Which skill levels can "
"you teach?"
msgstr ""
"Hur ska du bedöma gruppens kunskapsnivå? Vilka nivåer kan du undervisa på?"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"If relevant, report your experience to the Tor Project Community and UX "
"teams."
msgstr ""
"Rapportera erfarenheterna till The Tor Projects gemenskaps- och UX-team om "
"det är relevant."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"If you need more help, make sure the partners you're bringing in are aware "
"of the safety needs of the community, and communicate with your contacts in "
"the community to make sure they're okay with you bringing in additional "
"trainers."
msgstr ""
"Om du behöver mer hjälp ska du se till att de samarbetspartner du tar in "
"känner till gemenskapens säkerhetsbehov. Stäm även av med dina kontakter i "
"gemenskapen att det är i sin ordning att ta in ytterligare utbildare."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Inform participants how much time the training will take, and when breaks "
"will happen. Make sure you take breaks!"
msgstr ""
"Berätta för deltagarna hur lång tid utbildningen tar och när pauserna hålls. "
"Se till att ta pauser!"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Inform participants how participants can contact you securely after the "
"training."
msgstr ""
"Berätta för deltagarna hur de kan kontakta dig på ett säkert sätt efter "
"utbildningen."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Inform participants when and how you'll offer hands-on help (if at all)."
msgstr ""
"Berätta för deltagarna när och hur du erbjuder praktisk hjälp, om sådan "
"erbjuds."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Inform participants when you'll take questions, either during the training, "
"at the end, or both. Make sure to tell participants that all questions are "
"welcome."
msgstr ""
"Berätta när deltagarna kan ställa frågor, under utbildningen, i slutet eller "
"både och. Var tydlig med att alla frågor är välkomna."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Introduce yourself and allow participants to introduce themselves. You may "
"consider doing an icebreaker."
msgstr ""
"Presentera dig och låt deltagarna presentera sig. Du kan överväga en "
"inledande lära-känna-övning."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Is safe for your attendees to visit."
msgstr "Är säker för deltagarna att besöka."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Make sure to send reminders to those who signed up to your workshop, sharing "
"venue address, date and time of workshop, and reminding them what equipment "
"they should bring."
msgstr ""
"Skicka påminnelser till dem som har anmält sig till workshopen med platsens "
"adress, datum och tid samt vilken utrustning de bör ta med."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Make sure you have plenty of stickers to hand out to participants!"
msgstr "Se till att ha gott om klistermärken att dela ut till deltagarna!"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Make sure your presentation is up-to-date (both information and screenshots) "
"and save your presentation in two file formats -- for example, odp and pdf "
"-- and on at least one additional device -- for example, on your computer "
"and on a USB stick."
msgstr ""
"Se till att presentationen är aktuell, både information och skärmbilder. "
"Spara den i två filformat, till exempel ODP och PDF, och på minst en "
"ytterligare enhet, till exempel både på datorn och ett USB-minne."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Offers material for workshops such as a whiteboard, projector, and screen."
msgstr ""
"Tillhandahåller material för workshoppar, såsom whiteboardtavla, projektor "
"och duk."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Once you've answered those questions, you're ready to plan your training!"
msgstr "När du har besvarat frågorna är du redo att planera utbildningen!"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Other questions to ask yourself before deciding to do a training:"
msgstr ""
"Andra frågor att ställa dig innan du bestämmer dig för att hålla en "
"utbildning:"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Promote your event in your community's spaces, taking safety into "
"consideration."
msgstr ""
"Marknadsför evenemanget i gemenskapens kanaler med hänsyn till säkerheten."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Provides WiFi access to guests."
msgstr "Ger gäster tillgång till Wi-Fi."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Running security training is a fun and rewarding way to help your community "
"conduct human rights work safely."
msgstr ""
"Att hålla säkerhetsutbildningar är ett roligt och givande sätt att hjälpa "
"gemenskapen att bedriva människorättsarbete på ett säkert sätt."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Security trainings can help people communicate and use the internet safely, "
"but there are additional considerations to be made before training some at-"
"risk groups."
msgstr ""
"Säkerhetsutbildningar kan hjälpa människor att kommunicera och använda "
"internet säkert, men det finns ytterligare överväganden innan vissa "
"riskutsatta grupper utbildas."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Sense check"
msgstr "Rimlighetskontroll"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Share the agenda on a projector or on a whiteboard so that your participants "
"can ready themselves for the day."
msgstr ""
"Visa dagordningen med en projektor eller på en whiteboardtavla så att "
"deltagarna kan förbereda sig inför dagen."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Show the participants other resources like [sec.eff.org](https://"
"sec.eff.org)."
msgstr ""
"Visa deltagarna andra resurser, till exempel [sec.eff.org](https://"
"sec.eff.org)."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Show the participants the resources at [community.torproject.org](/) and "
"[support.torproject.org](https://support.torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Visa deltagarna resurserna på [community.torproject.org](/) och "
"[support.torproject.org](https://support.torproject.org)."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"That's why we recommend this resource from EFF's Security Education "
"Companion, [\"Am I the right person to give this training?\"](https://"
"www.securityeducationcompanion.org/articles/am-i-the-right-person)."
msgstr ""
"Därför rekommenderar vi resursen [”Am I the right person to give this "
"training?”](https://www.securityeducationcompanion.org/articles/am-i-the-"
"right-person) från EFF:s Security Education Companion."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Think about how you will evaluate your success at the training, collect "
"feedback (e.g. feedback form)."
msgstr ""
"Fundera på hur du ska utvärdera utbildningens resultat och samla in "
"återkoppling, till exempel med ett återkopplingsformulär."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"This resource can help you be sure that you're doing the best by the "
"community of people you wish to train."
msgstr ""
"Resursen kan hjälpa dig att säkerställa att du gör det bästa möjliga för "
"gemenskapen som du vill utbilda."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"Under many circumstances, social media is great for promotion, but for "
"higher risk groups, you may want to use a smaller word-of-mouth network or "
"require community members to share information individually to other trusted "
"people."
msgstr ""
"Sociala medier är ofta utmärkta för marknadsföring, men för grupper med "
"högre risk kan det vara bättre att använda ett mindre nätverk genom "
"personliga rekommendationer eller låta gemenskapsmedlemmar dela "
"informationen individuellt med andra betrodda personer."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "We recommend leaving the hands-on bit at the end of a workshop."
msgstr "Vi rekommenderar att den praktiska delen läggs i slutet av workshopen."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Will you be able to handle this alone? Or will you require partners?"
msgstr "Kan du hantera detta ensam eller behöver du samarbetspartner?"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid ""
"You can also start the training by asking participants to come up with their "
"own community agreements for the space."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också börja utbildningen med att låta deltagarna ta fram gemensamma "
"överenskommelser för utrymmet."

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "_Am I the right person to give this training?_"
msgstr "_Är jag rätt person att hålla den här utbildningen?_"

#: content/training/best-practices/contents.lr:page.cta
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/best-practices/
msgid "Best Practices for Trainers"
msgstr "Bästa praxis för utbildare"

