msgid "Training Resources"
msgstr "Resurser för utbildning"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"After running a couple of Tor trainings, you will find that first time users "
"have some similar questions about Tor."
msgstr ""
"Efter några Tor-utbildningar märker du att förstagångsanvändare ofta har "
"liknande frågor om Tor."

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"For an extensive resource, check [Support portal](https://"
"support.torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"En omfattande resurs finns i [supportportalen](https://"
"support.torproject.org)."

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"Outlined below are some of the most frequent questions we get during our "
"training sessions. Be prepared for these questions before running your "
"training."
msgstr ""
"Nedan finns några av de vanligaste frågorna vi får under utbildningar. "
"Förbered dig på dem innan du håller utbildningen."

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Can I browse HTTPS sites with Tor?](https://support.torproject.org/about-"
"tor/security/https-encryption-and-tor/)"
msgstr ""
"[Kan jag besöka HTTPS-webbplatser med Tor?](https://support.torproject.org/"
"about-tor/security/https-encryption-and-tor/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Does running Tor Browser make me a relay?](https://support.torproject.org/"
"about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay)"
msgstr ""
"[Blir jag ett relä när jag kör Tor Browser?](https://support.torproject.org/"
"about-tor/alt-design/make-every-user-a-relay)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Does using Tor Browser protect other applications on my computer?](https://"
"support.torproject.org/tor-browser/features/managing-identities/)"
msgstr ""
"[Skyddar Tor Browser andra appar på datorn?](https://support.torproject.org/"
"tor-browser/features/managing-identities/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Is it possible to find out the path that a client is taking on the Tor "
"Network?](https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/)"
msgstr ""
"[Går det att ta reda på vilken väg en klient tar genom Tor-nätverket?]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/abuse/help-trace-tor-user/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Is there a backdoor in Tor?](https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/"
"security/no-backdoor/)"
msgstr ""
"[Finns det en bakdörr i Tor?](https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/"
"security/no-backdoor/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Is using Tor with a VPN more secure?](https://support.torproject.org/tor-"
"browser/general/vpn-with-tor/)"
msgstr ""
"[Är det säkrare att använda Tor med ett VPN?](https://support.torproject.org/"
"tor-browser/general/vpn-with-tor/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Tor Browser won't connect, but it doesn’t seem to be an issue with "
"censorship.](https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/encountering-issues/"
"troubleshooting/)"
msgstr ""
"[Tor Browser ansluter inte, men problemet verkar inte bero på censur.]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/encountering-issues/"
"troubleshooting/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[What is a bridge?](https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/"
"what-is-a-bridge/)"
msgstr ""
"[Vad är en bro?](https://support.torproject.org/relays/getting-started/what-"
"is-a-bridge/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[What is the difference between using Tor Browser and 'incognito mode' or "
"private tabs? ](https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/general/tb-vs-"
"incognito-mode/)"
msgstr ""
"[Vad är skillnaden mellan Tor Browser och inkognitoläge eller privata "
"flikar?](https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/general/tb-vs-incognito-"
"mode/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[When I use Tor Browser, will anyone be able to tell which websites I visit?]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/)"
msgstr ""
"[Kan någon se vilka webbplatser jag besöker när jag använder Tor Browser?]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/protections/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Who funds Tor?](https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/who-"
"funds-tor/)"
msgstr ""
"[Vem finansierar Tor?](https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/introduction/"
"who-funds-tor/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Why did my search engine switch to DuckDuckGo? Or what is DuckDuckGo?]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/tor-browser/features/default-search-engine/)"
msgstr ""
"[Varför byttes min sökmotor till DuckDuckGo, och vad är DuckDuckGo?](https://"
"support.torproject.org/tor-browser/features/default-search-engine/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Why don't you prevent bad people from doing bad things when using Tor?]"
"(https://support.torproject.org/abuse/prevent-bad-people/)"
msgstr ""
"[Varför hindrar ni inte illasinnade personer från att göra dåliga saker med "
"Tor?](https://support.torproject.org/abuse/prevent-bad-people/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"[Why is it called Tor?](https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/"
"introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/)"
msgstr ""
"[Varför heter det Tor?](https://support.torproject.org/about-tor/"
"introduction/why-is-it-called-tor/)"

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid ""
"People who are new to the Tor project, quite often, ask similar questions, "
"and we can help you prepare for these questions."
msgstr ""
"Personer som är nya inom Tor ställer ofta liknande frågor, och vi kan hjälpa "
"dig att förbereda svaren."

#: content/training/faq/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/faq/
msgid "Tor Training FAQ"
msgstr "Vanliga frågor om Tor-utbildningar"

#: content/training/feedback/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/
msgid ""
"During training, it is very common that users experience pain points and "
"frustrations."
msgstr ""
"Det är mycket vanligt att användare stöter på problem och frustration under "
"en utbildning."

#: content/training/feedback/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/
msgid ""
"It's very important that you read the [User Research Guidelines](https://"
"community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/) and both participant and "
"training feedback beforehand, so you can better understand what to take "
"notes about and how to care about users data privacy."
msgstr ""
"Det är mycket viktigt att du i förväg läser [riktlinjerna för "
"användarundersökningar](https://community.torproject.org/user-research/"
"guidelines/) och återkopplingen från både deltagare och utbildare. Då "
"förstår du bättre vad du bör anteckna och hur användarnas dataintegritet ska "
"skyddas."

#: content/training/feedback/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/
msgid ""
"Knowing them can help the community to develop and make necessary user-"
"centered improvements on Tor tools."
msgstr ""
"Kunskap om problemen hjälper gemenskapen att utveckla och göra nödvändiga "
"användarcentrerade förbättringar av Tor-verktygen."

#: content/training/feedback/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/
msgid ""
"Use these materials to collect [participants' feedback](participant) about "
"the training, and [this form to report](trainer) your training and user "
"feedback to us."
msgstr ""
"Använd materialet för att samla in [deltagarnas återkoppling](participant) "
"om utbildningen och [det här formuläret](trainer) för att rapportera "
"utbildningen och användarnas återkoppling till oss."

#: content/training/feedback/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/
msgid ""
"We appreciate all the time you're taking to teach and improve Tor tools!"
msgstr ""
"Vi uppskattar all tid du lägger på att undervisa och förbättra Tor-verktygen!"

#: content/training/feedback/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/
msgid "We rely on user feedback to improve our software."
msgstr ""
"Vi förlitar oss på återkoppling från användare för att förbättra "
"programvaran."

#: content/training/feedback/contents.lr:page.cta
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/
msgid "Help us to improve Tor"
msgstr "Hjälp oss att förbättra Tor"

#: content/training/feedback/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/
msgid ""
"We rely on user feedback to improve our software. Use these resources to "
"collect feedback during your Tor Training."
msgstr ""
"Vi förlitar oss på återkoppling från användare för att förbättra "
"programvaran. Använd resurserna för att samla in återkoppling under Tor-"
"utbildningen."

#: content/training/feedback/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/
msgid "Training Feedback"
msgstr "Återkoppling om utbildningar"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid ""
"(Consider an answer of 1 as \"I don't think I need protection\", and 5 as "
"\"I really need protection\"):"
msgstr ""
"(Betrakta svaret 1 som ”Jag tror inte att jag behöver skydd” och 5 som ”Jag "
"behöver verkligen skydd”):"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "**Note:** *This file should be filled by the training participants.*"
msgstr "**Obs!** *Filen ska fyllas i av utbildningsdeltagarna.*"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "**Please share**:"
msgstr "**Vänligen dela med dig**:"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "**Thank you!**"
msgstr "**Tack!**"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "1. Is this your first Digital Security training?"
msgstr "1. Är detta din första utbildning i digital säkerhet?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "10. What gender do you identify as?"
msgstr "10. Vilken könsidentitet har du?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "11. Would you describe yourself mostly as a..."
msgstr "11. Hur skulle du främst beskriva dig själv?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "12. How old are you?"
msgstr "12. Hur gammal är du?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "13. How can this training be useful for your work?"
msgstr "13. Hur kan utbildningen vara användbar i ditt arbete?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid ""
"14. Are there any additional topics missing that you would still like to "
"learn?"
msgstr ""
"14. Saknas det några ytterligare ämnen som du fortfarande skulle vilja lära "
"dig om?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "2. Is this the first Tor training you attend?"
msgstr "2. Är detta den första Tor-utbildningen du deltar i?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid ""
"3. On a scale of 1 to 5, circle the option of how strongly you believe you "
"need to protect your privacy and security online."
msgstr ""
"3. Ringa in på en skala från 1 till 5 hur starkt du anser att du behöver "
"skydda din integritet och säkerhet på nätet."

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "4. What types of devices do you use to access the Internet?"
msgstr "4. Vilka slags enheter använder du för att komma åt internet?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "5. Have you used Tor before?"
msgstr "5. Har du använt Tor tidigare?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "6. How often do you use Tor?"
msgstr "6. Hur ofta använder du Tor?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "7. Which of the following Tor-powered products do you use?"
msgstr "7. Vilka av följande Tor-baserade produkter använder du?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "8. How often do you use a VPN?"
msgstr "8. Hur ofta använder du ett VPN?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "9. Which VPN do you use?"
msgstr "9. Vilket VPN använder du?"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "Country:"
msgstr "Land:"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "Date:"
msgstr "Datum:"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "Facilitator/Trainer:"
msgstr "Handledare/utbildare:"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"Feel free to contact us if you have any questions or suggestions at ``ux-"
"team@torproject.org``."
msgstr ""
"Kontakta oss gärna på ``ux-team@torproject.org`` om du har frågor eller "
"förslag."

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "Organization:"
msgstr "Organisation:"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "Training Participants Survey"
msgstr "Enkät för utbildningsdeltagare"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ At least once a day"
msgstr "▢ Minst en gång om dagen"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ At least once a week"
msgstr "▢ Minst en gång i veckan"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Between 20 - 40"
msgstr "▢ Mellan 20 och 40"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Day to day technology user"
msgstr "▢ Vanlig teknikanvändare"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Desktop or laptop computer"
msgstr "▢ Stationär eller bärbar dator"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Female"
msgstr "▢ Kvinna"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ I do not use a VPN"
msgstr "▢ Jag använder inte VPN"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Just in specific situations"
msgstr "▢ Endast i särskilda situationer"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Less than 20"
msgstr "▢ Under 20"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Male"
msgstr "▢ Man"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Mobile/cell phone"
msgstr "▢ Mobiltelefon"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ More than 40"
msgstr "▢ Över 40"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ N/A"
msgstr "▢ Inte tillämpligt"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Non binary"
msgstr "▢ Ickebinär"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Other:"
msgstr "▢ Annat:"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Prefer not to disclose"
msgstr "▢ Vill inte uppge"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Someone that has a good understanding of tools and how things work"
msgstr "▢ En person med god förståelse för verktyg och hur saker fungerar"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Tablet"
msgstr "▢ Surfplatta"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Technical Expert"
msgstr "▢ Teknisk expert"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Tor Browser for Android"
msgstr "▢ Tor Browser för Android"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Tor Browser for Desktop"
msgstr "▢ Tor Browser för datorer"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "▢ Yes - ▢ No"
msgstr "▢ Ja – ▢ Nej"

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid ""
"Use this form to collect participants' feedback about Tor training sessions. "
"Print, distribute and ask participants to fill it by the end of the training."
msgstr ""
"Använd formuläret för att samla in deltagarnas återkoppling om Tor-"
"utbildningar. Skriv ut och dela ut det och be deltagarna fylla i det i "
"slutet av utbildningen."

#: content/training/feedback/participants/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/participants/
msgid "Training participants survey"
msgstr "Enkät för utbildningsdeltagare"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "**Date:**"
msgstr "**Datum:**"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "**Facilitator:**"
msgstr "**Handledare:**"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "**Note:**"
msgstr "**Obs!**"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "**Organization:**"
msgstr "**Organisation:**"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "Activities Done"
msgstr "Genomförda aktiviteter"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"Add anything that can be useful for you, feel free to use bullet points."
msgstr ""
"Lägg till sådant som kan vara användbart för dig. Använd gärna punktlistor."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "Audience"
msgstr "Målgrupp"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"Describing the venue is helpful to understand the context of your HRD "
"audience and what is needed to improve your training next time. Share with "
"us some notes about it (for instance, if it is a community center, has "
"internet, etc)."
msgstr ""
"En beskrivning av platsen hjälper oss att förstå sammanhanget för "
"deltagarna, som är människorättsförsvarare, och vad som behöver förbättras "
"till nästa utbildning. Dela några anteckningar om den, till exempel om det "
"är ett allaktivitetshus och om internet finns."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "Feedback about Tor in general"
msgstr "Återkoppling om Tor i allmänhet"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "Feedback about Tor tools"
msgstr "Återkoppling om Tor-verktyg"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "How can Tor support you better next time?"
msgstr "Hur kan Tor ge dig bättre stöd nästa gång?"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "If possible, include gender diversity as well."
msgstr "Ta om möjligt även hänsyn till könsmångfald."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"List here up to 10 questions that the group brought up during the training."
msgstr "Lista upp till tio frågor som gruppen tog upp under utbildningen."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"List the participants' feedback about Tor here <small>(how they believe Tor "
"can support their work, what they expect from digital security tools, etc)</"
"small>."
msgstr ""
"Lista deltagarnas återkoppling om Tor här <small>(hur de tror att Tor kan "
"stödja deras arbete, vad de förväntar sig av verktyg för digital säkerhet "
"och så vidare)</small>."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"List the participants' feedback about the Tor tool they learned and "
"installed here <small>(Example: were participants able to install the Tor "
"tool? Did it work after installation? If it didn't, please list what device "
"- model and operating system - was the participant using, as well as the "
"kind of problems they experienced. If possible, also share the error log. If "
"you were able to troubleshoot and solve the problem, please share it)</"
"small>."
msgstr ""
"Lista deltagarnas återkoppling om Tor-verktyget som de lärde sig använda och "
"installerade här <small>(Exempel: Kunde deltagarna installera Tor-verktyget? "
"Fungerade det efter installationen? Om inte, ange vilken enhet – modell och "
"operativsystem – deltagaren använde och vilka problem som uppstod. Dela om "
"möjligt även felloggen. Om du kunde felsöka och lösa problemet får du gärna "
"beskriva lösningen.)</small>."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"List the participants' feedback about the training <small>(for instance: if "
"the participants need more trainings in the same topics, if they asked for "
"more tools on privacy and security, etc)</small>."
msgstr ""
"Lista deltagarnas återkoppling om utbildningen <small>(till exempel om de "
"behöver fler utbildningar om samma ämnen eller efterfrågade fler "
"integritets- och säkerhetsverktyg)</small>."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "Number of participants:"
msgstr "Antal deltagare:"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "Questions from the group"
msgstr "Frågor från gruppen"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"Tell us about the activity you just did, which tools did you cover, what was "
"the main goal for the activity. Feel free to use bullet points."
msgstr ""
"Berätta om aktiviteten du just genomförde, vilka verktyg som togs upp och "
"aktivitetens huvudsakliga mål. Använd gärna punktlistor."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "This file should be filled by the trainer/facilitator or note taker."
msgstr ""
"Filen ska fyllas i av utbildaren, handledaren eller den som för anteckningar."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "Training Feedback Report"
msgstr "Rapport om återkoppling från utbildningen"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "Venue Notes"
msgstr "Anteckningar om platsen"

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"We want to know who our users are. We don't like boolean options here, so a "
"qualitative descriptive paragraph illustrating if you are working with human "
"rights defenders, journalists, or students is very useful."
msgstr ""
"Vi vill veta vilka våra användare är. Vi vill inte ha ja/nej-alternativ här, "
"så ett kvalitativt beskrivande stycke om huruvida du arbetar med "
"människorättsförsvarare, journalister eller studenter är mycket användbart."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid ""
"This template guides the trainer through reporting user and trainer needs "
"when running a Tor training. Use it to report your training to us."
msgstr ""
"Mallen hjälper utbildaren att rapportera användarnas och utbildarens behov "
"under en Tor-utbildning. Använd den för att rapportera utbildningen till oss."

#: content/training/feedback/trainer/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/feedback/trainer/
msgid "Training report"
msgstr "Utbildningsrapport"

#: content/training/partners/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/partners/
msgid ""
"Since 2018, we have formed partnerships with the following organizations. "
"They have organized Tor trainings, collected user feedback, promoted the Tor "
"Project mission and values."
msgstr ""
"Sedan 2018 har vi bildat partnerskap med följande organisationer. De har "
"ordnat Tor-utbildningar, samlat in återkoppling från användare och främjat "
"The Tor Projects uppdrag och värderingar."

#: content/training/partners/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/partners/
msgid ""
"Since 2018, we have formed parterships with the following organizations."
msgstr "Sedan 2018 har vi bildat partnerskap med följande organisationer."

#: content/training/partners/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/partners/
msgid "Partners"
msgstr "Partner"

#: content/training/resources/contents.lr:community-resources.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/resources/
msgid ""
"All training material is available under the [Creative Commons Attribution-"
"ShareAlike License 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/) (CC "
"BY-SA 4.0)."
msgstr ""
"Allt utbildningsmaterial är tillgängligt under licensen [Creative Commons "
"Erkännande-DelaLika 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/) "
"(CC BY-SA 4.0)."

#: content/training/resources/contents.lr:community-resources.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/resources/
msgid ""
"To request a Tor training for your organization or community, please contact "
"us through the email [training at torproject.org]"
"(mailto:training@torproject.org)."
msgstr ""
"Kontakta oss via [training at torproject.org]"
"(mailto:training@torproject.org) för att begära en Tor-utbildning för din "
"organisation eller gemenskap."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"1. **Your threat model.** A high-profile activist already under a lot of "
"surveillance, for example, might attract more attention when reaching out to "
"other activists to run a digital security training."
msgstr ""
"1. **Din hotmodell.** En framträdande aktivist som redan övervakas intensivt "
"kan till exempel dra till sig mer uppmärksamhet när den kontaktar andra "
"aktivister för att hålla en utbildning i digital säkerhet."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"2. **The laws and regulations in the country.** Consult with local lawyers "
"and local freedom of expression organizations and learn whether your country "
"has a record in prosecuting individuals engaging in similar types of "
"activities."
msgstr ""
"2. **Landets lagar och regler.** Rådgör med lokala jurister och "
"organisationer för yttrandefrihet och ta reda på om landet tidigare har "
"lagfört personer som ägnat sig åt liknande verksamhet."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"3. **The types of training.** Not all trainings carry the same weight in "
"terms of potential risk."
msgstr ""
"3. **Utbildningstypen.** Alla utbildningar medför inte samma möjliga risk."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"4. **The audience.** Gathering university students might not attract "
"attention, but if you're gathering a group of journalists working with "
"leaked documents about government corruption, you might need to take extra "
"care to reach out to them in a private way."
msgstr ""
"4. **Målgruppen.** Att samla universitetsstudenter kanske inte väcker "
"uppmärksamhet, men om du samlar journalister som arbetar med läckta dokument "
"om myndighetskorruption kan du behöva kontakta dem på ett extra varsamt och "
"privat sätt."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"5. **The training venue.** Running a Tor training in some spaces could "
"expose your participants' identities."
msgstr ""
"5. **Utbildningsplatsen.** En Tor-utbildning på vissa platser kan avslöja "
"deltagarnas identiteter."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"Additionally, while many countries do not have laws specifically prohibiting "
"the activity of running a digital security training, the use of digital "
"security tools may still be criminalized in certain countries under other, "
"broader laws."
msgstr ""
"Även om många länder inte har lagar som uttryckligen förbjuder utbildningar "
"i digital säkerhet kan användningen av digitala säkerhetsverktyg vara "
"kriminaliserad i vissa länder genom andra, bredare lagar."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"Additionally, your communication with us is not protected by any legal "
"privilege, so law enforcement may subpoena and obtain any information you "
"give us."
msgstr ""
"Din kommunikation med oss skyddas inte heller av någon juridisk sekretess. "
"Brottsbekämpande myndigheter kan därför begära ut och få den information du "
"lämnar till oss."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "Anonymity software?"
msgstr "Anonymitetsprogramvara?"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"Are there laws in my country that require Internet Service Providers (ISPs) "
"to track my online activity?"
msgstr ""
"Finns det lagar i mitt land som kräver att internetleverantörer spårar min "
"nätaktivitet?"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "Cryptography?"
msgstr "Kryptografi?"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "Does my country prohibit me from using:"
msgstr "Förbjuder mitt land att jag använder:"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "Evaluating risks"
msgstr "Bedöm risker"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"For example, talking about privacy in the digital age might be appreciated, "
"but teaching how to circumvent government censorship could be a serious "
"felony."
msgstr ""
"Att tala om integritet i den digitala tidsåldern kan till exempel "
"uppskattas, medan undervisning om att kringgå myndighetscensur kan vara ett "
"allvarligt brott."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"For example, using Tor Browser may be viewed as illegal or anti-government "
"activity."
msgstr ""
"Användning av Tor Browser kan till exempel betraktas som olaglig eller "
"regeringsfientlig verksamhet."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"Has anyone in my country ever been criminalized based on their internet "
"activity? (This does not necessarily need to be specific to digital security "
"training or use of Tor.)"
msgstr ""
"Har någon i mitt land kriminaliserats på grund av sin internetaktivitet? Det "
"behöver inte uttryckligen ha gällt utbildning i digital säkerhet eller "
"användning av Tor."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"However, in some countries and in certain circumstances, it's possible that "
"simply a gathering as human rights defenders could be risky, illegal, or "
"even lead to imprisonment, physical assaults, large fines, threats, "
"placement on government watch lists, and targeting for surveillance."
msgstr ""
"I vissa länder och under vissa omständigheter kan dock enbart en sammankomst "
"med människorättsförsvarare vara riskabel eller olaglig och till och med "
"leda till fängelse, fysiska angrepp, höga böter, hot, placering på "
"myndigheters bevakningslistor eller riktad övervakning."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"However, we may be able to put you in touch with lawyers who are capable of "
"addressing your questions and/or concerns."
msgstr ""
"Vi kanske dock kan förmedla kontakt med jurister som kan besvara dina frågor "
"eller hantera din oro."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"Ideally, you should use a private space where you control the participants' "
"entrance."
msgstr ""
"Helst bör du använda en privat plats där du styr deltagarnas tillträde."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"If the space isn't private, check before the training to find out if "
"participants are comfortable with revealing their identity to a third party."
msgstr ""
"Om platsen inte är privat bör du före utbildningen kontrollera om deltagarna "
"är bekväma med att avslöja sin identitet för tredje part."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"If you want to run a Tor training for the first time and you don't know how "
"to assess the political and social environment, we strongly encourage you "
"read this document and, in case of doubt, to reach out to the Tor Community "
"Team privately."
msgstr ""
"Om du vill hålla en Tor-utbildning för första gången och inte vet hur den "
"politiska och sociala miljön ska bedömas rekommenderar vi starkt att du "
"läser dokumentet och vid tveksamhet kontaktar Tors gemenskapsteam privat."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "Is it illegal for me to access certain websites?"
msgstr "Är det olagligt för mig att besöka vissa webbplatser?"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "Note, this is not an exhaustive list of questions."
msgstr "Observera att detta inte är en uttömmande lista med frågor."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"Please note that we are not lawyers, and any information we give you does "
"not constitute legal advice."
msgstr ""
"Observera att vi inte är jurister och att informationen vi ger inte utgör "
"juridisk rådgivning."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"Some potential risks of running a digital security training are only valid "
"in specific contexts."
msgstr ""
"Vissa möjliga risker med att hålla en utbildning i digital säkerhet gäller "
"endast i särskilda sammanhang."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"Some questions you may want to answer before running a digital security "
"training include:"
msgstr ""
"Några frågor som du kan behöva besvara innan du håller en utbildning i "
"digital säkerhet är:"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "Some relevant resources include:"
msgstr "Några relevanta resurser är:"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "The potential risks associated with running a Tor training depend on:"
msgstr "De möjliga riskerna med en Tor-utbildning beror på:"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"To our knowledge, no Tor trainer has ever faced consequences as a result of "
"training others or speaking about Tor."
msgstr ""
"Såvitt vi känner till har ingen Tor-utbildare någonsin drabbats av följder "
"på grund av att ha utbildat andra eller talat om Tor."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "[EFF Know your rights](https://www.eff.org/issues/know-your-rights)"
msgstr ""
"[EFF – Känn till dina rättigheter](https://www.eff.org/issues/know-your-"
"rights)"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "[EFF Tor legal FAQ](../../relay/community-resources/eff-tor-legal-faq/)"
msgstr ""
"[EFF:s juridiska frågor och svar om Tor](../../relay/community-resources/eff-"
"tor-legal-faq/)"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "[OONI disclaimer](https://ooni.org/about/risks/)"
msgstr "[OONI:s ansvarsfriskrivning](https://ooni.org/about/risks/)"

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid ""
"Things you should be aware of before running a digital security training."
msgstr ""
"Saker du bör känna till innan du håller en utbildning i digital säkerhet."

#: content/training/risks/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/training/risks/
msgid "Risks"
msgstr "Risker"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Any relevant logs and/or screenshots"
msgstr "Alla relevanta loggar eller skärmbilder"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"As a small thank you for helping us keep Tor Browser stable and bug-free, "
"Alpha Testers can collect [special badges](https://forum.torproject.org/"
"badges) by reporting bugs on the Tor Forum."
msgstr ""
"Som ett litet tack för att du hjälper oss att hålla Tor Browser stabil och "
"fri från fel kan alfatestare samla [särskilda märken](https://"
"forum.torproject.org/badges) genom att rapportera fel på Tor-forumet."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Collect new forum badges"
msgstr "Samla nya forummärken"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Describe what you expected to happen instead"
msgstr "Beskriv vad du förväntade dig skulle hända i stället"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Download the latest [Tor Browser Alpha](https://www.torproject.org/download/"
"alpha/) available for your platform."
msgstr ""
"Hämta den senaste [Tor Browser Alpha](https://www.torproject.org/download/"
"alpha/) för din plattform."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Each new version of Tor Browser Alpha is accompanied by a release post on "
"the [Tor Blog](https://blog.torproject.org/category/applications/) and "
"[Forum](https://forum.torproject.org/c/feedback/tor-browser-alpha-feedback/"
"6) that includes a short, specific list of changes to test."
msgstr ""
"Varje ny version av Tor Browser Alpha åtföljs av ett versionsinlägg på [Tor-"
"bloggen](https://blog.torproject.org/category/applications/) och [forumet]"
"(https://forum.torproject.org/c/feedback/tor-browser-alpha-feedback/6) med "
"en kort och konkret lista över ändringar att testa."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Earn the bronze Alpha Tester badge for reporting your first bug that gets "
"liked by a Tor Project team-member, and keep testing to unlock the silver "
"and gold badges too."
msgstr ""
"Få bronsmärket Alpha Tester när du rapporterar ditt första fel som gillas av "
"en medlem i ett team inom The Tor Project. Fortsätt testa för att även låsa "
"upp silver- och guldmärkena."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Feeding back to our developers"
msgstr "Ge återkoppling till utvecklarna"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Firstly, check to see if the issue is unique to Tor Browser Alpha, or if "
"it’s present in [Tor Browser’s stable release](https://www.torproject.org/"
"download/) and/or Firefox as well."
msgstr ""
"Kontrollera först om problemet endast finns i Tor Browser Alpha eller även i "
"[den stabila Tor Browser-versionen](https://www.torproject.org/download/) "
"eller Firefox."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Happy testing!"
msgstr "Lycka till med testningen!"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "How did you install Tor Browser?"
msgstr "Hur installerade du Tor Browser?"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"However, Firefox updates can introduce new bugs to Tor Browser in "
"unpredictable ways. As such, we encourage you to continue to test features "
"and functionality beyond what's listed in the changelog too."
msgstr ""
"Firefox-uppdateringar kan dock införa nya fel i Tor Browser på oförutsägbara "
"sätt. Därför uppmuntrar vi dig att även fortsätta testa funktioner utöver "
"dem som nämns i ändringsloggen."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"If you’re the first to discover the issue, please create a new thread in the "
"[Tor Browser Alpha Feedback](https://forum.torproject.org/c/feedback/tor-"
"browser-alpha-feedback/6) category."
msgstr ""
"Om du är den första som upptäcker problemet skapar du en ny tråd i kategorin "
"[Tor Browser Alpha Feedback](https://forum.torproject.org/c/feedback/tor-"
"browser-alpha-feedback/6)."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"In addition to finding and reporting bugs, Alpha testers are also encouraged "
"to provide feedback about new and experimental features to the team before "
"they reach Tor Browser stable."
msgstr ""
"Utöver att hitta och rapportera fel uppmuntras alfatestare att ge teamet "
"återkoppling om nya och experimentella funktioner innan de når den stabila "
"Tor Browser-versionen."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Instead, please limit your use of Tor Browser Alpha and Nightly to preview "
"new features, test their performance and provide feedback before their "
"release."
msgstr ""
"Begränsa i stället användningen av Tor Browser Alpha och Nightly till att "
"förhandsgranska nya funktioner, testa deras prestanda och lämna återkoppling "
"före lanseringen."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Make sure to include the following details:"
msgstr "Ta med följande uppgifter:"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Once you’ve verified that the problem you’ve encountered is indeed an issue "
"with Tor Browser Alpha, check the [Tor Browser Alpha Feedback category]"
"(https://forum.torproject.org/c/feedback/tor-browser-alpha-feedback/6) on "
"the Forum to see if it’s been reported already. If so, you can add your "
"report to the same thread."
msgstr ""
"När du har bekräftat att problemet verkligen gäller Tor Browser Alpha söker "
"du i kategorin [Tor Browser Alpha Feedback](https://forum.torproject.org/c/"
"feedback/tor-browser-alpha-feedback/6) på forumet för att se om det redan "
"har rapporterats. Lägg i så fall till din rapport i samma tråd."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Or, if you have a GitLab account, post any bugs you find using the templates "
"provided in [applications/tor-browser](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"applications/tor-browser/-/issues) (but make sure to search the project for "
"duplicates first)."
msgstr ""
"Om du har ett GitLab-konto kan du i stället rapportera fel med mallarna i "
"[applications/tor-browser](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/applications/"
"tor-browser/-/issues). Sök först efter dubbletter i projektet."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Outline the steps necessary to reproduce the issue"
msgstr "Beskriv stegen som krävs för att återskapa problemet"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Sign up for an account on the [Tor Forum](https://forum.torproject.org/) (if "
"you'd like to submit your feedback there)."
msgstr ""
"Skapa ett konto på [Tor-forumet](https://forum.torproject.org/) om du vill "
"lämna återkopplingen där."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Start testing and follow the steps below to feed back any issues you "
"discover to our developers."
msgstr ""
"Börja testa och följ stegen nedan för att rapportera eventuella problem som "
"du upptäcker till våra utvecklare."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Summarize the issue concisely"
msgstr "Sammanfatta problemet kortfattat"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "To become an Alpha Tester all you need to do is:"
msgstr "Det enda du behöver göra för att bli alfatestare är att:"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"To help keep Tor Browser available on Windows, Linux, MacOS and Android, we "
"rely on a community of volunteer Alpha testers to try out early versions of "
"Tor Browser before their general release."
msgstr ""
"För att Tor Browser ska fortsätta vara tillgänglig för Windows, Linux, macOS "
"och Android förlitar vi oss på en gemenskap av frivilliga alfatestare som "
"provar tidiga versioner av Tor Browser innan de släpps till allmänheten."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"Tor Browser Alpha and Nightly are unstable versions of Tor Browser and "
"should not be used for activities that could put you at risk."
msgstr ""
"Tor Browser Alpha och Nightly är instabila versioner av Tor Browser och bör "
"inte användas för aktiviteter som kan utsätta dig för risker."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "What are the risks?"
msgstr "Vilka är riskerna?"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"What platform are you using? E.g. Windows 11, Debian 11.3, MacOS 12.3, "
"Android 12 etc."
msgstr ""
"Vilken plattform använder du? Till exempel Windows 11, Debian 11.3, macOS "
"12.3 eller Android 12."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "What security level Tor Browser is set to?"
msgstr "Vilken säkerhetsnivå är Tor Browser inställd på?"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "What to look out for"
msgstr "Vad du bör vara uppmärksam på"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"What type of device are you using? E.g. Lenovo ThinkPad, MacBook Air, "
"Samsung Galaxy S22, Google Pixel 6 etc."
msgstr ""
"Vilken typ av enhet använder du? Till exempel Lenovo ThinkPad, MacBook Air, "
"Samsung Galaxy S22 eller Google Pixel 6."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"What version of Tor Browser Alpha are you using? E.g. Tor Browser 11.5a9"
msgstr ""
"Vilken version av Tor Browser Alpha använder du? Till exempel Tor Browser "
"11.5a9."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"You can also find a more general list of browser functionality worth "
"checking on the [Tor Browser Wiki](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"applications/tor-browser/-/wikis/Quality-Assurance)."
msgstr ""
"Du hittar även en mer allmän lista över webbläsarfunktioner som är värda att "
"kontrollera på [Tor Browser-wikin](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"applications/tor-browser/-/wikis/Quality-Assurance)."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/user-research/open/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/user-research/personas/contents.lr:page.section
#: content/user-research/reports/contents.lr:page.section
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/open/
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/personas/
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/reports/
msgid "User research"
msgstr "Användarundersökning"

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid ""
"We rely on a community of volunteer Alpha testers to try out early versions "
"of Tor Browser before their general release. Sign up to become an Alpha "
"tester."
msgstr ""
"Vi förlitar oss på en gemenskap av frivilliga alfatestare som provar tidiga "
"versioner av Tor Browser innan de släpps till allmänheten. Anmäl dig som "
"alfatestare."

#: content/user-research/become-tester/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/become-tester/
msgid "Become an alpha tester"
msgstr "Bli alfatestare"

#: content/user-research/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/
msgid ""
"Our user research is founded on the premises of consent, respect, and "
"empathy."
msgstr "Vår användarundersökning bygger på samtycke, respekt och empati."

#: content/user-research/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/
msgid "The way we build tools also builds community."
msgstr "Sättet vi bygger verktyg på bygger också gemenskap."

#: content/user-research/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/
msgid ""
"We practice human-centered design when we build tools for internet freedom."
msgstr ""
"Vi arbetar människocentrerat när vi utvecklar verktyg för internetfrihet."

#: content/user-research/contents.lr:page.body
#: content/user-research/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/
msgid "We respect our users' privacy when we conduct research."
msgstr "Vi respekterar användarnas integritet när vi genomför undersökningar."

#: content/user-research/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/
msgid ""
"You can make an impact in your community by learning from our methods and "
"helping us with user research."
msgstr ""
"Du kan göra skillnad i din gemenskap genom att lära dig av våra metoder och "
"hjälpa oss med användarundersökningar."

#: content/user-research/contents.lr:page.cta
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/
msgid "Learn about Tor users"
msgstr "Lär känna Tors användare"

#: content/user-research/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/
msgid "User Research"
msgstr "Användarundersökningar"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"**We strongly recommend that you run through the plan for your session with "
"the trainer**."
msgstr ""
"**Vi rekommenderar starkt att du går igenom planen för sessionen tillsammans "
"med utbildaren**."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"1. Write your [report](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/"
"master/community/user_research_reporting.md) (keep it simple)."
msgstr ""
"1. Skriv din [rapport](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/"
"master/community/user_research_reporting.md) (håll den enkel)."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"2. Upload it to our [Gitlab repository](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/"
"research/-/blob/master/README.md)."
msgstr ""
"2. Ladda upp den till vårt [GitLab-arkiv](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"ux/research/-/blob/master/README.md)."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"3. Create issues in the [Research repository](https://gitlab.torproject.org/"
"tpo/ux/research/-/issues)."
msgstr ""
"3. Skapa ärenden i [forskningsarkivet](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/"
"research/-/issues)."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"4. Allow the UX team time to discuss each issue and forward it to developers "
"when necessary."
msgstr ""
"4. Ge UX-teamet tid att diskutera varje ärende och vid behov vidarebefordra "
"det till utvecklarna."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "Additional links"
msgstr "Ytterligare länkar"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"After your research is complete we'll ask you to fill a form with your "
"address so we can send you a researcher kit too (including a t-shirt and "
"stickers)."
msgstr ""
"När undersökningen är klar ber vi dig fylla i ett formulär med din adress så "
"att vi även kan skicka ett forskarpaket till dig (med bland annat en T-shirt "
"och klistermärken)."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"At Tor, we don't collect invasive data about user behavior, only the data "
"necessary to improve our services. We test our software, not people."
msgstr ""
"På Tor samlar vi inte in integritetskränkande uppgifter om användarbeteende, "
"utan endast de uppgifter som behövs för att förbättra våra tjänster. Vi "
"testar vår programvara, inte människor."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "Be a good listener and open-minded"
msgstr "Var en god lyssnare och ha ett öppet sinne"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Before ending the session, coordinate with the trainer to solicit feedback "
"from the participants."
msgstr ""
"Innan du avslutar sessionen bör du samordna med utbildaren för att be "
"deltagarna om återkoppling."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Before your session, read and print the [Demographics questionnaire](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/master/"
"scripts%20and%20activities/2020/user_demographics-en.md) and [User Research "
"Reporting](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/master/"
"community/user_research_reporting.md) templates."
msgstr ""
"Läs och skriv ut mallarna för [demografienkäten](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/master/"
"scripts%20and%20activities/2020/user_demographics-en.md) och [rapportering "
"av användarundersökningar](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/"
"blob/master/community/user_research_reporting.md) före sessionen."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Congrats! You're going to run your first User Research session for Tor – and "
"we're delighted to have you on board!"
msgstr ""
"Grattis! Du ska hålla din första användarundersökningssession för Tor – och "
"vi är glada att ha dig med!"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "Coordinate with the trainer and the Tor UX team"
msgstr "Samordna med utbildaren och Tors UX-team"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "Describe and Ask for consent"
msgstr "Beskriv undersökningen och be om samtycke"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Distribute the demographics questionnaire among the participants, and help "
"answer their questions about how to fill it in if they have any."
msgstr ""
"Dela ut demografienkäten till deltagarna och hjälp dem att besvara "
"eventuella frågor om hur den ska fyllas i."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Don't forget to thank the participant again at the end of the interview."
msgstr "Glöm inte att tacka deltagaren igen i slutet av intervjun."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"During the training session we listen to the stories people tell us about "
"their lives, the laws of the jurisdictions they live in, and the "
"difficulties they are going through."
msgstr ""
"Under utbildningssessionen lyssnar vi på människors berättelser om sina liv, "
"lagarna i de jurisdiktioner där de bor och de svårigheter som de möter."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"First of all, make sure you read the [Tor Code of Conduct](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/code_of_conduct)."
msgstr ""
"Se först till att du har läst [Tors uppförandekod](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/code_of_conduct)."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "From elsewhere on the web:"
msgstr "Från andra delar av webben:"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "From the Tor Project:"
msgstr "Från The Tor Project:"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "Get prepared!"
msgstr "Förbered dig!"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Give each participant a different color of post-it per question and ask them "
"to fill it in with what they think about: 1. the software, service or skill "
"they just learned; 2. the Tor Project; and 3. Tor in general."
msgstr ""
"Ge varje deltagare en olikfärgad post-it-lapp för varje fråga och be dem "
"skriva vad de tycker om 1. programvaran, tjänsten eller färdigheten de just "
"har lärt sig, 2. The Tor Project och 3. Tor i allmänhet."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Here you will find helpful guidelines that are designed to make your "
"research easier for both you and your audience."
msgstr ""
"Här hittar du praktiska riktlinjer som är utformade för att underlätta "
"undersökningen för både dig och deltagarna."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "How to submit your findings"
msgstr "Så skickar du in dina resultat"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you don't think you'll have time to format your report using the [User "
"Research Reporting template](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/"
"blob/master/community/user_research_reporting.md), we will happily accept "
"your findings another way - for example, you can take pictures or send us "
"your raw notes."
msgstr ""
"Om du inte tror att du hinner formatera rapporten med [mallen för "
"rapportering av användarundersökningar](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/"
"research/-/blob/master/community/user_research_reporting.md) tar vi gärna "
"emot resultaten i ett annat format – du kan till exempel fotografera eller "
"skicka dina råanteckningar."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"If you're planning to install any Tor software during your exercise or "
"interviews you may need to download it before the session."
msgstr ""
"Om du planerar att installera Tor-programvara under övningen eller "
"intervjuerna kan du behöva hämta den före sessionen."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"It's easier to have this material printed and in hand, however if you prefer "
"you can use digital copies instead."
msgstr ""
"Det är enklast att ha materialet utskrivet och till hands, men du kan "
"använda digitala kopior om du föredrar det."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "It's very important for us to hear back from you too."
msgstr "Det är också mycket viktigt för oss att få återkoppling från dig."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "Keep in mind that you might not have Internet access at the venue."
msgstr "Tänk på att du kanske inte har internetåtkomst på platsen."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "Learn"
msgstr "Lär dig"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Listening is a skill that helps build bridges. We believe this doesn't just "
"apply to our services, but our communities too."
msgstr ""
"Att lyssna är en färdighet som hjälper till att bygga broar. Vi tror att "
"detta gäller både våra tjänster och våra gemenskaper."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "Report to Tor UX team"
msgstr "Rapportera till Tors UX-team"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "Respect privacy"
msgstr "Respektera integriteten"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Thank the participant for their willingness to participate and explain that "
"we are testing the product, not them."
msgstr ""
"Tacka deltagaren för att hen vill delta och förklara att det är produkten, "
"inte personen, som testas."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "The interview process"
msgstr "Intervjuprocessen"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "The interview should not last longer than 20 minutes."
msgstr "Intervjun bör inte ta längre tid än 20 minuter."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"The two of you should work together to hand out post-its to the audience."
msgstr "Ni två bör samarbeta med att dela ut post-it-lappar till deltagarna."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Their feedback can also take the form of questions - keep in mind that any "
"feedback is a good feedback."
msgstr ""
"Återkopplingen kan också bestå av frågor – kom ihåg att all återkoppling är "
"värdefull."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"This way, we can learn how to facilitate better access to information "
"through Tor. By listening, we learn."
msgstr ""
"På så sätt kan vi lära oss hur vi bättre kan underlätta åtkomsten till "
"information via Tor. Genom att lyssna lär vi oss."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"We don't keep or publish the names or contact details of research "
"participants, and any time you're going to handle participant data (be it "
"via impressions, survey submissions, or other records) you should ask for "
"their consent in writing using the [consent form](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/master/"
"scripts%20and%20activities/2021/consent_form.md) beforehand."
msgstr ""
"Vi sparar eller publicerar inte forskningsdeltagarnas namn eller "
"kontaktuppgifter. När du ska hantera deltagardata, till exempel intryck, "
"enkätsvar eller andra uppgifter, måste du först be om skriftligt samtycke "
"med hjälp av [samtyckesformuläret](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/"
"research/-/blob/master/scripts%20and%20activities/2021/consent_form.md)."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"We want to know how the session was for you, how we can improve our support "
"going forward, and if you plan to keep running user research for Tor in the "
"future."
msgstr ""
"Vi vill veta hur du upplevde sessionen, hur vi kan förbättra vårt stöd "
"framöver och om du planerar att fortsätta genomföra användarundersökningar "
"för Tor."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"When the training commences, be sure to let everyone know your role and why "
"you're taking notes during the session."
msgstr ""
"När utbildningen börjar ska du berätta för alla vilken roll du har och "
"varför du antecknar under sessionen."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"While we're not interested in the specific characteristics of individual "
"participants, it's important for us to be able to determine the reach of our "
"training sessions, usability workshops and interviews."
msgstr ""
"Vi är inte intresserade av enskilda deltagares särskilda egenskaper, men det "
"är viktigt att vi kan bedöma räckvidden för våra utbildningar, "
"användbarhetsworkshoppar och intervjuer."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"You can take notes on the printed material you will carry with you, or on "
"your computer."
msgstr ""
"Du kan anteckna på det utskrivna materialet som du tar med dig eller på "
"datorn."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"You don't have to do this alone - we can support you with meetings, guides, "
"and mentorship too if you wish."
msgstr ""
"Du behöver inte göra detta ensam – vi kan också hjälpa dig med möten, guider "
"och mentorskap."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"You'll also need to bring your chosen usability test and its accompanying "
"methodology, if applicable."
msgstr ""
"Du behöver också ta med det användbarhetstest du har valt och, om "
"tillämpligt, den tillhörande metoden."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"Your agenda must be aligned and leave sufficient time to run your interviews "
"or exercise at the end of the training session."
msgstr ""
"Dagordningen måste vara välplanerad och lämna tillräckligt med tid för "
"intervjuerna eller övningen i slutet av utbildningssessionen."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid ""
"[Reach out to the UX Team.](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/team#how-to-"
"reach-us)"
msgstr ""
"[Kontakta UX-teamet.](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/team#how-to-reach-"
"us)"

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.subtitle
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "We collect only necessary data to improve our services."
msgstr ""
"Vi samlar endast in de uppgifter som behövs för att förbättra våra tjänster."

#: content/user-research/guidelines/contents.lr:page.title
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/guidelines/
msgid "User Research Guidelines"
msgstr "Riktlinjer för användarundersökningar"

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"**Decision-making process.** We don't have a single model for decision "
"making."
msgstr "**Beslutsprocess.** Vi har ingen enskild modell för beslutsfattande."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid "**Open source for privacy.**"
msgstr "**Öppen källkod för integritet.**"

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"**We don't track participants.** We care about your privacy and security."
msgstr ""
"**Vi spårar inte deltagare.** Vi värnar om din integritet och säkerhet."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"**We don't trick participants.** We don't use trick questions in our "
"research."
msgstr ""
"**Vi lurar inte deltagare.** Vi använder inte kuggfrågor i våra "
"undersökningar."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"Add the title of your research, then select the Usability Testing template "
"option and fill it in."
msgstr ""
"Ange en titel för undersökningen, välj sedan mallen Usability Testing och "
"fyll i den."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"After choosing which study to run, open an issue in our [GitLab page]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research)."
msgstr ""
"När du har valt vilken studie du ska genomföra skapar du ett ärende på vår "
"[GitLab-sida](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research)."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"After conducting your research, it's normal to be excited to see your "
"feedback implemented as soon as possible."
msgstr ""
"När undersökningen är genomförd är det naturligt att vilja se återkopplingen "
"förverkligas så snart som möjligt."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"As a transparent research space our surveys, studies, and reports are all "
"public, and participants are free to view past studies prior to taking part "
"- however they are not advised to do so."
msgstr ""
"Eftersom vi bedriver forskning öppet är alla våra enkäter, studier och "
"rapporter offentliga, och deltagarna kan läsa tidigare studier innan de "
"deltar – men vi rekommenderar inte att de gör det."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"As a volunteer we also ask that you read and follow our [Code of Conduct]"
"(https://community.torproject.org/policies/code_of_conduct), as well our "
"[Guidelines for Research](../guidelines/)."
msgstr ""
"Som volontär ber vi dig även att läsa och följa vår [uppförandekod](https://"
"community.torproject.org/policies/code_of_conduct) och våra [riktlinjer för "
"forskning](../guidelines/)."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid "Checklist"
msgstr "Checklista"

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"However all feedback must be discussed internally across the different teams "
"at the Tor Project first."
msgstr ""
"All återkoppling måste dock först diskuteras internt mellan de olika teamen "
"inom The Tor Project."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"If this is your first time running a User Research session for the Tor "
"Project, we recommend starting with one of these studies. Both can be "
"conducted on a rolling basis and ran remotely."
msgstr ""
"Om det är första gången du genomför en användarundersökningssession för The "
"Tor Project rekommenderar vi att du börjar med en av dessa studier. Båda kan "
"genomföras fortlöpande och på distans."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"If we invite you to participate in a study, we won't track you and any "
"recordings will be erased after the report is complete."
msgstr ""
"Om vi bjuder in dig att delta i en studie spårar vi dig inte, och eventuella "
"inspelningar raderas när rapporten är klar."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"If you don't have one yet, [request a GitLab account](https://"
"support.torproject.org/misc/bug-or-feedback/)."
msgstr ""
"Om du ännu inte har ett konto kan du [begära ett GitLab-konto](https://"
"support.torproject.org/misc/bug-or-feedback/)."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"If you're already familiar with the Tor Project and user testing, have a "
"look at our [current needs for user research](../open/) and see which study "
"better suits you."
msgstr ""
"Om du redan känner till The Tor Project och användartestning kan du titta på "
"våra [aktuella behov av användarundersökningar](../open/) och se vilken "
"studie som passar dig bäst."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"In addition, collecting these demographics is required for specific studies "
"to support human rights."
msgstr ""
"För vissa studier är det dessutom nödvändigt att samla in dessa demografiska "
"uppgifter för att stödja mänskliga rättigheter."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"Learn more about our users by reading [Tor's user personas](../personas/)."
msgstr ""
"Lär dig mer om våra användare genom att läsa [Tors användarpersonor](../"
"personas/)."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"Not all of the data collected in our research is disclosed to the public, "
"but our general findings are."
msgstr ""
"Alla uppgifter som samlas in i våra undersökningar offentliggörs inte, men "
"våra övergripande resultat gör det."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"Open an issue in the [UX Research Repository](https://gitlab.torproject.org/"
"tpo/ux/research/-/issues)."
msgstr ""
"Skapa ett ärende i [UX Research-arkivet](https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/"
"ux/research/-/issues)."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"Please read our [Guidelines](../guidelines/) to get to know this process "
"more."
msgstr ""
"Läs våra [riktlinjer](../guidelines/) för att lära dig mer om processen."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid "Please remember to update the issue as your research evolves."
msgstr ""
"Kom ihåg att uppdatera ärendet i takt med att undersökningen utvecklas."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"Read and follow our [Code of Conduct](https://community.torproject.org/"
"policies/code_of_conduct)."
msgstr ""
"Läs och följ vår [uppförandekod](https://community.torproject.org/policies/"
"code_of_conduct)."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"Read the guidelines on [how to do user research with Tor](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/master/README.md)."
msgstr ""
"Läs riktlinjerna för [hur man genomför användarundersökningar med Tor]"
"(https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/master/README.md)."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"Remember to drop us an email telling us about your plans so we can follow "
"and support your research."
msgstr ""
"Kom ihåg att skicka ett e-postmeddelande till oss om dina planer så att vi "
"kan följa och stödja undersökningen."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"This means that it's often necessary to run the same research more than once "
"to validate your findings, and meet the expectations of the engineers, "
"developers, designers, researchers and others at Tor."
msgstr ""
"Det innebär att samma undersökning ofta behöver genomföras mer än en gång "
"för att resultaten ska kunna verifieras och motsvara förväntningarna hos "
"ingenjörer, utvecklare, formgivare, forskare och andra inom Tor."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"To protect our participants' privacy we take care to anonymize their "
"responses and avoid recording our sessions."
msgstr ""
"För att skydda deltagarnas integritet anonymiserar vi deras svar och "
"undviker att spela in sessionerna."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid "We advise volunteers not to record their sessions at all."
msgstr "Vi rekommenderar att volontärer inte spelar in sina sessioner alls."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"We also ask anyone running research not use software hosted by third parties "
"like cloud providers."
msgstr ""
"Vi ber också alla som genomför undersökningar att inte använda programvara "
"som tillhandahålls av tredje part, till exempel molntjänster."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"We believe it's important to collect basic demographics to help us "
"understand if we are meeting our mission regarding diversity and inclusion."
msgstr ""
"Vi anser att det är viktigt att samla in grundläggande demografiska "
"uppgifter för att förstå om vi uppfyller vårt uppdrag när det gäller "
"mångfald och inkludering."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"We don't collect personal data in our [Demographics](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/master/"
"scripts%20and%20activities/2020/user_demographics-en.md), and all questions "
"are optional."
msgstr ""
"Vi samlar inte in personuppgifter i vår [demografienkät](https://"
"gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/ux/research/-/blob/master/"
"scripts%20and%20activities/2020/user_demographics-en.md), och alla frågor är "
"frivilliga."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"We expect participants to be honest with us, and we must be honest about our "
"questions in return."
msgstr ""
"Vi förväntar oss att deltagarna är ärliga mot oss, och i gengäld måste vi "
"vara ärliga om våra frågor."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid ""
"We use free and open source software to analyze our data, and we recommend "
"our volunteers do the same."
msgstr ""
"Vi använder fri programvara med öppen källkod för att analysera våra data "
"och rekommenderar att våra volontärer gör detsamma."

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid "Where to start"
msgstr "Var du kan börja"

#: content/user-research/how-to-volunteer/contents.lr:page.body
#: https://community.torproject.org/user-research/how-to-volunteer/
msgid "Why do we run Demographics?"
msgstr "Varför genomför vi demografienkäter?"

